window.VTMB=window.VTMB||{};window.VTMB.powers={"021XfazezI4dLLcP":{"id":"021XfazezI4dLLcP","n":"Thrown Voice","d":"presence","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene","act":"Full","am":"Auspex 1","sum":"The vampire can cause their voice to emanate from any point within sight, whether as a whisper or shout.","fx":"If using this power in combination with Irresistible Voice, Presenceless Voice, or similar powers, they must roll as usual.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"123"},"amr":[{"k":"auspex","l":1}]},"06VSxeT9wIUnyplx":{"id":"06VSxeT9wIUnyplx","n":"Sway the Flock","d":"animalism","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Animal Ken","dur":"One night","act":"Full","sum":"The vampire can influence the general mood of animals over a wide area.","fx":"Any mundane attempt to control the animals increases in Difficulty equal to the number of successes on the test.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"21"}},"08qt92VLJXZhilIR":{"id":"08qt92VLJXZhilIR","n":"Gift of Malkav","d":"dementation","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Insight vs. Wits + Composure","dur":"See p. 52.","act":"Full","sum":"The madness of Malkav, the source of Dementation, is not a curse, but a noble burden. To be different or odd is to see things from another angle. Sometimes, that difference must be imposed for a subject to truly know.","fx":"The victim gains the effects of a Malkavian clan bane at a bane severity equal to the user’s Dementation rating + their power bonus with the user choosing the Attributes which the bane affects.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"66"}},"0LQccZ1x4K4nxfzt":{"id":"0LQccZ1x4K4nxfzt","n":"Plug-In","d":"alchemy","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse check","pool":"Resolve + Alchemy","dur":"If lighting a room: one scene. If powering a device, until it reaches half battery charge.","ing":"The alchemist’s blood, sanguine blood, liquid nitrogen, tungsten shavings, and a broken battery.","sum":"The alchemist is able to produce a low-level electrical current from their body, powering lights, chargers, or other devices.","fx":"The alchemist fills with electrical currents that can be used to power small devices, such as a smartphone, a personal computer, or a light bulb.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade Players Guide","page":"103"}},"0RJLAeYQ6Qb2nvxE":{"id":"0RJLAeYQ6Qb2nvxE","n":"Airborne Momentum","d":"alchemy","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Strength + Alchemy vs Strength+Athletics (if resisted)","dur":"One scene","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, choleric and sanguine human blood, champagne, bird blood, helium, scopolamine or belladonna extract","sum":"This formula enables the alchemist to lift themselves from the ground, achieving a state of swift flight or floating. They can fly in any direction, including up or down, though their carrying capacity is limited.","fx":"The flier can carry a human-sized mass, though their speed drops to walking speed.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition Corebook","page":"287"}},"0SiShiQ0dqU05QdL":{"id":"0SiShiQ0dqU05QdL","n":"Flaying Touch","d":"vicissitude","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Strength + Brawl","dur":"One attack","act":"Full","am":"Potence •","sum":"With this cruel power employed by the most cruel of the Tzimisce, the vampire can tear away a victim’s skin as easily as removing a robe, all without disturbing the muscles and other tissue beneath.","fx":"The damage type is Aggravated against mortals, but Superficial against creatures who do not require organs and blood to live, like vampires.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"204"},"amr":[{"k":"potence","l":1}]},"0vBUUccWQfdNSYkn":{"id":"0vBUUccWQfdNSYkn","n":"Fluent Endurance","d":"fortitude","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"The vampire is able to call upon their supernatural resilience effortlessly, and rarely tempt their Hunger when doing so.","fx":"Whenever the vampire uses a Blood Surge to augment a Stamina or Fortitude test, they may reroll the Rouse Check.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"79"}},"0yE0xXcbME7JWQAP":{"id":"0yE0xXcbME7JWQAP","n":"Gorgon’s Scales","d":"fortitude","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until the scene ends or the Resonance is lost, whichever comes first.","act":"Free","sum":"The Resonance of the blood in the vampire’s system grants them various defenses against the powers of other Cainites, or protects them from common vampire weaknesses.","fx":"On activation the vampire gains a set of immunities or resistances dependent on the Resonance of the blood they most recently fed upon.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"83"}},"1BzOe9rz9XaSBeI1":{"id":"1BzOe9rz9XaSBeI1","n":"Serpent’s Kiss","d":"serpentis","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","act":"Free","sum":"The vampire’s fangs grow longer and hollow, allowing them to inject a bit of their own blood in return while they feed or bite in combat.","fx":"When the vampire bites or kisses another, they may make a Rouse check to force some of their own vitae into their victim.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"151"}},"1HoOQgugvUV0jN4N":{"id":"1HoOQgugvUV0jN4N","n":"Quietus Mastery","d":"quietussanguinis","lv":5,"cost":"Free/One Rouse Check in addition to the cost of the power amplified","pool":"N/A","dur":"Per power augmented","act":"Passive","sum":"As the user masters the Discipline said to have been created by Haqim himself, the vampire figures out how all Gifts of the Blood are connected, and how all the Paths of Quietus lead to the same destination.","fx":"Powers of any Quietus Path that require touch or transmission by poison are now available to the vampire by making a gesture with their hand towards the victim (those who succeed on a Wits…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"148"}},"1LicHjeWmsabtdBD":{"id":"1LicHjeWmsabtdBD","n":"Kiss of Lachesis","d":"temporis","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Occult vs. Stamina + Occult (or Fortitude)","dur":"Instant Margins Effect 0 margins Up to 24 hours 1 margin Up to one week 2 margins Up to one month 3 margins Up to one year 4 margins Up to a decade 4 margins Up to a century 5 margins Up to one century per margin over 5","act":"Full","sum":"Vampires with this power gain limited mastery over the physical age of objects and individuals.","fx":"The vampire briefly touches the target and concentrates for a turn (in combat this requires any combination of Strength/Dexterity + Athletics/ Brawl).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"170"}},"1fZvCDHP5Sp8osvj":{"id":"1fZvCDHP5Sp8osvj","n":"Haunting Illusions","d":"chimerstry","lv":2,"cost":"One point of Willpower per target","pool":"N/A","dur":"As power modified by this.","act":"As power augmented","sum":"Haunting Illusions makes it possible for hallucinations created by Chimerstry to only be visible to a single (or more) persons, potentially driving people mad as others do not believe them to be experiencing what is clearly real to them.","fx":"To weave Ignis Fatuus or Fata Morgana into subtlety, the caster must spend a point of Willpower per target they intend to inflict in addition to the Rouse Check required by Ignis Fatus or Fata Morgana.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"48"}},"1jhUjpxgwj4V1wNw":{"id":"1jhUjpxgwj4V1wNw","n":"Hinder Mending","d":"quietuscruciatus","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"The poison remains potent for nights equal to the user’s Quietus rating","act":"Minor -2 dice/free","sum":"With Hinder Mending, the vampire concocts a special poison that prevents usage of vitae for mending, disrupting vampire targets and their other creations that utilise vitae to heal.","fx":"This contact poison has the same system as Scorpion’s Touch (see below) and is applied the same way).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"141"}},"23MgLiaYiMQ1R8Ol":{"id":"23MgLiaYiMQ1R8Ol","n":"Sense the Cycle","d":"valerenwatcher","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Instant, but the bonus lasts for the rest of the night.","act":"Free","sum":"Rather than diagnosing the sick and dying, the nascent third eye of the Watchers sees the cycle of life entire. They see the ebb and flow of lives in the streets, not the vitality locked within veins and organs.","fx":"For this power to work, the user must be able to see the target and their surroundings with their 3rd eye.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"195"}},"2FlHM1glzNQc71I0":{"id":"2FlHM1glzNQc71I0","n":"Many Voices, One Mouth","d":"dementation","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check in addition to the cost of the power amplified","pool":"Manipulation + Insight vs. Wits + Composure","dur":"As per amplified","act":"Full","sum":"A Malkavian is one part of a greater hole, and same can be said for other users of Dementation. With the Voice of Many, a Malkavian can amplify their voice to be able to carry terrible power.","fx":"Every power of Dementation may now affect as many targets as the user wants, all at once.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"68"}},"2OncQUrs2BhNOotH":{"id":"2OncQUrs2BhNOotH","n":"Swarm of Shadows","d":"obtenebration","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Wits + Occult","dur":"One scene","act":"Full","pre":"Arms of Ahriman or Fires of the Abyss","sum":"As the Lasombra masters their control over the inky, primordial blackness, they turn the darkness into a weapon. They can draw tentacles from shadowed reaches and use them to attack enemies nearby.","fx":"(Note that they, being shadows, move across surfaces, not air, and any distances must take this into account.)","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"112"},"prer":["Arms of Ahriman","Fires of the Abyss"]},"2SM1YRbKDsGkCI2N":{"id":"2SM1YRbKDsGkCI2N","n":"Flesh of Marble","d":"fortitude","lv":5,"cost":"Two Rouse Checks","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene","act":"Free","sum":"The power of the Blood causes the skin of the vampire to harden, taking on a marble-like sheen that is still supple but stops almost any blow before momentarily breaking and reforming.","fx":"With this power active, the vampire ignores the first source of physical damage each turn, including fire but not sunlight.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"83"}},"2gHWfRHhwuhQBFpl":{"id":"2gHWfRHhwuhQBFpl","n":"Shatter Stone","d":"melpominee","lv":5,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","pre":"Death of the Drum","sum":"By adjusting the pitch from a glass-shattering alto to an earthquake-like bariton, the vampire is able to destroy objects by their own voice.","fx":"Death of the Drum power now also deals Aggravated Health damage equal to the margin.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"88"},"prer":["Death of the Drum"]},"2kEoo3BHkvZ92fjJ":{"id":"2kEoo3BHkvZ92fjJ","n":"Prowness From Pain","d":"fortitude","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene","act":"Free","sum":"Injuries and impairments now only fuel the powers of the vampire, who grows stronger and faster from each blow, rend, or tear received. Only utter destruction can stop one who calls upon this Fortitude power.","fx":"Upon activating the power the vampire no longer suffers any dice penalties from Health damage sustained, such as physical Impairment.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"84"}},"2lNzdsUL7ADEvznm":{"id":"2lNzdsUL7ADEvznm","n":"Seal the Beast’s Maw","d":"fortitude","lv":3,"cost":"Two Rouse Checks","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene","act":"Free","sum":"Through rigorous discipline and training, this individual has learned to exert their will to stave off the call of the Hunger for a short time.","fx":"At any time during a scene, the vampire may make two Rouse Checks, and if their Hunger doesn’t increase, they can ignore the effects of Hunger for the remainder of the scene.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"82"}},"2xKRL3rbNoy4DQPO":{"id":"2xKRL3rbNoy4DQPO","n":"Touch of the Aethereal","d":"spiritus","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene.","act":"Free","sum":"Normally, touching spirits while they’re incorporeal is impossible. With Touch of the Aethereal, that becomes a certain possibility and opens threats of physical harm to spirits.","fx":"For the rest of the scene, the user is able to physically touch and harm spirits, dealing damage to them as if they were a mortal.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"162"}},"309PrYWApnXI8llg":{"id":"309PrYWApnXI8llg","n":"Beast’s Instincts","d":"animalism","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until toggled off","act":"Passive","sum":"Instincts of the Beast compel the vampire to animalistic behaviour culminating in Frenzies. This bestial mindset is not without its own usefulness, however.","fx":"This power may be toggled off and on. While active, the vampire receives a +3 dice bonus to non-supernatural Survival tracking rolls, Animal Ken and Awareness rolls.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"13"}},"39vEISaU71keyKcn":{"id":"39vEISaU71keyKcn","n":"Tongue of Apep","d":"serpentis","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene","act":"Free","sum":"Vampires are, by nature, cold-blooded and showing minimal signs of life. Setites take it much further, able to mask any signs of lies.","fx":"The user’s tongue splits into that of a snake and the character adds their Serpentis rating, to all pools involving telling lies and half-truths.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"151"}},"3GMygXzM20k8OroG":{"id":"3GMygXzM20k8OroG","n":"Presenceless Voice","d":"presence","lv":2,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"The voice of the user becomes like that of a siren, able to entrance or terrify by itself, without the user having to be present.","fx":"They do not need to see the target, and the target does not have to be in their presence save to be close enough to hear their voice.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"122"}},"3QUPaIOcDQOQdIGw":{"id":"3QUPaIOcDQOQdIGw","n":"Stain the Soul","d":"dementation","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Insight vs. Wits + Composure","dur":"See p. 52.","act":"Full","sum":"The user of Dementation speaks to their victim a truth beyond truth, and the victim is left stunned. The user of forces the target’s very soul into self-doubt, temporarily twisting the target’s morality.","fx":"The character rolls Manipulation + Insight against Composure + Wits of the victim with whom they’re communicating (p. 52).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"67"}},"3SmjCAyzZpcP16w8":{"id":"3SmjCAyzZpcP16w8","n":"Clairvoyance","d":"auspex","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Awareness","dur":"A few minutes for information gathering. Monitoring lasts as long as the user has uninterrupted focus.","act":"Full, see Duration","sum":"By closing their eyes and entering a light trance, the vampire becomes master of its surroundings.","fx":"Roll Intelligence + Awareness against a Difficulty based on the security and level of activity of the area.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"35"}},"3XNMkkpalBvVBv9V":{"id":"3XNMkkpalBvVBv9V","n":"Defractionate","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, sanguine and melancholic human blood, O-negative human blood (only a few ml), moldy spinach, hot black coffee, sodium octanoate","sum":"This formula results in a homeopathic elixir. When added to fractionated medical-supply blood, the elixir returns it to freshness, allowing vampires without the Iron Gullet merit to obtain nutrition from it.","fx":"For each success on the distillation roll, they get enough elixir to turn one blood bag (slakes 1 Hunger) from fractionated to unfractionated blood.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition Corebook","page":"285"}},"3ww0d4XkUwWNdBQw":{"id":"3ww0d4XkUwWNdBQw","n":"Shadow Step","d":"obtenebration","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Instant","act":"Full","sum":"Masters of Obtenebration can enter a patch of darkness that is large enough to admit them and step through an otherworldly space to emerge in another shadow roughly within eyesight of the first.","fx":"The vampire must enter a shadow large enough to cover them, and emerge from another one turn later.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"113"}},"3xFvtH6GxeXH5904":{"id":"3xFvtH6GxeXH5904","n":"Blood’s Curse","d":"quietussanguinis","lv":2,"pool":"Intelligence + Occult vs. Stamina + Occult (or Fortitude)","dur":"Until dawn","act":"Passive","am":"Quietus Cruciatus 2","sum":"The vampire temporarily manipulates the Clan Curse of their victim and thickens an adversary’s Blood, amplifying their weakness.","fx":"Add two (or four on a Critical Win or at least 3 margins) to the victim’s Blood Potency for purposes of Bane severity and feeding penalty (for vampires) only.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"146"},"amr":[{"k":"quietuscruciatus","l":2}]},"41m6obHK2Hm4nTLt":{"id":"41m6obHK2Hm4nTLt","n":"Fatal Flaw","d":"auspex","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Insight vs. Composire vs. Subterfuge","dur":"Until the target heals its damage.","act":"Minor -2 dice","am":"Necromancy Path •","sum":"Everything breaks, and the vampire using this power can see the signs before they happen. By observing the subtle work of entropy the vampire can glean the Achilles’ heel of a target to exploit.","fx":"If the target within the line of sight of the vampire has at least one point of Health damage, the vampire may roll Intelligence + Insight vs.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"29"},"amr":[{"k":"path:necromancy","l":1}]},"4IfLNFmvpmXMm2wP":{"id":"4IfLNFmvpmXMm2wP","n":"Holy Mission","d":"valerenwarrior","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"In the ancient days, the Salubri were the vanguard that guided the children of Set (the younger brother of Abel and Caine from whom humanity originates according to the myths) from the infernal.","fx":"The vampire gains a dice bonus to resist temptations of sin and infernalism as well as a dice bonus to defend against the powers of Daimonion, Dark Thaumaturgy, Spectre Arcanoi, Fomori powers and demonic powers be they Lores or Arcana.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"190"}},"4JZpDzCObMifIuTJ":{"id":"4JZpDzCObMifIuTJ","n":"Blood Talk","d":"quietussanguinis","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One Rouse Check allows for 5 minutes of telepathy","act":"Free","sum":"A form of blood telepathy, the user is capable of talking directly to someone’s blood which then resonates within the mind of the user.","fx":"For this power to work, the user must possess at least one droplet of the target’s blood at hand.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"147"}},"4LjHz2LiGlEhPGWQ":{"id":"4LjHz2LiGlEhPGWQ","n":"Gift of Osiris","d":"bardo","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Osiris","dur":"Until the next sunset when they have to make their awakening roll.","act":"Full","sum":"Despite supposedly dying at the hands of Set’s assassins, Osiris still lives and watches over his children. He has made a promise – a prophecy – that he shall one day return to restore his children as humans.","fx":"The user also loses access to all vampiric boons like their resistance to damage to their powers.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"41"}},"4OnJqDqywc6dmOcA":{"id":"4OnJqDqywc6dmOcA","n":"Blessing’s Warning","d":"auspex","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Insight vs. Composure + Subterfuge","dur":"One scene","act":"Full","am":"Daimonion •","pre":"Sense the Unseen","sum":"The Tremere obtained knowledge of this art from the Baali bloodline in exchange for unknown favors (probably related to the purge of the Salubri).","fx":"This power perceives the world in exactly like Auspex ••• Scry the Soul except that the ofllowing questions are available to them when scrutinising a single person or looking for a specific thing in the entire room:","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"26"},"amr":[{"k":"daimonion","l":1}],"prer":["Sense the Unseen"]},"4QrfXaUqqnkp7tnp":{"id":"4QrfXaUqqnkp7tnp","n":"Mother of Monsters","d":"serpentis","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until the creatures are slain or reabsorbed.","act":"Full","am":"Animalism 2","pre":"Bond Famulus","sum":"Echidna was called the Mother of Monsters. This power allows the Setite to birth small typhonic beasts from their flesh.","fx":"The user can choose a different mythological form for the beast. However, these monsters must be obviously unnatural.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"153"},"amr":[{"k":"animalism","l":2}],"prer":["Bond Famulus"]},"4TpRZdmkOPZ0iZvV":{"id":"4TpRZdmkOPZ0iZvV","n":"Sense Death","d":"valerenwarrior","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Insight or Medicine vs. Composure + Subterfug","dur":"One scene","act":"Minor -2","sum":"As the Healers learn where the subject hurts to heal, the Warriors learn it to know where they strike.","fx":"The user may ask questions equal to the margin and get a correct response. The example questions are:","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"190"}},"4URCI7pFQTQMVD76":{"id":"4URCI7pFQTQMVD76","n":"Samiel’s Vengeance","d":"valerenwarrior","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Composure + Resolve","dur":"One attack","act":"Free","sum":"Samiel was the first Salubri Warrior, said to have perished in the war against the infernal host.","fx":"This power may only be used on those who have successfuly harmed the vampire within the present scene.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"193"}},"4f2QmAevqQ2gxQ8n":{"id":"4f2QmAevqQ2gxQ8n","n":"Hourglass of the Mind","d":"temporis","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"Wits + Awareness","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive/Free","sum":"Your body and the Beast itself have been modified by your skills in Temporis, giving you the ability to always know the flow of time and even some resistance against the drowsiness that compels vampires to sleep.","fx":"Additionally, the vampire instinctively knows when time is disrupted by any supernatural effect (Wits + Alertness roll at Difficulty 2, adjusted for distance and intensity by the…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"167"}},"4gLhgUYXQ796CXBE":{"id":"4gLhgUYXQ796CXBE","n":"Exuberance","d":"potence","lv":3,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive, but it may be turned off to not strain the user","act":"Passive","sum":"The vampiric form is a curious beast, able to support unfathomable levels of strength upon the slightest of frames without demonstrating any strain.","fx":"Whenever using Potence (including pools using half the Potence rating, such as Prowess), the vampire treats their Potence rating as if it were two levels higher — this can take the relative Discipline rating above the normal limit of 5.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"117"}},"4mRDMC9OyeA3izmn":{"id":"4mRDMC9OyeA3izmn","n":"Locked in Time","d":"temporis","lv":4,"cost":"Free, one Willpower point","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","pre":"Locked Contemplation","sum":"By honing their ability to lock away a person’s perceptions of time, the","fx":"After the initial win, the user may continue adding months by rolling against a Difficulty of 3, accumulating more margins over time to extend the duration.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"171"},"prer":["Locked Contemplation"]},"55IbHGBuh57YU4Ve":{"id":"55IbHGBuh57YU4Ve","n":"Mask of Ages","d":"obfuscate","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse check","pool":"See general rules for Obfuscate","dur":"Until sunrise or ended by the user.","act":"Free","sum":"This simple use of Obfuscate allows the vampire to disguise their apparent age, perhaps allowing them to Masquerade as their mortal identity longer than most.","fx":"The user also adds their Obfuscate rating to any tests to impersonate someone of their projected age (including themselves at that age) or when evading someone looking for them via photo or description.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"97"}},"5EhwIXzdARJIYTAT":{"id":"5EhwIXzdARJIYTAT","n":"Unswayable Mind","d":"fortitude","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","am":"Auspex 1","sum":"The user gains a mystical ability to resist any attempts to sway them through mundane charms, coercion, and wiles. Some exhibit Unswayable Mind as zen-like calm, others as supernatural stubbornness.","fx":"The user adds their dots in Fortitude as extra dice in any roll made to resist coercion, intimidation, seduction, or any other attempt to sway the user’s mind against their will.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"79"},"amr":[{"k":"auspex","l":1}]},"5Q7zKcBwDSn3cKOp":{"id":"5Q7zKcBwDSn3cKOp","n":"Quietus Mastery","d":"quietusanimae","lv":5,"cost":"Free/One Rouse Check in addition to the cost of the power amplified","pool":"N/A","dur":"Per power augmented","act":"Passive","sum":"As the user masters the Discipline said to have been created by Haqim himself, the vampire figures out how all Gifts of the Blood are connected, and how all the Paths of Quietus lead to the same destination.","fx":"Powers of any Quietus Path that require touch or transmission by poison are now available to the vampire by making a gesture with their hand towards the victim (those who succeed on a Wits…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"138"}},"5XGhVtWLyxnmBg3w":{"id":"5XGhVtWLyxnmBg3w","n":"Unchain the Wrathful Beast","d":"vicissitude","lv":5,"cost":"Two Rouse Checks after the Beast enters the host in addition to Drawing Out the Beast","pool":"N/A","dur":"See system","act":"Full","am":"Animalism •••••","pre":"Drawing Out the Beast","sum":"A Fiend with this power may project their Beast into a hapless host, where it immediately sets about warping flesh and bone to better accommodate its monstrousness.","fx":"The Rouse Checks may be rerolled according to Blood Potency as normal.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"210"},"amr":[{"k":"animalism","l":5}],"prer":["Drawing Out the Beast"]},"5aGgjf86bhq5AngL":{"id":"5aGgjf86bhq5AngL","n":"Red State","d":"alchemy","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"Permanent until the target imbibes a choleric Dyscrasia.","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, sanguine and phlegmatic mortal blood, iron oxide.","sum":"A hypnotic ointment or potion that erases the specific memories of an ally or associate’s misdeeds.","fx":"It slips free of the mind like amnesia, and cannot be restored. Being told, “Saphir killed your sister, man!","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"79"}},"5awAT0Wz4ZGtRMas":{"id":"5awAT0Wz4ZGtRMas","n":"Relentless Grasp","d":"potence","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene","act":"Free","sum":"The vampire’s grip becomes impossibly strong and once they get a good hold of something they are almost impossible to dislodge, short of dismemberment.","fx":"The vampire adds their Potence rating as additional dice to any attempt that involves holding on to something.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"117"}},"5kKVRBNmMKV73jVD":{"id":"5kKVRBNmMKV73jVD","n":"Mist Form","d":"protean","lv":5,"cost":"One to Three Rouse Checks","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until the vampire falls to sleep or torpor or ends the power","act":"Full, see system","sum":"The vampire gains the legendary power to turn into a cloud of mist, perceivable to the eye but untouchable by anything save fire, sunlight, and supernatural aggression. They can fit through pipes, crevices, and cracks.","fx":"The transformation takes three turns, though it can be sped up with additional Rouse Checks on a one-for-one basis.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"132"}},"5ws5DMm3IACwXu7F":{"id":"5ws5DMm3IACwXu7F","n":"Copycat","d":"alchemy","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"Twenty minutes (usually one scene if you’re smart).","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, choleric and phlegmatic mortal blood, mirror glass, donor blood, Boquila trifoliolata leaves, chameleon skin.","sum":"Mercurians might not be able to turn into mist or mesmerize onlookers into overlooking them, but Copycat’s the next best thing.","fx":"That feeling remains for the next twenty minutes, slightly itchy and tight as the Copycat brew slowly loses potency.","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"78"}},"6DZfi1qkBX4xIFig":{"id":"6DZfi1qkBX4xIFig","n":"Sleep of a Mummy","d":"serpentis","lv":2,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive, but the user may disable it if they wish so.","act":"Passive","sum":"The elder Setites are at a constant threat of tomb raiders and zealous hunters in their homeland which is why many have developed a power to allow them to not only appear as a long-dead mummified corpse but also shield…","fx":"If the user is in daysleep or torpor, they cannot be distinguished from a corpse as they appear like a dried up corpse.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"152"}},"6Mg3S52kSF8q0lQ7":{"id":"6Mg3S52kSF8q0lQ7","n":"Typhonic Maw","d":"serpentis","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive.","act":"Passive","sum":"The user’s throat becomes as flexible as that of a snake and their teeth become even sharper, allowing them to tear more than flesh away from their victims when biting.","fx":"Whenever the user achieves a successful bite attack, they slake one point of Hunger on a successful bite attack and increase a target Cainite’s Hunger by 1.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"151"}},"6OqQDVgHV6dRVEj4":{"id":"6OqQDVgHV6dRVEj4","n":"Shatter the Vessel","d":"spiritus","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Animal Ken","dur":"Instant","act":"Minor -2","sum":"With but a whisper, the user is able to convince a wall to come down, armour to dissolve or a weapon to shatter by appealing to its spirit and promising it freedom or greater rewards.","fx":"For an object to shatter, the user must win succeed on a Manipulation + Animal Ken roll against a Difficulty of 2.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"164"}},"6obrFw9p4F9cx13r":{"id":"6obrFw9p4F9cx13r","n":"Blood Dance","d":"quietussanguinis","lv":1,"cost":"Free (or One Rouse Check if using own Blood)","pool":"Intelligence + Craft","dur":"One scene or until lapsed by user","act":"Full","sum":"By focusing, the user is able to command spilled blood into shapes. This power is greatly useful when one has to clean up other’s mistakes or traces of assassination.","fx":"By making a successful Intelligence + Craft roll, the user may craft the blood into any chape or image they desire.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"144"}},"75Dm3FcKqdYimLhB":{"id":"75Dm3FcKqdYimLhB","n":"Slake by Spirit","d":"spiritus","lv":4,"cost":"One Willpower point","pool":"Manipulation + Animal Ken","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive/Minor -2","sum":"When venturing the umbra or the untouched wilderness, many users of Spiritus must feed somehow, even if it comes to the detriment of the lesser spirits on whose energies they slake.","fx":"In combat, this can be done as a minor action, incurring a penalty of two dice. Average and greater spirits may resist with Composure + Resolve against the user’s Resolve + Animal Ken.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"164"}},"7NsK8LA29ryan78j":{"id":"7NsK8LA29ryan78j","n":"Cache","d":"obfuscate","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"See general rules for Obfuscate","dur":"One scene or until dawn or ended by the user.","act":"Free","pre":"Ensconce","sum":"The vampire may use this power to hide objects and make them difficult to find just by touching them.","fx":"The user may make an additional Rouse Check to extend the duration for the remainder of the night. In that case, the enshrouded object remains hidden until dawn.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"97"},"prer":["Ensconce"]},"7SWgi70vfuzmy9u1":{"id":"7SWgi70vfuzmy9u1","n":"Lord of the Land","d":"animalism","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check in addition to the cost of the power amplified","pool":"N/A","dur":"As the duration of the power.","act":"Full","sum":"True masters of Animalism are not limited by distance.","fx":"From a mechanical standpoint, a character’s territory may not be larger than their mechanical Domain.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"23"}},"7TyNyxj0iUzUgXdh":{"id":"7TyNyxj0iUzUgXdh","n":"Infernal Birthright","d":"daimonion","lv":5,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","pre":"Investiture of the Blood","sum":"Not as much of a power as merely extending the properties found within blood of Daimonion users, the user manifests same powers that demons and their minions do.","fx":"You also count your Blood Potency as both Torment and Divinity for all intents and purposes save Faith Hunger as Investiture of the Blood uses Rouse Checks instead of Faith Checks.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"60"},"prer":["Investiture of the Blood"]},"7YnPSYwz4qwy01L3":{"id":"7YnPSYwz4qwy01L3","n":"Earthmeld","d":"protean","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One day or more, or until disturbed. Power may be ended sooner by the vampire rising.","act":"Full","sum":"Becoming one with the soil, the vampire sinks into the earth. Unless in torpor, the vampire rises again the following night.","fx":"No test is required, but the vampire must be on a natural surface: rocks, raw earth, grass, etc. This power does not work on concrete, asphalt, or other artificial surfaces.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"129"}},"7dsFNuOGOBtQEUFH":{"id":"7dsFNuOGOBtQEUFH","n":"Faster than Light","d":"celerity","lv":4,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","pre":"Blink","sum":"The vampire’s unnatural speed protects them from the undead’s deadliest banes — fire and sunlight.","fx":"When using Blink, the vampire makes an additional Rouse check, enabling them to pass through patches of sunlight or flame without sustaining damage or feeling their effects.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"46"},"prer":["Blink"]},"7n661Upp9I8E8V2x":{"id":"7n661Upp9I8E8V2x","n":"Intelligent Ash","d":"thanatosis","lv":5,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","pre":"From Ashes","sum":"By sharpening their senses in their Ash form, the user is able to both see and hear by sensing vibrations. The greater control over their form also allows them movement.","fx":"While in ash form, the user is now able to hear and see most of what they would if they weren’t in their ash form.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"181"},"prer":["From Ashes"]},"7w2UAf3PNoLKP8hB":{"id":"7w2UAf3PNoLKP8hB","n":"Slower than Harm","d":"temporis","lv":4,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","pre":"Slow Walker","sum":"The vampire bends time to protect them from the undead’s deadliest banes — fire and sunlight.","fx":"When using Slow Walker, the vampire makes an additional Rouse check, enabling them to pass through patches of sunlight or flame without sustaining damage or feeling their effects.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"173"},"prer":["Slow Walker"]},"7wWc3wbWufuceMjK":{"id":"7wWc3wbWufuceMjK","n":"Unerring Pursuit","d":"auspex","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Insight vs. Composire vs. Subterfuge","dur":"One night plus one for each success (or in the margin, in the case of a vampire target) mental or physical weak points.","act":"Minor -2 dice","am":"Dominate •","sum":"Locking eyes with a subject, the vampire coaxes forth a supernatural bond between themselves and the victim.","fx":"The user locks eyes with the target, if only for a split second, and rolls Resolve + Insight. On a win, the effect lasts for one night, plus one for each success in the margin.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"29"},"amr":[{"k":"dominate","l":1}]},"88ttazce38pjGvbu":{"id":"88ttazce38pjGvbu","n":"Quick Swap","d":"mytherceria","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Occult vs. Wits + Strength","dur":"Indefinitely as it would take another use of this power to swap it again. Normally moving the object is also a method.","act":"Full","sum":"The user can swap the position of two inanimate objects in an instant. This could swap a scrap of paper in their hand with a shotgun, or swap the blade someone holds with a piece of hot coal that was in a fire.","fx":"The inanimate objects must both be within the line of sight of the user, and be something that the user can carry in one hand without great effort.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"93"}},"8HybBTiT2NslFwjb":{"id":"8HybBTiT2NslFwjb","n":"Unseen Passage","d":"obfuscate","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"See general rules for Obfuscate","dur":"One scene or until detection or the user stops the power.","act":"Free","sum":"With this power, the vampire can now move around while staying hidden. The user is functionally invisible, per the usual Obfuscate limitations.","fx":"Only if the observer has their attention drawn to the user can they make a detection roll.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"98"}},"8IHSC52IJ7kPJBlm":{"id":"8IHSC52IJ7kPJBlm","n":"The Unfettered Heart","d":"protean","lv":4,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"Having mastered the power of Protean, the very insides of the user become malleable, almost viscous. The heart, seat of the vitae and unlife of the vampire, detaches and moves freely, if sluggishly, within the chest.","fx":"Increases the Difficulty on any noncombat test to stake the vampire by three. In Melee combat, only if the stake-wielder rolls a Critical Win does the stake penetrate the user’s heart.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"131"}},"8KgXc14GEiAkDD5q":{"id":"8KgXc14GEiAkDD5q","n":"Sword of the Righteous","d":"valerenwarrior","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One attack","act":"Free","sum":"The decree of Saulot is the holy mission of the Salubri and other few that were permitted to study Valeren: wipe out the infernalist taint from the face of the world.","fx":"The vampire pays the cost of a Rouse Check and their arms or a melee weapon become coated in pale flame that may pierce supernatural darkness and negate its penalties such as of Nocturne (Obtenebration •••).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"194"}},"8ekqFnCHiJv2OavK":{"id":"8ekqFnCHiJv2OavK","n":"Uncanny Grip","d":"potence","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One Scene","act":"Free","sum":"Focusing their unnatural strength into their toes and fingers, the vampire grips and burrows their extremities into almost any surface, enabling them to climb and even hang otherwise unsupported from walls and ceilings.","fx":"The user might also be able to climb copper or bronze cladding or other softer metal surfaces, at the Storyteller’s discretion Thin glass surfaces (though generally not the glass curtain walls of modern office buildings) may shatter under the stress.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"116"}},"8uw0QLki4Le0q25e":{"id":"8uw0QLki4Le0q25e","n":"Eyes of the Beast","d":"protean","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"As long as desired","act":"Free","sum":"The vampire can will a supernatural red gleam into their eyes, giving them sight even in the total absence of light.","fx":"While active the user ignores any sight penalties imposed by darkness, including supernatural.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"127"}},"91uGCuaTS29ja736":{"id":"91uGCuaTS29ja736","n":"Ghost in the Machine","d":"obfuscate","lv":3,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive/As power used","act":"Passive","sum":"The user can now transmit the effects of Obfuscate through electronic media, allowing the vampire to appear invisible or masked when viewed live on screen.","fx":"The observer adds +3 to their Difficulty on tests to identify the user on film, video, in photographs, or the like taken during active Obfuscation.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"100"}},"95QwMXDEumGDkHUj":{"id":"95QwMXDEumGDkHUj","n":"Saraimu","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Alchemy","dur":"The blob falls apart one to three weeks after it was created. The Storyteller may roll a die to determine the exact time. If its masters die before it does, the saraimu knows enough alchemy to prolong its existence until it can find — and burrow its way into — a new alchemist.","ing":"A cup of vitae each from three vampires including the alchemist, baking powder, crushed chalk (optional, for a soft voice), iron nails (for strength), battery acid (for oomph)","sum":"This formula creates a sentient blob of slime to serve the alchemist and the other vampires whose vitae it comes from as a familiar.","fx":"As the mixture bubbles, they stir in the nails, and when they add the battery acid and activate the mixture, it hisses aggressively and comes to something resembling life.","src":{"book":"Tattered Façade","page":"107"}},"9EBoXS4kQf47rhJN":{"id":"9EBoXS4kQf47rhJN","n":"Choir of the Damned","d":"valerenwatcher","lv":3,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","pre":"Lulliby of the Damned","sum":"Mastering the tune, the user may now hide multiple companions from evil creatures.","fx":"By spending a point of Willpower per additional passanger, the user may extend the effect of Lulliby of the Damned to those who stay within a radius equal to the user’s Wits rating.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"197"},"prer":["Lulliby of the Damned"]},"9KSi7NkbyL5FAQfw":{"id":"9KSi7NkbyL5FAQfw","n":"Lethe’s Call","d":"dominate","lv":5,"cost":"Two Rouse Checks","pool":"Manipulation + Subterfuge vs. Intelligence + Resolve","dur":"Indefinite","act":"Full, extended","pre":"Cloud Memory or Forgetful Mind","sum":"The memories of others are a plaything to the vampire, who is able to blank out large swaths with but a glance.","fx":"The user tests Manipulation + Subterfuge vs target’s Intelligence + Resolve, though unprepared mortals cannot resist this power.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"76"},"prer":["Cloud Memory","Forgetful Mind"]},"9Ybrh3KeN0M9yA7K":{"id":"9Ybrh3KeN0M9yA7K","n":"Awe","d":"presence","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene or until intentionally ended","act":"Free","sum":"Anyone in the presence of the vampire finds their attention inexplicably drawn to them. Those listening to the vampire speak might suddenly agree on subjects where they once held different viewpoints.","fx":"Add the Presence rating to any Skill roll involving Persuasion or Performance as well as to other Charisma related rolls, at the Storyteller’s discretion.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"121"}},"9jUHPQwcRFDwcZYE":{"id":"9jUHPQwcRFDwcZYE","n":"Pariah’s Caress","d":"valerenwatcher","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Persuasion vs. Composure + Occult","dur":"24 hours for each point on the margin.","act":"Passive","sum":"Watchers must contend with the Wan Kuei, other vampires who do not subscribe to the idea of the lineage of Caine, and stranger beings such as mages.","fx":"The user must first touch the target and smear a bit of their vitae on them, preferably with a Stealth roll. After that, the user rolls Manipulation + Persuasion vs.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"197"}},"9q0wLUj6xcxMb1DA":{"id":"9q0wLUj6xcxMb1DA","n":"Daunt","d":"presence","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene or until intentionally ended","act":"Free","sum":"Instead of attracting people, the vampire uses Presence to repel.","fx":"Add the user’s Presence rating to any Intimidation rolls.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"121"}},"9wAj10XP7PDB8Hq9":{"id":"9wAj10XP7PDB8Hq9","n":"Aid from the Spirits","d":"spiritus","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Charisma + Intimidation","dur":"The dice bonus fades at dawn or when used up.","act":"Minor -2","sum":"Spirits need not be complicated forms of intelligent “life” such as that of animals. Truth be told, most are spirits of concepts, like the fork you are using when you are eating.","fx":"The vampire receives a number of bonus dice to handle that item, equal to the number of margins. A critical win adds another die.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"160"}},"A0xUxsy4DQXby65y":{"id":"A0xUxsy4DQXby65y","n":"Debilitative Poison","d":"quietuscruciatus","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"The poison is potent for one scene","act":"Minor -2 dice/free","sum":"With Hinder Mending, the vampire concocts a special poison that prevents usage of vitae for mending, disrupting vampire targets and their other creations that utilise vitae to heal.","fx":"This contact poison has the same system as Scorpion’s Touch (see below) and is applied the same way).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"140"}},"ACZnxCjunRw5Fkbp":{"id":"ACZnxCjunRw5Fkbp","n":"Fear of the Void","d":"daimonion","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Intimidation","dur":"Until the effect ends.","act":"Full","sum":"Once you know a subject’s beliefs or desires, manipulating them is easy. Converting vices of pleasure into waves of existential terror or shattering their beliefs on the spot is a greater trick.","fx":"For this power to work, the victim must be able to hear the user and the user must know either the target’s ambition or desire or at least one of the target’s convictions.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"56"}},"AOU7HCPmsqbEbhtw":{"id":"AOU7HCPmsqbEbhtw","n":"Silence the Sane Mind","d":"dementation","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Insight vs. Wits + Composure","dur":"See p. 49.","act":"Full","sum":"The vampire forces the victim to say nothing, to bear mute witness to evil through scrambling their ability to communicate.","fx":"Anyone affected by this Power finds it impossible to meaningfully communicate — their voice makes no sound, writing becomes illegible, their gestures or signs shudder spastically, and even…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"66"}},"AS1JADRlI4uN96BG":{"id":"AS1JADRlI4uN96BG","n":"Scent of Prey","d":"animalism","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Investigation","dur":"One scene or night","act":"Full","sum":"The mind-numbing fear of realizing one’s role as prey is unique, and vampires versed in sensing the Beast can learn to recognize it in those who experience it.","fx":"Each success on the roll allows them to sense and track the position of a mortal who has witnessed what a Camarilla vampires would call a “Masquerade violation.” (The user senses the…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"19"}},"AaLsyGGKZeBgwVvH":{"id":"AaLsyGGKZeBgwVvH","n":"Shadow Steed","d":"obtenebration","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until the animal is destroyed or released back into darkness by the vampire. The vampire may have a number of these active equal to their Obtenebration rating.","act":"Full","am":"Animalism 1","sum":"During the Dark Ages, Lasombra were known for their shadow calvary when combining this power with Solid Shadows. When the Lasombra joined the Sabbat, this power took on a more aggressive purpose.","fx":"The vampire forms a shadow imbued with animalistic intelligence by splattering some of their blood into a shadow.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"110"},"amr":[{"k":"animalism","l":1}]},"AaWzfTzZNuRC3dOP":{"id":"AaWzfTzZNuRC3dOP","n":"Unseen Spirit","d":"obfuscate","lv":3,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive.","am":"Daimonion •• or Spiritus •• or Ephemera Path ••or Necromancy Path ••","sum":"Ghosts naturally are immune to all mind-altering powers such as Obfuscate as long as they remain unmanifested within the Underworld.","fx":"Your Obfuscate now affects spirits (ghosts, naturae, demons) as it would normal humans.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"102"},"amr":[{"k":"daimonion","l":2},{"k":"spiritus","l":2},{"k":"path:ephemerapathornecromancy","l":2}]},"AdpKntgYG916viii":{"id":"AdpKntgYG916viii","n":"Resilient Will","d":"fortitude","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One Scene or until the protection has been depleted","act":"Free","am":"Auspex •","sum":"The will of a vampire is the will of an immortal creature whose drive can lead them onto centuries-lasting grudges and feuds.","fx":"Once activated, the vampire reduces Superficial Willpower damage equal to their Fortitude rating without it affecting their Willpower tracker.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"79"},"amr":[{"k":"auspex","l":1}]},"AxHL5tDohCGuDtEb":{"id":"AxHL5tDohCGuDtEb","n":"Horrid Reality","d":"chimerstry","lv":5,"cost":"One point of Willpower in addition to the power enhanced","pool":"N/A","dur":"The damage is taken for one turn while the illusion remains.","act":"Free/as power enhanced","sum":"Quite possibly the most horrid and fear-inducing usage of Chimerstry, Horrid Reality allows Fata Morgana to create hallucinations so realistic that they can straight up inflict harm upon others by convincing their bodies of it.","fx":"The user may choose to enhance the illusions created by Ignis Fatuus and Fata Morgana to the point of dealing harm.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"51"}},"AzaUdW388RCtKql8":{"id":"AzaUdW388RCtKql8","n":"Inner Mastery","d":"vicissitude","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Medicine","dur":"Permanent until healed or altered again. See Characteristics.","act":"Full, see system.","pre":"Rend the Osseous Frame","sum":"Approaching the legendary apotheosis, the goal of those walking the Road of Metamorphosis, the user’s body and mind become one, being able to exercise complete control over the body as well as the mind.","fx":"If the subject is avoiding the user’s touch and the time required to perform an alteration is one turn or instant, alteration first requires a successful roll with any combination of Strength/Dexterity + Athletics/ Brawl.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"209"},"prer":["Rend the Osseous Frame"]},"B21DfERlY3YVhKlH":{"id":"B21DfERlY3YVhKlH","n":"Strengthen the Soul","d":"quietusanimae","lv":3,"cost":"Free","pool":"Resolve + Occult vs. Intelligence + Composure","dur":"The effect persists in a person for a month or until the vampire who drank the blood feeds again, whichever comes sooner","act":"Minor -2","pre":"Internal Awareness","sum":"The user awakens the subject blood’s making them more alert to the hidden things.","fx":"Those drinking the blood of the user find themselves having frequent “gut feelings” about things they should not be possible to sense.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"136"},"prer":["Internal Awareness"]},"B72DbSBTIABFMVDV":{"id":"B72DbSBTIABFMVDV","n":"Speak From the Heart","d":"alchemy","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"The messages take about sixty seconds. They persist in the carrier until death, or until someone drinks their blood.","ing":"A soft drink, the alchemist’s Blood, melancholic human blood, mercury, ink or paint.","sum":"Known as message in a butthole in California, this creates an elixir that is, to all appearances, some flavor of soda. Some patsy, usually mortal, drinks the soda.","fx":"Grape soda can carry seventy-one words or less. Orange reveals a sketched image in the drinker’s mind for about a minute.","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"75"}},"BDmftmFPk8DMwkuC":{"id":"BDmftmFPk8DMwkuC","n":"Enduring Beasts","d":"fortitude","lv":2,"cost":"Free (for famulus); One Rouse Check (for other animals)","pool":"Stamina + Animal Ken (for nonfamulus animals)","dur":"One Scene, permanent for famulus.","act":"Full","am":"Animalism 1","sum":"The user shares a small portion of their unnatural toughness with the animals they influence. Teeming swarms and great beasts alike exhibit a resistance to fleeting injuries almost equal to the vampire themself.","fx":"The vampire can choose to extend some of their Fortitude powers to animals affected by their Animalism.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"80"},"amr":[{"k":"animalism","l":1}]},"BFn4zlF9oGU8boYx":{"id":"BFn4zlF9oGU8boYx","n":"Animal Succulence","d":"animalism","lv":3,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"The vampire can slake additional Hunger by feeding on animals.","fx":"Feeding from animals slakes 1 additional Hunger, and the vampire counts their Blood Potency as two levels lower in regards to penalties to slaking Hunger from animal blood.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"17"}},"BVG10UOw1FYvBKxi":{"id":"BVG10UOw1FYvBKxi","n":"Cylcopean Sentinel","d":"thanatosis","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until retreived or the eye is destroyed","act":"Full","am":"Corpse in the Monster Path •","sum":"For the rotting descendants of Troglodytia, their permanently putrescent bodies are a source of amazing powers.","fx":"The eye sees everything in front of it but only in its direct field of vision. It can only see though and no other senses are transmitted by the eye.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"177"},"amr":[{"k":"path:corpseinthemonster","l":1}]},"BVVkZx3HdtzTVO4x":{"id":"BVVkZx3HdtzTVO4x","n":"Anima Walk","d":"auspex","lv":4,"cost":"One Willpower point per scene","pool":"Resolve + Occult","dur":"Until ended. Auspex users should be aware that there are means by which spirits and sorcerers can imprison their souls.","act":"Full","sum":"For witches to fly, they must use magic and toxicology. A master of Auspex requires nothing so vulgar.","fx":"The user rolls Resolve + Occult. Difficulty should reflect the character’s ability to bring the place up clearly in their imagination.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"32"}},"BXnmQ8B7w2tmaOus":{"id":"BXnmQ8B7w2tmaOus","n":"See the Hidden World","d":"valerenwatcher","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Instant","act":"Passive","sum":"The eye of Valeren can pierce the veils between worlds, showing the vampire the world from a more spiritual perspective.","fx":"When activated, the vampire pierces the spiritual layers and is able to see discorporealised spirits, demons and even ghosts.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"195"}},"BivD0NJRJPQCS140":{"id":"BivD0NJRJPQCS140","n":"Aspect of the Beast","d":"spiritus","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Animal Ken","dur":"One scene unless ended before that. A Critical Win extends the effect for the rest of the night.","act":"Minor -2","sum":"The users of Spiritus are known for also drawing parts of spirits and their concepts into themselves to boost their powers, often in bargains with the said spirits to bring vengeance to this who hunt animals for fun and destroy their habitats for profits.","fx":"This power takes one full turn to take effect as the user collects the spirits of the area and usually makes some sort of a promise to them.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"161"}},"BlK9yMhGaw3j5qnc":{"id":"BlK9yMhGaw3j5qnc","n":"Soul Exchange","d":"valerenwatcher","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Occult vs. Composure + Resolve","dur":"Permanent.","act":"Full","sum":"Scholar and thief, the twin childer of Zao-lat are seldom seen these nights.","fx":"A win against allows the user to switch the souls of the two targets.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"200"}},"Bn4DwN9OUVJ8xTZy":{"id":"Bn4DwN9OUVJ8xTZy","n":"Shape of the Beast’s Wrath","d":"protean","lv":4,"cost":"Two Rouse Checks","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until the vampire falls to sleep or torpor or ends the power","act":"Full","pre":"Shape of the Beast","sum":"Users of this power are often mistaken for Tzimisce employing the Vicissitude power Zulo Form.","fx":"During transformation, the character may only defend using their normal dice pools.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"130"},"prer":["Shape of the Beast"]},"BnIrciv8UdXnBbk1":{"id":"BnIrciv8UdXnBbk1","n":"Tongue of the Asp","d":"serpentis","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene or until ended by the user","act":"Free","sum":"Calling upon the asp, the royal animal of dynastic and Roman Egypt, the user channels extends their tongue Roman Egypt, the user channels extends their tongue which becomes barbed, sharp and coated with a lethal contact poison.","fx":"The user instantly protrudes what can only be described as a tongue that has been turned into a sharp whip with the length of half a meter per dot of Serpentis the user possesses.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"152"}},"BwtoUtVRpqDAJzUn":{"id":"BwtoUtVRpqDAJzUn","n":"Blood Tempering","d":"quietussanguinis","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Craft","dur":"No item enchanted by this has never withered by age alone, for now. Almost every old scroll in Alamut is under the effect of this power.","act":"Full","sum":"The older a Cainite target at the end of an assassin’s blade, the greater the chance of the target utilising powerful Disciplines fueled by their older Blood to fend off an attacker.","fx":"First the user must splatter the object with vitae after which most usually utter a prayer to the spirits, seeking to petition them to instill the object with vampiric longevity and metaphysical strength.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"144"}},"C0YyjmplcWEtxPMo":{"id":"C0YyjmplcWEtxPMo","n":"Dagon’s Call","d":"quietuscruciatus","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Awareness vs. Stamina + Occult (or Fortitude)","dur":"The user’s vitae remains potent in the victim’s system for a week or until the user has activated the power 3 times, using up all of their blood within the victim.","act":"Full to activate the power. Applying blood depends on the method","sum":"With the slightest scratch delivering a dab of blood to mingle with that of the target’s, Dagon’s Call twists a victim’s own blood against them.","fx":"In order to use this power, the character’s blood must first be ingested or enter the target’s bloodstream, usually through drinking (even from a ghoul belonging to the character) or being pierced by a bloodied weapon.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"141"}},"C1jovv2VZec0EsoJ":{"id":"C1jovv2VZec0EsoJ","n":"Ripples of the Blood","d":"quietusanimae","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Insight","dur":"The intense emotion and the Resonance with it wither away after a week (or until a vampire feeds again or falls to slumber, whichever comes sooner).","act":"Full","sum":"With this power, a vampire can leave an emotional echo that resonates in their own blood or the blood of those from whom they feeds.","fx":"For this power to work, the user must first make their Rouse Check and make roll of Manipulation + Insight against a Difficulty of 3 and focus on a specific emotion belonging to a Resonance.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"136"}},"CK0CDBUGhEM2TmV9":{"id":"CK0CDBUGhEM2TmV9","n":"Apparition","d":"chimerstry","lv":3,"cost":"One point of Willpower","pool":"N/A","dur":"As Ignis Fatuus or Fata Morgana","act":"Minor action of -2 dice","sum":"Characters with Apparition can give a static illusion created with either Dweomer or Ignis Fatuus the semblance of movement. Such an illusion moves as the character directs.","fx":"As long as the vampire concentrates on the illusion cast by Ignis Fatuus or Fata Morgana, they can make it move in any way they wish, within reason.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"49"}},"CKzIIzD2Y3AkjeTD":{"id":"CKzIIzD2Y3AkjeTD","n":"Toughness","d":"fortitude","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One Scene","act":"Free","sum":"All vampires with this power exhibit an innate ability to ignore damage that would otherwise inconvenience and even disable others of their kind.","fx":"Subtract the Fortitude of the defender from all Superficial Health damage sustained. This occurs before halving the damage, and cannot reduce the damage below one.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"81"}},"CLRRKYJo0e7vlY2W":{"id":"CLRRKYJo0e7vlY2W","n":"Scorpion’s Touch","d":"quietuscruciatus","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"The poison remains potent for nights equal to the user’s Quietus rating","act":"Free","sum":"Scorpion’s Touch transmutes the Cainite vitae, which is usually healing and nurturing, into a deadly poison capable of harming victims by touch alone.","fx":"Spitting the poison can happen instantly during the first turn while coating a weapon is a -2 dice Minor Action.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"141"}},"CbMkI3GeemDqm8TE":{"id":"CbMkI3GeemDqm8TE","n":"Soaring Leap","d":"potence","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"Possessing unholy strength in more than arms and fists, the user can leap far higher and further than any mortal.","fx":"The user can jump a number of meters equal to three times their Potence level vertically, and five times their Potence level horizontally.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"116"}},"CekkPun84OCNQaTX":{"id":"CekkPun84OCNQaTX","n":"Mosh Pit","d":"melpominee","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Charisma + Performance vs. Composure + Wits","dur":"Until the Frenzy ends. The Resonance changes back once the effect ends as well.","act":"Full","sum":"With but a syllable, the vampire’s voice enflames all the humours of rage within a person, turning them into a violent beast.","fx":"The target’s Resonance is changed at choleric and, if they are a vampire or another creature with the vampiric Beast, they must make a Fury Frenzy test against a equal to the user’s Melpominee rating.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"87"}},"CoyjAKqIhRNy43du":{"id":"CoyjAKqIhRNy43du","n":"Dead Man’s Hand","d":"spiritus","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check and two Willpower points.","pool":"N/A, Composure + Resolve vs. Composure + Resolve","dur":"Until the vessel is destroyed.","act":"Full","sum":"Some say the legend of James Butler Hickok’s (better known as “Wild Bill” Hickok) death is that he was shot in the back. That’s the story mortals have used to justify what really happened on August 1, 1876.","fx":"As long as the vampire holds the object, it can act normally but with a dice pool no greater than your Road Rating.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"164"}},"DFQzC2vBBlIuiv5q":{"id":"DFQzC2vBBlIuiv5q","n":"The Sword of Malkav","d":"dementation","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Insight vs. Wits + Composure","dur":"See p. 52.","act":"Full","pre":"Stain the Soul","sum":"With this terrifying Discipline, the Malkavian wrecks a victim’s very sense of reality.","fx":"If successful, the victim’s belief, perceptions, and understanding shift in order to facilitate the falsehood which the user must formulate, usually in a single sentence.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"68"},"prer":["Stain the Soul"]},"DHrRjPi4OJFSyIf1":{"id":"DHrRjPi4OJFSyIf1","n":"Blacklight Surprise","d":"alchemy","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"At least one hour, plus an additional hour for every success the alchemist scores with the dice. If the light source breaks, the formula burns off.","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, sanguine and choleric mortal blood, sunflower seeds, hand sanitizer, Luminol.","sum":"The sun is the bane of the undead, but this formula can lend Phoebus’ hideous strength to a common UV flashlight or blacklight bulb, for the Kindred unlucky enough to be downrange of it.","fx":"A UV source smeared with Blacklight Surprise does 1 point of Aggravated damage every turn its light hits a vampire.","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"75"}},"DUe4neoPjRj3BiM7":{"id":"DUe4neoPjRj3BiM7","n":"Shatter","d":"fortitude","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene (or until hit)","act":"Free, does not count towards maximum Discipline powers activated in a turn.","pre":"Shatter","sum":"When a fist hits concrete, it’s usually the fist that breaks. So it is with this power, where a vampire turns a blow against the one delivering it. This power has been known to break weapons and shatter bones.","fx":"Anyone who makes a successful Brawl attack against the user suffers the damage which Toughness subtracts as Superficial Health damage.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"83"},"prer":["Shatter"]},"DcxWOBKaO4XM4J6i":{"id":"DcxWOBKaO4XM4J6i","n":"Summon Spirit Beast","d":"spiritus","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Charisma + Animal Ken","dur":"Until the spirit departs from the material plane, usually when it loses interest.","act":"Full","sum":"The user summons one of the spirits native to the area to fulfil a command, a spirit of a dog on a street or bear in a forest. Once summoned, the spirit materializes, taking on an ordinary form.","fx":"A win on a Charisma + Animal Ken roll at a Difficulty of 2 allows the user to summon a spirit of a summoning of a large animal or two small or medium animals.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"162"}},"DjqQTkALrHgRFJD8":{"id":"DjqQTkALrHgRFJD8","n":"Hypnosis","d":"melpominee","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"Charisma + Performance vs. Composure + Wits","dur":"One scene","act":"Full","sum":"The vampire begins to sing and focuses the power of their voice onto a target within their line of sight, forcing them into an euphoric or a catatonic-like state.","fx":"The victim finds themselves unable to move or act whatsoever, even to defend, as long as the user takes no other action but to keep up the music.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"86"}},"DmDkls5yiUpMElwx":{"id":"DmDkls5yiUpMElwx","n":"Draugh of Endurance","d":"fortitude","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene or until expired, whichever comes first.","act":"Full","sum":"The Blood of the vampire becomes saturated with the power of Fortitude, conveying a part of that power to anyone who drinks of it.","fx":"The drinker gains the same powers as the donor’s, up to that level.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"82"}},"E90iCu5xnZE2h5qF":{"id":"E90iCu5xnZE2h5qF","n":"Scent of Caine","d":"auspex","lv":2,"cost":"Free","pool":"Wits/Resolve + Awareness","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","am":"Bloodlife Path ••","sum":"Vigilant to the point of paranoia, the Tremere wisely fear the reprisals of other clans and the vengeance of Saulot’s warrior brood.","fx":"Whenever a vitae-bearing creature approaches (vampire, ghoul, revenant) within range of the character’s normal senses, the Storyteller secretly rolls (or the player, if the Storyteller is…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"28"},"amr":[{"k":"path:bloodlife","l":2}]},"ECIzsqmiwPeeyHaU":{"id":"ECIzsqmiwPeeyHaU","n":"Hinder the Gifts of Caine","d":"quietuscruciatus","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"1 turn + for each point of margin.","act":"Free/Minor","sum":"The older a Cainite target at the end of an assassin’s blade, the greater the chance of the target utilising powerful Disciplines fueled by their older Blood to fend off an attacker.","fx":"The the target may not perform Rouse Checks for any purpose. To break out of the effect early, the victim may perform Rouse Checks equal to the margin they lost on the roll.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"142"}},"EGB1Opx2s5gVKLHx":{"id":"EGB1Opx2s5gVKLHx","n":"Grace of Anubis","d":"bardo","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One story.","act":"Full","sum":"By making a pact with the god who welcomes the souls into the Duat, the vampire is able to save their companion from certain doom of curse they themselves possess and are even able to save their lives.","fx":"By making the sign of Anubis with their vitaeon the target’s forehead, they are able to bestow upon them a protection from vampirism for the rest of the story.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"40"}},"EGkJiFomzEc58eNj":{"id":"EGkJiFomzEc58eNj","n":"Flight (•)","d":"flight","lv":1,"sum":"The user cannot yet fly, but they may glide. They can gently descend from any height, and strong winds may provide enough lift to carry them great distances.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"78"}},"EIdg8AGIQWGsXB88":{"id":"EIdg8AGIQWGsXB88","n":"Hospital Chains","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Distillation Roll vs. Stamina","dur":"The restriction on improvement lasts for 2 days per point of margin; on a critical win, it lasts 2 days for each success on the Distillation roll.","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, phlegmatic mortal blood, a sample from a fatal carcinoma, hydrofluoric acid.","sum":"Hospital Chains keeps Kindred and mortals from recovering from injuries. Because sometimes, when you teach someone a lesson, you want to give them a study aid to make sure it sticks.","fx":"Once Hospital Chains touches an injured person, they cannot clear physical injury by any means. Blood is Roused in vain; hospital visits yield no improvement, only bills.","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"76"}},"ELakN6OrypHlaTSY":{"id":"ELakN6OrypHlaTSY","n":"Eyes of the Serpent","d":"serpentis","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"Charisma + Intimidation","dur":"Until the eye contact breaks or until the victim takes at least a point of damage.","act":"Minor -2","sum":"Myths of the cobra and asp — as well as the Greek Medusa — ascribe hypnotic ability to them, and Set’s first gift to his childer is a facsimile of that power.","fx":"While in use, the user gains night vision and may penetrate supernatural darkness as they see as snakes do by warmth.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"150"}},"ERVN6GlIKHjgdSDG":{"id":"ERVN6GlIKHjgdSDG","n":"Mass Manipulation","d":"dominate","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check in addition to the cost of the power amplified","pool":"Manipulation + Subterfuge vs. Intelligence + Resolve","dur":"Per power augmented","act":"Per power used","sum":"The vampire can now command entire gatherings of mortals, and in some cases even groups of vampires. The vampire can use this power both to issue instructions and to manipulate memories.","fx":"The vampire can amplify any of their other powers to affect a group of people, mortal or vampire, at once. All of the victims need to see the eyes of the user.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"77"}},"EYjxURD2pj2rHSaV":{"id":"EYjxURD2pj2rHSaV","n":"Awaken the Sleeper","d":"alchemy","lv":5,"ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, choleric or sanguine human blood, adrenaline, ammonium carbonate, hartshorn, caffeine or benzedrine, melatonin","sum":"This formula results in an elixir which, when added to human blood, can awaken a vampire from Torpor.","fx":"For each success above 2 on the distillation roll, the elixir can awaken a vampire of that Blood Potency.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition Corebook","page":"287"}},"EhzypguTwiOgCplE":{"id":"EhzypguTwiOgCplE","n":"Drawing Out the Beast","d":"animalism","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Wits + Animal Ken vs Composure + Resolve","dur":"Standard frenzy duration","act":"Full","sum":"Cainites with this ability are so familiar with the vagaries of animals’ instinctive reactions that they can even read the reactions of their own Beasts.","fx":"Later stimuli can still provoke Frenzy in the user, but they can use this power as long as they can make Rouse Checks and further targets remain available.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"22"}},"F6SwJT08f8X6odl5":{"id":"F6SwJT08f8X6odl5","n":"Tormented Essence","d":"daimonion","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Occult vs. Dexterity + Athletics or some other dodge roll","dur":"One attack","act":"Full","sum":"The Daimonion users, as do all Baali, know their place in the universe and within the hierarchy of their masters. Suffering trickles downward, and the Daimonion users stand within that torrent.","fx":"Regardless, the power creates a missile that inflicts one point of Aggravated Health and Willpower damage upon a successful hit.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"57"}},"FIBjM3BBDHZsGCA6":{"id":"FIBjM3BBDHZsGCA6","n":"Gift of Apis","d":"bardo","lv":3,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"Some consider it a thing borrowed from Animalism, but the Children of Osiris consider it a boon of the bull-god Apis himself. Those possessing his boon are able to feed off animalism long after they’ve been sired.","fx":"The user halves (rounded up) their Blood Potency for the purposes of slaking Hunger from animals.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"39"}},"FO0wLUDLDiIOMRWF":{"id":"FO0wLUDLDiIOMRWF","n":"Terminal Decree","d":"dominate","lv":5,"cost":"No additional Hunger cost, but one’s own Humanity cost is potentially severe","pool":"Per power augmented","dur":"Passive","act":"Per power used","sum":"No longer hampered by the selfpreservation instincts of their victims, the vampire can now issue commands that directly lead to the harm or death of the victim.","fx":"Terminal commands now must be resisted (see individual powers regarding rolls involved), rather than failing automatically.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"77"}},"FRBpq5quYDDOz12B":{"id":"FRBpq5quYDDOz12B","n":"Malleable Visage","d":"vicissitude","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Medicine","dur":"Permanent until healed or altered again. See Characteristics.","act":"Full, see system.","sum":"The user may alter their own body in simple, cosmetic ways. They can be taller or stockier. They can change his voice by reshaping their larynx. They can adopt new skin tone, new eye color, new hair, and so on.","fx":"The user may perform one of the sample alterations below on themselves.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"202"}},"FgfzYjaUzOdGiK7Z":{"id":"FgfzYjaUzOdGiK7Z","n":"Feral Speech","d":"animalism","lv":2,"cost":"Free/One Rouse Check to summon animals","pool":"Manipulation/Charisma + Animal Ken","dur":"One Scene Successes Response Total Failure/ A random fraction of the Botch creatures respond, but are hostile to the character 0 No response; you may try again One animal responds 1 2 One-quarter of the animals within range respond 3 Half the animals within range respond 4 Three-quarters of the animals within range respond 5+ All animals within range respond","act":"Full action to summon, minor action of -2 dice to talk with animalism or command them.","sum":"This power allows the Cainite to hark back to the days before the fall of Babel, when all speech was one.","fx":"No expenditure or die roll is necessary to activate this power, but the character must spend one turn getting the animal’s attention and looking into its eyes in order to key their own Beast to the creature’s language.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"15"}},"FmAtvvBadZB0rLpV":{"id":"FmAtvvBadZB0rLpV","n":"Unliving Hive","d":"animalism","lv":3,"cost":"No additional cost","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","am":"Daimonion 1","sum":"Most often seen amongst the rare yet dreaded Baali, this unnerving power allows the user to extend their animal influence to swarms of insects such as flies or roaches.","fx":"The vampire can bind the swarm as a famulus, and some even give it the ability to nest inside the cavities of their body.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"19"},"amr":[{"k":"daimonion","l":1}]},"FmLseFL4XD6TRJAJ":{"id":"FmLseFL4XD6TRJAJ","n":"Shadow Servant","d":"obtenebration","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene/night, whichever is shorter from the shadow’s point of view.","act":"Full","sum":"The vampire gives independent life to a part of their shadow and can use it to spy on or unnerve their enemies.","fx":"The shadow travels at running speed and can effortlessly slip under doors, climb walls, or slip into or through the smallest cracks, although it cannot endure brightly lit areas.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"111"}},"Fmi1gCkpLwZIdstE":{"id":"Fmi1gCkpLwZIdstE","n":"Blessings of Set Typhon","d":"serpentis","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until the vampire falls to sleep or torpor or ends the power BLESSINGS OF SET-TYHON FORMS","act":"Full","pre":"Apep’s Venom The vampire turns into a massive mythical cobra wreathed in darkness. Its minimum length is 1 meter/yard and maximum is equal to twice the user’s Serpentis rating. This form is greatly enjoyed by the priesthood of Apep and all those who walk the Path of Apep or some other chaos-philosophy.","sum":"One of the favourite of the Followers of Set who typically master only a single form with their high priests mastering all of them.","fx":"Upon transformation, the vampire gains the Physical Attributes, senses, and native Skills, specialties and abilities associated with that form (see next page) and also gains that form’s…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"153"},"prer":["some other chaos-philosophy."]},"FsFxmBmcYL7BskD7":{"id":"FsFxmBmcYL7BskD7","n":"Clear the Field","d":"presence","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Charisma + Persuasion","dur":"The effect lasts for a scene, but those under its spell might remain by spending a point of Willpower.","act":"Full","am":"Dominate 3","sum":"Developed by adherents to the Path of Chivalry to clear a battlefield of weak foes, as they found no honor in killing them. In the modern era, it is used more often to clear a room of people to enjoy solitude.","fx":"The user rolls Charisma + Persuasion against Wits + Composure of those within a space equal to a large room around them.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"122"},"amr":[{"k":"dominate","l":3}]},"FwISAKsmcngxuzFh":{"id":"FwISAKsmcngxuzFh","n":"Transmogrify the Mortal Clay","d":"vicissitude","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Medicine","dur":"Permanent until healed or altered again. See Characteristics.","act":"Full, see system.","pre":"Malleable Visage","sum":"While Malleable Visage is relatively inoffensive, Transmogrify the Mortal Clay is where Vicissitude’s real power takes shape as the user gains mastery over muscle and flesh at a deeper level.","fx":"If the subject is avoiding the user’s touch and the time required to perform an alteration is one turn or instant, alteration first requires a successful roll with any combination of Strength/Dexterity + Athletics/ Brawl.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"204"},"prer":["Malleable Visage"]},"GAcS0VdUN9uMVkzj":{"id":"GAcS0VdUN9uMVkzj","n":"Night Shades","d":"obtenebration","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Wits + Occult","dur":"One scene","act":"Full","sum":"This ability allows Cainites to craft lifelike images and illusions out of darkness that are nearly indistinguishable from reality.","fx":"For each success, the character may create one image that the size of a human or smaller, or they may pool their successes to create one very large illusion.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"112"}},"GUCW5YycBLC8eQwV":{"id":"GUCW5YycBLC8eQwV","n":"Tabula Rasa","d":"dominate","lv":4,"cost":"Two Rouse Checks","pool":"Manipulation + Subterfuge vs. Composure + Resolve","dur":"Indefinite","act":"Full, extended","pre":"Mesmerise","sum":"Less memory manipulation than eradication, this callous power does away with subtlety and wipes every trace of memory from a victim, leaving them a pliant effigy of themselves.","fx":"The user Rouses their Blood, holds the gaze of their victim, and must then engage in an extended conflict of Manipulation + Subterfuge versus the victim’s Composure + Resolve, accumulating ten margins during an entire scene.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"75"},"prer":["Mesmerise"]},"GcM4sNlAQ4ZNmdue":{"id":"GcM4sNlAQ4ZNmdue","n":"Friends List","d":"alchemy","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Alchemy","dur":"One scene","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, phlegmatic blood, the eyes of a whippoorwill or owl or other nocturnal bird, and a silver thread.","sum":"This formula allows the alchemist to see the connections between mortals and Kindred.","fx":"Upon activating this power, the alchemist makes an Intelligence + Alchemy test to see a thin, silver thread connecting a mortal to a vampire they have some sort of connection with.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade Players Guide","page":"104"}},"Gf3QTHXnk8SbVSmc":{"id":"Gf3QTHXnk8SbVSmc","n":"Discipline Channeling","d":"alchemy","lv":4,"cost":"The same as the channeled power.","pool":"The same as the channeled power.","pre":"Concoct Ashe","ing":"Crushed leaves from the indigo plant.","sum":"Counterfeiting Disciplines is part and parcel of Thin-Blood Alchemy’s use, but the ability to channel a Discipline from the ashes of a deceased vampire is a form of necromantic Alchemy, at least according to Dr.","fx":"When using Concoct Ashe, this formula may be used to imbue remains with the abilities of the vampire they once formed.","src":{"book":"Cults of the Blood Gods","page":"47"},"prer":["Concoct Ashe"]},"GqqEmEhOXOfowkPV":{"id":"GqqEmEhOXOfowkPV","n":"Counterfeit (Level 3 Power)","d":"alchemy","lv":4,"sum":"At level 4, the Alchemist can develop formulae that counterfeit level 3 powers of other Disciplines (and Blood Sorcery powers that affect the caster’s own Blood, but never Rituals).","fx":"Use the counterfeited power’s own cost and system, substituting the Alchemist’s Thin-Blood Alchemy rating for the Discipline rating wherever one is called for.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition Corebook","page":"287"}},"GxjANpV7XVFgIHt2":{"id":"GxjANpV7XVFgIHt2","n":"Sight of the Blood","d":"quietussanguinis","lv":1,"cost":"Free, blood required is neglible","pool":"Wits + Awareness","dur":"One Scene","act":"Free","sum":"The sorcerers of Haqim were made with a purpose and entrusted by Haqim to keep watch over the spirits close to the material plane and hunt for demons infesting it.","fx":"They are able to see nearby spirits. Ghosts are not proper spirits by definition as they have an ectoplasmic corpus.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"145"}},"HDWkrRD98sS79jL3":{"id":"HDWkrRD98sS79jL3","n":"Dream Combat","d":"valerenwarrior","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Composure + Resolve vs. Composure + Resolve","dur":"Until one character is defeated or the user ends this power before that.","act":"Full","sum":"Warrior Salubri use Dream Combat to confront ghosts, demons and other spirits that they cannot affect physically.","fx":"The target is pulled into the dream world and may not leave until the user of this power has been defeated or ended this power by their own will.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"194"}},"HFhOzbqkUYOT97iX":{"id":"HFhOzbqkUYOT97iX","n":"Siren’s Voice","d":"melpominee","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Charisma + Performance vs. Wits + Composure","dur":"As per system.","act":"Full","sum":"By singing or reciting the most beautiful melodies and verses those around them ever heard in their life or unlife, the vampire effectively shields themselves from harm.","fx":"All who hear the vampire and intend to be hostile against them must make a Composure + Wits roll against the successes rolled by the user of the power.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"88"}},"HeI6Jx7RQxpFd40s":{"id":"HeI6Jx7RQxpFd40s","n":"Taste of the Body","d":"quietuscruciatus","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"By sipping blood, those capable of listening to the Blood are able to find out more about the constitution, muscle density, the quality of their blood and probably even estimate what kind of food a mortal eats.","fx":"The user gains a die bonus to all Physical Skill-based rolls against a person whose blood they tasted (even a bite attack provides enough of a sample).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"139"}},"HkbiHC7F3uUhIiAu":{"id":"HkbiHC7F3uUhIiAu","n":"Patience of the Norns","d":"temporis","lv":4,"cost":"Free, one Willpower point","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","pre":"Leaden Movement","sum":"The vampire may now either expand her power’s circumference to engulf multiple targets at once or localize it on a single focused point to freeze an object in place.","fx":"The character may now use Leaden Movement on as many enemies within their line of sight as they have dots in Wits + Temporis.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"171"},"prer":["Leaden Movement"]},"Hy1LpvVrBFUrNDXq":{"id":"Hy1LpvVrBFUrNDXq","n":"Hold the Power","d":"mytherceria","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Insight vs. Composure + Wits","dur":"Same table as Mind Steal (p. 71).","act":"Full","pre":"Mind Steal","sum":"Not only can the vampire steal experience of mundane tasks earned over years of practice but they can even copy powers of the Blood.","fx":"Hold the Power may only on those who possess vampiric Disciplines, including ghouls and revenants, and for all intents and purposes shares the system of Mind Steal except that on a win…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"94"},"prer":["Mind Steal"]},"I7EZ1YU0Kci6wi8X":{"id":"I7EZ1YU0Kci6wi8X","n":"Gift of Ra","d":"bardo","lv":5,"cost":"Free","pool":"Resolve + Osiris","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"Ra is, technically, the grandfather of all Children of Osiris.","fx":"The user is fully immune to fire and all frenzies induced by the fire.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"41"}},"I8LO2Pxwubl9oZ8p":{"id":"I8LO2Pxwubl9oZ8p","n":"Elevate","d":"alchemy","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Stamina + Alchemy","dur":"One scene","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, sanguine mortal blood, fermented chocolate, rice vinegar, black coffee, often some kind of fun street drug.","sum":"When you’re at the party and feeling like a thrill, go find the guy by the bathrooms. No, not the guy selling speed and molly to sweaty dancers. The other guy, the one that stands way too still.","fx":"El also can act as a carrier for regular street drugs, although the effects shift unpredictably if usually toward ecstatic stimulation.","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"74"}},"ID99ksE4FOsibaPz":{"id":"ID99ksE4FOsibaPz","n":"The Spirit Beast","d":"spiritus","lv":5,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","pre":"The Wild Beast","sum":"Conceding one’s body to a spirit is rarely a good option, unless you are a master of Spiritus.","fx":"When using the Wild Beast, the user is also immune to sunlight and resists the urge to sleep.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"165"},"prer":["The Wild Beast"]},"IDT1mOd7gwaDKFHv":{"id":"IDT1mOd7gwaDKFHv","n":"Cloud Memory","d":"dominate","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"Manipulation + Subterfuge vs. Wits + Resolve","dur":"Indefinitely","act":"Full","sum":"By uttering the phrase “Forget!” the user can make the Dominated victim forget the current moment as well as the last few minutes, enough to mask a superficial feeding or a chance meeting.","fx":"Clouding the memory of a resisting victim or another vampire requires standard Dominate requirements, the verb “Forget!” and Manipulation + Dominate vs Wits + Resolve roll.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"71"}},"IKasYNCtj0yxikzP":{"id":"IKasYNCtj0yxikzP","n":"Ishtar’s Touch","d":"quietusanimae","lv":2,"cost":"One or more Rouse Checks","pool":"Composure + Resolve vs. Intelligence + Composure","dur":"The poison remains potent for nights equal to the user’s Quietus rating","act":"Minor -2","sum":"The vizier version of Scorpion’s Touch is Ishtar’s Touch.","fx":"This contact poison has the same system as Scorpion’s Touch (p. 122) and is applied the same way).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"135"}},"IPEqwHDcIjpNZ6YM":{"id":"IPEqwHDcIjpNZ6YM","n":"Counterfeit (Level 4 Power)","d":"alchemy","lv":5,"sum":"At level 5, the Alchemist can develop formulae that counterfeit level 4 powers of other Disciplines (and Blood Sorcery powers that affect the caster’s own Blood, but never Rituals).","fx":"Use the counterfeited power’s own cost and system, substituting the Alchemist’s Thin-Blood Alchemy rating for the Discipline rating wherever one is called for.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition Corebook","page":"288"}},"ISbZGoHpY6drYcdq":{"id":"ISbZGoHpY6drYcdq","n":"Lingering Kiss","d":"presence","lv":2,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"A number of nights equal to the user’s Presence rating.","act":"Free","sum":"The Kiss of a vampire induces near-ecstasy in the victim, but this power leaves other Kisses in the dust.","fx":"The vampire can choose to use this power during each feeding where they sate at least one Hunger.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"121"}},"IUGLWyrcnixmSAm5":{"id":"IUGLWyrcnixmSAm5","n":"Sense the Unseen","d":"auspex","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"Wits/Resolve + Awareness","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"The senses of the vampire become attuned to dimensions beyond the mundane, allowing them to sense presences otherwise hidden from the naked eye.","fx":"Against an entity actively trying to stay hidden, the Storyteller can call for a blind roll (“Lisa, roll seven dice for me”) as a contest against the target’s relevant pool.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"25"}},"IaLISYuVP57uNBkO":{"id":"IaLISYuVP57uNBkO","n":"Checkout Time","d":"alchemy","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"The written time span determines the duration, but cannot exceed nine nights.","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, phlegmatic mortal blood, embalming fluid, myrrh, a toad’s skull.","sum":"Thin-bloods traveling great distances face challenges. Being shipped as a literal corpse can, for the clever, mitigate them.","fx":"The subject can be the alchemist themself.","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"74"}},"IwSkIcOHIClA2S0e":{"id":"IwSkIcOHIClA2S0e","n":"Ease Wounds","d":"valerenhealer","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Medicine","dur":"Instant","act":"Minor -2","sum":"While yet lacking the power to outright heal by the powers of Valeren, the vampire may at least ease the wounds of another.","fx":"At the cost of a Rouse Check, the user may touch their target and roll Intelligence + Medicine (Difficulty 2) to instantly convert a number of Aggravated Health damage to Superficial equal to the margins.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"183"}},"JGwXiK892IB5CyYb":{"id":"JGwXiK892IB5CyYb","n":"Fire Voice","d":"dementation","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Insight vs. Wits + Composure","dur":"Instant/per turn.","act":"Full","sum":"By mentioning one of many truths the clan Malkavian knows, the user of Dementation may shatter their victim’s psyche and force them to cover in fear.","fx":"The character rolls Manipulation + Insight against Composure + Wits of the victim with whom they’re communicating (p. 52).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"67"}},"JHKI1t6jeIbcz20j":{"id":"JHKI1t6jeIbcz20j","n":"Scry the Soul","d":"auspex","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Insight vs Composure + Subterfuge","dur":"Until something in the aura changes, until the user lets the power lapse or rest of the scene.","act":"Full","sum":"By focusing on a person, the vampire can perceive the state of that person’s psyche as a shifting aur a of colors.","fx":"A win allows the user to ask the storyteller or the targeted player a number of questions equal to the margin.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"30"}},"JjO22BjUnJV9mrxK":{"id":"JjO22BjUnJV9mrxK","n":"Taste of the Soul","d":"quietusanimae","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Free","sum":"By sipping blood, those capable of listening to the Blood are able to find out more about the mental constitution, the ardour and the way the person acts or behaves, giving them an advantage in manipulating them.","fx":"The user gains a die bonus to all Social Skill-based rolls against a person whose blood they tasted (even a bite attack provides enough of a sample).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"135"}},"Jv6YdKvBeTVKklF9":{"id":"Jv6YdKvBeTVKklF9","n":"Umbrous Clutch","d":"obtenebration","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Wits + Obtenebration vs. Dexterity + Wits","dur":"Instant","act":"Full","sum":"The user creates a temporary gate out of the victim’s own shadow, causing them to fall through Oblivion and into the waiting arms of the user.","fx":"At the Storyteller’s discretion, a stationary victim not paying attention can be automatically caught.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"113"}},"KSaHsktrYGUkOkoz":{"id":"KSaHsktrYGUkOkoz","n":"Vicissitude Mastery","d":"vicissitude","lv":5,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Permanent until healed or altered again. See Characteristics.","act":"Passive","sum":"The vampire’s ability to command flesh becomes so great that they no longer require physical touch to initiate powers of Vicissitude.","fx":"The character may now use Shape Flesh (and its improvements) without requiring physical contact or retainment of the subject (those who fail resistance roll are in such a shock that only outside intervention may stop the process).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"210"}},"KSaWajfJSHCx77qW":{"id":"KSaWajfJSHCx77qW","n":"Raptorous Touch","d":"quietuscruciatus","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene unless ended sooner","act":"Free","sum":"Using fangs to drink is sometimes to inefficient for those grappling or striking their enemies. Raptorous Touch allows its user to drink blood through skin contact alone.","fx":"System: The vampire must first touch the target (any combination of Dexterity/Strength and Athletics/Brawl would suffice) against the target’s def-nsive roll (usually a dodge).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"142"}},"Kh9A9Lx1ZjgpABax":{"id":"Kh9A9Lx1ZjgpABax","n":"Silence of Death","d":"quietuscruciatus","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Free","sum":"A gift of Haqim to his children born without the ability to mask themselves, Silence of Death offers a shroud of silence to hide the sounds made by the user and their close allies, perfect for ambushes or simply walking around unheard.","fx":"The user’s blood begins to vibrate at a frequency that disrupts hearing and silences the footsteps, clothing, minor collisions, and other sounds in a 6-meter radius, giving themselves and others a two-dice bonus on all Stealth rolls.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"140"}},"KhXCOV3RCmk0Eko3":{"id":"KhXCOV3RCmk0Eko3","n":"Beast Mode","d":"alchemy","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"One scene","ing":"The alchemist’s vitae, choleric or sanguine human blood, vitae of Blood Potency 4+, phenylcyclohexyl piperidine, adrenaline injector, spoiled two percent milk, sodium bicarbonate","sum":"Every Duskborn knows that their vampiric powers are weaker than those of a true Kindred.","fx":"When consumed, the alchemist must succeed on a Willpower test (Difficulty 2) to avoid frenzy.","src":{"book":"Gehenna War","page":"51"}},"Ki5XXiYUFjtmQqL4":{"id":"Ki5XXiYUFjtmQqL4","n":"Share the Senses","d":"auspex","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Awareness vs Composure + Subterfuge","dur":"One scene, although it can be extended by an additional scene by spending a point of Willpower","act":"Full","sum":"By reaching out with their mind, the vampire can tap into the senses of another mortal or vampire, seeing, hearing, and feeling what they do.","fx":"This Difficulty can go up depending on distraction, distance, and other factors, such as the amount of the user’s Blood that remains in the target.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"32"}},"Koj8ktHEpXGkemXV":{"id":"Koj8ktHEpXGkemXV","n":"Pain for Pleasure","d":"valerenhealer","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Medicine","dur":"One scene with a Critical Win (or 3+ margins) extending it to the rest of the night.","act":"Minor -2","sum":"Rewiring mental perceptions, the target begins to experience pain as suiting pleasure. This is often used to soothe the passing of those dying in agony caused by blades of sickness.","fx":"The vampire may either use this power on themselves or touch another to use it, rolling Intelligence + Medicine against a Difficulty of 3.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"187"}},"LKDsKQsztzVLlaS9":{"id":"LKDsKQsztzVLlaS9","n":"Internal Awareness","d":"quietusanimae","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"Composure + Occult","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"Vampires learning Quietus Animae very quickly learn that blood is tied to everything in the body, from humours to the very soul that is extinguished through diablerie.","fx":"The user may also use Internal Awareness instead of normal rolls on standard contests against mind-altering powers such as Dementation.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"134"}},"LWGBbyB1vKiCfQSD":{"id":"LWGBbyB1vKiCfQSD","n":"A Thousand Cuts","d":"celerity","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One action","act":"Free","sum":"While the powers of Celerity do not lend themselves to the application of force, the vampire’s ungodly speed allows them to land a blinding amount of cuts and slashes.","fx":"The vampire may add their Celerity rating to any single Brawl or Melee attack (not otherwise augmented by a Discipline) made with claws or an edged weapon.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"44"}},"LXXW8moPTmjGSKxa":{"id":"LXXW8moPTmjGSKxa","n":"Blood Awakening","d":"quietusanimae","lv":4,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","pre":"Read the Blood’s Desire","sum":"By ingesting blood, the user is able to further break it down into memories, experiences and opinions, perfect for knowing who to call into plots and who to have executed.","fx":"The user may also select the following effects when using Read the Blood’s Desire:","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"137"},"prer":["Read the Blood’s Desire"]},"LjvUf9yp4f6R6Fnn":{"id":"LjvUf9yp4f6R6Fnn","n":"Strike the Slow","d":"temporis","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"A single attack","act":"Free","sum":"The user pushes themselves through a crack in time, effectively slowing the world around themselves from their perspective, to make an attack against what is essentially a stationary target.","fx":"The user makes a Brawl or a Melee attack against their opponent at a static Difficulty of 1 due to the target appearing frozen.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"174"}},"LmBKeF5SYD5Laz0N":{"id":"LmBKeF5SYD5Laz0N","n":"Guise of the Departed","d":"obfuscate","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Performance vs. Wits + Insight","dur":"Until dawn","act":"Passive","am":"Thanatosis •• or Corpse in the Monster Path ••","sum":"The user can absorb the spiritual residue of a recently departed mortal, stealing not only their living appearance but also bearing and mannerisms.","fx":"A win creates a convincing disguise and gives appropriate Looks Merits, but the user must roll Manipulation + Performance vs Wits + Insight contests against anyone close to the copied…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"98"},"amr":[{"k":"thanatosis","l":2},{"k":"path:corpseinthemonster","l":2}]},"LqLDf6s7vSKeRfkD":{"id":"LqLDf6s7vSKeRfkD","n":"See the True Shape","d":"auspex","lv":2,"cost":"Free","pool":"Wits/Resolve + Medicine","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","am":"Vicissitude •• or Protean ••","sum":"A vampire with this power may recognize flesh that has been magically reshaped.","fx":"The vampire scrutinises the target and her player rolls Wits + Medicine (Wits may be swapped with Resolve for intential scrutiny) + Body Crafts against the successes of whatever power…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"28"},"amr":[{"k":"vicissitude","l":2},{"k":"protean","l":2}]},"LsTMhG7o341sJgiv":{"id":"LsTMhG7o341sJgiv","n":"Blood of Mandagloire","d":"alchemy","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse check","dur":"This formula stays active in the herd’s blood for three nights after dosing.","ing":"The Alchemist’s Blood, melancholic human blood, ketamine or Thorazine, melted human fat, verdigris","sum":"This concoction can taint an entire herd, but must be imbibed by the victims within a few hours of being distilled.","fx":"After taking this concoction the herd takes on a melancholic Resonance and becomes sluggish and unresponsive.","src":{"book":"Second Inquisition","page":"46"}},"LwiHti8M1IbGk2YS":{"id":"LwiHti8M1IbGk2YS","n":"Majesty","d":"presence","lv":5,"cost":"Two Rouse Checks","pool":"Charisma + Intimidation vs Composure + Resolve","dur":"One scene","act":"Full","sum":"The Presence of the user becomes a conduit for Dominate. The vampire now only needs their voice to be heard in order to employ Dominate powers.","fx":"People in the presence of the user can only stare, slackjawed, or avert their eyes in fear or submission.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"126"}},"M0t28Ik00LHBY0iq":{"id":"M0t28Ik00LHBY0iq","n":"Repeat","d":"temporis","lv":2,"cost":"Free","pool":"Intelligence + Occult vs. Wits + Intelligence","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"Repeating the same course of an action that has failed you is often a sign of madness — or a sign that you are being influenced by a user of Temporis.","fx":"Upon a win, the victim’s current action is interrupted and they are forced to repeat a simple action they took in previous two turns such as attacking the same target in the same way or repeating a sentence.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"168"}},"M226R2a2ITywBZR9":{"id":"M226R2a2ITywBZR9","n":"Lure of the Blood","d":"quietusanimae","lv":2,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Free","sum":"The vitae of the Children of Haqim is feared by the other Clans as rumours (spread by the Haqimites themselves) state that a single sip is enough to blood bond a person.","fx":"Every time the user’s vitae is consumed, it counts as two for the purposes of the Blood Oath/Blood Bond, meaning that the vizier may achieve a Blood Oath/Blood Bond in only two nights.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"135"}},"M8Zm3ivs0BageZe8":{"id":"M8Zm3ivs0BageZe8","n":"Weight of a Feather","d":"protean","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"Wits + Survival","dur":"As long as desired","act":"Free","sum":"The vampire can reduce their effective mass and density, making themselves almost weightless.","fx":"As long as the power is in effect, the vampire is immune to damage from falls, collisions, and being thrown.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"128"}},"MA4x0OQk8rAXqKHg":{"id":"MA4x0OQk8rAXqKHg","n":"Rayzeel’s Song","d":"valerenhealer","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check, one Willpower point per subject","pool":"Charisma + Performance","dur":"The subjects remain affected for the rest of the night, but lose the benefits at the end of the first conflict.","act":"Several minutes of songs or recitations","sum":"Music soothes the savage breast. Voice and instruments heal the soul and confer focus. Rayzeel is said to have crafted the Song to draw Saulot out of depression after the Baali Wars.","fx":"The subjects suffer no Physical or Mental Impairment for the rest of the scene and reduce their Called Shot Penalties by one.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"187"}},"MIWquRwdK4nPvL6b":{"id":"MIWquRwdK4nPvL6b","n":"Silentia Mortis","d":"quietusanimae","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene","act":"Free","sum":"Haqim’s gift to his children so that they may plot in secret near hostile ears, Silentia Mortis offers a shroud of silence to hide their steps and voice so that they may scheme by whispers in the shadows.","fx":"The users blood begins to vibrate at a mystic frequency and fully silences their footsteps, voice, clothing, minor collisions, and other sounds of their person, giving them a two-dice bonus on all Stealth rolls.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"135"}},"MIljBlybOL9Tpiey":{"id":"MIljBlybOL9Tpiey","n":"Pleague of Beasts","d":"animalism","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Animal Ken","dur":"One night","act":"Full","sum":"The vampire can mark an individual, making them the target of focused animal attention. Whatever beasts or vermin are in the area seek the target out to bark, peck, scratch, and generally make their night miserable.","fx":"Suffering a dice penalty to all Skill pools equal to the margin on the win unless they can physically isolate themselves from the local wildlife.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"18"}},"MJejvWALn3Qe8H38":{"id":"MJejvWALn3Qe8H38","n":"Marrow Sucker","d":"thanatosis","lv":3,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"All animals contain a spark of life. This power allows you to scrape, suck, and savor those small bits of life out of dead things, be they animal or human, to allow you to survive.","fx":"The bones turn into a grey, pulpy mass which the vampire must then swallow.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"178"}},"MWDtk1cXqjo29dAF":{"id":"MWDtk1cXqjo29dAF","n":"Sense the Beast","d":"animalism","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"Wits/Resolve + Awareness vs Composure + Subterfuge","dur":"Passive","act":"Free","sum":"The vampire can sense the Beast present in mortals, vampires, and other supernaturals, gaining a sense of their nature, hunger, and hostility.","fx":"Wits may be substituded with Resolve if the user is actively trying to use the power.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"14"}},"Mbcm6u3hsDcdUZME":{"id":"Mbcm6u3hsDcdUZME","n":"I Am Legion","d":"daimonion","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Leadership","dur":"Until the creature exits, willingly or forcefully.","act":"Full","sum":"One of the Baali's most devious methods of avoiding detection, this subtle magic allows the Baali to forge a temporary pact with a “speaking demon” or other malevolent spirit (Storyteller's discretion as to what sort of being is appropriate).","fx":"The player must succeed in a Manipulation + Leadership roll (Difficulty 0) to ensnare a suitable demon or spirit.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"57"}},"MdQxqsGcATiDDoQ1":{"id":"MdQxqsGcATiDDoQ1","n":"Tank","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"Until the alchemist takes damage or the scene ends.","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, choleric blood, oaked wine or bourbon, and Kevlar fibers or cement or ground tortoiseshell.","sum":"The alchemist can use this formula to help strengthen their resistance against damage, albeit only temporarily.","fx":"The first time the alchemist sustains damage in a scene, reduce the damage by five. The formula then expires.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade Players Guide","page":"105"}},"MjswudDCnoojdgNk":{"id":"MjswudDCnoojdgNk","n":"Mirror of Trust","d":"alchemy","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse check","dur":"One hour","ing":"The Alchemist’s Blood, sanguine human blood, truth serum, a white chrysanthemum taken from a grave","sum":"This mixture, when imbibed by the Alchemist, makes them compelling and attractive, overwhelming other blankbodies’ self-control and encouraging them to speak honestly and frankly, especially in response to direct questions.","fx":"The Alchemist has 3 extra dice on Persuasion or Intimidation rolls to make another person or blankbody be honest with them","src":{"book":"Second Inquisition","page":"46"}},"MlbjDcmml85z6FLI":{"id":"MlbjDcmml85z6FLI","n":"Flight (•••)","d":"flight","lv":3,"sum":"The user can fly up to 45 miles per hour/60 km per hour and carry up to 50 lbs./25 kg, if their Strength allows for it.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"78"}},"Mveb3lreXArq9UtS":{"id":"Mveb3lreXArq9UtS","n":"Serpent’s Flesh","d":"serpentis","lv":1,"cost":"Free/One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until ended by the user or one scene.","act":"Free","sum":"With this power, the Setite’s flesh becomes leathery, scaly, slimy, and otherwise monstrous. Their body becomes flexible and malleable, and they become harder to hurt.","fx":"Should the user wish to appear more subtle and not unnerving to common mortals, they must spend a point of Willpower to contain the transformation.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"151"}},"N0Ts5gr12g6JepbB":{"id":"N0Ts5gr12g6JepbB","n":"Implant Suggestion","d":"dominate","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Persuasion vs. Composure + Resolve","dur":"One scene","act":"Full","am":"Presence •","sum":"The vampire possesses the power to change the very personality or opinions of a subject, at least temporarily.","fx":"Eye-contact is required as with most Dominate powers.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"75"},"amr":[{"k":"presence","l":1}]},"N2cYRHw49pz3rrKW":{"id":"N2cYRHw49pz3rrKW","n":"The Wild Beast","d":"spiritus","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Animal Ken","dur":"Until dawn unless ended before that.","act":"Free","sum":"There are many restless spirits lurking around violent creatures, especially the undead.","fx":"The user’s nails elongate as their hands become claws, counting as a +2 piercing Brawl weapon dealing Aggravated Health damage to mortals and spirits (materialised or not) and unhalved Superficial Health damage to vampires.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"163"}},"N9D5SId7unhbkF78":{"id":"N9D5SId7unhbkF78","n":"Aura of Sloth","d":"mytherceria","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Persuasion","dur":"One Scene or until intentionally ended.","act":"Full","sum":"This power forms an aura that mentally fatigues those within it, able to put mortals to sleep with ease, and even affecting the time supernaturals need before they must rest.","fx":"The aura can expand to up to 10 metres from the user in all directions, not being obstructed by physical obstacles such as walls.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"93"}},"NrPpA8ZM9aL79yOa":{"id":"NrPpA8ZM9aL79yOa","n":"Theft of Will","d":"dominate","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Occult","dur":"One turn","act":"Full","am":"Any Blood Sorcery Path •••","sum":"Developed by Tremere elders to deal with spells of mischievous neonates a lesson, Theft of Will allows its user to Dominate magic itself and take control of nearby magic made by other sorcerers such as Wards and curses.","fx":"First, the user must know that there is a magical effect to take control of such as by Sense the Unseen (for things like Wards and spells) or aura reading Scry the Soul (for things like curses).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"76"},"amr":[{"k":"any:path","l":3}]},"OAbSxVfdnHJnV0jw":{"id":"OAbSxVfdnHJnV0jw","n":"Ride the Wild Wind","d":"animalism","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check. Free if used on famulus.","pool":"Manipulation + Animal Ken","dur":"A scene/indefinitely (see above)","act":"Full","sum":"Cainites who know Ride the Wild Mind are able to dislodge their own souls from their bodies and seat them in the bodies of wild animals.","fx":"The character cannot possess worms or other creatures without eyes, as they have no easy passage for the soul.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"19"}},"OtoYw9nwbM1euKZk":{"id":"OtoYw9nwbM1euKZk","n":"The Choir of Orpheus","d":"melpominee","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check in addition to the cost of the power amplified","pool":"N/A","dur":"As per power amplified.","act":"Passive","sum":"The master of Melpominee may now unleash their voice at an entire crowd of people.","fx":"The vampire can amplify any of their other powers to affect all, including their allies, who hear their voice, at once.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"89"}},"OwJpP9weoLQfWHuG":{"id":"OwJpP9weoLQfWHuG","n":"Conceal","d":"obfuscate","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Subterfuge","dur":"One night, with an additional night per point of margin on the win.","act":"Passive","pre":"Cloak of Shadows","sum":"This ability allows the user to cloak an inanimate object such as a door, a car, or a small house.","fx":"This power cannot affect anything larger than a two-story house or any object moving under its own power (such as a moving carriage).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"103"},"prer":["Cloak of Shadows"]},"P6ESJ69BkSmj9NBm":{"id":"P6ESJ69BkSmj9NBm","n":"Shepard’s Watch","d":"valerenhealer","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Composure + Resolve vs. Composure + Resolve","dur":"One scene","act":"Full to activate, free to maintain or drop","sum":"The third eye opens and flares a bright white, illuminating a barely-visible ward around the user and his charge. No foe may breach this sacred shield.","fx":"Those within it at its creation and those permitted by the user may leave and return, and the barrier moves with the user.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"188"}},"P97on6ARJjj8oMmm":{"id":"P97on6ARJjj8oMmm","n":"Whiff-Its","d":"alchemy","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"Until dawn","ing":"The alchemist’s vitae, phlegmatic or sanguine human blood, cologne or perfume, fresh compost, ammonia, crushed fingernails from an animal","sum":"Some Kindred are rumored to be able to sniff out a particular resonance. Among the Duskborn, others have learned to sniff out the resonance (or lack thereof) of true Kindred and distinguish the most potent among them.","fx":"For the next night, the alchemist can catch the scent of the Kindred with the highest Blood Potency in the area (as determined by the Storyteller).","src":{"book":"Gehenna War","page":"50"}},"PDvxXFwRVQEHi7bu":{"id":"PDvxXFwRVQEHi7bu","n":"Split Second","d":"celerity","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Roughly one action, as determined by the Storyteller.","act":"Free","sum":"The speed at which the vampire moves catches up with their supercharged perception, allowing them to react to events around them at a moment’s notice.","fx":"The player can supersede the Storyteller’s narration of events, within reason.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"46"}},"PFaMW4YA1A7jhMKT":{"id":"PFaMW4YA1A7jhMKT","n":"Quietus Mastery","d":"quietuscruciatus","lv":5,"cost":"Free/One Rouse Check in addition to the cost of the power amplified","pool":"N/A","dur":"Per power augmented","act":"Passive","sum":"As the user masters the Discipline said to have been created by Haqim himself, the vampire figures out how all Gifts of the Blood are connected, and how all the Paths of Quietus lead to the same destination.","fx":"Powers of any Quietus Path that require touch or transmission by poison are now available to the vampire by making a gesture with their hand towards the victim (those who succeed on a Wits…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"144"}},"PGV4hwS94LLmSi2v":{"id":"PGV4hwS94LLmSi2v","n":"Tenebrous Avatar","d":"obtenebration","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene or until ended","act":"Full","sum":"The Cainite using this power can transform her body into an inhuman shadow. The form this living shadow takes depends more on the character’s inner nature than on their mastery of Obtenebration.","fx":"The transformation takes one turn, during which the vampire is unable to do anything else.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"114"}},"PIxtEKK4i1O5YRUA":{"id":"PIxtEKK4i1O5YRUA","n":"Debilitative Poison","d":"quietuscruciatus","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"The poison is potent for one scene","act":"Minor -2 dice/free","sum":"With Hinder Mending, the vampire concocts a special poison that prevents usage of vitae for mending, disrupting vampire targets and their other creations that utilise vitae to heal.","fx":"This contact poison has the same system as Scorpion’s Touch (see above) and is applied the same way).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"142"}},"PWDoZCNBnSQ3V6Nh":{"id":"PWDoZCNBnSQ3V6Nh","n":"Ease Mind","d":"valerenhealer","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Medicine","dur":"Instant","act":"Full","sum":"The vampire soothes the mental or emotional turmoil of their subject, restoring to them a modicum of steadfastness.","fx":"Alternatively, the user restores one Aggravated Willpower damage level for every three successes in the margin.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"184"}},"PZ8TNVtrjT6xxvOB":{"id":"PZ8TNVtrjT6xxvOB","n":"Baal’s Caress","d":"quietuscruciatus","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"The poison remains potent for one story.","act":"Free/Minor","pre":"Scorpion’s Touch","sum":"A refinement of Scorpion’s Touch, Baal’s Caress allows a vampire to transform her blood into an acidic toxin that burns any living or undead flesh, usually accomplished by licking a blade to lubricate it before assaulting an opponent.","fx":"Identical to Scorpion’s Touch save that the damage is increased to Aggravated against all beings.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"143"},"prer":["Scorpion’s Touch"]},"PeFYHQ6g14GRTnhR":{"id":"PeFYHQ6g14GRTnhR","n":"Coax the Tendons","d":"vicissitude","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Medicine","dur":"Permanent","act":"Full","sum":"Normally, mortals a are unable to restore missing limbs without cutting-edge advancements in Medicine or powerful rituals unless they’ve lost the limbs while a ghoul.","fx":"They may reattach a lost limb or graft additional and new ones, potentially healing a related Crippling Injury.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"203"}},"Pi9xxIyIu4P5iCSZ":{"id":"Pi9xxIyIu4P5iCSZ","n":"Rush Job","d":"celerity","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One Scene","act":"Free","sum":"The vampire can perform time-consuming tasks with blinding speed, their fingers and hands blurring as they write, repair, or build things in record time.","fx":"When active, this power lets the vampire complete Skill-related tasks that would otherwise take whole turns in the span of a few seconds, and can treat a full action as a minor action (p. 209).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"43"}},"PptXQ2S1p1lXCtrB":{"id":"PptXQ2S1p1lXCtrB","n":"Mind’s Defences","d":"dementation","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Insight vs. Wits + Composure","dur":"See p. 52.","act":"Full","sum":"Dementation reveals. It shatters the mind’s defences to reveal the bare and unfiltered truth to the mind.","fx":"The target receives a dice bonus or a dice penalty equal to half the user’s Dementation rating rounded up on rolls to resist Frenzy and any means of mind-influence (Presence, Obfuscate, Dementation, but not Dominate) or Persuasion.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"64"}},"PqWVXlvtMZJak0ww":{"id":"PqWVXlvtMZJak0ww","n":"Permanencz","d":"chimerstry","lv":4,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Illusions last until dismissed now, or until the character makes more than they are able to maintain.","act":"Passive","sum":"Like Apparition, Permanency stacks with other, simpler Chimerstry powers.","fx":"Illusions crafted by Ignis Fatuus or Fata Morgana are now permanent until dismissed (this includes illusions “programmed” with Apparition, for which concentration is no longer needed).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"50"}},"Pz4D6UkzlMXpwFEo":{"id":"Pz4D6UkzlMXpwFEo","n":"Weaken the Blood of the Ancients","d":"quietussanguinis","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse check","pool":"Intelligence + Occult vs. Stamina + Occult (or Fortitude).","dur":"Until dawn","act":"Full","am":"Quietus Cruciatus 3","pre":"Blood’s Curse","sum":"With this power, the user commands Blood and the Curse of Caine itself, manipulating Generation and Blood Potency of their victim.","fx":"The user lowers their Generation and increases their Blood Potency for every point of Generation/ Blood Potency impacted, to the lowest Generation and highest Blood potency equal to the victim’s own.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"149"},"amr":[{"k":"quietuscruciatus","l":3}],"prer":["Blood’s Curse"]},"QAQkIUXkWFeonFbL":{"id":"QAQkIUXkWFeonFbL","n":"Burning Touch","d":"valerenwarrior","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until the user lets go.","act":"Free","sum":"The character’s grasp inflicts searing pain akin to being burnt with a red-hot iron. This power inflicts no damage, but painfully disrupts the vital energies of the target.","fx":"By grasping, punching or touching the target (which in combat could be done with any combination of Strength/Dexterity + Brawl/Athletics) the user causes a surge of fiery pain rushing from…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"192"}},"QEMo3vThCQeGH9nG":{"id":"QEMo3vThCQeGH9nG","n":"Shadow Cast","d":"obtenebration","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene","act":"Minor -2 dice","sum":"Obtenebration is powerful but can often be foiled by the simple lack of appropriate shadows from which to summon its manifestations.","fx":"As long as the power is active, the user casts this shadow, which cannot be removed except by direct sunlight.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"109"}},"QHczqtYXLekTvRtR":{"id":"QHczqtYXLekTvRtR","n":"Animal Dominion","d":"animalism","lv":5,"cost":"Two Rouse Checks/An additional Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Animal Ken","dur":"Until the directive is fulfilled, but animals usually return to their standard ways after a story/passive effect.","act":"Full","sum":"The power the vampire holds over beasts is now great enough to command flocks and packs as if they were extensions of their own body.","fx":"The power does not allow the user to summon animals, but compels those already present to obey.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"22"}},"QLgFKSr1w92khjHe":{"id":"QLgFKSr1w92khjHe","n":"Mortal Illness","d":"thanatosis","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Medicine vs. Stamina + Medicine (or Fortitude)","dur":"The ailment activates when the user willed it to activate when creating it.","act":"Full","sum":"Harbingers of disease, the user of Thanatosis creates an ailment to induce a complete shutdown of function and death.","fx":"See Paralysis of Death for that system) and rolls Manipulation + Medicine vs. the victim’s Stamina + Medicine (or Fortitude, if they possess it).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"180"}},"QOOAugbKp704iPYI":{"id":"QOOAugbKp704iPYI","n":"Solid Shadows","d":"obtenebration","lv":3,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Per power augmented","act":"Passive","am":"Fortitude 1","sum":"With their mastery of Obtenebration, the user may now imbue shadows with physical substance, making them literal physical entities.","fx":"As the Lasombra folklore states, the user can finally wield the Abyss itself.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"111"},"amr":[{"k":"fortitude","l":1}]},"QPf0ZCQ5xQPehjOi":{"id":"QPf0ZCQ5xQPehjOi","n":"Read the Blood’s Desire","d":"quietusanimae","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Insight","dur":"Instant","act":"Full","pre":"Taste of the Soul","sum":"By mixing a subject’s blood with theirs, their blood extracts information on the subject’ desire, beliefs and surface thoughts.","fx":"For this power to work, the user must first possess at least one drop of the subject’s blood that is not older than 48 hours and place it in a cup that they fill with their own (covered by the power’s own Rouse Check).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"136"},"prer":["Taste of the Soul"]},"QQteMTyra5blgGTr":{"id":"QQteMTyra5blgGTr","n":"Truth of Blood","d":"quietusanimae","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Insight vs. Composure + Occult (or Fortitude)","dur":"One scene or until the user removes their finger from the blood container or until the subject overpowers the user.","act":"Full","sum":"As a means to assure that their judgments are firmly grounded in truth, this power allows a vampire to use the blood of an individual being questioned to divine not only the truth of the subject’s words, but the truth behind those words.","fx":"To use this power, the Cainite must have one point of the target’s blood, which she pours into an open container capable of holding the fluid indefinitely, such as a basin or goblet.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"137"}},"QeJ5DF7PhFdSdxyF":{"id":"QeJ5DF7PhFdSdxyF","n":"Toxic Personality","d":"alchemy","lv":4,"cost":"One or two Rouse Checks","pool":"Strength or Dexterity + Alchemy vs. Dexterity + Athletics","dur":"One scene","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, choleric blood, potash or lye, animal spleen, cheesecloth, and iodine.","sum":"The alchemist secretes powerful, caustic bile from their pores and orifices, corroding metals, wood, and living tissue.","fx":"When active, the power allows the alchemist to corrode any material in seconds by simply making contact with it and gains +2 damage on brawl attacks as their mere touch becomes acid.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade Players Guide","page":"105"}},"QiHMltIkNfxkdDxb":{"id":"QiHMltIkNfxkdDxb","n":"Shedding the Mask","d":"dementation","lv":5,"cost":"None","pool":"N/A","dur":"As power augmented.","act":"Passive","sum":"A Malkavian is one part of a greater hole, and same can be said for other users of Dementation. With the Voice of Many, a Malkavian can amplify their voice to be able to carry terrible power.","fx":"Dementation of the user is now more powerful and counts its margins as greater by 2 for the purposes of extending the effect.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"68"}},"QvagF67uSWgXXlis":{"id":"QvagF67uSWgXXlis","n":"Draugh of Elegance","d":"celerity","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One night; for vampires,until the next feeding or the vampire reaches Hunger 5","act":"Full","sum":"The Blood of the vampire becomes saturated with the power of Celerity, conveying a part of that power to anyone who drinks of it.","fx":"The drinker gains the same non-Amalgam powers as the donor’s, up to that level.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"45"}},"Qy2ZfDeLQpfrxykt":{"id":"Qy2ZfDeLQpfrxykt","n":"Fist of Caine","d":"potence","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene","act":"Free","pre":"Lethal Body","sum":"The vampire’s bare hands can inflict grievous injuries, lethal to both mortals and other vampires. They can dismember, pierce, impale, decapitate, and even rip a heart out of the chest.","fx":"For one scene the user can inflict Aggravated Health damage to mortals and supernaturals alike while Brawling, as they literally rend flesh and tear their opponents limb from limb with their bare hands.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"119"},"prer":["Lethal Body"]},"R6lpmyMrTAjKHhW1":{"id":"R6lpmyMrTAjKHhW1","n":"Earth’s Perseverance","d":"fortitude","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One Scene","act":"Free","sum":"A vampire with this power is almost impossible to move when it is active. The vampire draws upon the strength of the earth, grounding themselves and drawing upon its permanence to keep them rooted in place.","fx":"When this power is activated, the only way the vampire moves is if they choose to do so independently.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"80"}},"RGaXZegfaVIe0SO6":{"id":"RGaXZegfaVIe0SO6","n":"Far Reach","d":"alchemy","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Alchemy vs Strength + Athletics","dur":"One turn unless held (see above).","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, choleric human blood, melted nylon fibers or a grated refrigerator magnet or weird nootropics ordered off the internet","sum":"This formula allows the alchemist to use their mind to grab, hold, and push objects or people without touching them.","fx":"The alchemist can lift, push, or pull a physical object or person under 100 kg, within their sight and closer than 10 meters.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition Corebook","page":"284"}},"RP8iy9nkzaKFF1Ll":{"id":"RP8iy9nkzaKFF1Ll","n":"Prowess","d":"potence","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene","act":"Free","sum":"Vampires with Potence gain far greater strength from their Blood than those who lack it.","fx":"When activated, add the Potence rating of the user to their unarmed damage value as well as to feats of Strength, and add half their Potence rating (round up) to their Melee and thrown weapon damage","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"117"}},"RZtlej2QwmsmBcUb":{"id":"RZtlej2QwmsmBcUb","n":"Ignis Fatuus","d":"chimerstry","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check, one Willpower point","pool":"Manipulation + Subterfuge","dur":"The illusion remains until the vampire chooses to end the illusion or can no longer sense it.","act":"Minor of -2 dice","sum":"The vampire can create simple static illusions that can confound a single sense.","fx":"On a Win, The vampire can create illusions that affect a single sense in an area of roughly 7 cubic meters per dot the vampire has in Chimerstry, and the vampire must be able to sense the area in which they create the illusion.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"48"}},"RdBft4OKExkLvndY":{"id":"RdBft4OKExkLvndY","n":"Rumor","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Alchemy vs Wits + Awareness","dur":"One scene, and thereafter until something (or someone) persuasively contradicts the target’s agreement (“I would never have agreed to that! I must have been drugged!”).","ing":"The alchemist’s blood, phlegmatic blood, pepper, oil, and graphite or mercury.","sum":"Alchemists frequently use this formula during negotiations to try and sway at least one person to their side; however, it can be easy to spot if anyone is paying close enough attention.","fx":"To get the target to actually act on their agreement (e.g., sign investment papers) usually requires a further Manipulation + Subterfuge (or similar) contest, but the alchemist can add…","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade Players Guide","page":"105"}},"RtR9sI8ABr9IPTYo":{"id":"RtR9sI8ABr9IPTYo","n":"Haruspex","d":"auspex","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Occult","dur":"One night","act":"Full","pre":"Premonition","sum":"Certain oracles, mystics, and necromancers maintain that in those final, fleeting moments before death claims another soul, the dying consciousness opens up to the secrets of the cosmos and witnesses the infinite.","fx":"Characters gain a one-die bonus if they killed the victim themselves, or two dice if they’re killed while undergoing the scrying process (such a torturous death likely grants Stains).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"29"},"prer":["Premonition"]},"S1rkxEpFY2GGpEOt":{"id":"S1rkxEpFY2GGpEOt","n":"Irresistable Voice","d":"presence","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Mnipulation + Insight vs. Composure + Resolve test","dur":"One Scene","act":"Full","am":"Dominate 1","sum":"The Presence of the user becomes a conduit for Dominate. The vampire now only needs their voice to be heard in order to employ Dominate powers.","fx":"The user must touch the subject and win a Manipulation + Presence vs Composure + Resolve test for the power to take effect.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"124"},"amr":[{"k":"dominate","l":1}]},"S9flW9NBm4MFpZM1":{"id":"S9flW9NBm4MFpZM1","n":"Dread Gaze","d":"presence","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Charisma + Intimidation vs. Composure + Resolve.","dur":"One turn/as normal Frenzy","act":"Full","sum":"Briefly exposing their vampiric nature, the user instills a single subject with utter terror.","fx":"Displaying their fangs, their face twisted in a predatory grimace, the user rolls a contest of Charisma + Intimidation against their target’s Composure + Resolve.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"122"}},"SCRoxk6dqfbWki4i":{"id":"SCRoxk6dqfbWki4i","n":"Morphean Blow","d":"valerenwarrior","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check, one Willpower point","pool":"Composure + Resolve vs. Composure + Resolve","dur":"8 hours or until the subject is awakened","act":"Full","sum":"Healers use sleep to accelerate the healing process. Warriors use sleep to incapacitate enraged foes.","fx":"The target is forced into sleep from which they awaken if they take a point of health damage.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"191"}},"SLc1666mACrdabmF":{"id":"SLc1666mACrdabmF","n":"Spirit’s Touch","d":"auspex","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Insight","dur":"One turn.","act":"Full","sum":"By touching an inanimate object or the ground at a location, the vampire can sense the emotional residue left by those who have handled that object or visited the location in the past.","fx":"Each point of margin on the roll allows the user to sense roughly one additional previous handler (description, name, type of a creature) and set of circumstances, counting backwards from the most recent.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"34"}},"STIGl7Kxl3niuB1K":{"id":"STIGl7Kxl3niuB1K","n":"Vanish","d":"obfuscate","lv":4,"cost":"As per power augmented","pool":"Wits + Subterfuge vs. Wits + Awareness","dur":"As per power augmented","act":"Passive","sum":"The vampire can activate powers like Cloak of Shadows, Cache and Unseen Passage even while under direct observation.","fx":"This power can only be used once per scene.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"104"}},"Si8WPLueR6KmyASS":{"id":"Si8WPLueR6KmyASS","n":"Tracing the Blood","d":"animalism","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Awareness","dur":"One scene","act":"Free","pre":"Sense the Beast","sum":"Though their deep connection to the Beast, the vampire understands when other vampires call upon their Blood.","fx":"Results are based on the margin of success, and all targets must be within their sensory range.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"17"},"prer":["Sense the Beast"]},"SqeYe3nw5JK0CEXy":{"id":"SqeYe3nw5JK0CEXy","n":"Ensconce","d":"obfuscate","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"See general rules for Obfuscate","dur":"One scene or ended by the user.","act":"Free","sum":"The vampire is able to supernaturally conceal small objects in their hands or on their person. The power doesn’t make visible objects invisible. Rather, it makes a searcher ignore them when they’d otherwise notice.","fx":"The vampire can hide a number of small, hand-held objects in their hands or on their person equal to their Obfuscate rating.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"96"}},"SrCpIA2zXZPt6k4L":{"id":"SrCpIA2zXZPt6k4L","n":"Summon","d":"presence","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Charisma + Subterfuge vs. Composure + Intelligence","dur":"One night plus one per point of margin","act":"Full","sum":"The vampire can call to themselves any person, mortal or vampire, upon whom they’ve previously used Awe, Entrancement, or Majesty, or who has tasted their Blood at least once.","fx":"The target hears the summoning, but may or may not heed it.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"125"}},"TC0k8RpLQgQLgJXN":{"id":"TC0k8RpLQgQLgJXN","n":"Chain of Command","d":"dominate","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until the command is carried out or the scene ends, whichever comes first","act":"Passive","pre":"Mesmerise","sum":"Those laboring under the will of the vampire drag others along with their actions, demanding help and obedience with a will fueled by their master.","fx":"After delivering a Mesmerize command, the vampire can choose to invoke this power by immediately making another Rouse Check.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"72"},"prer":["Mesmerise"]},"TIR8kEnS69tKgZQm":{"id":"TIR8kEnS69tKgZQm","n":"Predator’s Lure","d":"presence","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Charisma + Subterfuge vs. Composure + Resolve","dur":"One scene or until they are within 10 feet (3 meters) of the user.","act":"Minor -2","sum":"The vampire uses their Presence to lure a victim closer, whether for conversation or for bloodier purposes.","fx":"Against supernatural creatures, the user must win a test of Charisma + Subterfuge vs. the victim’s Composure + Resolve.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"122"}},"TJLaXdBIwdu2k3cq":{"id":"TJLaXdBIwdu2k3cq","n":"Madrigral","d":"melpominee","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Charisma + Performance vs. Composure + Wits","dur":"One night.","act":"Full","sum":"Power of words and suggestions is well understood by even those new to Mepominee. By weaving words with emotions and things that alter someone’s mental state, the vampire can twist others around their little finger.","fx":"The target must hear at least one full sentence from the vampire for this power to properly work. The vampire rolls Charisma + Performance vs. the target’s Composure + Wits.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"86"}},"TQsOAsyBCAOhvW1v":{"id":"TQsOAsyBCAOhvW1v","n":"Lullaby Of the Damned","d":"valerenwatcher","lv":2,"cost":"Resolve + Subterfuge vs. Wits + Awareness","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene unless the humming stops before that.","act":"Free","sum":"By humming a mystic tune, the vampire conceals their presence from spirits that would otherwise be immune to the mind-altering effects of Disciplines such as obfuscate.","fx":"A vampire drawing too much attention to themselves must roll Resolve + Subterfuge at a difficulty of 3 again and any malign entities nearby may roll theirs again.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"196"}},"TTTshfqUGYOPXsZx":{"id":"TTTshfqUGYOPXsZx","n":"Short Circuit","d":"alchemy","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"N/A","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, battery acid, melancholy blood, and salt water.","sum":"An alchemist can use this formula to overload the batteries in any electronic or electrical equipment, including car batteries or the fuses of a building.","fx":"This allows an alchemist to, for example, cause a blackout of an entire building by touching a power outlet, or a car by brushing against its body.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade Players Guide","page":"105"}},"TX16TBrDBG7i18ed":{"id":"TX16TBrDBG7i18ed","n":"Fluid Tardiness","d":"temporis","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"Users of Temporis often feel around them that the world is just too slow, even when they are not actively focusing on manipulating time.","fx":"Whenever the vampire uses a Blood Surge to augment a Dexterity or Temporis test, they may reroll the Rouse Check.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"167"}},"TdawSe560UhDzd8q":{"id":"TdawSe560UhDzd8q","n":"Voice of Orpheus","d":"melpominee","lv":2,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","am":"Mortis 1 (or some other school of sorcery with necromantic Paths at 1 dot)","sum":"With this rare ability of a rare Discipline, the user may now affect those who dwell in the Lands of the Dead with their voice.","fx":"The user’s voice penetrates the Shroud with ease, being able to affect denizens of the Shadowland and its visitors from the land of the living.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"87"},"amr":[{"k":"school:mortis","l":1},{"k":"path:necromancy","l":1}]},"TeqiS7j4XcLgW48g":{"id":"TeqiS7j4XcLgW48g","n":"Imposter’s Guise","d":"obfuscate","lv":5,"cost":"Free","pool":"M/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","pre":"Mask of a Thousand Faces","sum":"With some preparation the vampire can make themselves appear exactly as a specific individual of any build and gender when using Mask of One Thousand Faces.","fx":"The user must study the face to be copied for at least five minutes, from different angles.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"105"},"prer":["Mask of a Thousand Faces"]},"ThlHm13Euxua98ll":{"id":"ThlHm13Euxua98ll","n":"Flight (•••••)","d":"flight","lv":5,"sum":"The user can fly up to 75 miles per hour/120 km per hour and carry up to 200 lbs./100 kg, if their Strength allows for it.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"78"}},"Tx3qogGeyImpkEyY":{"id":"Tx3qogGeyImpkEyY","n":"Changeling Ward","d":"mytherceria","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Subterfuge vs. Wits + Resolve","dur":"The ward lasts for a duration indicated by the number of margins on the vampire’s roll.","act":"Full","sum":"Externalising their emotional confusion, the vampire creates a ward that disorients and befuddles anyone who sees it. They can inscribe such a ward on an object, a location, or a person.","fx":"The size of the ward is one meter across for an object or 3 meter radius for a warding circle around a location.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"92"}},"U7E5ukOZ7ChqpfF6":{"id":"U7E5ukOZ7ChqpfF6","n":"Hag’s Wrinkles","d":"thanatosis","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A, Stamina + Subterfuge vs. Wits + Awareness","dur":"Vampires retain the effects until they next awaken while mortals would require some kind surgery or magic to return to a “normal” state.","act":"Free","sum":"Perpetual rot makes the character’s flesh malleable. The Samedi can open large folds in her flesh, storing objects in them like a kangaroo’s pouch.","fx":"The user twists their flesh and rolls Stamina + Subterfuge (Difficulty 2) to create pockets within which they may safely hide items up to a volume of their palm.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"176"}},"UA2WulvKoL2Riv2k":{"id":"UA2WulvKoL2Riv2k","n":"Mercurian Tongue","d":"alchemy","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"One night, or until the alchemist feeds from someone with the same native language as the alchemist.","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, blood of a mortal who speaks a different native language than the alchemist, the tongue of a fish or bird, hot sauce from another country, and copper filings.","sum":"The alchemist can speak the native language of the mortal whose blood they used in the formula, and the native languages of those they feed from until they next sleep.","fx":"The alchemist can speak the native language of the mortal whose blood they used in the formula.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade Players Guide","page":"103"}},"ULwlBCWchJtxh5r5":{"id":"ULwlBCWchJtxh5r5","n":"Shadow Perspective","d":"obtenebration","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until ended","act":"Full","sum":"The vampire can project their senses into any shadow within line of sight, seeing and hearing as if they were hiding within any part of it. This includes their own shadow, as manipulated by Shadow Cast.","fx":"Following a Rouse Check, the presence of the vampire’s senses in the shadow is undetectable by anything but supernatural means.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"111"}},"UN8MW0dh7fOGZqWJ":{"id":"UN8MW0dh7fOGZqWJ","n":"Peacemaker","d":"valerenwatcher","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check, one Willpower point","pool":"Road rating vs. Willpower","dur":"One turn per user’s Road rating","act":"Full","sum":"Watchers are arbiters and negotiators, dealing with hostile supernatural beings on behalf of all Cainites. Keeping the peace is paramount.","fx":"The aura lasts for as many turns as they have dots in their Road rating or until they leaves the area, though once used, tempers rarely surge again.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"198"}},"UR58Gh4CQNdCPbpl":{"id":"UR58Gh4CQNdCPbpl","n":"Taking the Pain","d":"valerenhealer","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Medicine","dur":"One scene. A Critical Win or 3+ margins extends it to the rest of the night","act":"Minor -2","sum":"The user alters the target’s perception of pain, soothing their wounds.","fx":"The user touches the target and rolls Intelligence + Medicine (Difficulty 2).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"185"}},"UW6EKlyGDoibCdN3":{"id":"UW6EKlyGDoibCdN3","n":"Exile the Spawn of Typhon","d":"bardo","lv":3,"cost":"Free","pool":"Resolve + Intimidation","dur":"One scene.","act":"Full cover before them.","sum":"It was Typhon, the master of Set who had cast the curse of bloodlust upon Osiris and created the entire race of bloodleeches.","fx":"The user must have the target within their line of sight within 10 meters for this power to work, rolling Resolve + Intimidation against their target’s Composure + Resolve.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"39"}},"UdAtyhH3FYbKaMUY":{"id":"UdAtyhH3FYbKaMUY","n":"Sense With Beasts","d":"auspex","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve+ Awareness","dur":"One scene, although it can be extended by an additional scene by spending a point of Willpower","act":"Minor of -2 dice","am":"Animalism •","sum":"Beloved by the Tzimisce, the user shares their senses with animals, seeing and hearing as they do. Animalism through it (or on it). The user may hop from one insect to another for free without any additional rolls.","fx":"They may perceive the world through its senses.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"28"},"amr":[{"k":"animalism","l":1}]},"Uiq0KzqiTbxDYCQC":{"id":"Uiq0KzqiTbxDYCQC","n":"Awaken the Zulo Shape","d":"vicissitude","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until the vampire goes to daysleep or ends the power.","act":"Full","sum":"When one considers the primeval forests of Transylvania, the thought demon-haunted often comes to mind.","fx":"The transformation takes one turn to complete, during which the user can only defend using their normal dice pools.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"207"}},"UvqJv6187b325wxo":{"id":"UvqJv6187b325wxo","n":"Blood Sweat","d":"quietussanguinis","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Insight vs. the victim’s Humanity/Road rating","dur":"One action","act":"Full","sum":"The user coaxes the target’s blood to stir and exit the body through pores and orifices.","fx":"The target takes a number of Aggravated Health damage equal to the margins.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"148"}},"UwzEiWsaRPnF7qUp":{"id":"UwzEiWsaRPnF7qUp","n":"Counterfeit (Level 1 Power)","d":"alchemy","lv":2,"sum":"At level 2, the Alchemist can develop formulae that counterfeit level 1 powers of other Disciplines (and Blood Sorcery powers that affect the caster’s own Blood, but never Rituals).","fx":"Use the counterfeited power’s own cost and system, substituting the Alchemist’s Thin-Blood Alchemy rating for the Discipline rating wherever one is called for.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition Corebook","page":"285"}},"V92p3RpfB5drdRfF":{"id":"V92p3RpfB5drdRfF","n":"Heaven’s Gate","d":"valerenhealer","lv":5,"cost":"Three Rouse Checks","pool":"Intelligence + Medicine","dur":"Instant.","act":"Full","sum":"The apex of Valeren involves miraculous healing of body and soul, even reversing death itself.","fx":"This power may only be used on an individual dead less than a week, who did not die of old age and whose soul was not consumed or destroyed in some manner via Necromancy or Warrior Valeren (or similar effects).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"188"}},"VciXQeQ2cqdth1c4":{"id":"VciXQeQ2cqdth1c4","n":"Envelop","d":"alchemy","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Wits + Alchemy vs Stamina + Survival","dur":"Until scene ends or the alchemist ends the effect voluntarily.","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, melancholic and phlegmatic human blood, potassium chlorate, smog or halon gas","sum":"This formula creates a mist that clings to a victim, blinding it and <<2 8 5>> (in the case of mortals) causing suffocation.","fx":"In addition, the alchemist can make the mist suffocate a mortal with a contest of Wits + Alchemy vs. Stamina + Survival.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition Corebook","page":"285"}},"VlVrHzYqNEYW3dpx":{"id":"VlVrHzYqNEYW3dpx","n":"Wear Their Skin","d":"thanatosis","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Stamina + Medicine","dur":"The skin of the target rots after three days even if it was supernaturally preserved, making it useless for the purposes of this power.","act":"Full","sum":"By carefully removing a mortal’s face (or entire skin), the user is able to craft themselves a mask or an entire bodysuit to take the form of the one to whom the skin originally belonged.","fx":"First, the user needs to carve out a facemask an entire bodysuit (Dexterity + Medicine or Crafts against a Difficulty of 3 to craft) from a person.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"179"}},"Vp6nfTPqWtqYuLE1":{"id":"Vp6nfTPqWtqYuLE1","n":"Lightning Strike","d":"celerity","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"A single attack","act":"Free","sum":"Faster than the eye can follow, the vampire can strike with fist or melee weapon at such speed that the opponent is unable to defend or take evasive action.","fx":"An opponent possessing Celerity 5 or Temporis 5 can nullify this power by making their own Rouse Check, defending at the same speed.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"46"}},"VsTmj728hy8YlyjE":{"id":"VsTmj728hy8YlyjE","n":"Walk with Caine","d":"quietussanguinis","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Free","sum":"The Banu Haqim sneer at the Tremere’s ability to thicken the blood, with the Warlocks obviously fooled that somehow the strength of one’s blood gives one authority.","fx":"Diablerising a person with this power counts their normal Generation and Blood Potency Same goes with siring and other such things.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"149"}},"Vxkw9ZGFZBmAPmZO":{"id":"Vxkw9ZGFZBmAPmZO","n":"Blood Forging","d":"quietussanguinis","lv":2,"pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","pre":"Blood Tampering","sum":"Quietus Sanguinis allows for alteration of materials, making sorcerers the experts on creating supernatural items.","fx":"Items enchanted by Blood Tampering can now physically interact with, defend from and and harm spirits even if they are immaterial.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"146"},"prer":["Blood Tampering"]},"W6WkHsoNpxTkVbZs":{"id":"W6WkHsoNpxTkVbZs","n":"Soul Mask","d":"obfuscate","lv":4,"cost":"One Check","pool":"Intelligence + Subterfuge","dur":"One scene","act":"Free","sum":"Princes and ashen priests guarding their courts and cathedrals typically post as guards at least some Cainites with Scry the Soul.","fx":"Failing to reach the added Difficulty lets the reader see only the false personality the user has crafted, without any hint that the reader is being misled.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"103"}},"WGKdoR25Z27mhtp0":{"id":"WGKdoR25Z27mhtp0","n":"Face of Death","d":"thanatosis","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A, Manipulation + Medicine vs. Stamina + Medicine (or Fortitude)","dur":"Vampires retain the effects until they next awaken while mortals would require some kind surgery or magic to return to a “normal” state.","act":"Free, Minor -2 when used against others","sum":"By channeling decay into their body, the user is able to assume the visage of a cadaver to safely hide among the dead – should the need arise.","fx":"The user loses a dot of Dexterity to a minimum of 1 and assumes the visage of a corpse, giving them a dice bonus equal to the user’s Thanatosis rating to a Composure + Subterfuge roll to…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"175"}},"WIL6TWkGL2JniOz1":{"id":"WIL6TWkGL2JniOz1","n":"Investiture of the Blood","d":"daimonion","lv":2,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"The tainted blood of those using Daimonion offers boons in a similar manner as demons to their thralls.","fx":"The vampire gains a number of Arcana (see p. XX for demon systems and powers) dots equal to their Daimonion rating + their Blood Potency.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"54"}},"WTBMRGVI45p67BrP":{"id":"WTBMRGVI45p67BrP","n":"Profane the Holy","d":"daimonion","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Occult","dur":"Until the victim wins the contest or the scene ends","act":"Minor -2 dice","sum":"The vampire creates and weaponises corruption and doubt even in places it did not exist. the victim begins to deteriorate rapidly.","fx":"The vampire looks at a user of True faith or at a holy symbol or a relic and rolls Resolve + Occult vs.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"53"}},"WUDjkM0FgeE703Kr":{"id":"WUDjkM0FgeE703Kr","n":"Mastery over the Blood","d":"quietussanguinis","lv":5,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"The user coaxes the target’s blood to stir and exit the body through pores and orifices.","fx":"Upon purchasing this power, the user acquires Taste of the Soul, Taste of the Body and Taste of the Mind and their bonuses are increased to two dice (which scales with power bonus as normal).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"148"}},"WYl5hBMnj59Govia":{"id":"WYl5hBMnj59Govia","n":"Crash Down","d":"potence","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Strength + Athletics","dur":"One use/turn","act":"Full","pre":"Soaring Leap","sum":"Their strength an elemental force, the vampire can slam their fist or foot into the ground, creating a shockwave that throws their opponents prone.","fx":"Upon using Soaring Leap, the vampire may activate Crash Down, and deal damage to a small area of effect.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"118"},"prer":["Soaring Leap"]},"WbnDfit31YhPcU7g":{"id":"WbnDfit31YhPcU7g","n":"Unerring Aim","d":"celerity","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"A single attack","act":"Free","am":"Auspex 2","sum":"The world around them slowing to a crawl, the vampire can aim and throw or fire any weapon at a target as if the target were stationary.","fx":"An opponent possessing Celerity 5 can nullify this powerby making their own Rouse Check, defending at the same speed.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"45"},"amr":[{"k":"auspex","l":2}]},"WbpVliMWYvCApeuu":{"id":"WbpVliMWYvCApeuu","n":"Necrotic Mastery","d":"thanatosis","lv":5,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","pre":"Putrefaction","sum":"By reaching the pinnacle of Thanatosis, the user becomes a master of necrotic energies, allowing them to lay waste on entire populations with ease.","fx":"Putrefaction now lasts for the rest of the scene or until ended, whichever comes first.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"181"},"prer":["Putrefaction"]},"WdHVbiKLsryqgGgF":{"id":"WdHVbiKLsryqgGgF","n":"Wolf’s Lament","d":"obfuscate","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse check","pool":"See general rules for Obfuscate","dur":"Until the wolves stop howling, which could take an entire night.","act":"Free","am":"Animalism ••","pre":"Feral Speech (Animalism ••)","sum":"The wolf’s howl echoes across the land, carrying messages in its mournful song. Nosferatu and Gangrel with this Amalgam may do the same, enabling them to howl messages that carry for miles.","fx":"Prior to using this power, the player must convey their intended message to the Storyteller and receive approval.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"99"},"amr":[{"k":"animalism","l":2}],"prer":["Feral Speech"]},"Wl0awqOcRr8Ycqfv":{"id":"Wl0awqOcRr8Ycqfv","n":"Intangible Vessel","d":"mytherceria","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene or until intentionally ended.","act":"Full","sum":"The vampire can cause a nearby object to temporarily lose its tangibility for mortals and supernaturals, making it untouchable for anyone other than the vampire and those they desire to touch it.","fx":"Only the user and those they allow can touch this object. Other beings — mortal, animal or supernatural — cannot interact with it, as they seem to go straight through it.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"91"}},"WrXhOU2lkOH6MUyX":{"id":"WrXhOU2lkOH6MUyX","n":"Defy Bane","d":"fortitude","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Wits + Survival (to activate reflexively)","dur":"One scene or until expired, whichever comes first.","act":"Free","sum":"By preparing themselves with an expenditure of power, the vampire can make themselves temporarily resistant to fire and sunlight as well as other grievous wounds that would threaten them with Final Death.","fx":"The user can convert a number of Aggravated damage equal to their Fortitude rating to Superficial damage when sustained.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"81"}},"WytUW3md48A96VR9":{"id":"WytUW3md48A96VR9","n":"Ghost’s Passing","d":"obfuscate","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"See general rules for Obfuscate","dur":"One session","act":"Full","am":"Animalism •","sum":"The vampire can bestow a measure of subtlety to the animals under their influence, masking their steps from mundane methods of tracking.","fx":"They are also more subtle, and have a two-dice bonus to most Stealth tests.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"98"},"amr":[{"k":"animalism","l":1}]},"X9mrZFblhFOtpwDW":{"id":"X9mrZFblhFOtpwDW","n":"Shadow Play","d":"obtenebration","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene","act":"Free","sum":"While this ability does not allow characters to create shadows that do not already exist, it allows one to manipulate, move, and animate ambient shadows.","fx":"The user adds one die to a character’s Intimidation and Stealth dice pools for the remainder of the scene.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"107"}},"XSqojhShBp2g0m5a":{"id":"XSqojhShBp2g0m5a","n":"Fortify the Inner Facade","d":"fortitude","lv":3,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive, but it can be dropped by the user.","act":"Free","am":"Auspex •","sum":"Instead of hardening the vampire’s physical frame, this power allows the user to protect their thoughts and emotions from supernatural prying.","fx":"Increases the Difficulty of using Scry Soul (Auspex 3), Telepathy (Auspex 5), and similar mind-reading or emotion-perceiving powers on the user by half their Fortitude rating (round up).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"82"},"amr":[{"k":"auspex","l":1}]},"Xk1Pl6Bi3dDxjv37":{"id":"Xk1Pl6Bi3dDxjv37","n":"Cleansed in Blood","d":"quietussanguinis","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Occult","dur":"Instant.","act":"See below","sum":"By using the power of vitae to cleanse and restore, the vampire releases their blood, allowing it to wash over another and carry away spiritual impurities from outside influences.","fx":"The character baptizes the forehead of the intended subject with their Blood, then places their hands on the subject’s head.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"147"}},"XmTCIpDOIR9xa1gP":{"id":"XmTCIpDOIR9xa1gP","n":"Brutal Feed","d":"potence","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One feeding/turn","act":"Free","sum":"Known as the “Savage Kiss”, this power allows the user to employ an unholy inner strength when draining a victim. In mere seconds, the attacker swallows torrents of blood while mauling the victim.","fx":"The vampire can drain a human completely in seconds, usually within a single turn.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"117"}},"Xrj5OZDFcu5GuXqi":{"id":"Xrj5OZDFcu5GuXqi","n":"Clio’s Kiss","d":"temporis","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Stamina + Occult","dur":"See system","act":"Free","pre":"Rewind","sum":"Named for the muse of history, Clio’s Kiss circumvents the tides of time by projecting a vampire into the past, allowing her to retrieve something (or someone) to be carried forth to the present.","fx":"The user rolls Stamina + Occult at a Difficulty of 2 with margins determining the length of time that a character may project back just like with Rewind.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"173"},"prer":["Rewind"]},"Y1OuY0sMj4RBZHNd":{"id":"Y1OuY0sMj4RBZHNd","n":"See with Lies","d":"chimerstry","lv":5,"cost":"One point of Willpower","pool":"N/A","dur":"Spreading your senses through an illusion lasts for a scene per point of Willpower spent with three Willpower points being enough to cover the entire night.","act":"Concentration counts as a Full Action","sum":"See with Lies allows the user of Chimerstry to extend their own senses through their illusions, possibly giving them the ability to permanently control them from afar if used correctly or craft illusions like birds through which they may soar into the sky and see with.","fx":"The user may choose to sense as their illusions do, feeling, hearing and viewing eveything from their perspective by spending a point of Willpower.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"51"}},"Y8gFJbD6SJ6MIZQS":{"id":"Y8gFJbD6SJ6MIZQS","n":"Father’s Judgment","d":"valerenhealer","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Occult vs. Composure + Resolve","dur":"One scene","act":"Full","sum":"The Blood is Caine’s gift. The Salubri pronounce judgment on those who misuse it.","fx":"The target counts their Hunger as higher by the number equal to the margin for the purposes of activation but not for the purposes of Hunger Dice.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"188"}},"YPUZjizwutcxus6H":{"id":"YPUZjizwutcxus6H","n":"Unweave","d":"temporis","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Dexterity + Athletics or Melee","dur":"One scene unless ended sooner by the user.","act":"Free","sum":"The user is able to push their senses of time even further, now able to actively manipulate their own sense of time as they perceive the world even more slowly, allowing them to parry the attacks with ease.","fx":"The user does not suffer diminishing dice pools when defending against multiple ranged attacks using Dexterity + Athletics, able to quite literally see arrows and bullets fly past at them.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"169"}},"YWYvnkwEUKvL2rc1":{"id":"YWYvnkwEUKvL2rc1","n":"Blissful Gaze","d":"valerenhealer","lv":5,"cost":"One Willpower point in addition to standard power cost","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"The mere presence of a Salubri Healer heralds victory. To those within her gaze, wounds knit themselves together, and even a steel kiss tastes sweet.","fx":"This power enhances Valeren powers of every Path.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"188"}},"Yg2e9YJyRVf4E4VG":{"id":"Yg2e9YJyRVf4E4VG","n":"Sculpt the Flowing Wound","d":"fortitude","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive/See System.","act":"Passive","am":"Vicissitude ••","sum":"Common among Tzimisce knights, a vampire with this power may vastly accelerate their healing by concentrating and willing flesh to mold back to its original form.","fx":"The vampire activates this power as they would Mending and heals a number of Superficial Health damage equal to their Blood Surge value.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"81"},"amr":[{"k":"vicissitude","l":2}]},"Yi7IaDSqhQ0chKYT":{"id":"Yi7IaDSqhQ0chKYT","n":"Slow Walker","d":"temporis","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One turn","act":"Free","sum":"Like a Celerity user, the adept of Temporis is able to, in the eyes of those who do not possess Celerity or Temporis, seemingly teleport from one location to the other.","fx":"The vampire moves towards a target, covering any distance under 10 × their Temporis rating in meters while still having enough time to perform an action, such as an attack, during the turn.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"170"}},"YuE4vlCqqzJUXjcJ":{"id":"YuE4vlCqqzJUXjcJ","n":"Scorpion’s Curse","d":"quietussanguinis","lv":2,"cost":"Free, blood required is neglible","pool":"Wits + Awareness","dur":"Weeks equal to the Quietus rating. Weeks turn to months on a Critical win or if the sorcerer scores at least 3 margins on the test.","act":"5 minutes, Full","sum":"Unlike the warriors, the variant of the Scorpion’s Touch among sorcerers can last for days and act as a ward, preventing unwanted visitors and theft.","fx":"The “Ward” can only cover the space of about a meter across and only lasts for a number of days equal to the caster’s Quietus rating due to the transmuted poison vitae losing power (as this is not real sorcery).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"146"}},"YvXtxfKQFX8Ay0E2":{"id":"YvXtxfKQFX8Ay0E2","n":"Grace of the Passed","d":"valerenwarrior","lv":3,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive/the Skills and Specialties last for a number of days equal to the margins, but the user may only “hold” up to the Skills of a single person at a time.","act":"Passive","pre":"Ending the Watch","sum":"A more utilitarian enhancement to Ending the Watch, it allows the user to syphon the memories and experiences of the subject.","fx":"Ending the Watch now allows you to swap a number of Skills equal to margins with the victim, up to the user’s rating in Warrior Valeren.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"192"},"prer":["Ending the Watch"]},"YwAJfpHnI7ybEx3E":{"id":"YwAJfpHnI7ybEx3E","n":"Cat’s Grace","d":"celerity","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"The vampire gains a balance and grace equal to and surpassing world-class trapeze artists. They can walk and even run across ledges and wires effortlessly and can keep their balance on the slimmest of supports.","fx":"Note that this power does not allow them to balance on support that cannot take their weight.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"42"}},"Z9WitTHwpeJ3Pmo0":{"id":"Z9WitTHwpeJ3Pmo0","n":"Feral Weapons","d":"protean","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until the vampire falls to sleep or torpor or ends the power","act":"Free","sum":"The vampire can extend their natural weapons to monstrous proportions.","fx":"When activated, the vampire adds a +2 modifier to their Brawl damage, and causes Aggravated Health damage to mortals.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"128"}},"ZI5UcW3r3PaSKEcb":{"id":"ZI5UcW3r3PaSKEcb","n":"Fluent Strength","d":"potence","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"The vampire is able to call upon their supernatural strength effortlessly, and rarely tempt their Hunger when doing so.","fx":"Whenever the vampire uses a Blood Surge to augment a Strength or Potence test, they may reroll the Rouse Check.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"116"}},"ZIgYLpTgh52KD95A":{"id":"ZIgYLpTgh52KD95A","n":"Mosh Pit","d":"melpominee","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Charisma + Performance vs. Composure + Wits","dur":"Until the frenzy ends. The Resonance changes back once the effect ends as well.","act":"Full","sum":"With but a syllable, the vampire’s voice enflames all the humours of rage within a person, turning them into a violent beast.","fx":"The target’s Resonance is changed at choleric and, if they are a vampire or another creature with the vampiric Beast, they must make a fury frenzy test against a difficulty of 3.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"86"}},"ZWrmiihIOoQEK0bw":{"id":"ZWrmiihIOoQEK0bw","n":"Apep’s Venom","d":"serpentis","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until the victim is healed, resists, or dies.","act":"Free","sum":"While later levels of Serpentis promise great forms of ancient god-like entities, huge cobras of shadow or half-human half-snake creatures tend to make people run away as fast as they can.","fx":"The vampire’s fangs become hollow, more slender and venomous. The user does not suffer a Called Shot penalty to bite attacks.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"152"}},"ZZ2SEY9o5dY51Wiv":{"id":"ZZ2SEY9o5dY51Wiv","n":"Fireskin","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"One scene","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, powdered elemental salamander bone, tobacco, sulfur.","sum":"Originally created to safely superheat Athanor Corporis, the Fireskin formula allows Kindred — and mortals brave enough to gulp it down — to literally plunge into fire without fear.","fx":"They do +1 fire damage when they strike with their body (only the additional damage counts as fire), and can increase that to +2 if they manage to grapple someone.","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"76"}},"ZwQAgDpFr12WK2iE":{"id":"ZwQAgDpFr12WK2iE","n":"Reveal Temperament","d":"auspex","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Insight vs. Composire vs. Subterfuge","dur":"One scene","act":"Full","sum":"The vampire can smell the Resonance of the target, as well as any Dyscrasia they harbor in their blood. They can also smell if another vampire has recently fed as well as the Resonance (if any) of their latest victim.","fx":"When the power is active the user can test Intelligence + Insight vs a target’s Composure + Subterfuge.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"25"}},"Zy2s0CyZat8EMK3Z":{"id":"Zy2s0CyZat8EMK3Z","n":"Flight (••••)","d":"flight","lv":4,"sum":"The user can fly up to 60 miles per hour/90 km per hour and carry up to 100 lbs./50 kg, if their Strength allows for it.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"78"}},"a22KBXhU7gQWYCk6":{"id":"a22KBXhU7gQWYCk6","n":"Echo of the Subtle Vizier","d":"obtenebration","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check in addition to the Dominate power used","pool":"N/A","dur":"One hour per success on the power activation roll.","act":"Passive","am":"Dominate ••","sum":"A Lasombra with this power may silently whisper commands to a target’s shadow without ever making a sound.","fx":"The vampire must see the target’s shadow as they activate a Dominate power, suspending it by one hour for each success rolled.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"108"},"amr":[{"k":"dominate","l":2}]},"aAZAhHbTDuFJ4fPB":{"id":"aAZAhHbTDuFJ4fPB","n":"Condemnation","d":"daimonion","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Occult vs. Composure + Occult","dur":"Unless the victim breaks the curse, it lasts until the vampire lifts it by simply willing it according to the table below. A critical win doubles the duration. Only one trait curse may be active at a time and recasting the power removes the previous one if it scores more successes.","act":"Full","sum":"The Children of Baal relish the opportunity to importune dark energies into the waking world.","fx":"The victim must be in the line of sight (magical or physical) and the curser must know the victim’s name (or a celestial name, for a demon).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"55"}},"aCQuwRW59JN9WQqh":{"id":"aCQuwRW59JN9WQqh","n":"Moment of Clarity","d":"alchemy","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"One scene","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, phlegmatic blood, cadmium, nootropics, and ash from burned pages of a meaningful text to the alchemist (scripture, favorite childhood novel).","sum":"The alchemist is able to temporarily submerge their vampiric instincts, harnessing the power of the Beast to support, rather than disturb, their mental acumen.","fx":"Upon activation, the alchemist gains mental clarity, their wits sharpen, and the Beast is temporarily sated.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade Players Guide","page":"106"}},"adEQVNCGLbGKu2XT":{"id":"adEQVNCGLbGKu2XT","n":"Grandest Trick","d":"mytherceria","lv":5,"cost":"Two Rouse Checks","pool":"Resolve + Insight","dur":"Until the following night.","act":"Free","sum":"After draining all the life from a mortal, the vampire gets the grand power to mimic aspects of mortality until the next night whilst maintaining their ability to use their Mytherceria discipline powers at the cost of draining their willpower.","fx":"They heal like a mortal, take damage like a mortal, feel, taste and digest things like a mortal and, most importantly, sun does not damage them.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"95"}},"aj4J3kXjMLWOl2u6":{"id":"aj4J3kXjMLWOl2u6","n":"Creeping Infection","d":"thanatosis","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Medicine vs. Stamina + Medicine (or Fortitude)","dur":"One scene unless ended sooner by the user. The ailment persists in mortals until they are fed at least one Rouse Check’s worth of vitae or are healed through advanced medicine or miraculous means.","act":"Full","sum":"Users of Thanatosis are able to concoct new ailments to devastate their foes with ease and their breath alone is capable of decimating entire groups of mortals.+","fx":"Those within a radius equal to twice the user’s Thanatosis rating may roll Stamina + Medicine (or Fortitude, if they possess it) to resist their effects.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"179"}},"ajNh8UaDONOmtDOG":{"id":"ajNh8UaDONOmtDOG","n":"Co-Walker","d":"temporis","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One action","act":"Free","sum":"By seeing cracks through time and space, the user of Temporis is able to, at least for a second, be in two places at the same time.","fx":"After making a Rouse Check, the user is able to do two physical actions in the same turn, appearing as if in multiple places at the same time.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"170"}},"axh2JmJOepFMNowy":{"id":"axh2JmJOepFMNowy","n":"Forgetful Mind","d":"dominate","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Subterfuge vs. Intelligence + Resolve","dur":"Indefinitely","act":"Full","sum":"The vampire can rewrite whole swathes of the victim’s memories, as long as they can keep the victim’s gaze and full, uninterrupted attention.","fx":"Each point of margin allows the user to add or remove an Additional memory. The victim recalls the edits vaguely, foggy ideations that can fall apart under close questioning.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"72"}},"b0kXDqjFH7Ie2ew8":{"id":"b0kXDqjFH7Ie2ew8","n":"Inside the Hourglass","d":"temporis","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene or until ended","act":"Free","sum":"Though still unable to stop time or reverse it in a greater state, the user of Temporis with this power is able to slow down their perception just enough to be able to properly respond and react to everyone’s actions,…","fx":"Activating this power requires one Rouse Check and extending it requires an additional Check for each turn it is kept active.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"170"}},"b1mX0LXy7mjQ38Cc":{"id":"b1mX0LXy7mjQ38Cc","n":"Bleed Out","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"cost":"Free","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, Melancholic human blood, diuretics, energy drinks, cornflower","sum":"Hunting down and subduing a victim poses significant risk for the Duskborn, and they take their unlives into their own hands with each hunt they embark upon.","fx":"On a total failure, their blood turns septic and can feed nobody. On a win, victims choke and drown on their own blood over an agonizing hour.","src":{"book":"Tattered Façade","page":"107"}},"b4OroSvLA1UuklrU":{"id":"b4OroSvLA1UuklrU","n":"Whence All Comes","d":"thanatosis","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Medicine","dur":"Variable (see system)","act":"Minor -2","sum":"Disposal of corpses is a useful trick of the Cappadocians that Troglodytia taught her children, allowing them to live on even after the purge of the Cappadocians by acting as cleaning crews for hire.","fx":"On a Win, the body begins to dissolve into ash over the course of the next 5 turns with each additional margin reducing the time it takes to dissolve by a turn with at least 5 margins or a Critical Win dissolving the body instantly.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"176"}},"b7aEh1F57LpzQMhQ":{"id":"b7aEh1F57LpzQMhQ","n":"Blissful Slumber","d":"protean","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until ended by the user or the user wakes from Torpor, otherwise until sunset","act":"Full","sum":"Not all vampires who wander rest beneath the earth. vampires using this power can assume the appearance of true death, even appearing to withstand sunlight while in such a state.","fx":"While so transformed, the vampire cannot move or physically communicate, but retains enough of their senses to understand what is happening around them.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"129"}},"b83cqL0oezWOkEbM":{"id":"b83cqL0oezWOkEbM","n":"Ancestral Dominion","d":"dominate","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Intimidation vs. Resolve + Occult","dur":"Until the command is carried out or the scene ends, whichever comes first.","act":"Passive with Mesmerise","pre":"Mesmerise","sum":"Vampires of great age and potency find it possible to exert their will via the Blood, without the traditional need for eye contact and verbal communication with their target.","fx":"For every Generation separating the user of this power from their target, the resisting vampire gains an additional die to their roll.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"74"},"prer":["Mesmerise"]},"bTEo5EqGAw8IvYoz":{"id":"bTEo5EqGAw8IvYoz","n":"Haze","d":"alchemy","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"One scene or until voluntarily ended.","ing":"In addition to the alchemist’s Blood and phlegmatic human blood, dry ice or cigar smoke or auto exhaust","sum":"This formula creates a field of mist that follows the user, rendering them more difficult to target with ranged weapons and concealing their identity.","fx":"Anyone attempting to identify the user or hit them with ranged weapons suffers a two-dice penalty to their pool.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition Corebook","page":"285"}},"bzHqHo9owfQtkxYD":{"id":"bzHqHo9owfQtkxYD","n":"Invigorating Display","d":"presence","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Charisma + Performanc","dur":"One scene","act":"Full","pre":"Awe","sum":"After working an audience into a state of blissful euphoria, the vampire inhales the energy of the crowd, taking a fragment of their collective energy deep into their dead lungs to experience its unique Resonance.","fx":"The vampire spends a scene entertaining a crowd of mortals (a minimum of ten people are required), Rousing the Blood and making a Charisma + Performance test against Difficulty 3…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"123"},"prer":["Awe"]},"c2Bv2YmQMC6Bc4zx":{"id":"c2Bv2YmQMC6Bc4zx","n":"Erode","d":"quietuscruciatus","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Composure + Resolve","dur":"One night","act":"Full","sum":"By touching their victim, the user turns the target’s own blood against them and causes their body to rapidly fail in strength, potentially leading to death.","fx":"(Those with Fortitude may resist with Stamina + Fortitude). On a win, the victim loses two dots in their Strength, Dexterity and Stamina, to a minimum of 0, and suffers Physical Impairment.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"143"}},"c3XN18YrAnNzhGoQ":{"id":"c3XN18YrAnNzhGoQ","n":"Purification of Wu Zao","d":"valerenwatcher","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Dice Pools: Composure + Resolve vs. Composure + Resolve","dur":"Instant","act":"Full","sum":"Mages, Wan Kuei, and shapeshifters all command spirits and demons. These creatures exist in their own worlds, but infest our own.","fx":"If the vampire wins, they may expel the spirit from its host.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"196"}},"cQT03JKulxKnWM7X":{"id":"cQT03JKulxKnWM7X","n":"Nocturne","d":"obtenebration","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene","act":"Full","sum":"Nearby shadows spread outwards as the vampire blankets the area in a layer of darkness, while sounds become muffled and indistinct.","fx":"The user makes a Rouse Check and spends a turn concentrating, spreading the shadow over the desired surfaces.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"112"}},"cQm5uTERPqogO94z":{"id":"cQm5uTERPqogO94z","n":"Bond Famulus","d":"animalism","lv":1,"cost":"The animal must be fed the user’s Blood on three separate nights, each of which requires a Rouse Check by the user. The amount of Blood needed to sustain the ghoulstate of the animal after this is negligible. Players starting with this power have completed this process and can chose a famulus for free. Note that all famuli are animal ghouls and receive benefits as such (p. XX).","pool":"Manipulation + Animal Ken","dur":"Only death releases a famulus once bound. As long as it receives vampire Blood on a regular basis, the famulus does not age.","act":"Passive/Issuing commands is a minor action of -2 dice","sum":"When Blood Bonding an animal, the vampire can make it a famulus, forming a mental link with it and facilitating the use of other Animalism powers.","fx":"Without the use of Feral Whispers, below, giving commands to the animal requires a Manipulation + Animal Ken Test (Difficulty 2); increase Difficulty for more complex orders.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"14"}},"cQyok73cJifOsnME":{"id":"cQyok73cJifOsnME","n":"Whispers from the Deep","d":"daimonion","lv":2,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive.","act":"Passive","sum":"Usually, those seeking to learn from a demon must do so by petitioning a demon who is usually relucant to provide anything without a bargain (masterfully rigged in their favour).","fx":"The user hears whispers of arcane secrets and powers, offering advice when needed.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"55"}},"cRhaKf7eCzp2mArc":{"id":"cRhaKf7eCzp2mArc","n":"Glare of Lies","d":"auspex","lv":1,"cost":"Free (but see below)","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until deactivated, at which point the eye is allowed to close.","act":"Free","am":"Valeren • (Any Path)","sum":"Upon activating this power, a Salubri’s third eye opens (if they developed it) and narrows in close scrutiny. The Cainite gains the ability to see the harmony of truth and the disharmony of deception.","fx":"Add your Auspex rating to all Insight rolls to detect deliberate lies of others. Successful Insight roll leaves no doubt that the heard statement is a lie.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"24"},"amr":[{"k":"any:valeren","l":1}]},"cbsdeabOqIz8Jn9k":{"id":"cbsdeabOqIz8Jn9k","n":"Death of the Drum","d":"melpominee","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Charisma + Performance vs. Stamina + Composure","dur":"A number of turns equal to the margin. A critical win extends it to the rest of the scene.","act":"Full","sum":"Considered one of the more disturbing powers of Melpominee, Death of the Drum weakens bones, kills cells, distorts vision and cracks glass with ease.","fx":"The vampire emits a sound that that weakens a target, rolling Charisma + Performance vs. the target’s Composure + Wits.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"87"}},"cjzMEDrkocFxtv1S":{"id":"cjzMEDrkocFxtv1S","n":"Energy Syphon","d":"valerenwatcher","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Occult vs. Composure + Resolve","dur":"One scene or until the victim shakes it off by spending Willpower.","act":"Minor -2","sum":"Practitioners of Path of the Watcher eventually run into many different types of supernatural creatures such as magicians, ghosts, demons and other monstrosities.","fx":"The user touches their victim and rolls Intelligence + Occult vs. Composure + Resolve.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"197"}},"cmkngrlZ4mV6CRdA":{"id":"cmkngrlZ4mV6CRdA","n":"Flight (••)","d":"flight","lv":2,"sum":"The user can fly up to 30 miles per hour/ 45 km per hour and carry up to 20 lbs./10 kg safely.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"78"}},"czyYyqVPfGMbzCeW":{"id":"czyYyqVPfGMbzCeW","n":"Seculsion","d":"obfuscate","lv":4,"cost":"As per power augmented","pool":"Manipulation + Subterfuge vs. Resolve + Awareness","dur":"Margin number of scenes or nights, or until broken","act":"Passive","am":"Dominate 1","sum":"This ability allows the user to invert the powers of Obfuscate on a subject, making them blind to every person in the vicinity.","fx":"The user catches the eye of the victim and must then succeed at a Manipulation + Subterfuge vs. Resolve + Awareness test.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"104"},"amr":[{"k":"dominate","l":1}]},"d1BceDqf7vxIRhK5":{"id":"d1BceDqf7vxIRhK5","n":"Fae Sight","d":"mytherceria","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"Intelligence + Awareness","dur":"One scene or until ended","act":"Passive","sum":"The fae see the world brighter and in more ways than a mortal could possibly imagine.","fx":"The user may reflexively roll Intelligence + Awareness against a Difficulty equal to the number of successes of any supernatural power that does not stem from an undead source (excluding Mytherceria) and is within their sensory range.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"90"}},"dP0zVZBl2V4zyhhl":{"id":"dP0zVZBl2V4zyhhl","n":"Spirit Whisperer","d":"spiritus","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene or until ended.","act":"Free","sum":"The user’s eyesight attunes to the umbra, beyond of what even the necromancers are capable of perceiving.","fx":"Upon activation, the user is able to see spirits (including ghosts) with their own eyes and are able to hear them and hold conversations.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"161"}},"dXeIjduUA6N7p7LR":{"id":"dXeIjduUA6N7p7LR","n":"Mask of a Thousand Faces","d":"obfuscate","lv":3,"cost":"One or more Rouse Checks","pool":"Manipulation + Performance","dur":"Until the character falls unconscious or stops the illusion.","act":"Free","sum":"While using this ability, the Cainite remains fully visible but changes their appearance to fit a particular image.","fx":"See the following page for the level of change the character can then make to their appearance.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"100"}},"dffWIcfHXHn70NnH":{"id":"dffWIcfHXHn70NnH","n":"Awaken the Parasite","d":"animalism","lv":3,"cost":"One","pool":"Resolve + Animal Ken vs. Road rating or Stamina + Wits","dur":"One scene","act":"Full","am":"Daimonion 1","pre":"Unliving Hive","sum":"Vampires are dead, but that doesn’t mean they’re devoid of life.","fx":"The victim must be within close proximity to the vampire (<10 meters). Results are based on the margin of the contest, while a critical win also increases a vampire target’s Hunger by one:","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"17"},"amr":[{"k":"daimonion","l":1}],"prer":["Unliving Hive"]},"diuepUte6YtiqYS4":{"id":"diuepUte6YtiqYS4","n":"Trap the Shadow","d":"valerenwarrior","lv":3,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until the phylactery-prison is shattered.","act":"Passive","pre":"Ending the Watch","sum":"In war against infernal cults and malign spirits, sometimes banishing them whence they came from is not as useful due to an already prepared army of sinners ready to summon their masters again.","fx":"They may force the creature to inhabit any object within the vampire’s line of sight, but hallow ones are preferred for symbolism.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"192"},"prer":["Ending the Watch"]},"dqPXHI7aAiWtrQ0A":{"id":"dqPXHI7aAiWtrQ0A","n":"Face of the Victim","d":"vicissitude","lv":1,"cost":"Free/One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until reaching Hunger 5, or using this power again.","act":"Two full turns","sum":"Quicker than Malleable Visage, the vampire may steal the appearance of their victims.","fx":"After fully exsanguinating a mortal or a humanoid like a vampire, the user may activate the power for free and assume their physical appearance.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"203"}},"du2da0K70OAyW912":{"id":"du2da0K70OAyW912","n":"Words as Daggers","d":"quietusanimae","lv":5,"cost":"An additional Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","pre":"Sweat of Guilt","sum":"With this power the vampire completely destroys the victim’s defences, making them a puppet succeptable to input from strangers.","fx":"When activating Sweat of Guilt, the user may make an additional Rouse Check to force an internal self-flaggelation.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"138"},"prer":["Sweat of Guilt"]},"e6b9PPH3k2cWCcjU":{"id":"e6b9PPH3k2cWCcjU","n":"Blink","d":"celerity","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Dexterity + Athletics, or as needed","dur":"One turn","act":"Free","sum":"The vampire swiftly closes in on a foe, engaging or escaping in the blink of an eye. To an unprepared observer the user almost appears to teleport, a rush of wind the only sign of their passing.","fx":"The vampire moves in a straight line toward a target, covering any distance under 50 meters while still having enough time to perform an action, such as an attack, during the turn.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"44"}},"eA7UQEaxrjI6bhbK":{"id":"eA7UQEaxrjI6bhbK","n":"Mens Sana","d":"valerenhealer","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Occult","dur":"The effect is instant with lasting effects having the duration of a scene, extended to roughly 24 hours on a Critical Win or 3+ margins.","act":"Minor -2","pre":"Ease Mind","sum":"By focusing the power of their green-glowing third eye and the lessons of empathy of Saulot, the vampire shields another from supernatural influence, either erecting a mental barrier or purging it as one does illnesses.","fx":"The user touches a target and rolls Resolve + Occult at Difficulty of 3.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"186"},"prer":["Ease Mind"]},"eGwgsSJ7toLqRRUu":{"id":"eGwgsSJ7toLqRRUu","n":"Squirm","d":"protean","lv":1,"cost":"Free or One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"As long as desired","act":"Free","sum":"Some vampires who use Protean turn their flesh and bones rubbery, allowing them to squeeze into impossibly tight places. Some use this Power to hide in walls or block their havens with entrances few can follow through.","fx":"Add the user’s Protean rating to any dice pools to wriggle through tight spaces, escape a grapple, or escape any form of restraints.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"128"}},"eHdDuyHHVyHEziev":{"id":"eHdDuyHHVyHEziev","n":"Slow Cuts","d":"temporis","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One attack","act":"Free","sum":"By slowing time around them for a swift moment, the user is able to deliver an uncountable amount of quick cuts and slashes against an opponent.","fx":"The vampire may add their Temporis rating to any single Brawl or Melee attack (not otherwise augmented by a Discipline) made with claws or an edged weapon.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"169"}},"eIehD2MBWY0FCsM9":{"id":"eIehD2MBWY0FCsM9","n":"Diamond Skin","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"Until the margin is used up; on a critical win on the Distillation roll, the effect lasts for one scene.","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, melancholic human blood, ground up granite, diamonds, or ceramics, lotion or oil.","sum":"For all their potential, the thin-blooded are fragile, at least compared to other vampires.","fx":"A number of Aggravated damage points equal to the alchemist’s successes on the Distillation roll become Superficial damage to the user.","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"76"}},"eKpTIg7HNx4nlCsp":{"id":"eKpTIg7HNx4nlCsp","n":"Voice of Erictho","d":"dominate","lv":3,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","am":"Mortis 2 or some other necromantic sorcery at 2","sum":"Perfected by Thessalian Cappadocians and later popularised among the Giovanni, the Voice of Erictho extends the properties of Dominate to work against unembodied ghosts who would usually be immune to it just like with any other mind-afflicting power.","fx":"The user may spend a point of Willpower to affect ghosts with Dominate as they are normally immune to mind-controlling effects.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"74"},"amr":[{"k":"school:mortis","l":2},{"k":"path:necromancy","l":2}]},"eTDZAFUnjZI1NzFX":{"id":"eTDZAFUnjZI1NzFX","n":"An Ear For Lies","d":"dementation","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene or until the user stops focusing.","act":"Free","am":"Auspex •","sum":"Lying is not a thing that comes natural to humans as the body and the mind itself finds it uncomfortable. A prudent user of Dementation can notice the physical signs of lies and sense their veil clouding the mind’s eye.","fx":"Add the Dementation rating to all Insight rolls to detect lies of others.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"64"},"amr":[{"k":"auspex","l":1}]},"eXYnM8Osb1WDnq1H":{"id":"eXYnM8Osb1WDnq1H","n":"Eye of Unfogiving Heaven","d":"valerenhealer","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check and one Willpower point","pool":"Half of Road rating rounded down","dur":"One turn","act":"Full","sum":"Upon invoking this power, a Salubri’s third eye opens impossibly wide and burns incandescent gold. The orb becomes as a reflection of the sun itself, illuminating the area and searing the flesh of the undead.","fx":"As the power’s light emits as radiance rather a beam, it knows neither friend nor foe. Even the user is not wholly immune to his light, damage as they would normally from the sun.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"187"}},"edjrYrY2gjT2iUkL":{"id":"edjrYrY2gjT2iUkL","n":"Transcend the Prison of Form","d":"vicissitude","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Medicine","dur":"Permanent until healed or altered again. See Characteristics.","act":"Full, see system.","pre":"Rend the Osseous Frame","sum":"The vampire may now change their form in its entirety, changing into liquid states, making themselves lighter allowing them to sprout functional wings, etc.","fx":"If the subject is avoiding the user’s touch and the time required to perform an alteration is one turn or instant, alteration first requires a successful roll with any combination of Strength/Dexterity + Athletics/ Brawl.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"208"},"prer":["Rend the Osseous Frame"]},"edkcfpah4Ci9UMvO":{"id":"edkcfpah4Ci9UMvO","n":"Taste of Bliss","d":"quietusanimae","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Stamina +Athletics against Dexterity + Athletics","dur":"Power’s effects break at the next sunrise.","act":"Full","sum":"Shocking even those who are experts at Presence, the Taste of Bliss allows a vampire to simulate a blood bond – effectively trapping the victim in emotional slavery by exhaling a red mist carrying their vitae.","fx":"The user softly exhales a fine reddish mist towards the target which creeps up to them slowly enough for them to attempt to dodge.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"138"}},"epHhOU7kaDWvTuyx":{"id":"epHhOU7kaDWvTuyx","n":"Unburden the Bestial Soul","d":"valerenhealer","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check and two Willpower points","pool":"Stamina + Insight vs. Composure + Resolve","dur":"Until a soul is released or fights its way out","act":"Full","sum":"The third eye opens and a shaft of golden radiance lances out, transfixing the victim. Something barely perceptible wafts out of the subject’s mouth, drawn into the vampire’s body. It is the victim’s soul.","fx":"Vampiric souls with a Road rating of 0 cannot be healed with this power, they’re best left to the Warrior Caste of the Salubri.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"189"}},"esTbdGKRDQjwVOPE":{"id":"esTbdGKRDQjwVOPE","n":"Aura Absorption","d":"mytherceria","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Insight vs. Composure + Subterfuge","dur":"The effects last until the user of the power drifts asleep, restoring their own aura.","act":"Full","sum":"The fae feed on emotions of the living beings, or so the legends say. As is so often the case in Cainite lore, every legend and every lie holds a bit of truth within itself.","fx":"This power may be used only once a night on the same target. On a win, the user can select one of the following effects from the list below and for each margin on the roll.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"91"}},"f3TG4IiIyK2BA4Wu":{"id":"f3TG4IiIyK2BA4Wu","n":"Form of the Storm","d":"serpentis","lv":4,"cost":"One to three Rouse Checks","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene or until willingly ended.","act":"Full","sum":"Becoming an avatar of Set, the user of Serpentis is able to assume a magnificent and rare form of a small sandstorm, becoming untouchable and enter any rooms that are not hermetically sealed.","fx":"The transformation takes three turns to complete by default, but the user is able to speed it up by making additional Rouse Checks to lower it by one turn for each Rouse Check made, with…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"157"}},"fI6nCQBYFDMNM2lV":{"id":"fI6nCQBYFDMNM2lV","n":"Witness of Ahriman","d":"dominate","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"The vampire rolls Manipulation + Intimidation vs. Wits + Composure. The power does not work if there is no darkness or shadows around.","dur":"See system.","act":"Full","am":"Obtenebration 2","sum":"With this subtle power, the vampire’s eyes dilate to the infinite depths of the Abyss, filling a target who meets her gaze with fear. Shadows plague the victim’s mind, gnawing at their sanity and resolve.","fx":"The vampire rolls Manipulation + Intimidation vs Composure + Wits.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"74"},"amr":[{"k":"obtenebration","l":2}]},"fZ12XNmYS9JNbc0G":{"id":"fZ12XNmYS9JNbc0G","n":"Shape of the Beast","d":"protean","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until the vampire falls to sleep or torpor or ends the power","act":"Minor -2","sum":"The Damned reaches a plateau of symbiosis with the night when they expresse Shape of the Beast.","fx":"Upon transformation, the vampire gains the Physical Attributes, senses, and native Skills and specialties associated with that animal (see p.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"129"}},"fjG8SXITq8KTrbSZ":{"id":"fjG8SXITq8KTrbSZ","n":"Soul’s Breath","d":"valerenwatcher","lv":4,"cost":"Willpower point per target","pool":"Intelligence + Occult vs. Composure + Occult","dur":"Until ended or for turns equal to the margin.","act":"Full","sum":"The Watchers carry a terrible and a miraculous secret with them unknown to almost anybody else: the Curse of Caine to subsist on blood and bitter ashes is a lie.","fx":"The user slakes a point of Hunger while the victim’s Hunger increases by 1 if a vampire or, if their victim is a human, they are drained by a point of Hunger (make note of harmful feedings when slaking too much).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"198"}},"fkjUftBNMd7JWeN1":{"id":"fkjUftBNMd7JWeN1","n":"Swarm","d":"protean","lv":5,"cost":"Two Rouse Checks","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until the vampire falls to sleep or torpor or ends the power","act":"Full","pre":"Shapechange","sum":"No longer constrained to a singular form by their transformational gifts, the vampire dissolves their body into a mass of insects, reptiles, or other vermin.","fx":"The vampire Rouses the Blood and spends a full turn, their body breaking down into a swarm of creatures.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"132"},"prer":["Shapechange"]},"fzi1ND9FGqdOlsG7":{"id":"fzi1ND9FGqdOlsG7","n":"Cloak of Shadows","d":"obfuscate","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"See general rules for Obfuscate","dur":"One scene or ended by the user.","act":"Free","sum":"Standing perfectly still, the user blends into the surroundings. As long as they have some kind of cover, make no sound, and don’t move, only mechanical or supernatural means can detect them.","fx":"The effect lasts until the user moves or they are detected by other means.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"96"}},"g4a6ptp3yvmpdhgG":{"id":"g4a6ptp3yvmpdhgG","n":"Troll the Pious","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"On a location, one dose lasts a couple of months. On an object, two months if no one touches it, one month if it’s handled infrequently, a week if it’s handled often. On a person, a dose lasts three days, and on the first day their skin looks waxy and oily.","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, melancholic mortal blood, used hot tub water, cornstarch, a body hair from a living green-eyed natural redhead.","sum":"The pus-colored paste produced by this formula resembles the nontoxic glue given to pre-school children and has a similar waxy smell.","fx":"The procedure produces enough goo to wax about three square meters of floor — you can rub it into carpet, but it’s messy — or anoint one person all over, or smear a dozen books or about half the tools in a small workshop.","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"78"}},"g5zUNyGlQ0ZSVmEh":{"id":"g5zUNyGlQ0ZSVmEh","n":"Blood Essence","d":"quietuscruciatus","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Medicine","dur":"The preserved heart remains until destroyed or consumed. Note that Cainite hearts can only be destroyed by things that deal Aggravated Health damage to vampires such as the Sun or fire.","act":"Full","sum":"Members of the Warrior Caste of the Banu Haqim are the preferred option when somebody wishes to arrange a contract for assassination of another vampire. Why?","fx":"First, the user must exsanguinate the victim down to their last point of Hunger. If the victim is a vampire, they must be in torpor and be fully drained as if one is to commit diablerie.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"139"}},"gHGsh45JYFhbkskT":{"id":"gHGsh45JYFhbkskT","n":"Banishing Sign of Thoth","d":"bardo","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Occult","dur":"One action","act":"Free, does not count as an activated power for the limit.","sum":"The character gestures, turning aside any supernatural effect aimed at them. The source of the effect does not matter. They can thwart, or at least blunt, the strength of any mystical attack.","fx":"Whenever the user is about to be struck by a supernatural power such as Disciplines, Rituals, Arcanoi of ghosts or Arcanae of demons, the user may make a Resolve + Occult roll and make a…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"38"}},"gMI39QzMESrRC22b":{"id":"gMI39QzMESrRC22b","n":"Thrown Voice","d":"melpominee","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene or a night on a critical win, if the player so chooses.","act":"Full","sum":"The vampire can cause their voice to emanate from any point within sight, whether as a whisper or shout.","fx":"Thrown Voice allows for usage of any other Melpominee power and any other powers that fit the requirements such as Presence with Presenceless Voice (vanilla Melpominee level 2 power of Presence).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"87"}},"gTMNjnEe5yjFctW0":{"id":"gTMNjnEe5yjFctW0","n":"Heart Thief","d":"serpentis","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Permanent (or until the heart is destroyed/returned)","act":"Full","sum":"With a quick snatch, the user is able to take away a part of someone’s body, most commonly the heart. This does not destroy a vampire victim, unless the attacker then destroys the stolen heart.","fx":"After activation, the user makes an unarmed Strength + Brawl (-2 success Called Shot) attack against their opponent’s defensive roll like Dexterity + Athletics dodge, dealing damage as normal.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"159"}},"ggZ2hVRZRGvPvLfO":{"id":"ggZ2hVRZRGvPvLfO","n":"Rewind","d":"temporis","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Occult","dur":"Until ended Margins Effect 0 margins Up to 24 hours 1 margin Up to one week 2 margins Up to one month 3 margins Up to one year 4 margins Up to a century 5 margins Up to one millenium 6+ margins Up to one millenium + five centuries per margin over 5","pre":"Leaden Movement","sum":"The True Brujah usually use this power to confirm historical events, but many find it useful to discover the secrets of their peers and their enemies.","fx":"First, the user must be standing directly where they wish to travel back in time. The user then makes a Intelligence + Occult roll at a Difficulty of 2.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"172"},"prer":["Leaden Movement"]},"gjvghM87yrxbLkym":{"id":"gjvghM87yrxbLkym","n":"Arms of Ahriman","d":"obtenebration","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Wits + Brawl","dur":"One scene or until ended or destroyed","act":"Free","am":"Potence 2","sum":"The vampire summons shadowy extensions from unlit spots in the area, within line of sight. Local shadows distort as they flow across walls and floors and converge on one or more hapless victims.","fx":"Additional arms can be created by splitting the dice pool, enabling the user to engage multiple opponents.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"107"},"amr":[{"k":"potence","l":2}]},"gmQHJoOWQI03ezvw":{"id":"gmQHJoOWQI03ezvw","n":"Spectral Puppeteer","d":"auspex","lv":5,"cost":"Two Rouse Checks","pool":"Resolve + Insight vs. Wits + Subterfuge","dur":"Until ended, voluntarily or involuntarily.","act":"Full","am":"Dominate •••••","pre":"Anima Walk","sum":"Only a few Tremere have mastered this diabolical art, enabling them to seize control of a mortal with their spiritual form.","fx":"In order to use this power, a vampire must have sent her consciousness into the astral plane with the Auspex •••• power Anima Walk.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"36"},"amr":[{"k":"dominate","l":5}],"prer":["Anima Walk"]},"gocjf5vUxtgkYVY7":{"id":"gocjf5vUxtgkYVY7","n":"Read the Room","d":"auspex","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Insight","dur":"Instantaneous, or one scene on a critical or three margins.","act":"Full","sum":"The vampire senses the overriding opinion of a crowd, fueling their understanding about how many would support or oppose a suggestion.","fx":"The vampire activates the power and mentally poses a question they want answered, as though they were taking a poll, then tests Intelligence + Insight.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"30"}},"hBC25Gav35yyvtoR":{"id":"hBC25Gav35yyvtoR","n":"Locked Contemplation","d":"temporis","lv":2,"cost":"One Willpower point/One Rouse Check","pool":"Wits + Awareness, Manipulation + Occult vs. Wits + Intelligence","dur":"Instant/One minute per margin.","act":"Free/Full","sum":"Due to the efficacy of this simple ability, most True Brujah think it likely their Antediluvian has remained trapped in the instant Troile’s fangs pierced his throat in perpetuity.","fx":"The primary effect of this power may be activated reflexively as a defensive action. The player spends one Willpower point and rolls Wits + Awareness.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"167"}},"hLq4idiKfw5BZkRw":{"id":"hLq4idiKfw5BZkRw","n":"Freezer Fluid","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse check","dur":"One scene","ing":"The Alchemist’s Blood, melancholy and phlegmatic human blood, echinacea, possum scent glands, local anaesthetic or ricin","sum":"When ingested by or injected into a blankbody, this serum freezes their limbs, making them clumsy and possibly even helpless. Wood absorbs it; plastic remains inert; it sublimes rapidly from metal.","fx":"For every success the Alchemist wins by, the victim loses 2 dice from all physical dice pools.","src":{"book":"Second Inquisition","page":"47"}},"hcw8RmrfM4v3k7t3":{"id":"hcw8RmrfM4v3k7t3","n":"Martian Purity","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"Two rounds","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, choleric mortal blood, iron filings, gunpowder ash.","sum":"The name refers not to Martian in the extraterrestrial sense, but to the Roman god Mars and his association with iron, the choleric principle and similar mystical correspondence.","fx":"It ignites on contact with air, doing 2 points of Aggravated damage to the carrier. It is up to the Storyteller whether this works on individual supernatural infections.","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"77"}},"hkY6jORBMJw9AwFS":{"id":"hkY6jORBMJw9AwFS","n":"Eyes of Chaos","d":"dementation","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Investigation","dur":"Information is acquired after a short time of investigating/until the dice bonus is exhausted.","act":"Full","am":"Auspex •","sum":"Fleeting clarity hides within insanity; a shattered mirror reflects more than one unbroken one.","fx":"This power may only be used when scrutinising a complex pattern or event, such as the interactions of a vampiric court or the clash of an army.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"65"},"amr":[{"k":"auspex","l":1}]},"hrOCyOU9jqDFhrkd":{"id":"hrOCyOU9jqDFhrkd","n":"Gift of Anubis","d":"bardo","lv":2,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"The jackal-headed god of funerary rites does not forget the suffering of the Children of Osiris, doomed to feast on humans.","fx":"The user halves (rounded up) their Blood Potency for the purposes of slaking Hunger from corpses.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"38"}},"ht90tex3FejdZG12":{"id":"ht90tex3FejdZG12","n":"The Body Impolitic","d":"vicissitude","lv":3,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"Arguably the most ghoulish of Vicissitude’s gifts, The Body Impolitic allows the user to invest a portion of her sentience in the flesh of their body, then sever it from the trunk to do the vampire’s bidding.","fx":"The user retains full awareness of any spilled body parts and may move them as if they are connected.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"207"}},"hyWtnBHZVtjZvQEE":{"id":"hyWtnBHZVtjZvQEE","n":"Animal Messenger","d":"animalism","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check for each night","pool":"None, though the Famulus must test Resolve + Streetwise / Survival (or equivalent) if the target’s location is unknown","dur":"One or more nights depending in length of search","act":"Full action","pre":"Bond Famulus","sum":"The vampire can commune with the beasts of the wild and the city. Feral Whispers allows two-way communication with animals.","fx":"If the location of the recipient is unknown the Famulus must track them down, making a tracking test (see above) at a Difficulty of 2, or resisted by the target’s Intelligence +…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"14"},"prer":["Bond Famulus"]},"i5C0NcYgZnO9lBOX":{"id":"i5C0NcYgZnO9lBOX","n":"Mandagloire","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Stamina + Alchemy vs. Stamina + Resolve","dur":"Three turns","ing":"The alchemist’s blood, phlegmatic blood, human fat, candle wax, ether, sesame oil, iron sulfate or verdigris, and borax.","sum":"Also called “The Funk” by alchemists who copy and adjust the formula.","fx":"Supernatural creatures who fail feel the effects of rigor mortis: a two-dice penalty on all Physical rolls from intense cramping.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade Players Guide","page":"104"}},"i6iGp8tVBoe0wi4C":{"id":"i6iGp8tVBoe0wi4C","n":"Shush the Beast","d":"valerenwatcher","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check, one Willpower point","pool":"Composure + Resolve vs. Composure + Resolve","dur":"Until the user awakens next","act":"Full","sum":"Masters of Valeren may finally silence the Beast for good at the cost of suppressing themselves as a person as well.","fx":"The Beast is numbed (or placated?) and the vampire is immune to all forms of Frenzy.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"199"}},"iD3RrspdCRAHmcoR":{"id":"iD3RrspdCRAHmcoR","n":"Earthshock","d":"potence","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One use/turn","act":"Full","sum":"Their strength an elemental force, the vampire can slam their fist or foot into the ground, creating a shockwave that throws their opponents prone.","fx":"No additional test is needed to create the shockwave.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"119"}},"iDjdouD4kXYCpdtd":{"id":"iDjdouD4kXYCpdtd","n":"Healer’s Touch","d":"valerenhealer","lv":3,"cost":"Two Rouse Checks","pool":"Intelligence + Medicine","dur":"The target heals over the course of three turns. If interrupted, the power’s healing effects are void.","act":"Three Full Actions","pre":"Ease Wounds","sum":"The signature power of the Healers stems from the ability to apply the vampiric regenerative process to others. The third eye opens wide, shedding slick sanguine light.","fx":"The vampire cannot target themselves with this power.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"185"},"prer":["Ease Wounds"]},"iLJulmXD9nEw656E":{"id":"iLJulmXD9nEw656E","n":"Observant Eye","d":"valerenwarrior","lv":2,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"After the Warlocks began their purge of the Salubri, the third eye was essentially a target for others which is why the Salubri tended to conceal it.","fx":"When rolling perception rolls against danger (such as Awareness against surprise attacks, Sense Death of Valeren and Sense the Unseen of Auspex), the user rolls the same dicepool twice and…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"191"}},"iMo09mBr3toqLxkT":{"id":"iMo09mBr3toqLxkT","n":"Necrotic Gaze","d":"thanatosis","lv":5,"cost":"Free/One Rouse Check in addition to the cost of the power amplified","pool":"N/A, Manipulation + Medicine vs. Stamina + Medicine (or Fortitud e)","dur":"Passive/ Per power augmented","act":"Passive","sum":"Master of ailments and rotting flesh, the user no longer requires close contact to afflict their targets.","fx":"Powers of Thanatosis such as Putrefaction and Whence All Came require no skin contact. If the power has no contest pools, it is Manipulation + Medicine vs.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"181"}},"iTbPXa428tKUhzdO":{"id":"iTbPXa428tKUhzdO","n":"Reclaim the Gift of Humanity","d":"bardo","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Composure + Insight","dur":"Until sunset for the vampire, three nights for mortal victims","act":"Full","am":"Auspex 2","sum":"The dead experience emotion, passion even, but all too often, these are but a dulled reflection of the feelings experienced by the living.","fx":"The vampire must spend a scene in close proximity to a mortal target but needn’t directly engage them.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"38"},"amr":[{"k":"auspex","l":2}]},"iWiCFbplW5xo0lOs":{"id":"iWiCFbplW5xo0lOs","n":"Resilience","d":"fortitude","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"Endowed with supernatural endurance, the user can strengthen their physical resolve.","fx":"The user adds their Fortitude rating to their Health track.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"79"}},"iYsoJea9px8WTbvs":{"id":"iYsoJea9px8WTbvs","n":"Flowering Amaranth","d":"alchemy","lv":5,"cost":"Everyone participating must roll one Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Alchemy vs. Willpower pool + Blood Potency","ing":"Blood from the alchemist and participating thin-bloods (up to three thin-bloods total), juice of red amaranth flowers from a plant fertilized with blood, pulverized leeches, hydrogen sulfide, and neon.","sum":"This form of shared diablerie draws virtue from the vitae of a full-blooded Kindred into the alchemist and their assistants.","fx":"The alchemist rolls Resolve + Alchemy; each additional thin-blood participant can add one die to the pool by spending 2 Willpower.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade Players Guide","page":"106"}},"iZ39WTaQZK0P1ozo":{"id":"iZ39WTaQZK0P1ozo","n":"Pacts of Blood","d":"spiritus","lv":4,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","pre":"Aspects of the Beast","sum":"Reaching the ability to contain more spiritual power within them, the user is able to grasp towards more spirits which in turn improves their ability to benefit from spirits.","fx":"Aspects of the Beast power no longer requires a roll. The user is now able to take the same aspect as many times as they want.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"164"},"prer":["Aspects of the Beast"]},"iaHDRZ6nk3JYtEPH":{"id":"iaHDRZ6nk3JYtEPH","n":"The False Sip","d":"protean","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene or more","act":"Free","am":"Fortitude 2","sum":"The vampire’s mastery of their own form can prevent any blood (or Blood) swallowed from entering their system, allowing them to avoid poisoning or the forming of Blood Bonds.","fx":"The character must activate this power immediately upon consuming blood from any source.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"128"},"amr":[{"k":"fortitude","l":2}]},"idyQ554xYgxjYFoo":{"id":"idyQ554xYgxjYFoo","n":"Body Paint","d":"alchemy","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Dexterity + Craft; Stamina + Resolve","dur":"Permanent, unless erased by flesh colored Body Paint.","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, choleric mortal blood, tattoo inks, henna, marker fluid, or any substance that stains skin.","sum":"This formula allows the alchemist to create tattoos with personal touches beyond human tattoo artists. Sometimes, an alchemist’s client can customize their ink further.","fx":"On Distillation rolls with 1–3 successes, the body paint dries faster, and the alchemist must Win a Dexterity + Craft test at Difficulty 3 to finish their work before drying.","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"73"}},"ijse9ElEa9P1k29r":{"id":"ijse9ElEa9P1k29r","n":"Aura Syphon","d":"valerenwatcher","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Subterfuge against Wits + Resolve","dur":"One story or until the vampire dispels it","act":"Minor -2","sum":"A power that arises suspicion and paranoia in those who know of it (and the Tremere very well do know of it), Aura Syphon allows a vampire to overwrite their own aura using the aspects of another person’s aura or to “adopt” another person’s aura in its entirety.","fx":"The user perceives all possible information from the victim’s aura (see Scry the Soul for information samples) and may decide to take whatever aura features they wish such as appearing like…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"198"}},"imwhmRDqQJpBa2Vi":{"id":"imwhmRDqQJpBa2Vi","n":"Peaceful Touch","d":"valerenwatcher","lv":2,"cost":"Free","pool":"Composure + Resolve vs. Composure + Resolve","dur":"Turns equal to the user’s Watcher Valeren rating + the margin on the roll","act":"Free","sum":"Watchers deal in knowledge, but knowledge threatens the most powerful of men — the brutal nights during the Wolf of Qin’s purges are still fresh in the minds of their elders.","fx":"The target cannot make any hostile actions against the vampire for turns equal to the user’s Watcher Valeren rating + the margin on the roll unless they spend a point of Willpower each turn.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"196"}},"imyKIqqnCdXIk4RC":{"id":"imyKIqqnCdXIk4RC","n":"Friend of the Spirits","d":"spiritus","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"The user’s very aura becomes attuned more alluring to the spirits, appearing as either one of them or something friendly to them, allowing the users of Spiritus to demand more from them without enraging the spirits.","fx":"The user adds their Spiritus rating, to all non-physical pools directly involving the spirits of animals and concepts.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"160"}},"ix9yGG5vFF2NQLwZ":{"id":"ix9yGG5vFF2NQLwZ","n":"Concoct Ashe","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"pool":"Intelligence + Thin- Blood Alchemy","ing":"A destroyed vampire’s ashes, an open flame reaching 1,500°C, aluminum filings.","sum":"The process of creating the Ashe drug is a form of Blood Alchemy in itself, and generally takes place in a laboratory or workshop due to the need for an open flame and metal filings.","fx":"On a total failure, the sample is ruined and a Beast Shard (see p. XX) emerges in the area.","src":{"book":"Cults of the Blood Gods","page":"46"}},"jEr2uYuHA4espRNU":{"id":"jEr2uYuHA4espRNU","n":"On-Demand Sunburn","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"None","dur":"Until unleashed or next sunset, whichever comes first.","ing":"Blood of the Alchemist, choleric AT: mortal blood, gold shavings, mercury, as well as assorted halogens (usually chlorine or bromide). The formula also needs to be subjected to sunlight for several hours before use, and alchemists employing athanor corporis usually “juice up” on Portable Shade (see above) for this.","sum":"A dread tool of the Path of the Sun, On-Demand Sunburn traps sunlight in the very body of its user, enabling them to unleash it as a destructive force through their own skin, searing themselves and their prey in a sizzling embrace.","fx":"On activation, the alchemist becomes an unliving battery of sunlight with a single charge seething in their veins.","src":{"book":"Sabbat: The Black Hand","page":"53"}},"jQZ1cQYgQdq8ZaVO":{"id":"jQZ1cQYgQdq8ZaVO","n":"Presenceless Voice","d":"melpominee","lv":4,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"A powerful upgrade to Melpominee, the vampire no longer requires the line of sight to afflict others with Melpominee.","fx":"The vampire’s powers of Melpominee may be transmitted without the need for a line of sight, allowing the vampire to use their powers through voice technology.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"88"}},"jmdUU8EImWZCM29s":{"id":"jmdUU8EImWZCM29s","n":"Corrosive Vitae","d":"quietussanguinis","lv":1,"cost":"One or more Rouse Checks","pool":"N/A","dur":"N/A","act":"Free/Depending on the application","sum":"Altering the properties of some of their own Blood, the user can make it highly corrosive to dead substances, able to corrode most items down to steaming sludge, given enough time and Blood shed.","fx":"The user concentrates for a turn and forces Blood through an open, usually self-inflicted, wound.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"145"}},"jwQ50R5Q7Ml7cWhW":{"id":"jwQ50R5Q7Ml7cWhW","n":"Half-Living Conductor","d":"alchemy","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Stamina + Alchemy","dur":"One scene or until voluntarily ended.","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, choleric and sanguine mortal blood, molten conductive metal (gold, silver, copper, and aluminum are popular choices), ground rubber, rainwater from a thunderstorm.","sum":"This formula grants the alchemist protection from one of the most primal forces of nature: lightning itself.","fx":"The alchemist is immune to all physical damage taken from any electrical source, be it lightning, tasers, live wires, or a supernatural ability.","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"79"}},"jxcFL5MIxT4n39sV":{"id":"jxcFL5MIxT4n39sV","n":"Isthar’s Disfavour","d":"quietusanimae","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Occult vs. Intelligence + Composure","dur":"Power’s effects break at the next sunrise.","act":"Full","pre":"Isthar’s Touch","sum":"With this power the vampire completely destroys the victim’s defences, making them a puppet succeptable to input from strangers.","fx":"The victim automatically counts as if they’ve rolled a 0 on rolls to resist Social Skills and mind-altering Disciplines unless the victim rolls a Critical Win on the roll.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"138"},"prer":["Isthar’s Touch"]},"k6YiRLqqdGSO9WGd":{"id":"k6YiRLqqdGSO9WGd","n":"Glimpse the Gulf Beyond","d":"daimonion","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check and one Willpower point","pool":"Intelligence + Occult vs. Composure + Resolve + Daimonion","dur":"Until the effect ends.","act":"Full","sum":"There are worlds beyond worlds and places beyond space and time; this power allows a Baali to shatter the boundaries between such zones of cosmic terror and the mundane world.","fx":"A single success is enough to create a portal to the Beyond with the maximum of its radius area equal to the successes in meters.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"58"}},"kQm6paYdg2w9FN5l":{"id":"kQm6paYdg2w9FN5l","n":"Ignore Me","d":"dominate","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Subterfuge vs. Composure + Resolve","dur":"One month","act":"Full","am":"Obfuscate 2","sum":"Some people fade into the Background easily. A vampire that haunts a specific location can program the people there to completely ignore them while they moves about the grounds.","fx":"The vampire tells their subject “ignore me” and rolls Manipulation + Subterfuge against their Composure + Resolve.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"71"},"amr":[{"k":"obfuscate","l":2}]},"kSla0w0Hcnh92Xn9":{"id":"kSla0w0Hcnh92Xn9","n":"Advanced Torpor","d":"alchemy","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"Until the target awakens from torpor.","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, choleric and phlegmatic mortal blood, neem extract, diazepam, diphenhydramine, chamomile flower.","sum":"This Formula induces torpor. For thin-blooded, it’s a last resort mending coma.","fx":"The alchemist creates (or for other Distillations, they or their vessel bleeds) a bright pink, watery fluid.","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"75"}},"kUB8hl7nRmDcRtCZ":{"id":"kUB8hl7nRmDcRtCZ","n":"Stir the Soul","d":"valerenhealer","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Insight","dur":"One scene. A Critical Win or 3+ margins extends it to the rest of the night","act":"Minor -2","sum":"With a touch, the user “heals” some part of their target that is missing, restoring a part of their lost and human self while the user’s third eye glows in a golden colour.","fx":"On a win the target’s Road rating increases be the number of margins on the roll. Additionally, the vampire will be able to digest the food they eat and enjoy it as they once did.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"185"}},"kWTos4bf1CDjgPAT":{"id":"kWTos4bf1CDjgPAT","n":"Mask of Isolation","d":"obfuscate","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Subterfuge vs. Charisma + Insight","dur":"One night","act":"Passive","am":"Dominate •","sum":"Subtle but effective, this power forces the effect of Mask of a Thousand Faces on an unwitting subject. The victim will no longer be seen for who they are, even by those closest to them.","fx":"The user locks eyes with the victim and must then succeed at a Manipulation + Subterfuge vs. Charisma + Insight test.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"102"},"amr":[{"k":"dominate","l":1}]},"kX3O2lXrTD6QGpUh":{"id":"kX3O2lXrTD6QGpUh","n":"Bring the Plague","d":"daimonion","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Occult vs. Stamina + Occult","dur":"Until the effect ends.","act":"Full","sum":"A Daimonion user with Bring the Plague calls down a Biblical plague on their enemies, cursing them with a highly infectious disease that plagues mortal and Cainite alike.","fx":"First the user states the number of transmissions (from 1 to unlimited, but only an idiot brings upon such an apocalypse just like that).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"58"}},"kzUT3Nsf7I4DqJ8d":{"id":"kzUT3Nsf7I4DqJ8d","n":"Restore Humantias","d":"bardo","lv":3,"cost":"Enough Rouse Checks to reach Hunger 5","pool":"N/A","dur":"Permanent","act":"Passive","sum":"The first thing that the Children of Osiris are taught is that Humanity does not have to be an inexorable slide into depravity. Instead, it is more akin to a climb up an extremely steep hill.","fx":"Whenever the user fails their Remorse roll, they get to roll another D10 at the cost of not healing any Willpower damage upon awakening.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"40"}},"lUDwBeTWFK4RH9OC":{"id":"lUDwBeTWFK4RH9OC","n":"Song of the Blooded","d":"valerenwarrior","lv":5,"cost":"Two Willpower points and two Rouse Checks","pool":"Charisma + Performance","dur":"The trance ends after a scene or when every foe is dead as their fears or they meet Final Death on the field, whichever comes first. When removing Health due to return to old Attribute ratings, remove undamanged Health first (or Superficial damage, if everything is damaged).","act":"Full","sum":"Samiel’s words were heard only by his childer. Only they know the secret doubts he spoke aloud, purging them from his heart so he could face his enemies with his potential unchecked.","fx":"Their Physical Attributes immediately increase to 6. A halo burns around them, incapable of being smothered by lesser Disciplines, rendering Stealth or darkness-induced penalties impossible.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"194"}},"lZAhESgYeuzg5dJO":{"id":"lZAhESgYeuzg5dJO","n":"Clarity of Emptyness","d":"auspex","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until toggled off","act":"Free","am":"Corpse in the Monster Path •• or Obtenebration •• or Temporis •","sum":"Developed independently by Cappadocian scholars and Abyss mystics of the Lasombra, this power allows a vampire to still their passions and think with pitiless detached clarity.","fx":"This power may be toggled off and on. While active, the vampire receives a +2 dice bonus to all Mental Rolls.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"24"},"amr":[{"k":"path:corpseinthemonster","l":2},{"k":"obtenebration","l":2},{"k":"temporis","l":1}]},"lfd8enJCskRykLgx":{"id":"lfd8enJCskRykLgx","n":"Psychomachia","d":"daimonion","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Occult vs Composure + Resolve","dur":"The phantasm vanishes on their defeat (physical defeat is performed by depleting the apparition’s health levels and mental by depleting its Willpower in a social combat or through some other means), after a scene or when the user’s concentration drops.","act":"Full","sum":"Prudentius was a Roman poet who wrote the Psychomachia – “the Battle of Souls,” describing the struggle of faith against idolatry and vice. The Baali know this game, and they play to win.","fx":"Upon a win, the caster summons a mist-like entity out of the target’s body, dealing a point of Aggravated Health damage to them.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"59"}},"lpr07zM8SfgGBNzs":{"id":"lpr07zM8SfgGBNzs","n":"Blurred Momentum","d":"celerity","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until the user lets it lapse","act":"Free","sum":"The vampire’s movement becomes a jittering blur, making it extremely difficult to land attacks on them even when they are not aware of the opponent or actively defending.","fx":"Activating this power requires one Rouse Check and extending it requires an additional Check for each turn it is kept active.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"45"}},"m4qqYzh2BKsdCXWZ":{"id":"m4qqYzh2BKsdCXWZ","n":"Gift of Sleep","d":"valerenhealer","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Composure + Resolve vs. Composure + Resolve","dur":"8 hours or until the subject is awakened","act":"Full","sum":"The ability to ease someone’s pain and to bestow sleep upon the restless is a valued one within the Healer caste.","fx":"The target is forced into sleep from which they awaken if they take a point of health damage.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"184"}},"mgQ5vYNDLZ3SQjkU":{"id":"mgQ5vYNDLZ3SQjkU","n":"Premonition","d":"auspex","lv":2,"cost":"Free/one Rouse Check","pool":"Wits/Resolve + Awareness","dur":"Passive/Until bonus is exhausted","act":"Free/Full if used consciously","sum":"The vampire experiences flashes of insight. These may take the form of raised hackles, sudden inspiration or even vivid visions.","fx":"Whether it gives the character a sudden vision of themselves walking into a trap, an inviting red glow over the second right turn during a chase, or the brief flash of a skeleton beneath…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"27"}},"mkSsLjnfLWuFFSSx":{"id":"mkSsLjnfLWuFFSSx","n":"Wrecker","d":"potence","lv":3,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"As Prowess","act":"Full","pre":"Prowess","sum":"The vampire is able to exert violent, indiscriminate force on a static object in order to shatter, smash, and destroy it.","fx":"The user counts their Potence rating twice when using Prowess for feats of strength that involve damage or destruction of an inanimate object.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"118"},"prer":["Prowess"]},"n5Tn2quP279eMZFy":{"id":"n5Tn2quP279eMZFy","n":"Timestop","d":"temporis","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Roughly one action, as determined by the Storyteller.","act":"Free","sum":"Already reaching the legendary powers that the elders of the True Brujah are said to possess, Timestop allows its user to quite literally stop time and move — crossing great distances or avoiding lethal dangers by a hair.","fx":"The player can supersede the Storyteller’s narration of events, within reason.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"174"}},"nHjmO1pb8wZlhebE":{"id":"nHjmO1pb8wZlhebE","n":"Profane Hieros Gamos","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Stamina + Resolve","dur":"Permanent until performed again.","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, melancholic and phlegmatic human blood, entheogenic substances.","sum":"To the Alchemist, rebirth and renewal are not locked behind the ritual of sacred union between two opposites.","fx":"Whoever imbibes the formula mixed with a Rouse Check worth of their own Blood instantly falls into a catatonic fever dream until the following night, the depths of their psyche plumbed for their personal idealized form, or a form strongly desired.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition Corebook","page":"286"}},"nQ80eWTy4kj2v1ev":{"id":"nQ80eWTy4kj2v1ev","n":"Inflame Desire","d":"presence","lv":4,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Full","am":"Obfuscate 1","sum":"The vampire can invisibly boost a subject’s present desire to the point that they will singlemindedly seek to satisfy it with little thought of their own well-being.","fx":"The user’s voice alone is now enough to Dominate a target.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"124"},"amr":[{"k":"obfuscate","l":1}]},"nXgzrfxzbwzNoZB8":{"id":"nXgzrfxzbwzNoZB8","n":"Rend the Osseous Frame","d":"vicissitude","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Medicine","dur":"Permanent until healed or altered again. See Characteristics.","act":"Full, see system.","pre":"Transmogrify the Mortal Clay","sum":"At this stage of mastery, the Tzimisce has progressed to manipulating bone. Used on its own, Rend the Osseous Frame can inflict terrible damage upon a subject.","fx":"If the subject is avoiding the user’s touch and the time required to perform an alteration is one turn or instant, alteration first requires a successful roll with any combination of Strength/Dexterity + Athletics/ Brawl.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"205"},"prer":["Transmogrify the Mortal Clay"]},"nYWKTJcnA30nPxEZ":{"id":"nYWKTJcnA30nPxEZ","n":"Dominion of Wu Zao","d":"valerenwatcher","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Composure + Resolve vs. Composure + Resolve","dur":"Blood Bond expires as normal.","act":"Full","pre":"Purification of Wu Zao","sum":"Said to have been discovered by Wao-Lat himself, the Dominion of Wu Zao allows the vampire to take command of a spirit.","fx":"If the vampire wins, the spirit becomes fully Blood Bound to the user, even if they would otherwise be immune to mind control or Blood Bond.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"199"},"prer":["Purification of Wu Zao"]},"ncy7En5EDy8kioCr":{"id":"ncy7En5EDy8kioCr","n":"Portable Shade","d":"alchemy","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Stamina + Alchemy","dur":"A number of hours equal to a Stamina + Alchemy test, or the next sunset, whichever comes first.","ing":"Blood of the Alchemist, sanguinic mortal blood, fresh plant leaves. Some alchemists also use various off-the-shelf sunblock ointments in the mix, though it is unknown whether they contribute significantly to the formula.","sum":"Portable Shade, or even more irreverently, “suntan lotion,” is a formula developed by Cainites on the Path of the Sun to augment a thin-blood’s already substantial resistance to sunlight to near mortal levels.","fx":"The user is able to endure sunlight without taking damage for a number of hours equal to the number of successes on the test.","src":{"book":"Sabbat: The Black Hand","page":"53"}},"neYBR1dlleIqcJrq":{"id":"neYBR1dlleIqcJrq","n":"Falsehood","d":"mytherceria","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene or until ended","act":"Free","sum":"Like the true fae, practitioners of Mytherceria find that they can blur truths and lies like one blends water and wine.","fx":"The user adds their Mytherceria rating to all rolls to lie, gaslight, confuse or trick others with Subterfuge.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"90"}},"nwDPXiCAi4FmAcwa":{"id":"nwDPXiCAi4FmAcwa","n":"Death’s Hidden Crawl","d":"protean","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"Your character may use this subtle application of Protean in order to subvert one of their greatest weaknesses: torpor.","fx":"It cannot be used while any sentient characters watch your character or while staked. When they have no witnesses in torpor, they can move no more than one meter or yard per hour.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"130"}},"nxTze37Ple8L9IjU":{"id":"nxTze37Ple8L9IjU","n":"Shadow Cloak","d":"obtenebration","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"Subtly applying the influence of the Abyss on ambient shadows, the user masks their appearance or seems more sinister and threatening.","fx":"The vampire gains a two-dice bonus to Stealth rolls, as well as on Intimidation.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"107"}},"o9HofJPw6KB2TnVR":{"id":"o9HofJPw6KB2TnVR","n":"Sense Vitality","d":"valerenhealer","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Insight or Medicine vs. Composure + Subterfug","dur":"One scene","act":"Minor -2","sum":"Sense Vitality allows its user to read the person’s physical and mental state, learning how much damage a target has suffered or what manner of a creature they are.","fx":"The user may ask questions equal to the margin and get a correct response. The example questions are:","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"183"}},"oMKgUGk6TxQWMApm":{"id":"oMKgUGk6TxQWMApm","n":"Mesmerise","d":"dominate","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Intimidation vs. Intelligence + Resolve","dur":"Until the command is carried out or the scene ends, whichever comes first.","act":"Full","sum":"The vampire can issue complex commands to a victim, as long as they have the subject’s gaze and their instructions can be heard.","fx":"Commanding a resisting victim or another vampire requires a contest of Manipulation + Intimidation vs Intelligence + Resolve.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"71"}},"oPBffLVnW84dfjtG":{"id":"oPBffLVnW84dfjtG","n":"Da Bomb","d":"alchemy","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"One week","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, Sanguine human blood, accelerants, matchstick heads, grains of sand from a sand timer","sum":"This Formula transforms a mortal vessel into a walking time bomb. This murderous concoction spells certain death for whoever drinks it but is just as lethal for those unlucky enough to be caught in the blast radius.","fx":"The alchemist can activate the Formula at any time by making a Rouse Check, but if not activated while still potent, it passes harmlessly from the drinker’s system.","src":{"book":"Tattered Façade","page":"108"}},"oX5BSyXQGB38f4mo":{"id":"oX5BSyXQGB38f4mo","n":"Fleetness","d":"celerity","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One Scene","act":"Free","sum":"Their mastery of Celerity now allows the vampire to move and react with dizzying speed.","fx":"Add the Celerity rating to user’s dice pool for non-combat Dexterity tests.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"43"}},"oYbTCGPn2ycUWj24":{"id":"oYbTCGPn2ycUWj24","n":"Putrescent Servitude","d":"thanatosis","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Medicine vs. Stamina + Medicine (or Fortitude)","dur":"See system AGGRESSIVE CORPSE","act":"Full","sum":"Users of Thantosis, perhaps due to the necromantic properties of the Discipline or due to the unlife-giving aspects of vampiric vitae, are able to animate a zombie-like creature to serve their needs.","fx":"The corpse rises as an aggressive corpse after a turn (see the statblock on the next page).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"178"}},"ohoAwuStbNrClrdS":{"id":"ohoAwuStbNrClrdS","n":"One with the Land","d":"protean","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One day or more, or until disturbed. Power may be ended sooner by the vampire rising.","act":"Full","am":"Animalism 2","pre":"Earth Meld","sum":"The vampire possesses such mastery over their own form that they may extend it even into their domain itself.","fx":"As with Earth Meld, except the vampire is not limited by the makeup of the surface where they take their rest.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"132"},"amr":[{"k":"animalism","l":2}],"prer":["Earth Meld"]},"okcPkls6OPcaMThm":{"id":"okcPkls6OPcaMThm","n":"Folderol","d":"mytherceria","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"One Scene","act":"Free","sum":"The fae see what others can not. Even in undeath, the practitioners of Mytherceria retain shards of such powers.","fx":"Add the Mytherceria rating to all Insight rolls to detect deliberate lies of others. Successful Insight roll leaves no doubt that the heard statement is a lie.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"90"}},"oy0CRhOjwM08MRRi":{"id":"oy0CRhOjwM08MRRi","n":"Purification","d":"valerenhealer","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Composure + Resolve","dur":"One scene with a Critical Win (or 3+ margins) extending it to the rest of the night.","act":"Full","sum":"Each caste of the Salubri have their own role to play in the war against the infernal.","fx":"If the vampire wins, they may expel the spirit from its host.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"184"}},"oyYBezXnVUdQpChR":{"id":"oyYBezXnVUdQpChR","n":"Spark of Rage","d":"presence","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Persuasion","dur":"One Scene","act":"Full","am":"Potence 3","sum":"Combining Potence and Presence, the vampire can incite anger and even Frenzy in onlookers, as easily as awe or dread.","fx":"When active, the user can add their Potence rating to any attempt to rile or incite a person or a crowd to violence.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"123"},"amr":[{"k":"potence","l":3}]},"p2ytAzKS8y7Ff5zw":{"id":"p2ytAzKS8y7Ff5zw","n":"Mind Steal","d":"mytherceria","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Insight vs. Composure + Wits","dur":"According to the table below or until dispelled by magics or powers like Cleansed in Blood (Quietus Sanguinis •••, p. 133). The user may also release the victim from the effect at will.","act":"Full","sum":"The fae are infamous for stealing people’s minds and memories. The Kiasyd have developed a similar power. The vampire may even keep these stolen memories, if theyre’s willing to pay the price for them.","fx":"The vampire may remove a number of Skill dots equal to the margins from the victim and add them to their own, up to the victim’s own maximum rating.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"94"}},"pQmsDHpSsITu1Eqn":{"id":"pQmsDHpSsITu1Eqn","n":"Sense the Sin","d":"daimonion","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Insight vs. Wits + Subterfuge","dur":"The bonus lasts until the conditions which give it are changed such as a loss of stains, change of the target’s Desire and so on.","act":"Free","sum":"Every jewel has a fault, and every man has a vice. The best way to shatter a jewel is to strike that fault, and the best way to shatter a man is to hammer his vice.","fx":"For this power to work, the user must have the target within the line of sight, observing their way of clothing, moving or topics they are discussing.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"53"}},"pRY6sU3kTE3glnxb":{"id":"pRY6sU3kTE3glnxb","n":"True Love’s Face","d":"presence","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Subterfuge vs. Composure + Wits","dur":"One scene","act":"Full","am":"Obfuscate 3","sum":"A sinister hybrid of Mask of a Thousand Faces and Entrancement, this Discipline technique enables a vampire to assume the form of a target’s true love.","fx":"To impersonate someone the victim has strong emotions for, the vampire must know their appearance and what the victim feels for them.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"124"},"amr":[{"k":"obfuscate","l":3}]},"pWUXkH1JrxqjnUHj":{"id":"pWUXkH1JrxqjnUHj","n":"Mental Maze","d":"obfuscate","lv":3,"cost":"One or three Rouse Checks","pool":"Manipulation + Subterfuge vs. Charisma + Insight","dur":"One night","act":"Passive","am":"Dominate •","sum":"Serpents maintain that Obfuscate is less about illusion and more about perception.","fx":"The vampire personally speaks the words “you cannot escape” to their victim and rolls Charisma + Obfuscate versus the target’s Wits + Resolve, with lower Generation vampires being immune per Dominate’s characteristics (p.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"102"},"amr":[{"k":"dominate","l":1}]},"pcKwaFB7BVqKlqSA":{"id":"pcKwaFB7BVqKlqSA","n":"Incubus Humour","d":"dementation","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Insight vs. Wits + Composure","dur":"See p. 52. The victim’s Resonance or Temperament changing also ends the power’s effects.","act":"Full","sum":"The vampire can inflame the humors of a victim within line of sight, eroding the victim’s self-control and amplifying their temperament to a fevered pitch.","fx":"For this power to work, the vampire must speak and roll Manipulation + Insight vs. Wits + Composure of the victim with whom they’re communicating (p. 52).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"64"}},"pf9ItGM27DbWq3mf":{"id":"pf9ItGM27DbWq3mf","n":"Marduk’s Whip","d":"quietussanguinis","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene or until ended","act":"Free","pre":"Blood Dance","sum":"When in need, the user of Quietus extends their blood into a whip capable of crystalizing to form a sharp but flexible weapon.","fx":"The blood crystalises into a piercing weapon of the user’s choice of damage rating equal to half the Quietus rating, rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"147"},"prer":["Blood Dance"]},"pg7YrZauhKvQl7Mi":{"id":"pg7YrZauhKvQl7Mi","n":"Rationalise","d":"dominate","lv":4,"cost":"No Additional Cost","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"The vampire’s victims now believe that anything they do under the influence of Dominate was a result of their own free will, and defend their actions, however absurd.","fx":"If pressed on their belief, the victim can make a Wits+Awareness test (Difficulty 5). A win makes them question their own statement, and possibly their sanity.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"75"}},"pi2s6eep1mefMMhY":{"id":"pi2s6eep1mefMMhY","n":"Leash the Beast","d":"animalism","lv":2,"cost":"One or Two Rouse Checks","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Free","sum":"You channel your Blood to your Beast, preventing it from awakening.","fx":"When you roll a 10 (potential Critical) on a normal die, you can turn that to a 9 (Success) by Rousing the Blood to activate this power.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"17"}},"pkuFsVZAeHa7jVVC":{"id":"pkuFsVZAeHa7jVVC","n":"Blessing of Haqim","d":"quietussanguinis","lv":2,"cost":"Free","pool":"Wits + Awareness","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","am":"Quietus Cruciatus 2","sum":"Quietus Sanguinis is taught to all within the Clan who hunt spirits, not just those who belong to the sorcerer caste. This power is an exemplary reason why, allowing all forms of Quietus to harm spirits.","fx":"All powers of all 3 Paths of Quietus may damage incorporeal as they do corporeal. This excludes ghosts, who are not as strictly immaterial due to possessing a body made out of ectoplasm.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"146"},"amr":[{"k":"quietuscruciatus","l":2}]},"plzS0BkRMRHZCgcn":{"id":"plzS0BkRMRHZCgcn","n":"Parlysis of Death","d":"thanatosis","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"Both the duration of the user’s poison and the victim’s paralysis last for a number of nights equal to the user’s Thanatosis rating + Blood Potency.","act":"Free","sum":"The user of Thanatosis transforms their vitae into a contact poison capable of delivering rigor mortis. Many a Samedi who has served as a mercenary has found this power extremely useful as it can be coated on weapons.","fx":"Spitting the poison can happen instantly during the first turn while coating a weapon is a -2 dice Minor Action.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"176"}},"pxg64dtMN1ddyZA7":{"id":"pxg64dtMN1ddyZA7","n":"Disruption","d":"chimerstry","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check and one point of Willpower","pool":"Manipulation + Subterfuge","dur":"One turn","act":"Minor action of -2 dice","sum":"A combat-oriented usage of Chimerstry, the ability to effect senses affects the targets so much that they find themselves stunned as their senses are overwhelmed.","fx":"Additionally, those who fail to resist using their Composure + Wits lose their next active action if they fail (but they can still defend and resist as normal, with a two-dice penalty.).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"50"}},"q3K11xnWREn84iOx":{"id":"q3K11xnWREn84iOx","n":"Drink the Mind","d":"auspex","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Insight","dur":"Permanent.","act":"Full","am":"Bloodlife Path or Quietus •••• (any Path)","sum":"Practiced most frequently by both the Assamites and Tremere, though according to vastly different principles of magic, this Discipline heightens the power of the Amaranth to steal memories and knowledge.","fx":"This power may be used whenever a character successfully commits diablerie.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"33"},"amr":[{"k":"path:lifeblood","l":4},{"k":"any:quietus","l":4}]},"qLZ6Y37LWqwBoI7E":{"id":"qLZ6Y37LWqwBoI7E","n":"Calm the Guilt","d":"bardo","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Checks","pool":"Composure + Insight vs. Wits + Subterfuge","dur":"The stains the user takes last until rolled away on a Remorse roll as normal.","act":"Full","sum":"The users of Bardo act as mentors and shepards for others struggling with their Humanity. With this power, the user is able to literally alleviate others of their burden and suffering by taking it onto themselves.","fx":"For this power to work, the user must have at least one empty space to receive a stain on their Humanity tracker and the target must have at least one stain and be on Humanity or one of its Paths.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"37"}},"qQ9WL9pZPMOzGRiP":{"id":"qQ9WL9pZPMOzGRiP","n":"Weaving","d":"celerity","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Dexterity + Athletics, Dexterity + Melee or as needed","dur":"One scene","act":"Free","pre":"Rapid Reflexes","sum":"A vampire with this power moves fast enough to perceive projectiles such as throwing knives or bullets as slow, and can sidestep them at leisure. Cost: One Rouse Check","fx":"The user does not suffer diminishing dice pools when defending against multiple ranged attacks using Dexterity + Athletics or with Dexterity + Melee as they may now parry projectiles with weapons.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"45"},"prer":["Rapid Reflexes"]},"qSnQCc4Tm5lKQRU7":{"id":"qSnQCc4Tm5lKQRU7","n":"Aura Memory","d":"mytherceria","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Insight","dur":"One turn","act":"Full","sum":"With this power, the vampire can absorb emotions and impressions off objects and places, allowing them to relive them while they ingest them. They touche the object, and remove its identity.","fx":"The player makes a Resolve + Insight roll, with the Difficulty determined by the Storyteller based on the age of the impressions and the mental and spiritual strength of the person who left them (Difficulty should not exceed 6).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"93"}},"qUvG0ZkEQup13HXx":{"id":"qUvG0ZkEQup13HXx","n":"Saturn’s Flux","d":"alchemy","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"As mentioned above, the effect kicks in within a day’s span of ingestion—sometimes waking Kindred from daysleep with agonizing cramps. Until used, the pellet seems to stay fresh indefinitely. Given that this stuff has only been around two years, it may just be that its shelf life has not yet been reached.","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, phlegmatic mortal blood, lead, laxative, horse hair.","sum":"This is a drug that breaks Blood Bonds, which is a pretty big deal.","fx":"To gain the effect, smoke it in a steel pipe on a bed of ash, taking precautions as Kindred must for dealing with a small open flame.","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"80"}},"qbIcKwXEQXuQyDEb":{"id":"qbIcKwXEQXuQyDEb","n":"Soul Haunting","d":"dementation","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Insight vs. Wits + Composure","dur":"See p. 52.","act":"Full","sum":"A brief speech to a target allows the vampire to touch the sacred or profane within her victim, destroying the banal concerns that keep those urges from making themselves known.","fx":"For this power to be activated, the user must converse with the victim for at least 3 turns and then roll Manipulation + Insight vs.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"66"}},"qpF0h7xYQWnh69ca":{"id":"qpF0h7xYQWnh69ca","n":"Mystic Sight","d":"auspex","lv":2,"cost":"Free","pool":"Intelligence + Awareness","dur":"One Scene","act":"Passive","am":"Any Blood Sorcery Path ••","pre":"Sense the Unseen","sum":"Referred to as “Quintessence Detection” by those Tremere who still know the meaning of these words and “Thaumaturgical Sight” by newer Tremere, this power allows its user to visualise magical effects that would otherwise have gone unnoticed.","fx":"Whenever a magic power is within their sensory range, the user may roll Intelligence + Awareness against a difficulty equal to the number of successes on a magic.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"27"},"amr":[{"k":"any:path","l":2}],"prer":["Sense the Unseen"]},"rFXxDF3yMZyknNcz":{"id":"rFXxDF3yMZyknNcz","n":"Nightingale’s Song","d":"dominate","lv":4,"cost":"N/A","pool":"As Mesmerise","dur":"N/A","act":"N/A","am":"Mytherceria 3","sum":"Dominate ordinarily cannot be used to force someone to tell the truth, but fae magics help you steal secrets. You can use Mesmerse to demand a target reveal a secret.","fx":"After successfuly ordering a subject with Mesmerise to reveal a secret, they reveal it; however, without a cleverly worded order, the secret may be unpredictable or just random, especially if it is \"Tell me what you know!\" or \"Tell me your secret!\".","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"75"},"amr":[{"k":"mytherceria","l":3}]},"rGKDezwrfWjwXbVw":{"id":"rGKDezwrfWjwXbVw","n":"Food Stain","d":"alchemy","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"Once created, the mystic potential of the substance persists until consumed or applied, but it starts to smell pretty bad after a week, even if refrigerated.","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, melancholic mortal blood, some highly colored flavoring such as BBQ sauce, mustard, cheez-puff flavor dust, etc.","sum":"Resembling ketchup, this elixir places a mark on a person who consumes it or is anointed with it. The alchemist can easily tell whether anyone later drinks the blood of the marked individual.","fx":"If someone — mortal or Kindred — is marked by consuming or contacting this goo, the next individual who feeds from them becomes obvious to the alchemist who made it.","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"74"}},"rd0W3n8hv8YhagrT":{"id":"rd0W3n8hv8YhagrT","n":"Traversal","d":"celerity","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Dexterity + Athletics","dur":"One turn","act":"Minor Action -2 dice","sum":"With blurring speed the vampire can run or climb along any surface, including vertical and even liquid mediums.","fx":"Make a Dexterity + Athletics roll with a Difficulty of 3 (inclined surface with traction) to 6 (slick vertical surface, open water), depending on the surface and angle.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"44"}},"roZNEt86wu4EDM7T":{"id":"roZNEt86wu4EDM7T","n":"Suffuse the Edifice","d":"presence","lv":4,"cost":"N/A","pool":"As power transmitted","dur":"As power transmitted or one night, whichever is longer.","act":"Free","sum":"While present in a building or similar locale the vampire is able to extend the powers of Awe, Daunt, and Majesty through the very structure of the building.","fx":"Anyone seeing the building from outside or who are present inside it needs to resist the power used as if the vampire was present, unless the vampire is within eyesight, at which point they themselves becomes the focus.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"125"}},"rpDGXoMpbe1H1kcj":{"id":"rpDGXoMpbe1H1kcj","n":"False Resonance","d":"chimerstry","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check and one Willpower point","pool":"Manipulation + Subterfuge","dur":"One scene. Permanency which makes it permanent until dismissed.","act":"Full","sum":"The user’s Chimerstry extends beyond normal sights now, able to fool even those capable of reading auras.","fx":"Failing to reach the added Difficulty lets the reader see only the false personality the user has crafted, without any hint that the reader is being misled.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"50"}},"rppkuVI6iYAp8LDz":{"id":"rppkuVI6iYAp8LDz","n":"Blur","d":"mytherceria","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene, or until intentionally ended.","act":"Full","sum":"The user appears to blur into a multitude of indistinct copies of themselves, obscuring their location and allowing them to evade the aim of their enemies.","fx":"When attempting to physically dodge or avoid an enemy attack, be it a physical blow or target spell, add half (rounded up) of your Mytherceria rating to the dice pool.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"91"}},"rqa2vLxyf3lAnqAS":{"id":"rqa2vLxyf3lAnqAS","n":"Mask Off","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Distillation roll vs target’s Stamina + Resolve","dur":"One scene","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, choleric and melancholic mortal blood, ground mustard seed, lemon juice, amphetamines, ground match heads.","sum":"Militant thin-bloods use this formula to hit true vampires where it hurts: their precious Masquerade.","fx":"The alchemist creates (or for other Distillations, they or their vessel bleed) a yellow-reddish paste.","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"77"}},"sHnVpdju2w3BjYRD":{"id":"sHnVpdju2w3BjYRD","n":"Unseen Strike","d":"celerity","lv":4,"cost":"Two Rouse Checks","pool":"Dexterity + Athletics vs Wits + Awareness","dur":"One turn","act":"Free","am":"Obfuscate ••••","pre":"Blink","sum":"This lethal power not only allows the vampire to vanish from plain sight but to instantly move to an enemy and deliver a fatal strike.","fx":"Unless the victim can react by beating the user’s Dexterity + Athletics with their Wits + Awareness in a contest, they are unable to defend against the attack and it is made against a set Difficulty of 1.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"45"},"amr":[{"k":"obfuscate","l":4}],"prer":["Blink"]},"sIt5TV48Ishn3Dsk":{"id":"sIt5TV48Ishn3Dsk","n":"Heart Laid Bare","d":"daimonion","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Insight vs. Composure + Subterfuge","dur":"The bonus lasts one night","act":"Minor -2 dice","sum":"While not true mind reading, this Power lets a vampire peer into the subconsciousness of a victim to gain a sense of what they desire — or fear — the most.","fx":"The test is made against Difficulty 0 on unsuspecting mortals, but mortals aware of vampiric abilities — as well as all supernatural creatures — can resist with Composure + Subterfuge.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"56"}},"sJsRBdwpsDPEqSFm":{"id":"sJsRBdwpsDPEqSFm","n":"Draugh of Might","d":"potence","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One night; for vampires, until the next feeding or the vampire reaches Hunger 5","act":"Full","sum":"The Blood of the vampire becomes saturated with the power of Potence, conveying a part of that power to anyone who drinks of it. This is the Potence equivalent of Draught of Elegance (p. XX).","fx":"The drinker gains the same powers as the donor’s, up to that level.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"118"}},"sSurPblZCvZgSdRI":{"id":"sSurPblZCvZgSdRI","n":"Doubletalk","d":"obfuscate","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Persuasion","dur":"One utterance","act":"Free","am":"Auspex •","sum":"Whereas most vampires use the powers of Obfuscate to hide objects or their own actions, some vampire d use it to mask their speech.","fx":"The vampire adds a secret message (up to one sentence) to their words that only a single intended listener can hear.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"97"},"amr":[{"k":"auspex","l":1}]},"sWJ6qvySLugqWsyf":{"id":"sWJ6qvySLugqWsyf","n":"Tear the Rift","d":"daimonion","lv":5,"cost":"Two Rouse Checks","pool":"Intelligence + Occult","dur":"See System","act":"Full","sum":"Vampires cannot call demons through common summoning and binding rituals that mortals can so readily use and must resort to other means such as sorcery. Vampires simply lack something that mortals possess, but what?","fx":"If the vampire knows a celestial or a True Name of a demon, they may use it to summon them by writing it with blood.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"60"}},"saI13KlU4VNstgn4":{"id":"saI13KlU4VNstgn4","n":"Taste of Death","d":"quietuscruciatus","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Stamina +Athletics vs. Stamina + Athletics","dur":"One turn/until the user stops exhaling.","act":"Full/Extended Minor -4 dice","sum":"The vampire softly breathes out a red mist towards their target or around themselves, burning lungs and skins of their victims and.","fx":"Alternatively, the power may be used to create a zone around the user, the range is reduced to half a meter/yard for each dot of user’s Stamina and Potence.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"143"}},"sjCACVJOcmrlxkms":{"id":"sjCACVJOcmrlxkms","n":"Blue State","d":"alchemy","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"The Stain remains until the characters have, at least, a very uncomfortable conversation.","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, melancholy and phlegmatic mortal blood, cobalt.","sum":"A mind-altering elixir with a sludgy cobalt color, when fed to a target or applied to their skin, it forces them to grudgingly and obsessively contemplate the next wrong thing one of their friends or allies does.","fx":"Someone under the effects of Blue State cannot forgive. The next time a friend or ally violates the target’s Convictions, the target takes 1 Stain.","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"76"}},"ssIIy1RGoMBhkJxR":{"id":"ssIIy1RGoMBhkJxR","n":"Rapid Reflexes","d":"celerity","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"While their bodies still can’t defy the laws of nature, vampires with this power perceive events instantly and can react to them with superhuman alacrity.","fx":"With this power vampires suffer no penalty to their defense pools for lack of cover against ranged projectile attacks.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"43"}},"t0dXo7qod19KqPeJ":{"id":"t0dXo7qod19KqPeJ","n":"Aspect of the Higher Beast","d":"spiritus","lv":3,"cost":"N/A","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","pre":"Summon Spirit Beast","sum":"Reaching further into the spirit realms, the user is able to call upon higher spirits to lend them their aid.","fx":"The user gains additional options for their aspects. Note that examples below are related to cultural areas of the Balkan.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"162"},"prer":["Summon Spirit Beast"]},"t0dlbeN9tN2E7J9s":{"id":"t0dlbeN9tN2E7J9s","n":"Heightened Senses","d":"auspex","lv":1,"cost":"Free (but see below)","pool":"N/A","dur":"Until deactivated. Having the power active for longer stretches of time without rest (more than a scene), especially so for high-stimulus environments, might necessitate spending Willpower, at the Storyteller’s discretion.","act":"Free","sum":"The vampire’s senses sharpen to a preternatural degree, giving them the ability to see better where others would not, hear ultrasonic frequencies and smell the fear of cowering prey.","fx":"The user adds their Auspex rating to all mundane perception rolls.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"25"}},"t9ioF9kGISGORqcd":{"id":"t9ioF9kGISGORqcd","n":"Flicker","d":"potence","lv":4,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"Suffused by inhuman prowess, every part of the vampire’s body becomes able to project the sum of their strength.","fx":"Performing unarmed melee attacks or feats of strength now counts as two-dice minor actions.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"119"}},"tDzbPgKEkUkW1Ee1":{"id":"tDzbPgKEkUkW1Ee1","n":"Compel","d":"dominate","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"Charisma + Intimidation vs. Intelligence + Resolve","dur":"No more than a single scene","act":"Full","sum":"With eye contact, the vampire can issue the victim a single-action command, no longer than a short sentence, to be obeyed to the letter. It must be possible to complete the command in a single turn.","fx":"Commanding a resisting victim, a victim the vampire has previously Dominated in the same scene, or another vampire requires a contest of Charisma + Intimidation vs Intelligence + Resolve.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"71"}},"tGBLuctXBZ5qnofu":{"id":"tGBLuctXBZ5qnofu","n":"Godform","d":"serpentis","lv":5,"cost":"One Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene or until willingly ended.","act":"Full","sum":"The true purpose of Serpentis is not only to imitate the divine worshipped by the Followers of Set, but to also become divine and ascend – as Set has promised, once the chains of aeons are shattered.","fx":"When buying this power, the user must make their own cosmetic appearance for their form as each is unique.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"157"}},"tHwkIH4bE0uFrdSk":{"id":"tHwkIH4bE0uFrdSk","n":"Sweat of Guilt","d":"quietusanimae","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Insight vs. the victim’s Humanity/Road rating","dur":"Impairment lasts for a scene","act":"Full","sum":"By reminding a person of how low they have stooped, vizier hurls insults at their core. Vampires break down in blood sweat and mortals cower in front of the vampire.","fx":"The victim must be able to hear the user and have fewer points in Humanity or Road/Path rating than the user for this power to work.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"137"}},"tWPnUzN0UXP6S3i8":{"id":"tWPnUzN0UXP6S3i8","n":"Submerged Directive","d":"dominate","lv":3,"cost":"No Additional Cost","pool":"N/A","dur":"Indefinitely","act":"Passive with Mesmerise","pre":"Mesmerise","sum":"When using Mesmerize, the vampire can now implant a posthypnotic suggestion, allowing the command to remain dormant until a specific stimulus occurs.","fx":"As Mesmerise, though the Storyteller might want to make any rolls in secret. There’s no way of knowing if the submerged suggestion works until the conditions are met.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"73"},"prer":["Mesmerise"]},"tXeXmXzsNFEbKQED":{"id":"tXeXmXzsNFEbKQED","n":"Counterfeit (Level 2 Power)","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"sum":"At level 3, the Alchemist can develop formulae that counterfeit level 2 powers of other Disciplines (and Blood Sorcery powers that affect the caster’s own Blood, but never Rituals).","fx":"Use the counterfeited power’s own cost and system, substituting the Alchemist’s Thin-Blood Alchemy rating for the Discipline rating wherever one is called for.","src":{"book":"Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition Corebook","page":"286"}},"taxy9A1mu4s1PjeU":{"id":"taxy9A1mu4s1PjeU","n":"Fluent Swiftness","d":"celerity","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"The vampire is able to call upon their supernatural speed effortlessly, and rarely tempt their Hunger when doing so.","fx":"Whenever the vampire uses a Blood Surge to augment a Dexterity or Celerity test, they may reroll the Rouse Check.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"43"}},"th40KrNxhKzBc6X8":{"id":"th40KrNxhKzBc6X8","n":"Primal Scream","d":"melpominee","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Charisma + Performance vs. Wits + Composure","dur":"As per system.","act":"Full","sum":"Fear is natural in all beings. Mortals cover before shadows, hide under their blankets against imaginary monsters while the mighty vampires flinch at a mere sight of an open fire.","fx":"The vampires and those with vampiric beasts must make a Fear Frenzy test against a Difficulty of 3.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"88"}},"u2WgMGR7bitPzrDY":{"id":"u2WgMGR7bitPzrDY","n":"Juice Box","d":"alchemy","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"As target formula","ing":"The ingredients required for the original formula, methuselah vitae, and an empty juice box, complete with traces of concentrated fruit juice.","sum":"More than a few Kindred of lower generations have longed for the ability to make use of Thin-Blood Alchemy Formulae.","fx":"Once distilled, the brew must rest in the juice box for 24 hours before activation. The result allows any Duskborn or Kindred to benefit from the brew created by the alchemist.","src":{"book":"Gehenna War","page":"51"}},"uAQMqzj0Z3DDmAjM":{"id":"uAQMqzj0Z3DDmAjM","n":"Reveal the Invisible Leash","d":"auspex","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Insight vs Composure + Resolve","dur":"For as long as the vampire is touching their target","act":"Full","sum":"With a simple touch, the vampire can sense who in a room their target considers themselves subordinate to.","fx":"The vampire must be in physical contact with their target and test Intelligence + Insight vs their target’s Composure + Resolve.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"30"}},"uFWxch9UxqNTqQV4":{"id":"uFWxch9UxqNTqQV4","n":"Fang-Stinger","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse check","dur":"One day","ing":"The Alchemist’s Blood, choleric human blood, foxglove, absinthe, laundry detergent or phosgene","sum":"This poison can be injected into a mortal’s bloodstream, dealing no damage to them (through the miracle of alchemical transformation) but inflicting considerable pain on a blankbody who feeds from them.","fx":"For every success the Alchemist wins by, the victim takes 2 levels of Aggravated damage.","src":{"book":"Second Inquisition","page":"47"}},"uGPVyRDB44Xl3is9":{"id":"uGPVyRDB44Xl3is9","n":"Lethal Body","d":"potence","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"Using this power, the user is capable of causing horrendous damage to mortals, tearing skin and breaking bones with bare fingers.","fx":"The user’s unarmed attacks can now do Aggravated Health damage to mortals, if desired. They also ignore one level of armor per Potence level of the user.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"116"}},"uOZfvOJQGHewhUaI":{"id":"uOZfvOJQGHewhUaI","n":"Slow Job","d":"temporis","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene","act":"Free","sum":"While not able to directly interfere with the living things due to the laws of time not yet heeding the user’s commands to such an extent, the Slow Job allows a user to perform an action that would take seconds much faster — at least that is show it would look to the outsiders.","fx":"When active, this power lets the vampire complete Skill-related tasks that would otherwise take whole turns in the span of a few seconds, and can treat a full action as a minor action.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"168"}},"uV2xkR225muJRtlv":{"id":"uV2xkR225muJRtlv","n":"Cloak the Gathering","d":"obfuscate","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check in addition to the cost of the power extended","pool":"Wits + Subterfuge vs. Wits + Awareness","dur":"As per power augmented","act":"Free","sum":"The vampire can shelter their companions under the cloak of Obfuscate.","fx":"The vampire can extend their power of Obfuscation to a number of additional willing subjects equal to their Wits, plus one for each additional Rouse Check made.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"105"}},"uYsqn4E0rhBdrcRt":{"id":"uYsqn4E0rhBdrcRt","n":"Master of Forms","d":"protean","lv":4,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","pre":"Shape of the Beast","sum":"While most users of Protean can assume one or two animal forms, some users of Protean have a vastly extended repertoire.","fx":"Rather, they can take on the form of any creature that falls within the limits of those abilities, different each time if they so wish.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"130"},"prer":["Shape of the Beast"]},"uZpEJIgvhvNwBVPh":{"id":"uZpEJIgvhvNwBVPh","n":"The Fogue’s Song","d":"melpominee","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"Charisma + Performance vs. Composure + Wits","dur":"One scene. A critical win extends the duration to the rest of the night.","act":"Free","sum":"Fogue, a never-ending audio heard by all Daughters of Cacophony and users of Melpominee, both irritates and distracts those who hear it. By focusing on it, the vampire can extend this “gift” onto other.","fx":"The vampire emits a sound that becomes stuck inside the target’s head, rolling Charisma + Performance vs. the target’s Composure + Wits.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"86"}},"usOM07Vt6CziG8ZC":{"id":"usOM07Vt6CziG8ZC","n":"Visceral Control","d":"dominate","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Intimidation vs. Stamina + Resolve","dur":"One scene","act":"Full","am":"Vicissitude 1","sum":"\"The Wyndham and everything in it obeys me.","fx":"While this can’t cause permanent damage without Terminal Decree, the effects can be quite debilitating.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"73"},"amr":[{"k":"vicissitude","l":1}]},"uwgUavNH2Pqjb5t8":{"id":"uwgUavNH2Pqjb5t8","n":"Hide the Truth","d":"daimonion","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Subterfuge","dur":"One roll","act":"Free","sum":"The vampire can hear their own blood whispering half-secrets, tactics and hints at how best to manipulate and take advantage of those around them.","fx":"The user may reroll a number of dice (including Hunger dice) on a single Insight or a verbal Subterfuge social test equal to vampire’s Daimonion rating + power bonus.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"52"}},"v2PMTD7eeBGikuWJ":{"id":"v2PMTD7eeBGikuWJ","n":"Bane of Spirits","d":"mytherceria","lv":3,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","am":"Daimonion/Spiritus/Ephemera or Necromancy Path 2","sum":"As a mind-influencing Discipline, Mytherceria tends not to afflict spirits, something not even the might true fae or lesser changelings are able to do.","fx":"They may always roll Awareness to catch Mytherceria at work, however.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"93"},"amr":[{"k":"daimonion","l":2},{"k":"spiritus","l":2},{"k":"path:ephemera","l":2},{"k":"path:necromancy","l":2}]},"vN3P5jsvCtSeYwYr":{"id":"vN3P5jsvCtSeYwYr","n":"Putrefaction","d":"thanatosis","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One turn","act":"Full","sum":"By touch alone, the user of Thanatosis is able to call the victim’s flesh to rot and decay, making their punches deliver damage far deeper and devastating blows.","fx":"The user must touch their victim (which can be performed in combat through any combination of Strength or Dexterity + Brawl or Athletics) and make a Rouse Check.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"177"}},"vZLyFincs4LwG8Eh":{"id":"vZLyFincs4LwG8Eh","n":"Fata Morgana","d":"chimerstry","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check, one Willpower","pool":"Manipulation + Subterfuge","dur":"The illusion remains until the vampire chooses to end the illusion or can no longer sense it.","act":"Full","sum":"Fata Morgana allows the vampire to create static illusions that affect any or all of the senses.","fx":"Before making the roll, the user must state what senses they wish to affect.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"48"}},"vylqkCnDxV2fMsg5":{"id":"vylqkCnDxV2fMsg5","n":"Vitae MSG","d":"alchemy","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","dur":"Once someone is anointed, the desire lasts until the next dawn, if they survive.","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, sanguine mortal blood, MSG, powdered sugar, knockoff (not genuine) Chanel No. 5.","sum":"A formula that makes consumption of blood even more pleasurable already has a built-in market.","fx":"Any vampire who sees or smells anyone who has Vitae MSG on them feels an intense desire to feed on them.","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"79"}},"w60Q9LVHSBU68Zbr":{"id":"w60Q9LVHSBU68Zbr","n":"Kingmaker","d":"presence","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"As power used.","act":"Minor -2","sum":"The power called Kingmaker lets the vampire extend their Presence to another individual and grant them social graces that normally is beyond them.","fx":"As a full action and with an additional Rouse Check, the user can provide the benefits of one of their Presence powers to another willing vampire, using their own Skill ratings and Blood Potency bonus of the vampire using Wingman.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"125"}},"wD9unHWOJfmvlWTb":{"id":"wD9unHWOJfmvlWTb","n":"Resist Typhon’s Corruption","d":"bardo","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"Typhon is the plague on this world and the skinchangers are right to refer to it as the great wyrm of corruption.","fx":"The user gains a dice bonus to resist all Frenzies equal to their Bardo rating.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"38"}},"wNpQbOshpube5Gq8":{"id":"wNpQbOshpube5Gq8","n":"Draugh of Decay","d":"thanatosis","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Stamina + Medicine","dur":"One night; for vampires, until the next feeding or the vampire reaches Hunger 5.","act":"Full","sum":"By feeding a Rouse Check of their vitae to another vampire or a ghoul, they are able to share some of their powers of Thanatosis with them.","fx":"The drinker gains the same powers as the donor’s, up to that level.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"180"}},"wRHxHcDPg3OLriuq":{"id":"wRHxHcDPg3OLriuq","n":"Possession","d":"auspex","lv":5,"cost":"Two Rouse Checks","pool":"Resolve + Insight vs. Wits + Subterfuge","dur":"Until ended, voluntarily or involuntarily.","act":"Full","am":"Dominate •••","sum":"With this power the vampire can strip the will of a mortal and completely possess their body, using it as their own.","fx":"This power can only be used on human mortals. If the mortal is a ghoul, they must first be Blood Bound to the user.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"35"},"amr":[{"k":"dominate","l":3}]},"wWBtXrgxBGFUKaJ4":{"id":"wWBtXrgxBGFUKaJ4","n":"Slow Grace","d":"temporis","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","sum":"The vampire’s perceptions of time permanently alter and they perceive everything a bit slower, giving them an edge in making critical moves to maintain balance.","fx":"Note that this power does not allow them to balance on support that cannot take their weight.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"167"}},"woSGamJMnagv5GU3":{"id":"woSGamJMnagv5GU3","n":"Pillar of Osiris","d":"bardo","lv":4,"cost":"Two Rouse Checks","pool":"Resolve + Occult","dur":"Until another area is consecrated with the Pillar of Osiris or until the caster perishes.","act":"Full","sum":"By consecrating and purifying grounds, the user of Bardo is able to erect a spiritual and immaterial monument to Osiris, empowering users of Bardo in the area.","fx":"The user must write out a prayer to Osiris on the floor they wish to consecrate with the effect only effecting an area of about a two-story house.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"40"}},"wp2VMEu0ChEvXfQg":{"id":"wp2VMEu0ChEvXfQg","n":"Entracement","d":"presence","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Charisma + Persuasion vs. Composure + Wits","dur":"One hour plus one per point of margin","act":"Full","sum":"The vampire focuses their unnatural allure on a single person, instilling in them a rapt fascination or infatuation akin to falling head over heels in love or meeting one’s lifelong idol.","fx":"The vampire only needs to gain the subject’s attention and win a contest of Charisma + Insight vs Composure + Wits.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"123"}},"xNJSPTe5PTQJ3THr":{"id":"xNJSPTe5PTQJ3THr","n":"Ending the Watch","d":"valerenwarrior","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check, one Willpower point","pool":"N/A","dur":"Instant","act":"Full","sum":"The Warriors trace their origin to Samiel’s ancient fury in the days after the Second City.","fx":"This power may only be used on non-undead who are either willing to die or are physically impaired.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"190"}},"xXZa9ghLPoHocsFT":{"id":"xXZa9ghLPoHocsFT","n":"Telepathy","d":"auspex","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check (plus one Willpower vs non-consenting vampires or other supernaturals)","pool":"Resolve + Insight vs. Wits + Subterfuge","dur":"Roughly one minute per Rouse Check. Increased to a full scene on consenting subjects.","act":"Full","sum":"At the higher levels of Auspex the vampire can now literally read minds, as well as project their own thoughts into the minds of others.","fx":"The character can detect one surface per point of margin. Some examples include:","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"34"}},"xaKbaL74ogEPjbqp":{"id":"xaKbaL74ogEPjbqp","n":"Meat Shields","d":"fortitude","lv":5,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene, or when the vampire leaves the presence of the affected mortals — whichever comes first.","act":"Free","sum":"In the company of weak mortals (the sick or dying, children, those physically wounded i.e.","fx":"With this Power active, the vampire temporarily increases their Fortitude by a number of dots equal to half the weak mortals present (rounded down).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"84"}},"xeT1yarwl7lC4LRG":{"id":"xeT1yarwl7lC4LRG","n":"Armour of Caine’s Fury","d":"valerenwarrior","lv":4,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Stamina + Resolve","dur":"One scene","act":"Free","sum":"The third eye opens, blazing redder than the setting sun. This radiance spreads along the Salubri’s desiccated veins in a flash until their entire body is enveloped in a web of radiant light that defies wounding.","fx":"For each point of margin, the user gains a point of Armour (stacking with any worn armour) and for each two points of margin (rounded down) the user gains a bonus die on rolls to resist being mentally influenced or cowed, including Fear Frenzy.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"193"}},"xn888xl5cb3hSWbW":{"id":"xn888xl5cb3hSWbW","n":"TLC","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","ing":"The alchemist’s Blood, animal blood, choleric mortal blood, nettles, iron pieces, meat glue.","sum":"The acronym stands for This Lick Cares or possibly Tastes Like Chicken. This formula creates a powder that imbues blood of living animals with the mystical qualities of mortal blood that the Beast craves.","fx":"The alchemist creates (or for other Distillations, they or their vessel bleed and must sift out) a bluish-brown powder.","src":{"book":"Blood Sigils","page":"77"}},"xoSrTH3ouZX9s1JS":{"id":"xoSrTH3ouZX9s1JS","n":"Taste of the Mind","d":"quietussanguinis","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Free","sum":"By sipping blood, those capable of listening to the Blood are able to find out more about the mental constitution and ability of the person","fx":"The user gains a die bonus to all Mental Skill-based rolls against a person whose blood they tasted (even a bite attack provides enough of a sample).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"145"}},"xwuvQRIG2xbQUzfR":{"id":"xwuvQRIG2xbQUzfR","n":"Unholy Mission","d":"daimonion","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"Passive","act":"Passive","am":"Fortitude 1","sum":"Few on this planet are as equipped to destroy and control the infernal as the Baali themselves, and this power is a perfect example of that.","fx":"The vampire gains a dice bonus to resist temptations of sin and infernalism as well as a dice bonus to defend against the powers of Daimonion, Dark Thaumaturgy, Spectre Arcanoi, Fomori powers and demonic powers be they Lores or Arcana.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"54"},"amr":[{"k":"fortitude","l":1}]},"xzI35yXq4yqZusBW":{"id":"xzI35yXq4yqZusBW","n":"Marduk’s Rattle","d":"quietussanguinis","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Resolve + Awareness vs. Composure + Occult (or Fortitude)","dur":"The user’s vitae remains potent in the victim’s system for a week or until the user has activated the power 3 times, using up all of their blood within the victim. This limit is shared with Dagon’s Call.","act":"Full to activate the power. Applying blood depends on the method","sum":"The sorcerers have developed Marduk’s Rattle — a variant of Dagon’s Call that ravages the mind of the person.","fx":"Identical to Dagon’s Call (p. 123 save for it dealing Superficial Willpower damage.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"147"}},"y1rgJrXBee1FZ30o":{"id":"y1rgJrXBee1FZ30o","n":"Star Magnetism","d":"presence","lv":5,"cost":"One additional Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"As power used","act":"Passive","sum":"The Presence powers of the user now effect people viewing them on live feeds or hearing them over the phone. Recorded images or messages do not retain the effect, however.","fx":"Awe, Daunt, and Entrancement can be transmitted through live feeds via screens or phones.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"126"}},"yGBaYV38Ma5W48WD":{"id":"yGBaYV38Ma5W48WD","n":"Quell the Beast","d":"animalism","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Manipulation + Persuasion/Animal Ken/Intimidation vs Stamina + Resolve","dur":"One scene, or a number of turns equal to the test margin plus one.","act":"Full","sum":"By locking eyes with a target, the vampire cows their inner Beast into temporary slumber.","fx":"They will not even act to preserve themselves unless they spend a point of Willpower in order to act for a turn.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"18"}},"ySvlFFGJCJKT5aVN":{"id":"ySvlFFGJCJKT5aVN","n":"Muffle the Steps","d":"obfuscate","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"See general rules for Obfuscate","dur":"One scene or ended by the user.","act":"Free","sum":"Popular among the Banu Haqim who not yet mastered similar gifts from Quietus, this power completely silences the user, nullifying all sound made by them.","fx":"The power gives the user a two-dice bonus to appropriate Stealth tests.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"97"}},"yhe0FJflcfMY4CLb":{"id":"yhe0FJflcfMY4CLb","n":"Sing, O Muse","d":"melpominee","lv":1,"cost":"Free","pool":"N/A","dur":"One Scene,","act":"Free","sum":"Users of Melpominee are often excellent singers, poets and others who have mastered the voice.","fx":"The character gains a dice-bonus on all of their Charisma Performance rolls equal to their Melpominee rating.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"85"}},"yiHe34HY6JOinHtg":{"id":"yiHe34HY6JOinHtg","n":"Measure of Will","d":"auspex","lv":2,"cost":"Free","pool":"Resolve+ Awareness","dur":"One scene, although it can be extended by an additional scene by spending a point of Willpower","act":"Full","sum":"A vampire with this power may gauge the strength of a target’s resolve and identity, often as an exploratory prelude to shattering and reshaping that mind.","fx":"The target does not sense any mental intrusion or foreign malevolence unless the roll botches.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"26"}},"ytdIAOkhChmcJjx5":{"id":"ytdIAOkhChmcJjx5","n":"From Ashes","d":"thanatosis","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"N/A","dur":"The transformation can only be ended by the user willingly ending it, the user awakening from daysleep or torpor or by special magics.","act":"Full","sum":"Using this rare power, the user is able to instantly turn into ash as if they have been burned by the Sun, allowing them to escape certain death and even become immune to sunlight.","fx":"The transformation into a small pile of ash takes a full turn. Once transformed, the user possesses no senses whatsoever other than touch.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"177"}},"z1wsp5qpV9J3DVWE":{"id":"z1wsp5qpV9J3DVWE","n":"Fires of the Abyss","d":"obtenebration","lv":2,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Wits + Occult","dur":"One scene or until ended or destroyed","act":"Free","am":"Daimonion 2","sum":"The vampire summons shadowy extensions from unlit spots in the area, within line of sight. Local shadows distort as they flow across walls and floors and converge on one or more hapless victims.","fx":"The user summons extensions of shadow tentacles wreathed in flame of shadow. Additional arms can be created by splitting the dice pool, enabling the user to engage multiple opponents.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"109"},"amr":[{"k":"daimonion","l":2}]},"z6030VvAq8Au4J1c":{"id":"z6030VvAq8Au4J1c","n":"Leaden Movement","d":"temporis","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check","pool":"Intelligence + Occult vs. Wits + Resolve","dur":"One turn for every two margins, rounded up. The effect is broken when a character suffers damage","act":"Free","sum":"With a gesture, the vampire may now lessen time’s flow to a mere trickle, causing those under the influence of this power to perceive time’s passage in a dizzying blur.","fx":"This power may be activated defensively before a dodge roll and requires a hand gesture (Wits + Occult against the user’s Wits + Subterfuge might detect something unusual).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"169"}},"zIozTbcRbG5C8YK6":{"id":"zIozTbcRbG5C8YK6","n":"Penitent Resilience","d":"fortitude","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse","pool":"N/A","dur":"One scene","act":"Free","am":"Valeren •••","sum":"With this power, a Salubri may briefly walk in the brightest sunlight without fear of injury. His purity defends him, allowing the sun to burn the Curse within and leave the flesh unmarred.","fx":"The vampire may reflexively spend one Rouse Check whenever the vampire is exposed to sunlight. For the Duration, sunlight deals no damage to the character.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"82"},"amr":[{"k":"any:valeren","l":3}]},"zTj3gSCAAn2uSYC8":{"id":"zTj3gSCAAn2uSYC8","n":"Chemically-Induced Flashback","d":"alchemy","lv":3,"cost":"One Rouse Check in addition to the cost of using Ashe","pre":"Concoct Ashe","ing":"A melted-down object belonging to the destroyed vampire.","sum":"By melting down a vampire’s possessions (the more important the better) during Ashe creation, an alchemist infuses the drug with memories from the destroyed vampire.","fx":"When using Concoct Ashe, this formula may be used to imbue remains with the memories of the vampire they once formed.","src":{"book":"Cults of the Blood Gods","page":"46"},"prer":["Concoct Ashe"]},"zodnALJcj1EHi9WH":{"id":"zodnALJcj1EHi9WH","n":"Ink Trace","d":"mytherceria","lv":1,"cost":"One Rouse Check to replicate","pool":"N/A","dur":"The ink is permanent.","act":"Full","sum":"By brushing their hand against writing, a drawing or something printed out in ink; the shapes the ink took are remembered in the Blood of the user.","fx":"Upon inspection, the replicating ink seems perfectly normal, however tests for the composition of the ink will reveal that it is made out of blood, although it cannot identify who’s, due to the blood’s altered state, and it has no sympathetic link.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"91"}},"02swPMg6EXyJ5xtz":{"id":"02swPMg6EXyJ5xtz","n":"Reflections of Hollow Revelation","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"The mystic smears black liquid (usually ink or tar) onto a reflective surface like a mirror or a crystal ball or mixes it with water to the point where it can no longer be seen throug.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"255"},"seq":"Maintaining the window requires concentration, however; the caster loses two dice from Awareness dice pools as long as the window is active.","tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Only"},"0WYPkEyFiIWLnXSL":{"id":"0WYPkEyFiIWLnXSL","n":"Gaze of Rigor Mortis","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"decay","sum":"The user’s eyes turn into portals to the deepest pits of the Underworld.","fx":"The sorcerer may spend a point of Willpower and look at a target, rolling Composure + Resolve against their Stamina + Resolve.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"280"},"aspects":"Duration","tag":"Decay Ritual (••)."},"0apYi3SCukox76ab":{"id":"0apYi3SCukox76ab","n":"Retarding Age","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"alchemy","sum":"A regimen of drugs or potions that slows aging. For each year of life on this regimen, the user only ages one month.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"265"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (••••)."},"0engH2bSdLicvvq4":{"id":"0engH2bSdLicvvq4","n":"Corruption (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"corruption","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"278"},"aspects":"Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special conditions), Number of Targets, Range and the Special Effects described below. This form of casting requires either eye contact (Resolve + Intimidation vs the target’s Wits + Awareness) or for the sorcerer to make a certain hand gesture (detectable by Wits + Occult vs. the sorcerer’s Wits + Subterfuge).","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"0nKuk8jtoep0BRLl":{"id":"0nKuk8jtoep0BRLl","n":"Eyes of the Dead (Nagaraja)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"necromancy","sum":"Perceiving the hand of entropy like ghosts, the caster can see if someone is injured, diseased, or dying, as well as whether the individual labors under any sort of curse or baleful magic.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"331"},"tag":"Necromancy Special Effect (•). Aspects: Duration and the Necromancy Special Effects."},"0vhbTG0ZT7pH2cOl":{"id":"0vhbTG0ZT7pH2cOl","n":"Endless Bound","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"conveyance","sum":"The only problem with the Path of Conveyance is that it is limited by Aspects for travelling. With this ritual, the user is able to go anywhere they want.","fx":"This ritual works (other than the time required) like a typical use of the Path, except that Distance is replaced by the Ritual’s Special Effect Aspect and that the user can travel as far…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"278"},"aspects":"Passengers, Travel Speed","tag":"Conveyance Ritual (•••••)."},"0zBp2fHxvvwwr8Zy":{"id":"0zBp2fHxvvwwr8Zy","n":"Perspeculor","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"pathofskulls","sum":"Using this ritual on a skull gives the caster the complete skillset of the individual it belonged to, including exceptional skills, specialties and attributes.","fx":"The sorcerer learns of capabilities of the previous skull’s “owner”: Attributes, Skills and Specialties of the character with great accuracy.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"376"},"aspects":"Number of Tartets","tag":"Path of Skulls Ritual (••)."},"16bUdgaYnQ5k2Vtj":{"id":"16bUdgaYnQ5k2Vtj","n":"Preserve Cadaver","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"reanimation","sum":"All necromancers using cadavers for their necromantic arts, or for eating them, want to prevent the stink from giving away their Haven or the cadaver to rot beyond use for their arts. This Ritual was developed b","fx":"Hunger slaked through this cadaver does not count as draining and killing a target and blood will yield no Resonance,.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"343"},"aspects":"Duration, Number of Targets","tag":"Reanimation Ritual (•)."},"1ElWw7n3rQEDPqDb":{"id":"1ElWw7n3rQEDPqDb","n":"Mass Hysteria","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"fear","sum":"One of the most horrific rituals ever to have been created, Mass Hysteria extends the fearmongering effects of this Path into a large radius.","fx":"This ritual has a cost of Rouse Checks equal to the rank of the Distance Aspect that cannot be rerolled in addition to the activation Rouse Check.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"308"},"aspects":"Distance, Duration, Fear Intensity","tag":"Fear Ritual (••••)."},"1NiaokhivUTEhm33":{"id":"1NiaokhivUTEhm33","n":"Exedo Animum","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"pathofskulls","sum":"Path of Skulls Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Number of targets (skulls targeted), duration (the duration aspect is always counted as one higher) as well as one of the following","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"376"},"tag":"Path of Skulls Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Number of targets (skulls targeted), duration (the duration aspect is always counted as one higher) as well as one of the following"},"1hsEuLWX8LKOjMsv":{"id":"1hsEuLWX8LKOjMsv","n":"Writ of Passage","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A sorcerer probably does not want their guest to be shocked by just about every protective spell they set within their home, not to mention that the standard way of excluding people from effects of wards by using their…","fx":"Win on the Ritual Test allows a target carrying the copy of the permission to pass unharmed through the wards the sorcerer designated at the creation of the permission (any and all of the…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"295"},"aspects":"Duration (ranks count as doubled),","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (••)."},"1qfNywuZD5KHLDzv":{"id":"1qfNywuZD5KHLDzv","n":"Locating the Oubliette","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"The ritualist mixes a dark liquid (usually ink or tar) with their own blood before smearing it across their eyes.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"252"},"seq":"Until the mystic arrives or the ritual’s duration ends, the sorcerer loses a die from all rolls not directly made to travel to the Oubliette as fast as possible as the Abyss continually beckons them.","tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (•). Aspects: Only"},"1rtts7VYcjskazMs":{"id":"1rtts7VYcjskazMs","n":"Saint Vitus’ Dance","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"masteryofthemortalshell","sum":"The infamous St. Vitus’ Dance, also known as Dance Mania and more famously as the Dancing Plague, was an event during which men, women and children alike danced until they dropped dead.","fx":"On the sorcerer’s win, the victims begin to dance and can take no physical actions other than direct themselves where to dance to and they can still dodge.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"330"},"aspects":"Duration, Number of Targets, Sympathetic Connection. Alternatively, Duration and Distance (as a radius).","tag":"Mastery of the Mortal Shell Ritual (••••)."},"283h8Gd7kUxE6U15":{"id":"283h8Gd7kUxE6U15","n":"Genius Loci (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"geniusloci","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"360"},"tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"2BxqtByuKAAlCt5m":{"id":"2BxqtByuKAAlCt5m","n":"Spirit Portal (Medium Umbra)","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"ephemera","sum":"This ritual allows the caster to enter the Medium Umbra.","fx":"The consecrated portal begins to glow in pale light when viewed by supernatural senses like the first dot of this Path and stepping through it will physically bring the Passenger Aspect’s worth of people into the spirit world physically.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"305"},"aspects":"Duration, Passengers","tag":"Ephemera Ritual (•••••)."},"2FfcxgmHbUmU94pz":{"id":"2FfcxgmHbUmU94pz","n":"Weight the Virtues (Followers of Set)","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"necromancy","sum":"Resisted by Wits + Subterfuge of a once-living being (ghosts, vampires, corpses: inanimate dead usually cannot resist) within the line of sight, each margin reveals a different deed to the caster from the most recent to the oldest.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"332"},"tag":"Necromancy Special Effect (••). Aspects: Duration and the Necromancy Special Effects."},"2Xl8624z6faR4FHz":{"id":"2Xl8624z6faR4FHz","n":"Urges","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"corruption","sum":"Corruption Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special conditions), Number of Targets, Range and the Special Effects described below.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"279"},"tag":"Corruption Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special conditions), Number of Targets, Range and the Special Effects described below. This form of casting requires either eye contact (Resolve + Intimidation vs the target’s Wits + Awareness) or for the sorcerer to make a certain hand gesture (detectable by Wits + Occult vs. the sorcerer’s Wits + Subterfuge)."},"2b6jMgipurdBAzbF":{"id":"2b6jMgipurdBAzbF","n":"Calix Secretus","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A small item is hallowed out and filled with blood or other liquid, up to 3 Hunger’s worth/3 pints.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"290"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (••). Aspects: The"},"2c4gQr54UTHL4Cgn":{"id":"2c4gQr54UTHL4Cgn","n":"Communicate with Kindred Sire","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"The caster uses the bond between sire and childe to open a bridge between minds, allowing the childe to create a telepathic link for the purpose of long-distance communication.","fx":"A win allows silent mental communication between the sire and childe for the rest of Duration. Any major disturbance on either end breaks the connection.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"323"},"aspects":"Duration","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (••)."},"2uH3J7acxLELK5qw":{"id":"2uH3J7acxLELK5qw","n":"High Winds or Heavy Sandstorm","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"weathercontrol","sum":"The wind speed rises to around 30 miles per hour or 50 kilometers per hour, with gusts of up to twice that. Ranged attacks are much more difficult: −3 dice penalty to firearm attacks and thrown weapons and archery.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"358"},"tag":"Weather Control Ritual (•••)."},"3ORGDQ2HBsQ5ouZH":{"id":"3ORGDQ2HBsQ5ouZH","n":"Preservation","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"enchantment","sum":"This Warding Circle variant allows a sorcerer to protect an object against the ravages of time.","fx":"The item withstands damage from normal wear and tear and the passage of time.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"294"},"aspects":"Duration (count ranks as doubled)","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (•)."},"3Q6UsuwNkZjdDEva":{"id":"3Q6UsuwNkZjdDEva","n":"Extraction","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"conjuration","sum":"A ritual frequently hung “just in case”, Extraction allows the sorcerer to take fallen or overwhelmed companions out of battle and to safety.","fx":"The willing targets are all transported right next to the sorcerer.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"275"},"aspects":"Distance, Weight, Number of Targets","tag":"Conjuration Ritual (••••)."},"3Um6BbEIKj12etnj":{"id":"3Um6BbEIKj12etnj","n":"Animate Vegetation","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"thegreenpath","sum":"The Green Path Special Effect (••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets (individual statblock as targets), Range and Green Power","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"353"},"tag":"The Green Path Special Effect (••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets (individual statblock as targets), Range and Green Power"},"3rrIC4a36to7KnIj":{"id":"3rrIC4a36to7KnIj","n":"The Banks of the Basca","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"transylvaniankraina","sum":"When the rains come in the Carpathians, the Bâsca leaps its banks and whole villages are swept away, along with any person, living or dead, unwise enough not to seek higher ground.","fx":"The koldun then makes a Rouse Check and performs a Spell Test using the Aspects of Duration, Range and Damage + Banks of the Basca (Aspect 3).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"368"},"aspects":"None, but the Spell Test uses Damage, Duration (how long the spell will go), Distance (how far the water will be empowered to go) and range (how wide the water will flow).","tag":"Transylvanian Kraina Ritual (•••)."},"4HGvOruei7KDUEci":{"id":"4HGvOruei7KDUEci","n":"Scry the Heartstone","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"enchantment","sum":"Those who would trace this ritual’s origins find two possibilities, one being a similar Gargoyle ritual and another a Tzimisce rite to keep their domain under control.","fx":"The sorcerer may sense the presence of all within an area.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"300"},"aspects":"Distance, Duration (ranks count as doubled)","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (•••••)."},"4icJU5A7i8enlGj5":{"id":"4icJU5A7i8enlGj5","n":"Amaranth’s Veil","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"enchantment","sum":"Those using supernatural powers to detect signs of diablerie must score two more margins/Difficulty increases by two or else they do not detect it. They detect everything else according to the normal Contest.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"289"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (••). Aspects: The"},"4zXcrhGiDcpU7hSJ":{"id":"4zXcrhGiDcpU7hSJ","n":"Vampire Strength","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"alchemy","sum":"The user gains three ranks’ worth of Potence powers, using the Potence rating of the vampire whose blood was used in this formula.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"266"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•••••)."},"5HtDcCDBwxxYWsb7":{"id":"5HtDcCDBwxxYWsb7","n":"Aura of Decay","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"decay","sum":"First probably invented by the Nagaraja, this Ritual merges the entropic energies of the Underwrold with that of the user.","fx":"The sorcerer sorcerer begins to radiate an aura of decay that lasts until ended or Duration expires (careful not to go to coffin with this activate — one might crumble the house above them).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"280"},"aspects":"Duration, Range (Radius) and Time Period (count as higher by one)","tag":"Decay Ritual (••)."},"5P37b3b1Nb1jqFRA":{"id":"5P37b3b1Nb1jqFRA","n":"Craftmaster","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"alchemy","sum":"This formula requires at least one Hunger’s worth of blood from someone.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"262"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (••)."},"5Pcq7Uiy1Bqd2R4e":{"id":"5Pcq7Uiy1Bqd2R4e","n":"Voice from the Abyss","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"abysscommunion","sum":"The mystic is able to send a message across the Abyss right into one who has had experience with the it.","fx":"Recipients must either possess one dot in Obtenebration or have visited either the Abyss itself or an Oubliette, carrying the shard of the Abyss with them wherever they may go.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"251"},"tag":"Abyss Communion Ritual (•••)."},"5PeOxjC1x3BnJeOO":{"id":"5PeOxjC1x3BnJeOO","n":"Death Curse","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"fortune","sum":"Not even practitioners of magic are above the feelings of hatred and desire for vengeance. With the Death Curse, the sorcerer takes their own life, ensuring that the curse plagues the victim.","fx":"The sorcerer gains a number of additional dice on this ritual equal to their current undamaged Willpower.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"313"},"aspects":"Per curse cast, but usually variant with the Sympathetic Connection is used, allowing the sorcerer to curse their victim’s bloodline.","tag":"Fortune Ritual (•)."},"6GqMvhzIbIiqzRr0":{"id":"6GqMvhzIbIiqzRr0","n":"Angra Mainyu Consumes Spenta Mainyu","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"The mystic drinks a goblet of hot tar (Stamina + Composure Test Difficulty 3 to not throw it up and continue the ritual) and suffers two points of Aggravated Health damage before making the Ritual Test.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"254"},"seq":"While the tar is inside the body, aura-reading powers may reveal the black tar which may confuse some to be the signs of diablerie while those in the know will recognise it as markings of an abyss mystic.","tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Only"},"6KCb1GGcDjLs5bMp":{"id":"6KCb1GGcDjLs5bMp","n":"Fortune (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"fortune","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"309"},"aspects":"Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special conditions), Number of Targets, Range and either Blessing or Curse Special Effects described below. This form of casting must be followed with a verbal curse within the victim’s earshot. The sorcerer can try to conceal it using less-known languages, but the observers can still try to roll Wits + Occult vs. the caster’s Wits + Subterfuge to try to discern negative and maledictive intent.","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"6LHAFY4Fwnw11jyW":{"id":"6LHAFY4Fwnw11jyW","n":"Marionette","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"masteryofthemortalshell","sum":"The victim’s body is under the control of the sorcerer who may perform actions with it using their casting Attribute + appropriate Skill like Melee or Aim.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"330"},"tag":"Mastery of the Mortal Shell Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets, Range and the following."},"6dNfOoDhy9G0JfkS":{"id":"6dNfOoDhy9G0JfkS","n":"Elemental Forces (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"elementalforces","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"284"},"aspects":"Damage, Range, Area, and the Special Effects:","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"6h3w1VkIX1evK9JE":{"id":"6h3w1VkIX1evK9JE","n":"Scrying Mirror","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"enchantment","sum":"The mirror allows for observation of a location or a person. Observing a designated person or a location is done by fulfilling the Sympathetic Connection Aspect.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"293"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: The"},"6qnnJeZqHaEzWTTX":{"id":"6qnnJeZqHaEzWTTX","n":"Unblinking Eye","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"corpseinthemonster","sum":"The necromancer casts an enchantment of vigilance that will enable them to awaken if something threatens their body in sleep or torpor.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"371"},"tag":"Corpse in the Monster Special Effect (•). Aspects: Corpse State"},"7TuSPTtHLShjEA71":{"id":"7TuSPTtHLShjEA71","n":"Homunculus","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"alchemy","sum":"One of the magna opera of alchemy, this formula creates a small artificial living being with some semblance of the alchemist themselves, frequently used as an assistant or a magical child.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"265"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•••••)."},"7oDU8nWgQKCTHvxO":{"id":"7oDU8nWgQKCTHvxO","n":"Awakening Dirt","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"enchantment","sum":"Grave dirt that the user sprinkles around where they will be sleeping. If the caster is threatened during their sleep, dreams will notify them of danger and they gain a five-dice bonus to Awakening.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"289"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•). Aspects: The"},"7sVMs0x23Tnofph2":{"id":"7sVMs0x23Tnofph2","n":"Oplite's charge","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"battle","sum":"All targets in range count their dexterity as 2 higher to calculate movement speed and gain an additional dot to the relevant skill for rolls made for rapid movement (parkouring, going through difficult terrain etc.)","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"267"},"tag":"Battle Special Effect (•). Aspects: Number of Targets, Range (as a radius)"},"7uoL05A0L7uYvqOb":{"id":"7uoL05A0L7uYvqOb","n":"Aegis","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"battle","sum":"Every target in range counts as having an armour value of 4. Does not stack with armour that is already worn.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"267"},"tag":"Battle Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Number of Targets, Range (as a radius)"},"7xTC3fRHYXqM4gHW":{"id":"7xTC3fRHYXqM4gHW","n":"Fascination (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"fascination","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"305"},"aspects":"In addition to the Aspects of Number of Targets, Range, and Sympathetic Connection, Fascination uses the Allure and Willbending Aspects.","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"7xTwKxIrCyTOHBwC":{"id":"7xTwKxIrCyTOHBwC","n":"Dedicate the Haven","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"enchantment","sum":"Probably one of the most commonly practiced rituals among masters of sorcery, Dedicate the Haven creates an unbreakable bond between a home and its master.","fx":"The ritual has been successfully performed.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"297"},"aspects":"None, see system.","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (••••)."},"8EyGSXL68yZS3ffn":{"id":"8EyGSXL68yZS3ffn","n":"Tame the Maddening Flame","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"enchantment","sum":"With the emergence of firefighters and fire extinguishers, this ritual often goes overlooked.","fx":"See systems for Warding Circles like increasing their size in Binding, Summoning and Warding Path.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"295"},"aspects":"Range(as a radius), Duration (ranks count as doubled)","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (••)."},"8Z74GuU1SazrWXQ3":{"id":"8Z74GuU1SazrWXQ3","n":"Dead Eyes","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"alchemy","sum":"A salve that can be applied to the eyes to allow the user to perfectly see everything through the Shroud for one night. Requires an eye of a dead person in the recipe.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"264"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•••)."},"8piLX7q11fOklPLM":{"id":"8piLX7q11fOklPLM","n":"Forced Medium","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"necromancy","sum":"Mediums are the people born with the natural ability to deal with the spirit worlds. They are who ghosts will come to in order to either ask them to solve a problem or else take over their body to compel them do so.","fx":"The target (who may resist with Composure + Resolve against the successes on the Ritual Test), acquires the Medium Merit (p.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"336"},"aspects":"Duration","tag":"Necromancy Ritual (•••)."},"8rwnYxX23SlKZDF3":{"id":"8rwnYxX23SlKZDF3","n":"Reinforced Jacket","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A piece of outfit granting four points of Armour that does not stack with normal armour.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"289"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•). Aspects: The"},"8zCEAUWTMoNAomdW":{"id":"8zCEAUWTMoNAomdW","n":"Uninvisibility Dust","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"alchemy","sum":"A dust that reveals invisible objects or creatures and disrupts illusions (typically, the successes on the formula’s creation roll are compared with successes of an illusion or invisibility power.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"264"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•••)."},"8zICSnan3m7MwRcC":{"id":"8zICSnan3m7MwRcC","n":"The Third Eye of Richard Argentis","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"This ritual summons forth a mysterious dark third eye, forged from abyssal energies, which rests upon the caster’s forehead and protects them from harm.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"253"},"seq":"Beyond having an inky-black orb in the middle of their forehead?","tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (•). Aspects: Only"},"92K2SZlDnIFA4aEq":{"id":"92K2SZlDnIFA4aEq","n":"Intimations of Mortality","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"corpseinthemonster","sum":"By evoking experiences of a human, the caster brings in the best and worst of humanity within them.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"372"},"tag":"Corpse in the Monster Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Corpse State"},"9AqX1WLk9bYdsSpg":{"id":"9AqX1WLk9bYdsSpg","n":"Breath of Flame","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"enchantment","sum":"The Gargoyle gains the ability to spit flammable vitae by making a Rouse Check and rolling Composure + Firearms vs. Dexterity + Athletics. On a win, + target takes three points of Aggravated Health damage.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"302"},"tag":"Enchantment Ritual (•••)."},"9DAwcHIaPhGF0c7O":{"id":"9DAwcHIaPhGF0c7O","n":"Healing (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"healing","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"314"},"aspects":"Healing, Number of Targets, Range.","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"9K8OOykjdHkH9lJs":{"id":"9K8OOykjdHkH9lJs","n":"Lazarus Rises","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"reanimation","sum":"This Ritual enables a necromancer to bring a freshly-dead body back to life, though not how its relatives and friends might remember it.","fx":"Following a successful Ritual roll (Difficulty 6), a wraith can enter the freshly-dead body and live in it as if it were their own.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"349"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Reanimation Ritual (•••••)."},"9T34Z2EgCl9I0x0K":{"id":"9T34Z2EgCl9I0x0K","n":"Maw of Ahriman","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"The ritualist’s mouth or another orifice becomes a void of inky blackness, destroying inanimate objects placed within in a matter of seconds.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"253"},"seq":"The ritualist cannot speak if the power was used on the mouth, as it most commonly is nor can they slake Hunger while this Gift is in effect, though, as any blood swallowed is annihilated.","tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (••). Aspects: Only"},"9f8owkaKG65vcNy3":{"id":"9f8owkaKG65vcNy3","n":"Alluring","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"fascination","sum":"Fascination Special Effect (••). Aspects: In addition to the Aspects of Number of Targets, Range, and Sympathetic Connection, Fascination uses the Allure and Willbending Aspects.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"306"},"tag":"Fascination Special Effect (••). Aspects: In addition to the Aspects of Number of Targets, Range, and Sympathetic Connection, Fascination uses the Allure and Willbending Aspects."},"9twlYG4qCcnEUckE":{"id":"9twlYG4qCcnEUckE","n":"Weather Control (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"weathercontrol","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"357"},"aspects":"Distance (treat the measurement as the radius of effect), Duration, and the following:","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"ABM6wvUnvaBUU9Ld":{"id":"ABM6wvUnvaBUU9Ld","n":"Flight","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"conveyance","sum":"Rather than relying specifically on moving from point A to point B, this ritual grants the caster or an other subject the ability to fly at their normal running speed, whether using a traditional tool like a witch’s…","fx":"The sorcerer may fly without having to recast the Path Spell over and over again. They retain the same sort of maneuverability they’d have running at the same speed.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"277"},"aspects":"Duration","tag":"Conveyance Ritual (•••)."},"ACBgrmDxT1JpqUSg":{"id":"ACBgrmDxT1JpqUSg","n":"Detox","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"alchemy","sum":"The user reduces damage from poisons by one for each margin on the Ritual Test. Once the protection is spent or the night ends, the effect goes out.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"261"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•)."},"ADYqnO6zXhm0F6M1":{"id":"ADYqnO6zXhm0F6M1","n":"Alcohol enhancer","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"alchemy","sum":"A powder that enhances alcohol. The drinker must roll Stamina + Resolve (Difficulty 4) or they fall asleep within turns equal to 5 minus the margin of failure.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"261"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•)."},"AE7kgbGzswtX8u7X":{"id":"AE7kgbGzswtX8u7X","n":"Smoldering Ruin","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"elementalforces","sum":"The most common target of the Lure of Flames is an individual enemy. It’s directly offensive magic, and blood magicians know it and use it as such. Sometimes, targeting individuals and even groups is too small scale.","fx":"Targets taking damage must succeed on a Dexterity + Survival roll (difficulty 3) or catch fire (see Lure of Flames/Balefire system for continous damage).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"287"},"aspects":"Range, Damage","tag":"Elemental Forces Ritual (•••••)."},"AJeHWcSVn18RPu6M":{"id":"AJeHWcSVn18RPu6M","n":"Soul of the Earth","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"enchantment","sum":"The Gargoyle is now able to embrace animals, turning them into Gargoyle animals. If the Gargoyle was at least of the 10th Generation, the animal also gains a dot in Flight and automatically grows wings.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"302"},"tag":"Enchantment Ritual (••)."},"AgEdDu0pHxlfJdvo":{"id":"AgEdDu0pHxlfJdvo","n":"Witches’ Runes","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"enchantment","sum":"In a given space, only the witch who cast them may can use their magic.","fx":"The full weight of Countermagic is brought upon everybody but the sorcerer (and those whose blood was mixed into the material used in the process).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"300"},"aspects":"Range (as a radius), Duration (ranks count as doubled),","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (•••••)."},"ApyDQJECXVjTQ0Dx":{"id":"ApyDQJECXVjTQ0Dx","n":"Heavy fog, rain, sandstorm or snow","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"weathercontrol","sum":"As Fog or a light breeze, Drive and Awareness and other perception rolls are impaired to a much greater extent; inflicting a -3 dice penalty.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"358"},"tag":"Weather Control Ritual (••)."},"AskqceHEs15b1pEO":{"id":"AskqceHEs15b1pEO","n":"Half-Shift","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"shapeshifting","sum":"Shapeshifting Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Duration, Scale and Subject described below. If the sorcerer is transforming others, then Range is also an Aspect.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"351"},"tag":"Shapeshifting Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Duration, Scale and Subject described below. If the sorcerer is transforming others, then Range is also an Aspect."},"AtC1FOTMxhrMI5jS":{"id":"AtC1FOTMxhrMI5jS","n":"Secure the Sacred Domain","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"enchantment","sum":"This potent a warding ritual can be used to close off an entire castle.","fx":"No portal may be lockpicked as the very spirit of the door is commanded not to open except for the sorcerer and those they consider allies (designated at beginning of the ritual).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"299"},"aspects":"Range (as a radius),Protection (ranks count as tripled), Duration","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (•••••)."},"B1PVgLA45zLL38yb":{"id":"B1PVgLA45zLL38yb","n":"Viscera Garden","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"thegreenpath","sum":"Blood sorcerers can grow Blood-addicted plants in special fields, using the crops as magical components or for enjoyment. It’s also a great way to get rid of a body, if the Blood sorcerer has the space.","fx":"In addition, plants grown in the plot are unusually hardy and vampires can ingest them (consuming these plants as food slakes no Hunger, but it stays down).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"354"},"aspects":"None","tag":"The Green Path Ritual (••)."},"B95xVmeblGBZfia4":{"id":"B95xVmeblGBZfia4","n":"Armour of Achilles","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"battle","sum":"All of the targets in range reduce incoming superficial damage (before halving) by 3 and reduce aggravated damage by 1.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"268"},"tag":"Battle Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Number of Targets, Range (as a radius)"},"B9imbtyz19t75f8b":{"id":"B9imbtyz19t75f8b","n":"Banish","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"necromancy","sum":"On a win against Composure + Resolve of targeted ghosts within the line of sight, the ghosts are forced to flee the area for the rest of the Duration.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"332"},"tag":"Necromancy Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Duration and the Necromancy Special Effects."},"BMHc24V7aoxNPopw":{"id":"BMHc24V7aoxNPopw","n":"Detection Blocker","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"enchantment","sum":"An amulet hiding the user from magical perception. When worn, it provides two dice to resist any supernatural power trying to detect the user, read their aura or thoughts.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"290"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••). Aspects: The"},"BMWZKhlKJzMgFS9O":{"id":"BMWZKhlKJzMgFS9O","n":"Brotherhood of Mystics","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"abysscommunion","sum":"Groups practicing Abyssal magics have each developed this ritual out of necessity: those who have given themselves over to the Abyss are both mistrusted and hated so it was important to be able to approach another Shadowed without fear of accidentally alarming a wrong person.","fx":"Only those who adhere to the Road of the Abyss or one of its Paths may perform this ritual with a success.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"251"},"tag":"Abyss Communion Ritual (•)."},"BU6n2Hx1yPUaKkab":{"id":"BU6n2Hx1yPUaKkab","n":"Cloak of Silence","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A cloak that hides the movements of the user. It allows them to move silently and undetected even across squeaky floors. Modern legends say it was developed to defeat the Nightingale floors of Nijo Castle.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"292"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: The"},"BWM2PHwAAxwtfRd9":{"id":"BWM2PHwAAxwtfRd9","n":"Danubian Voices","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"blackseakraina","sum":"Originating in the Black Forest and passing through a dozen nations en route to emptying into the Black Sea, the mighty Danube has been the sustaining artery of countless empires for as long as people have dwelt upon its banks.","fx":"The koldun drips the requisite blood into a river, stream, or other flowing waterway. Even the runoff from thawing snow or a heavy rain is enough to make use of this power.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"363"},"aspects":"Duration, Distance","tag":"Black Sea Kraina Ritual (•)."},"BXeWTN3Zap1svLWz":{"id":"BXeWTN3Zap1svLWz","n":"Benedictio Mortis","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"corpseinthemonster","sum":"By the blessing of death, the caster is able to assume the aspects of a cadaver, shedding many of their vampire weaknesses in turn.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"372"},"tag":"Corpse in the Monster Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Corpse State"},"Bm6WpkADrlvQFPGT":{"id":"Bm6WpkADrlvQFPGT","n":"Theft of Vitae","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"Performs a number of Feeding Actions on the targets equal to the Hunger Aspect, halved and rounded up, in a single turn by opening an arterial wound.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"319"},"tag":"Lifeblood Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Range, Number of Targets, Hunger (see below) and the following special effects"},"Bt5vNtDTkPCo96VB":{"id":"Bt5vNtDTkPCo96VB","n":"Pietrosu’s Hospitality","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"transylvaniankraina","sum":"Mount Pietrosu is the highest, and most dangerous, peak in the Carpathians, where the biting winds and frigid temperatures will kill an unprotected man in mere moments. A perfect setting to destroy one’s enemies.","fx":"Upon successful completion of the rite, the sorcerer is able to activate Pietrosu’s Hospitality making a Rouse Check, tossing their blood into the air (unless they are standing within sight…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"367"},"aspects":"None, but the Spell Test uses Damage, Duration and Range","tag":"Transylvanian Kraina Ritual (••)."},"Btdz1ffH0LmgEqON":{"id":"Btdz1ffH0LmgEqON","n":"Shapeshifting (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"shapeshifting","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"351"},"aspects":"Duration, Scale and Subject described below. If the sorcerer is transforming others, then Range is also an Aspect.","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"CAcpYtURoATSO7gj":{"id":"CAcpYtURoATSO7gj","n":"Weaving the Pontos","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"blackseakraina","sum":"Kolduny who have mastered this rite situate their havens on beautiful beaches made to look like jagged rocks by enchanting the shallow waters to deter anybody from disturbing them.","fx":"If anybody ever perceives the illusions to be a lie, this rite is nullified and must be performed again.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"366"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Black Sea Kraina Ritual (•••)."},"CMdO1HcLHor95FsZ":{"id":"CMdO1HcLHor95FsZ","n":"Blinding the Alloy Eye","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"By infusing a folded soft metal (usually aluminium) with abyssal energies, If successful (the Storyteller should keep the result of the test a secret), cameras around the caster will end up scrambling their image, though they will pick up everything else normally.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"253"},"seq":"Anybody who views the cameras will dream of the endless nothingness that is the Abyss, possibly alerting those in the know of what had happened.","tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (••). Aspects: Only"},"CTMsFsc2svj9f3Gq":{"id":"CTMsFsc2svj9f3Gq","n":"Fix the True Form","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"shapeshifting","sum":"Shapeshifters often find themselves in conflict with one another. They also run into stranger things with multiple forms. It forces anyone targeted by it to take on their “true” form if they.","fx":"The subject must oppose the Ritual Test’s successes with Stamina + Resolve or be transformed.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"352"},"aspects":"Range","tag":"Shapeshifting Ritual (••••)."},"CZ0eyQypwLox4usI":{"id":"CZ0eyQypwLox4usI","n":"Tornado","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"weathercontrol","sum":"Avoiding getting sucked into a tornado is a Strength + Athletics (difficulty 5) test, Modified by things such as having something to hold on or having shelter. Those who fail suffer damage equal to 3 + the margins.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"359"},"tag":"Weather Control Ritual (•••••)."},"CgYV9woJorj9sNNo":{"id":"CgYV9woJorj9sNNo","n":"Mike’s Cure-All","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"healing","sum":"The healer can force a patient’s body to purge all drugs and toxins through any, and sometimes all, possible exits. This includes vomiting, sweat, tears, diarrhea, etc.","fx":"The subject purges of all toxins and drugs.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"316"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Healing Ritual (•••)."},"CrquYnAY76is9JCY":{"id":"CrquYnAY76is9JCY","n":"Decay (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"decay","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"280"},"aspects":"Range, Weight (count as higher by one) and Time Period (count as higher by one):","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"CyZgidcNyjKhZUho":{"id":"CyZgidcNyjKhZUho","n":"Guest’s Herald","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"enchantment","sum":"This ritual places a notification ward on doors or other portals, creating a sound or some visual effect that notifies those close enough to hear or see it whenever a person other than the cast crosses or passes through it","fx":"It can be something that is heard by those nearby or silent. For example, small fireworks or a sound of chiming bells.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"295"},"aspects":"Duration (ranks count as doubled)","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (••)."},"CyjLPfycvPGg1vei":{"id":"CyjLPfycvPGg1vei","n":"Somnifacient","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"alchemy","sum":"Create a powdered or liquid sedative. The compound can be inhaled, ingested or absorbed through skin contact (often applied to a weapon or a projectile). To throw or blow it, Composure + Aim is used vs.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"262"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•)."},"D3C4gCCgRLUu4DKF":{"id":"D3C4gCCgRLUu4DKF","n":"Summon Plant Spirits (Naturae)","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"ephemera","sum":"Reaching into the Middle Umbra, the caster calls upon spirits of plants.","fx":"Caster may send psychic impressions in order to call all closest spirits of plants up to the Number of Targets as described under Ephemera Sample Rituals.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"304"},"aspects":"Number of Targets, Metaphysical Weight 1","tag":"Ephemera Ritual (•)."},"DDSaqn746EpTyMXG":{"id":"DDSaqn746EpTyMXG","n":"Apollo’s Aim","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"battle","sum":"All targets in range ignore Called Shot penalties for any ranged maneuvers.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"267"},"tag":"Battle Special Effect (••). Aspects: Number of Targets, Range (as a radius)"},"DKdGaU2dOP9PkZ26":{"id":"DKdGaU2dOP9PkZ26","n":"Rebirth in the Light of Haqim","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"Each Child of Haqim is initiated to the clan after Embrace with blood from the collective pool called the Heartsblood hidden in Alamut. Their head is anointed with the Blood and their true purpose calls to them.","fx":"The vampire of Banu Haqim may change their caste (a player selects their own while for everybody else it is according to the abilities of the vampire and the Will of Haqim.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"328"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (••••)."},"DMZLlU2exrvuBcQ3":{"id":"DMZLlU2exrvuBcQ3","n":"Fog or Light Breeze","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"weathercontrol","sum":"Vision is slightly impaired and sounds are muffled; a −2 dice penalty is imposed on all Awareness and combat aiming rolls, and the effective range of all ranged attacks are halved.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"358"},"tag":"Weather Control Ritual (•)."},"DiSgGrmWnD771Fnp":{"id":"DiSgGrmWnD771Fnp","n":"Last-Minute teleport","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"conveyance","sum":"Almost identical to the Extraction ritual of the Path of Conjuring, it is also a ritual frequently hung “just in case”. It allows the sorcerer to take fallen or overwhelmed companions out of battle and to safety.","fx":"Identical to extraction ritual (page prior).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"277"},"tag":"Conveyance Ritual (••••)."},"DmMWoPznRSthmYCE":{"id":"DmMWoPznRSthmYCE","n":"Purification of the Inferno","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"elementalforces","sum":"Practiced extensively by the battle magi of the Clan Tremere during the wars with the Tzimisce, Purification of the Inferno punishes with flames the first person to physically touch the sorcerer.","fx":"The first person to touch the magician after the ritual (by accident or design) immediately bursts into flames and takes flat damage equal to half the Damage Aspect (rounded up), including…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"287"},"aspects":"Damage, Duration","tag":"Elemental Forces Ritual (•••)."},"DojDaZf5upJ40ZAD":{"id":"DojDaZf5upJ40ZAD","n":"Host Spirit","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"reanimation","sum":"This Ritual allows a human to open their body to a symbiotic possession by a ghost.","fx":"If the wraith agrees to the proposition, it then enters the willing subjects’s body and can remain according to the Duration.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"344"},"aspects":"Duration","tag":"Reanimation Ritual (•••)."},"DuS4irl5zrUfV6Ic":{"id":"DuS4irl5zrUfV6Ic","n":"Running Shoes","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"enchantment","sum":"Shoes doubling the speed of the wearer when trying to outrun pursuit, giving them additional two points of Dexterity (up to 7).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"292"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (••••). Aspects: The"},"DvlVqXHvi1c7u6Ei":{"id":"DvlVqXHvi1c7u6Ei","n":"Speed Potion","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"alchemy","sum":"A potion that doubles the running speed of anyone who takes it.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"263"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (••)."},"DwJsX1fn2TEM3aH4":{"id":"DwJsX1fn2TEM3aH4","n":"Beguiling","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"fascination","sum":"Fascination Special Effect (•••). Aspects: In addition to the Aspects of Number of Targets, Range, and Sympathetic Connection, Fascination uses the Allure and Willbending Aspects.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"306"},"tag":"Fascination Special Effect (•••). Aspects: In addition to the Aspects of Number of Targets, Range, and Sympathetic Connection, Fascination uses the Allure and Willbending Aspects."},"DxHd7pwQHqQGAnDl":{"id":"DxHd7pwQHqQGAnDl","n":"Minions of Deep Marmora","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"blackseakraina","sum":"Legend says that the koldun Cyzicus, who ruled openly as king of the Dollonians in days of antiquity, discovered if he spilled his blood into the Sea of Marmora, strange beasts from its depths would emerge to do his bidding.","fx":"The koldun splashes some of their blood on the surface of water. Upon the successful completion of the Rite, a number of minions emerge equal to the Summoned Minions Aspect.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"365"},"aspects":"Duration, Summoned Minion (see system)","tag":"Black Sea Kraina Ritual (••••)."},"EFwI9lc1HBIkFGef":{"id":"EFwI9lc1HBIkFGef","n":"Eyes of Charon (Giovanni)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"necromancy","sum":"The caster’s eyes are set ablaze with pale blue flame that is visible from the Shadowlands. The caster can see, hear, and speak to ghosts in their vicinity, whichever side of the Shroud they are on.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"331"},"tag":"Necromancy Special Effect (•). Aspects: Duration and the Necromancy Special Effects."},"EHdrQUmiF62W6tMk":{"id":"EHdrQUmiF62W6tMk","n":"Trusty Firearm","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A custom Aim Skill weapon subtracting two from the success penalty of all called shots.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"290"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (••). Aspects: The"},"EM1LP2he7RnGQDwI":{"id":"EM1LP2he7RnGQDwI","n":"Verdant Haven","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"thegreenpath","sum":"The Green Path Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets (individual statblock as targets), Range and Green Power","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"353"},"tag":"The Green Path Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets (individual statblock as targets), Range and Green Power"},"ETWbW4OvJN4SjgKt":{"id":"ETWbW4OvJN4SjgKt","n":"Supernatural creatures","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"biothaumaturgy","sum":"Scale is unknown, but there is a tale told among Tremere apprentices of Goratrix operating on dragons.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"369"},"tag":"Biothaumaturgy Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: The"},"EigAvUJsQ67zR2It":{"id":"EigAvUJsQ67zR2It","n":"Cruel Whispers","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"illusion","sum":"Illusionists must often be masters of psychological warfare. They can’t create anything truly real, so they play on the fears and anxieties of their targets to control them.","fx":"If they fail and the Duration permits it, the subject may roll their Test again (usually at the end of each day).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"317"},"aspects":"Damage (cannot be greater than Senses; cannot be used if Duration isn’t at least 3), Duration, Number of Targets, Senses (only auditory is required, but more can really deal some psychological damage)","tag":"Illusion Ritual (••)."},"EkqmjflnsRicU951":{"id":"EkqmjflnsRicU951","n":"Mortuus in Vultu","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"corpseinthemonster","sum":"Inducing the corpse-appearance to the subject and stiffness of the body, the caster lowers Dexterity by one and the base Looks Merit by one rank (normal to Ugly, Ugly to Repulsive).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"371"},"tag":"Corpse in the Monster Special Effect (•). Aspects: Corpse State"},"Eng2bTmM1X8xR3XE":{"id":"Eng2bTmM1X8xR3XE","n":"Battle (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"battle","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"267"},"aspects":"Number of Targets, Range (as a radius), and the following:","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"Er3H8wIAfgGlG6fU":{"id":"Er3H8wIAfgGlG6fU","n":"Animate the Inanimate (Lesser)","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"enchantment","sum":"An animated servant (also called an automaton), such as a golem, a corpse or a robot, build it as an Average Mortal.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"291"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (••••). Aspects: The"},"EyzamJUXTvuZxM08":{"id":"EyzamJUXTvuZxM08","n":"Enter the Spirit World","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"geniusloci","sum":"The kolduny are masters of spirits, and a Genius Loci is the lord of the world. With this ritual, the koldun may enter the spirit world known as the Astral Umbra and middle worlds between it and the material world.","fx":"The effect depends on how the process was performed.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"362"},"aspects":"Duration, Passengers","tag":"Genius Loci Ritual (•••••)."},"F5xvlcORxGb0Xj1z":{"id":"F5xvlcORxGb0Xj1z","n":"Gravity Denial","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"conjuration","sum":"Known as “Fuck Newton” among the Anarch sorcerers, Gravity Denial allows the sorcerer to deny or alter gravity within a certain space.","fx":"The sorcerer may remove gravity from an area or shape it as they wish such as making it “centered” on a wall to allow them to walk or on a wall.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"276"},"aspects":"Duration, Range (as a spherical radius)","tag":"Conjuration Ritual (•••••)."},"FLYJpEMesR3GgPuF":{"id":"FLYJpEMesR3GgPuF","n":"Entrancing","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"fascination","sum":"Fascination Special Effect (••••). Aspects: In addition to the Aspects of Number of Targets, Range, and Sympathetic Connection, Fascination uses the Allure and Willbending Aspects.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"307"},"tag":"Fascination Special Effect (••••). Aspects: In addition to the Aspects of Number of Targets, Range, and Sympathetic Connection, Fascination uses the Allure and Willbending Aspects."},"FSRFuklcFabXBPsI":{"id":"FSRFuklcFabXBPsI","n":"Vampire Durability","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"alchemy","sum":"The target takes damage like a vampire, including from Sunlight. Bane Severity counts as a minimum of two.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"266"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•••••)."},"FnDCjuVo7I0IKhQm":{"id":"FnDCjuVo7I0IKhQm","n":"Minor Abyssal Possession","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"By beckoning a small spirit of the Abyss to enter a corpse, the ritualist turns it into an Mindless Corpse similar to that of necromancy (p. XX).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"253"},"seq":"When a corpse is raised in this manner, it is automatically hostile to everybody, but the sorcerer binds it to their will as necromancers do zombies if they possess a dot of Binding, Summoning and Warding Path. If not bought as a Retainer (one dot should suffice for 6 mindless cadavers), the zombie becomes aggressive and uncontrollable after a story as the bond breaks.","tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (•). Aspects: Only"},"Fwc05Xf18RoMB6vz":{"id":"Fwc05Xf18RoMB6vz","n":"Pontos Axeinos","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"blackseakraina","sum":"Before the Greeks settled its southern shoreline, they called the Black Sea Pontos Axeinos, the Inhospitable Sea.","fx":"The koldun may only evoke these effects when close to a large body of water or a source of water that eventually pours itself into a large body of water.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"365"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Black Sea Kraina Ritual (•••••)."},"GAlwsoPQsErDAVlM":{"id":"GAlwsoPQsErDAVlM","n":"Balefire (School: Dark Thaumaturgy)","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"elementalforces","sum":"The Effect is a variant of the Lure of Flames and functions identically save for the following.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"284"},"tag":"Elemental Forces Special Effect (••). Aspects: Damage, Range, Area"},"GDLrZQAqIB3UULSJ":{"id":"GDLrZQAqIB3UULSJ","n":"Boukephos’ Chosen Oubliette","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"The abyss mystic must paint a circle of pitch around the perimeter of an aboveground community – whether a hamlet, village, town, or city. This circle is broken if crossed by a child, or a believer with True Faith.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"258"},"seq":"None.","tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (••••••). Aspects: Only"},"GPkAYFPv1MgEJDUL":{"id":"GPkAYFPv1MgEJDUL","n":"Runes of Power","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"enchantment","sum":"Elders, paranoid of their apprentices reading forbidden tomes, often make use of this power to hide texts from them. Unwary neonates or intruders receive a nasty surprise when they read these words.","fx":"A character who sees the sigil must make a Composure + Resolve roll against the successes on the ritual roll.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"296"},"aspects":"Duration (ranks count as doubled)","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (•••)."},"GUfz2WwyMnBwztLS":{"id":"GUfz2WwyMnBwztLS","n":"Summon Minor Jaggling (Naturae)","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"ephemera","sum":"Reaching into the Middle Umbra, the caster calls upon a random Jaggling to come.","fx":"Caster may send psychic impressions in order to call all closest Jagglings up to the Number of Targets as described under Ephemera Sample Rituals.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"304"},"aspects":"Number of Targets, Metaphysical Weight 2, Spirit Reach 2","tag":"Ephemera Ritual (••)."},"GxqrpDe70RfJ4Kwl":{"id":"GxqrpDe70RfJ4Kwl","n":"Gift of the Immobile Form","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"enchantment","sum":"The ritualist instinctively knows if the ritual was a success, enabling them to predict a disaster and death of their servant.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"302"},"tag":"Enchantment Ritual (••••)."},"H7zrHXu0QJZ0UVJg":{"id":"H7zrHXu0QJZ0UVJg","n":"Summon Selene (Naturae)","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"ephemera","sum":"This Ritual summons a poweful Jaggling named Selene, one of the moon spirits.","fx":"Caster may send psychic impressions in order to call Selene as described under Ephemera Sample Rituals.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"304"},"aspects":"Number of Targets 1, Metaphysical Weight 3, Spirit Reach 3","tag":"Ephemera Ritual (•••)."},"HHoaRCszvqdJgwFw":{"id":"HHoaRCszvqdJgwFw","n":"Earthquake","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"elementalforces","sum":"The ground splits open below Area (count as higher by two) and engulfs, then crushes, the victims while dealing damage (equal to margins on the first roll or twice the Damage Aspect, whichever is lower).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"285"},"tag":"Elemental Forces Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Damage, Range, Area"},"HJBZvu9lwSZYawcY":{"id":"HJBZvu9lwSZYawcY","n":"Contradict","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"corruption","sum":"Corruption Special Effect (•). Aspects: Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special conditions), Number of Targets, Range and the Special Effects described below.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"279"},"tag":"Corruption Special Effect (•). Aspects: Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special conditions), Number of Targets, Range and the Special Effects described below. This form of casting requires either eye contact (Resolve + Intimidation vs the target’s Wits + Awareness) or for the sorcerer to make a certain hand gesture (detectable by Wits + Occult vs. the sorcerer’s Wits + Subterfuge)."},"HYFD53HU5tjlw7oU":{"id":"HYFD53HU5tjlw7oU","n":"Herbal Wisdom","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"thegreenpath","sum":"While not the best conversationalist in general, some plants do indeed have wisdom of the ages or just useful information about who passed by.","fx":"The plant may converse with the caster for the rest of the scene in a telepathic manner.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"356"},"aspects":"Number of Targets, Range","tag":"The Green Path Ritual (•••)."},"HcZQDZVPZMAtbRF1":{"id":"HcZQDZVPZMAtbRF1","n":"Gust of Wind","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"elementalforces","sum":"The spell affects everybody between the caster and Range (from the caster for pushing, to the caster for pulling) and has the width of Area.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"284"},"tag":"Elemental Forces Special Effect (••). Aspects: Damage, Range, Area"},"I3qDOtwXiqeb2kXV":{"id":"I3qDOtwXiqeb2kXV","n":"Master of the Domain","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"transylvaniankraina","sum":"All mortals must fear the Voivode. This rite allows koldun to take fear to the extreme, a perpetual aura of fear manifesting to make the vampire look large, dangerous, and constantly on the edge of frenzy.","fx":"Once the rite’s complete, the koldun gains a permanent additional die to attempts at Intimidation against both mortal and Cainite subjects within their domain.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"368"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Transylvanian Kraina Ritual (•••)."},"I9A4xW6gxyRSalWs":{"id":"I9A4xW6gxyRSalWs","n":"Glyph of Enlightenment","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"enchantment","sum":"Obviously created by the most paranoid of the sorcerers, Glyph of Enlightenment lets the thaumaturge utilise the glyph to send out their voice and even use their powers against enemies through it.","fx":"This ritual has the exact same system as the Glyph of Scrying except that the sorcerer can talk through it while focusing.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"297"},"aspects":"Duration (ranks count as doubled)","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (••••)."},"IHz4iz1jsRGWLWkD":{"id":"IHz4iz1jsRGWLWkD","n":"Dependence","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"corruption","sum":"Corruption Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special conditions), Number of Targets, Range and the Special Effects described below.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"279"},"tag":"Corruption Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special conditions), Number of Targets, Range and the Special Effects described below. This form of casting requires either eye contact (Resolve + Intimidation vs the target’s Wits + Awareness) or for the sorcerer to make a certain hand gesture (detectable by Wits + Occult vs. the sorcerer’s Wits + Subterfuge)."},"IolBvEPOFXJTEvV0":{"id":"IolBvEPOFXJTEvV0","n":"Wiseman’s Skull","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"enchantment","sum":"The skull of a dead person (usually another sorcerer) allowing the user to contact them for assistance.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"292"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (••••). Aspects: The"},"IpLSSd1r3pNmnUpX":{"id":"IpLSSd1r3pNmnUpX","n":"Cauldron of Blood","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"Lifeblood Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Range, Number of Targets, Hunger (see below) and the following special effects","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"319"},"tag":"Lifeblood Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Range, Number of Targets, Hunger (see below) and the following special effects"},"JLVWCvKQaJ7NaFhU":{"id":"JLVWCvKQaJ7NaFhU","n":"Ammorsus Vicarius","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"pathofskulls","sum":"Path of Skulls Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Number of targets (skulls targeted), duration (the duration aspect is always counted as one higher) as well as one of the following","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"376"},"tag":"Path of Skulls Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Number of targets (skulls targeted), duration (the duration aspect is always counted as one higher) as well as one of the following"},"JWHi7y5kaGxGKrFA":{"id":"JWHi7y5kaGxGKrFA","n":"Beasts of the Genius","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"geniusloci","sum":"When a koldun wants to see farther than her Genius Loci would usually allow, she can stand atop a mountain, tower, or other elevated location, and imbue an animal servitor with her Koldun Sorcery.","fx":"While in effect for the Duration (or until the koldun leaves the location of the Rite), the koldun is able to extend their senses through animals affected by this Rite, all at once like a spiritual hivemind.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"361"},"aspects":"Distance (counted as higher by one), Duration, Number of Targets, Passengers","tag":"Genius Loci Ritual (••)."},"Jccafiu1jerGHcg7":{"id":"Jccafiu1jerGHcg7","n":"Sprint","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"conveyance","sum":"Sometimes, a magician needs to travel a short distance quickly. Though preparations vary, mostly by practice, this Ritual always concludes by lacing up a pair of fast blue or red shoes.","fx":"Once they are on, the magician can run faster than any mundane human, so long as no one sees them do so.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"277"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Conveyance Ritual (•)."},"JmBQ18FDvRvnF61Z":{"id":"JmBQ18FDvRvnF61Z","n":"Fearless Heart","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"battle","sum":"All targets in range count their resolve and composure as 1 higher (up to 5)","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"268"},"tag":"Battle Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Number of Targets, Range (as a radius)"},"Jy99Zq1qzhEnQLtv":{"id":"Jy99Zq1qzhEnQLtv","n":"Roll Divination secretly for players","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"divination","sum":"The sorcerer never knows for sure how accurate their visions and interpretations of such might be.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"283"},"tag":"Divination Special Effect (•). Aspects: Divination uses only three Aspects. Time Period (past, present or future) and"},"K4i0HumU6BEzGilo":{"id":"K4i0HumU6BEzGilo","n":"Dust Storm","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"elementalforces","sum":"A storm of dust, scouring the area. Area Aspect is counted as higher by three. Those caught in it resist using Wits + Survival.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"285"},"tag":"Elemental Forces Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Damage, Range, Area"},"KMAm46NYUj5sLFwC":{"id":"KMAm46NYUj5sLFwC","n":"Body of a Sinner (Rosselini)","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"necromancy","sum":"All ghosts within a radius equal to the user’s Composure + Resolve who fail the resistance roll or willingly submit to it are forced to take on a corporeal form, whether they could do so on their own or not, for the Duration.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"333"},"tag":"Necromancy Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Duration and the Necromancy Special Effects."},"KPvDyy8dX6FzLukx":{"id":"KPvDyy8dX6FzLukx","n":"Enrich the Blood","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"This Ritual increases the potency of a human’s blood, allowing the vampire to take the same sustenance from a smaller quantity of blood.","fx":"On a Critical Win, two vampires can slake to Hunger 0 if they share the kill. If left alive, the effect on the target wanes after the Duration.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"321"},"aspects":"Duration","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (•)."},"KSwAns6b5fCWALqV":{"id":"KSwAns6b5fCWALqV","n":"The Unseen Change","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"enchantment","sum":"This ritual forces Lupines into their wolf form.","fx":"This creates a specialised Warding Circle Every werewolf (or another type of skinchanger) must contest the Ritual roll with their Stamina + Resolve.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"297"},"aspects":"Range(as a radius), Duration (ranks count as double)","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (•••)."},"KUtralYgGzEf56Pr":{"id":"KUtralYgGzEf56Pr","n":"Healing Coma","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"alchemy","sum":"The patient remains asleep for 12 hours and awakens with additional 3 superficial health damage healed. The patient cannot be awoken early except by taking a point of Aggravated Health damage. Undead do not benefit.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"262"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•)."},"KdJ3RtIHVY7QFoZp":{"id":"KdJ3RtIHVY7QFoZp","n":"Addiction","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"corruption","sum":"Corruption Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special conditions), Number of Targets, Range and the Special Effects described below.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"279"},"tag":"Corruption Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special conditions), Number of Targets, Range and the Special Effects described below. This form of casting requires either eye contact (Resolve + Intimidation vs the target’s Wits + Awareness) or for the sorcerer to make a certain hand gesture (detectable by Wits + Occult vs. the sorcerer’s Wits + Subterfuge)."},"KdvSi3SUPsOUPAeu":{"id":"KdvSi3SUPsOUPAeu","n":"Daemonic Possession","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"reanimation","sum":"The subject must either be a dead body or a body vacant by Baleful Exorcism.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"342"},"tag":"Reanimation Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets, Range and the following"},"Kk0VIJb0bwdOIQAH":{"id":"Kk0VIJb0bwdOIQAH","n":"Biothaumaturgy (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"biothaumaturgy","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","fx":"The sorcerer may apply one modification onto the subject for each success or margin if the victim is resisting (Stamina + Resolve).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"369"},"aspects":"The following:","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"KtAnqLJhBg9zFdot":{"id":"KtAnqLJhBg9zFdot","n":"Alchemy (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"alchemy","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"259"},"aspects":"Duration (count ranks as doubled), Dose (no limit of the rank) and the following:","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"LMaRenKEP57jDdVS":{"id":"LMaRenKEP57jDdVS","n":"Eyes of Ash","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"necromancy","sum":"The caster can see, hear, and speak to ghosts in their vicinity, whichever side of the Shroud they are on.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"331"},"tag":"Necromancy Special Effect (•). Aspects: Duration and the Necromancy Special Effects."},"LQ4KOGxT9qx6aRsv":{"id":"LQ4KOGxT9qx6aRsv","n":"Unknowing Leap","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"conveyance","sum":"Spells are all quite good and all, but unreliable. This ritual establishes a type of a portal. When a person enters it or steps on it, they are teleported to another designated location.","fx":"However, it removes the extra success required to go somewhere you don’t know about ahead of time, whether by fine tuning instruments or just meditating to improve your focus.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"276"},"aspects":"Same as the Path Spell","tag":"Conveyance Ritual (•)."},"LVr5VtALXfzfb89H":{"id":"LVr5VtALXfzfb89H","n":"Cry that Slays Light","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"Cainite wishing to shout the Cry That Slays Light must spend one week in absolute silence. They may not utter the briefest syllable or they must begin their quiet meditations again.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"257"},"seq":"At the end, the caster rolls their Road rating. Each failed die subtacts one from the character’s Humanity/Road rating. If this sudden degeneration reduces the vampire’s Road rating to zero, they rampage under the cover of darkness and kill everything and everyone they can find. When the darkness ends, it subsumes them into its being and their hunger is added to the Abyss.","tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (••••••). Aspects: Only"},"LX1tuICUuLV2pAfg":{"id":"LX1tuICUuLV2pAfg","n":"Warcry","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"battle","sum":"Make the Spell Test against the opponent’s Composure + Resolve, on a win they take a -2 dice penalty to their next attack against you.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"267"},"tag":"Battle Special Effect (••). Aspects: Number of Targets, Range (as a radius)"},"LdLcr9kQD7OjBKLO":{"id":"LdLcr9kQD7OjBKLO","n":"Darksight","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"The ritualist darkness their eyes and can see in pitch black darkness. Almost a prerequisite for Abyss Mysticism. The Ritualist can only enchant themselves with Darksight.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"252"},"seq":"The ritualist’s eyes grow darker and they lose a die penalty on all positive social interactions with those who can see their eyes.","tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (•). Aspects: Only"},"LdR4cnG7nBywHDBK":{"id":"LdR4cnG7nBywHDBK","n":"Letter Ward","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"bindingsummoningandwarding","sum":"Another form of making sure one’s letters are not read, a Letter Ward is a variant of the standard Ward meant for letters.","fx":"When anyone other than the recipient opens the letter, they must roll Stamina + Resolve vs. the successes on the Ritual Test.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"272"},"aspects":"Damage, Duration (ranks count as doubled)","tag":"Binding, Summoning and Warding Ritual (•)."},"LlR7oCqkB2JWnnXO":{"id":"LlR7oCqkB2JWnnXO","n":"Waves (Minor)","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"weathercontrol","sum":"Targets must beat the sorcerer’s Spell Test with their Stamina + Athletics or else they cannot swim forward.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"358"},"tag":"Weather Control Ritual (••)."},"LqPPrHuvrESUBupq":{"id":"LqPPrHuvrESUBupq","n":"Bar the Common Passage","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"enchantment","sum":"The thaumaturge places a ward on a door or another portal, giving it the strength to withstand even attacks from werewolves.","fx":"The warded object gains additional Health equal to twice the Protection Aspect.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"294"},"aspects":"Duration (ranks count as doubled), Protection (ranks count as doubled)","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (•)."},"LtLuGHV3SVSvOqLk":{"id":"LtLuGHV3SVSvOqLk","n":"Preservation Frame","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"enchantment","sum":"An oak frame that preserves anything placed in it for as long as it remains intact. It can only hold flat things, like documents and paintingss, and must be sealed with almond oil and sprinkled with pure water.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"289"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•). Aspects: The"},"Lwv1YmrzIlh9h1bD":{"id":"Lwv1YmrzIlh9h1bD","n":"Teleport Ward","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"conveyance","sum":"Magicians studying the Path of Conveyance quickly learn to defend themselves from it.","fx":"After the ritual is set, it is impossible for others to teleport inside the ward unless their casting pool scores more successes than this ritual.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"277"},"aspects":"Duration, Range (as a radius)","tag":"Conveyance Ritual (••)."},"M0xbAhbHgUr2d0U0":{"id":"M0xbAhbHgUr2d0U0","n":"Gift of Longevity","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"reanimation","sum":"Also known as the “siphoning gift” by those less in denial, this Ritual allows a vampire to transfer vitality from one mortal to another, extending one life by shortening the other.","fx":"The results become apparent quickly. For every five minutes of siphoning, the targeted mortal loses 10 years’ worth of life they could have lived to the other.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"349"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Reanimation Ritual (•••••)."},"M4ThiTzGit8AHIVI":{"id":"M4ThiTzGit8AHIVI","n":"Sorcerer’s Grimoire","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"enchantment","sum":"This Grimoire is capable of initiating even a sleeping mind into the mysteries of Sorcery.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"293"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: The"},"MRlwJWtMiycvDGEJ":{"id":"MRlwJWtMiycvDGEJ","n":"Abyss Communion (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"abysscommunion","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"250"},"aspects":"Accuracy, Time Period (past, present or future) and Query. See Divination p. 268 for Accuracy and Query Aspects.","seq":"The experience of communing with the Abyss is one that permanently scars. The Mystic begins to suffer nightmares (which are not exactly frightening to most Abyss Mystics) that drain their psyche. The vampire permanently recovers Superficial Willpower damage at the start of session equal to the lower of their Resolve or Composure. If the Attributes are equal, recover that amount -1 (example: Montano’s Resolve and Composure are both 5, and so he only recovers 4 Superficial Willpower damage).","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"MUqHhMrptRk9tp2M":{"id":"MUqHhMrptRk9tp2M","n":"Magical Phylactery","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"enchantment","sum":"An item (frequently a staff) or a piece of jewelry that gives the wearer a two-dice bonus on all rolls related to defending from, using or controlling magic.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"290"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (••). Aspects: The"},"Mg08a8tRf1GLlZbW":{"id":"Mg08a8tRf1GLlZbW","n":"Blood to Water","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"The Kindred pours purified water through their bloody fingers, transmuting all spilled blood in the area into water.","fx":"If the ritual is successful, blood (including the performer’s spilled Blood) exposed to the air is transmuted into water, leaving no traces behind.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"320"},"aspects":"Range (as radius)","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (•)."},"Mzc0bOwXxwRixae3":{"id":"Mzc0bOwXxwRixae3","n":"Chain the Sinners (Rosselini)","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"necromancy","sum":"The caster must speak the True Name of a ghost or have it in their line of sight while holding an object. On a win, the object becomes the ghost’s new fetter for all intents and purposes.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"333"},"tag":"Necromancy Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Duration and the Necromancy Special Effects."},"NKG2bhuA9qkeCfVa":{"id":"NKG2bhuA9qkeCfVa","n":"Contortion","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"masteryofthemortalshell","sum":"The sorcerer picks a body part to contort: head (Social and Mental), legs (Dexterity), arms (Strength). Dice pools with the associated Attributes and Skills suffer a two-dice penalty.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"329"},"tag":"Mastery of the Mortal Shell Special Effect (••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets, Range and the following."},"NMlJjNxFAaVdNhxX":{"id":"NMlJjNxFAaVdNhxX","n":"Amulet against the Shapers","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"enchantment","sum":"Same as Amulet against Magic except that it impacts Garou and other shapeshifters’ Gifts against the wearer.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"290"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••). Aspects: The"},"NYG78jdRGboqaKUp":{"id":"NYG78jdRGboqaKUp","n":"Spirit Portal (Low Umbra)","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"ephemera","sum":"This ritual allows the caster to enter the Low Umbra, specifically the Shadowlands.","fx":"The consecrated portal begins to glow in pale light when viewed by supernatural senses like the first dot of this Path and stepping through it will physically bring the Passenger Aspect’s worth of people into the spirit world physically.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"305"},"aspects":"Duration, Passengers","tag":"Ephemera Ritual (•••••)."},"NfZCQmRIUpiv3hoz":{"id":"NfZCQmRIUpiv3hoz","n":"Blood Oath of the Dead","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"necromancy","sum":"The Blood Bond is a potent tool that has held the Cainite society stable for centuries if not millenias and normally affects only humans, be they mortal or immortal.","fx":"This Ritual takes only a minute to perform.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"336"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Necromancy Ritual (•••)."},"NudfLlKyey55NBhI":{"id":"NudfLlKyey55NBhI","n":"Encrypt/Decrypt Letter","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"bindingsummoningandwarding","sum":"Used heavily in the Dark Ages when secrecy of one’s letters could make the difference between life and death, this ritual makes the contents of a letter illegible to those not meant to read it.","fx":"After the sorcerer is done writing the secret contents on a page, wall or a tablet, they make the Ritual roll and write down their successes.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"271"},"aspects":"Duration (ranks count as doubled)","tag":"Binding, Summoning and Warding Ritual (•)."},"NzJBuNnhReXI7Pmt":{"id":"NzJBuNnhReXI7Pmt","n":"Warrior’s Strength","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A bull torque made of pure obsidian. When smeared with blood it grants a single one-dot power of Potence to the torque.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"291"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••). Aspects: The"},"O0h7tKIwG5mykZhc":{"id":"O0h7tKIwG5mykZhc","n":"Blood Apocrypha","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"Kindred sorcerers have learned to embed messages into their blood, or a vessel when feeding.","fx":"As part of the ritual, a vampire, mortal, or beast messenger must consume the blood to transfer the message to their own body, otherwise the blood—and message—will rapidly sour.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"320"},"aspects":"Duration","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (•)."},"O3a9LWAcbyZ5fI6O":{"id":"O3a9LWAcbyZ5fI6O","n":"Spirit Portal (Astral)","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"ephemera","sum":"This ritual allows the caster to enter the High Umbra.","fx":"The consecrated portal begins to glow in pale light when viewed by supernatural senses like the first dot of this Path and stepping through it will physically bring the Passenger Aspect’s worth of people into the spirit world physically.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"305"},"aspects":"Duration, Passengers","tag":"Ephemera Ritual (•••••)."},"O3vPdyY4AU7BZNaM":{"id":"O3vPdyY4AU7BZNaM","n":"To the death","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"battle","sum":"All targets in range ignore physical impairment. Targets also do not exhaust themselve, allowing them to run or march with haste. When used in this manner, it is referred to as Iter Perenix.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"267"},"tag":"Battle Special Effect (••). Aspects: Number of Targets, Range (as a radius)"},"O5EcNu8a6wAtd7Ea":{"id":"O5EcNu8a6wAtd7Ea","n":"Amulet against Fae","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"enchantment","sum":"Same as Amulet against Magic (see below) except that it impacts Fae magic against the wearer.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"290"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••). Aspects: The"},"Ob7sWM3zv3lEcW1z":{"id":"Ob7sWM3zv3lEcW1z","n":"Aggressive Corpse","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"reanimation","sum":"The necromancer raises a dead body as an Aggressive Corpse.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"342"},"tag":"Reanimation Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets, Range and the following"},"OdPWV1f6yhgumej7":{"id":"OdPWV1f6yhgumej7","n":"Reanimation (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"reanimation","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"341"},"aspects":"Duration, Number of Targets, Range and the following Special Effects:","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"OuDqdVohLCUTNcsN":{"id":"OuDqdVohLCUTNcsN","n":"Shew Stone","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"necromancy","sum":"Practice of using stones for orientation is an old one, but only necromancers would literally use stones to orient themselves by infusing a small stone with spirits of the dead to track down a person as an esoteric compass.","fx":"On a Win, the stone begins to emit soft whispers which can only be heard if the person puts the stone very close to their ear.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"334"},"aspects":"Distance, Duration, Sympathetic Connection","tag":"Necromancy Ritual (•)."},"P5i4GabaRA1Asi4n":{"id":"P5i4GabaRA1Asi4n","n":"Consillium Mortui","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"pathofskulls","sum":"Path of Skulls Special Effect (••). Aspects: Number of targets (skulls targeted), duration (the duration aspect is always counted as one higher) as well as one of the following","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"376"},"tag":"Path of Skulls Special Effect (••). Aspects: Number of targets (skulls targeted), duration (the duration aspect is always counted as one higher) as well as one of the following"},"PITr3DVd39NQRsBc":{"id":"PITr3DVd39NQRsBc","n":"Manipulator Serum","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"alchemy","sum":"A powder or a liquid that, when inhaled by mouth, gives an extra dot of Manipulation and Subterfuge.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"265"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (••••)."},"PLKGJRdc8YT7Xes4":{"id":"PLKGJRdc8YT7Xes4","n":"Dance of the wind","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"battle","sum":"Every target in range counts any skill as 2 higher for rolls made to evading an attack, if they have taken no actions to attack then they take no penalties from dodging multiple attacks in one turn.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"267"},"tag":"Battle Special Effect (••). Aspects: Number of Targets, Range (as a radius)"},"PONe9sgz3reuNpqo":{"id":"PONe9sgz3reuNpqo","n":"Fear (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"fear","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"308"},"aspects":"Duration, Range, Number of Targets and the following:","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"PUvaBSIW4GiAThqF":{"id":"PUvaBSIW4GiAThqF","n":"Greek Fire","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"alchemy","sum":"Coats one weapon per dose in a substance that can burn for a scene, causing the weapon to deal two additional points of Aggravated Health damage from fire.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"264"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•••)."},"PW4S7J6vkAlSFYmP":{"id":"PW4S7J6vkAlSFYmP","n":"Ministraria di Morte","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"necromancy","sum":"Ghosts are a scarce resource in the competitive field of necromancers which is why tracking them down and being sure about it is crucial to the art.","fx":"The necromancer is given the information if the target has become a ghost and, if they are a ghost, they will be told if the person is now a normal wraith or a spectre.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"334"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Necromancy Ritual (•)."},"Pd9kczeLkAW25fVc":{"id":"Pd9kczeLkAW25fVc","n":"Dominion","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"enchantment","sum":"The Blood Sorcerer makes themselves the sovereign of supernatural powers in their own domain, thwarting others’ use of most vampiric abilities.","fx":"The Ritual lasts according to the Duration but can be broken by the destruction of at least one seal.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"299"},"aspects":"Range (counted as one higher and as a radius),Duration (ranks count as doubled)","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (•••••)."},"PiYAgAgWUpWLhfE3":{"id":"PiYAgAgWUpWLhfE3","n":"Clarion Call to the Loyal","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"necromancy","sum":"Trumpets will sound on the day of judgement, calling the dead to the final reckoning. While that is far away, the necromancers are able to emulate it by calling on long-dead warriors with their own trumpets.","fx":"Do not make the Ritual roll until the trumpet is ready to use which takes a single turn of action to do.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"337"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Necromancy Ritual (••••)."},"PjJ28QtSYB8kH7Br":{"id":"PjJ28QtSYB8kH7Br","n":"Knit the Veil","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"necromancy","sum":"The Shroud’s local rating is set to Impenetrable, preventing those from the other side from seeing or hearing anything and inflicting certain penalties (p. XX).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"332"},"tag":"Necromancy Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Duration and the Necromancy Special Effects."},"PlldMduHTpqNUUP9":{"id":"PlldMduHTpqNUUP9","n":"Summon the Dead","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"necromancy","sum":"Any ghost can be summoned to the caster. All the magician needs is the ghost’s True Name or a Fetter and to win against the ghost’s Composure + Resolve with their Spell Test.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"332"},"tag":"Necromancy Special Effect (••). Aspects: Duration and the Necromancy Special Effects."},"Q7f7C8gepxzmO468":{"id":"Q7f7C8gepxzmO468","n":"Facultas Emortua","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"pathofskulls","sum":"Path of Skulls Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Number of targets (skulls targeted), duration (the duration aspect is always counted as one higher) as well as one of the following","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"376"},"tag":"Path of Skulls Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Number of targets (skulls targeted), duration (the duration aspect is always counted as one higher) as well as one of the following"},"QDtMPgXb4eaOaYxI":{"id":"QDtMPgXb4eaOaYxI","n":"Humour Alignment","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"healing","sum":"This is an old ritual for curing chronic and congenital conditions. It dates back to the Middle Ages when Humorism was in vogue.","fx":"The subject heals Aggravated Health damage equal to the Healing Aspect and any Crippling Injuries save for missing limbs or grave mutilations.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"316"},"aspects":"Healing","tag":"Healing Ritual (••••)."},"QFKYtrtklw4kFqoN":{"id":"QFKYtrtklw4kFqoN","n":"Eldrich Mark","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"enchantment","sum":"Many enchanters are quite possessive of their work and sometimes mark it with a special mark as a form of “copyright” used early in the medieval period when one wanted to prove their abilities.","fx":"The surface “drinks” the liquid. The mark is invisible to the naked eye, but obvious to anyone with magically enhanced perceptions of any sort.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"294"},"aspects":"Duration","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (•)."},"QMKFeV69J5iEr7ew":{"id":"QMKFeV69J5iEr7ew","n":"Illusion (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"illusion","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"317"},"aspects":"Lies, Sense Manipulation","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"QO6CcnEBdrN8jX9e":{"id":"QO6CcnEBdrN8jX9e","n":"Animate the Inanimate (Greater)","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"enchantment","sum":"Identical to Animate the Inanimate (Lesser), except that the animated being is built as a Gifted Individual and costs as a two-dot retainer to permanently keep.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"292"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: The"},"QSkiPeIZJQoZYFfr":{"id":"QSkiPeIZJQoZYFfr","n":"Nightvision","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"alchemy","sum":"This formula eliminates any darkness penalty (not of supernatural darkness) by either enhancing the user’s visual senses or by giving them some sort of echo location. The user gains a dot in Wits, to a maximum of 5.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"263"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (••)."},"QVVr5qnra72x6Y9M":{"id":"QVVr5qnra72x6Y9M","n":"Principal Focus of Vitae Infusion","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"This ritual imbues a quantity of blood within the object upon which the ritual is cast. The object must be small enough for the vampire to carry in both hands, and it may be as small as a coin.","fx":"The amount of Blood stored can sate one Hunger for every two Rouse Checks made when storing the Blood.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"323"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (••)."},"QVp5H2wOcsLO6tnb":{"id":"QVp5H2wOcsLO6tnb","n":"Soul’s Reflection","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"blackseakraina","sum":"Water is in almost everything. A part of every plant, every animal, even a part of vampires in one form or another through their liquids.","fx":"The koldun may adjust the point of view, but their point of view must be within 5 meters of the subject/location.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"365"},"aspects":"Duration, Sympathetic Connection","tag":"Black Sea Kraina Ritual (•••••)."},"Qq1Q0qOsu7dNpPA7":{"id":"Qq1Q0qOsu7dNpPA7","n":"Disassociate","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"corruption","sum":"Corruption Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special conditions), Number of Targets, Range and the Special Effects described below.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"279"},"tag":"Corruption Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special conditions), Number of Targets, Range and the Special Effects described below. This form of casting requires either eye contact (Resolve + Intimidation vs the target’s Wits + Awareness) or for the sorcerer to make a certain hand gesture (detectable by Wits + Occult vs. the sorcerer’s Wits + Subterfuge)."},"QrJ5WVm6QmPT5gBB":{"id":"QrJ5WVm6QmPT5gBB","n":"Mercury's tongue","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"battle","sum":"All targets in range must try spend their turn trying to engage the caster or a target he designated (must be living and hostile to the targets).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"267"},"tag":"Battle Special Effect (•). Aspects: Number of Targets, Range (as a radius)"},"Qs4wNMqQgMsZo6EW":{"id":"Qs4wNMqQgMsZo6EW","n":"Ghost Town","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"haunting","sum":"This Ritual has long been used by the faevampires and the Giovanni who have bartered this Ritual from them to construct safe havens within the Shadowlands.","fx":"The user gains dots to spend on a Haven inside the Shadowlands equal to half of their succesess on the Ritual, rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"374"},"aspects":"Area, Corrosion (see below)","tag":"Haunting Ritual (•••••)."},"QsOPYWX6b11aazLI":{"id":"QsOPYWX6b11aazLI","n":"Enchantment (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"enchantment","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"288"},"aspects":"The following:","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"Qt2FnaEixU7rvql1":{"id":"Qt2FnaEixU7rvql1","n":"Foundation of the Chantry","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"enchantment","sum":"After slaying a white or albino mammal or bird indigenous to the area and soaking the stone in its blood, the sorcerer draws a map of the area (up to about a 12-mile radius) on the skull and places a polished sphere of amethyst skull’s eye socket or mouth.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"292"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: The"},"Qtk6PAuCD3fIxPde":{"id":"Qtk6PAuCD3fIxPde","n":"Corrosive Blood","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"Altering the properties of some of their own Blood, the user can make it highly corrosive to dead substances, able to corrode most items down to steaming sludge, given enough time and Blood shed.","fx":"Each point of Corrosion Aspect corrodes approximately 10 cm of matter in all directions from the splash; this takes approximately five minutes (longer on soft metals like copper or cast iron).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"320"},"aspects":"Area, Corrosion (see below)","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (•)."},"RBkiO5CUVnxKOxnR":{"id":"RBkiO5CUVnxKOxnR","n":"Storm, blizzard, massive sandstorm","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"weathercontrol","sum":"Combines effects of rain and high winds. All Predator Types suffer an increase in difficulty of two due to everybody staying indoors.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"358"},"tag":"Weather Control Ritual (•••)."},"RFFven2YTr2QgIpn":{"id":"RFFven2YTr2QgIpn","n":"Sleet","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"elementalforces","sum":"the caster shoots a stream of ice and/or freezing water. Targets can try to avoid the stream with a dodging roll or suffer Superficial Health damage equal to the margins or twice the Damage Aspect, whichever is lower).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"284"},"tag":"Elemental Forces Special Effect (•). Aspects: Damage, Range, Area"},"RKITZu1tBe2vNX0w":{"id":"RKITZu1tBe2vNX0w","n":"Algor Mortis","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"corpseinthemonster","sum":"Inducing the stiffness of death in the mind, the caster ignores all forms of Impairment penalties, may not be stunned and gains a +3 dice bonus against Persuasion, Intimidation, Insight and emotion-reading or thought-reading powers.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"371"},"tag":"Corpse in the Monster Special Effect (••). Aspects: Corpse State"},"RQniuIAVknAneObg":{"id":"RQniuIAVknAneObg","n":"Teleport Station","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"conveyance","sum":"Spells are all quite good and all, but unreliable. This ritual establishes a type of a portal. When a person enters it or steps on it, they are teleported to another designated location.","fx":"Sorcerer is automatically transported to the other teleporting station as a sign of the place working.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"278"},"aspects":"Distance, Duration","tag":"Conveyance Ritual (•••••)."},"Rqgx65A0oyBOKKo9":{"id":"Rqgx65A0oyBOKKo9","n":"Reclamation of Vitae","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"Lifeblood Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Range, Number of Targets, Hunger (see below) and the following special effects","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"319"},"tag":"Lifeblood Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Range, Number of Targets, Hunger (see below) and the following special effects"},"Rqw2EEb5AccJZZ9w":{"id":"Rqw2EEb5AccJZZ9w","n":"Heartseeker","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A stiletto or a stake which unerringly aims for the heart when wielded in rage. The wielder does not suffer a called shot penalty on staking rolls or rolls to aim for the heart.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"291"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••). Aspects: The"},"RxfqlMVVmbKWyN3e":{"id":"RxfqlMVVmbKWyN3e","n":"Intriguing","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"fascination","sum":"Fascination Special Effect (•). Aspects: In addition to the Aspects of Number of Targets, Range, and Sympathetic Connection, Fascination uses the Allure and Willbending Aspects.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"306"},"tag":"Fascination Special Effect (•). Aspects: In addition to the Aspects of Number of Targets, Range, and Sympathetic Connection, Fascination uses the Allure and Willbending Aspects."},"RyWGDz1BY1HsZoMi":{"id":"RyWGDz1BY1HsZoMi","n":"Patch the Corpse","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"corpseinthemonster","sum":"Coaxing the undead form to heal, the character is able to heal Superficial Health damage through rest like a mortal the next time they awaken.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"371"},"tag":"Corpse in the Monster Special Effect (••). Aspects: Corpse State"},"S2O5XzeydMewhEpy":{"id":"S2O5XzeydMewhEpy","n":"Lightning","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"elementalforces","sum":"Those hit with Lightning suffer (damage equal to twice the Damage Aspect or margins, whichever is lower).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"284"},"tag":"Elemental Forces Special Effect (••). Aspects: Damage, Range, Area"},"SFAxbWCqKL9OY7TI":{"id":"SFAxbWCqKL9OY7TI","n":"Transitive Bond","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"alchemy","sum":"This formula preserves one Rouse Check or one Hunger’s Worth of vitae from the same vampire per dose in addition to one Rouse Check activation cost (blood in doses cannot exceed blood used as ingredients) and allows it…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"264"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•••)."},"SOtikHZZ9iHvMBGp":{"id":"SOtikHZZ9iHvMBGp","n":"Enchanted Mail","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A silvered mail tunic that absorbs three points of Health damage before it breaks. If any attempt at cleaning or repair is made, the magic is lost.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"291"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (••••). Aspects: The"},"SiIwExbIHva2xeI5":{"id":"SiIwExbIHva2xeI5","n":"Ferryman’s Recal","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"reanimation","sum":"Ghouls are a long-term investment and a problem to replace, especially if they were a promising student who has been groomed by embrace.","fx":"On a Win, any wounds suffered before the Ritual, including the cause of the subject’s death and any decomposition, close, but do not entirely heal, leaving scars on the newly embraced vampire’s body.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"347"},"aspects":"Duration (counted as higher by 3) for how long the subject has been dead, Number of Targets","tag":"Reanimation Ritual (•••••)."},"SxWdpHs79i42DmRA":{"id":"SxWdpHs79i42DmRA","n":"Baleful Exorcism","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"reanimation","sum":"Targeted mortals roll Composure + Resolve. If the caster wins, their souls are expelled from their bodies for the Duration or until the body takes a point of damage.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"342"},"tag":"Reanimation Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets, Range and the following"},"SyC3elX9AmxG97Ir":{"id":"SyC3elX9AmxG97Ir","n":"Ex Nihilo","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"necromancy","sum":"This Ritual enables a vampire and their coterie to migrate into the Shadowlands, though doing so comes at great risk.","fx":"If successful, the vampire, a number of companions according to the Passenger Aspect, and any objects on their person may then enter the Shadowlands.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"338"},"aspects":"Passengers","tag":"Necromancy Ritual (•••••)."},"SycoVXlIQlA0mN03":{"id":"SycoVXlIQlA0mN03","n":"Boukephos’ Gateway","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"The mystic opens their very soul to the Abyss while staring into a mirror (which usually gives no reflection due to most mystics being of the Clan Lasombra) from the end of one night until the beginning of a new one,…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"254"},"seq":"None. Being on the Road of the Abyss can be considered a sequela.","tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Only"},"TRzcGIyO9wAJwSQn":{"id":"TRzcGIyO9wAJwSQn","n":"Pull of the Grave","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"reanimation","sum":"Islam and Christianity teach that death is the end of the physical life and that the souls of the dead will be called on the Judgment Day. Until then, the corpses must stay in the ground.","fx":"To perform this Ritual, the target must have a line of sight against the target.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"350"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Reanimation Ritual (•••••)."},"TS9Kwq8NFaBNtYRA":{"id":"TS9Kwq8NFaBNtYRA","n":"Curse in a Bottle","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"alchemy","sum":"This formula creates a liquid that, when drank, affects the person with a curse that was placed into the liquid.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"263"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (••)."},"TbH7nSt7RDGFYtDF":{"id":"TbH7nSt7RDGFYtDF","n":"Insane bravery","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"battle","sum":"All targets in range ignore mental impairment","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"267"},"tag":"Battle Special Effect (••). Aspects: Number of Targets, Range (as a radius)"},"TiTfsmX2yPylXbJL":{"id":"TiTfsmX2yPylXbJL","n":"Walk Through the Shroud","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"necromancy","sum":"A development of the Giovanni necromancers recently Embraced into the clan, this rite allows a necromancer to force their own soul to follow the course of one that actually dies, leaving their body behind and crossing…","fx":"The vampire’s soul to separate from their body in a manner similar to Anima Walk (Auspex 5, see p. 26) except that they’re for all intents and purposes a ghost.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"340"},"aspects":"Duration (Counted as higher by 1)","tag":"Necromancy Ritual (•••••)."},"Tj2yWmpTRfQ2obZc":{"id":"Tj2yWmpTRfQ2obZc","n":"Antiarrow Ring","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A silver toe-ring that, when worn on otherwise bare feet, protects from projectiles, giving a two-dice bonus to one wearing it for dodging projectiles with Athletics.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"289"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•). Aspects: The"},"TrVVkS6WuBYSgucv":{"id":"TrVVkS6WuBYSgucv","n":"Viscera Forest","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"thegreenpath","sum":"Almost a direct upgrade to Viscera Garden, this rare and powerful ritual allows the caster to convert existing plantlife into a large viscera garden spanning potentially entire forests, hence the name.","fx":"Unlike a Viscera Garden however, these plants must receive the Range aspect in either human or animal corpses (whichever was used to enact the ritual) every month, or else they wither and die within a week.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"356"},"aspects":"Range (as radius; counted as 1 higher)","tag":"The Green Path Ritual (••••)."},"UDBEn83QKyGFurYD":{"id":"UDBEn83QKyGFurYD","n":"Pontos Euxeinos","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"blackseakraina","sum":"The Greeks once called the Black Sea Pontos Euxeinos, the Hospitable Sea, as euphemism. For the koldun of the Black Sea Kraina, it truly can be, holding them in its embrace and healing them of even their worst injuries.","fx":"To intiate the rite, the koldun submerges themselves or somebody else they wish to heal into a pool of water and drips some of their blood.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"365"},"aspects":"Healing","tag":"Black Sea Kraina Ritual (••••)."},"UOouHUgdl67KujeG":{"id":"UOouHUgdl67KujeG","n":"Innocence’s Veil","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"The ritual allows the vampire to temporarily make any trace of diablerie on their part undetectable.","fx":"If the ritual is successful, signs of diablerie on the user cease to manifest.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"328"},"aspects":"Duration","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (••••)."},"USBSzShw3hn6xHYb":{"id":"USBSzShw3hn6xHYb","n":"Jupiter's might","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"battle","sum":"All targets in range inflict an extra +2 damage on all of their melee attack rolls made with mundane weapons or unarmed strikes.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"267"},"tag":"Battle Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Number of Targets, Range (as a radius)"},"UaeW6mv9KpOhQmPR":{"id":"UaeW6mv9KpOhQmPR","n":"Divination (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"divination","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"281"},"aspects":"Divination uses only three Aspects. Time Period (past, present or future) and:","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"Uay27rF3obyvOGJy":{"id":"Uay27rF3obyvOGJy","n":"Amulet against the Infernal","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"enchantment","sum":"Same as Amulet against Magic except that it impacts Infernal powers like Arcana and Dark Thaumaturgy against the wearer.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"290"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••). Aspects: The"},"Uf03iDfgiAsRsk1Z":{"id":"Uf03iDfgiAsRsk1Z","n":"Corpse in the Monster (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"corpseinthemonster","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"371"},"aspects":"Corpse State Special Effects","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"UsFkzdU4qd5P356m":{"id":"UsFkzdU4qd5P356m","n":"Nightmare Drums","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"necromancy","sum":"By sounding the drums of human skin and using a personal item of the target, the necromancer summons ghosts from the Shadowlands to haunt the dreams of their target.","fx":"On a Critical Win, they heal no Willpower whatsoever. The target may attempt to resist the Ritual’s effects with a Composure + Occult roll against the successes on the Ritual roll.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"337"},"aspects":"Duration, Sympathetic Aspect","tag":"Necromancy Ritual (••••)."},"UxCW5WkLU4FEu92w":{"id":"UxCW5WkLU4FEu92w","n":"Transubstantiation of the Seven","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"Probably the most famous ritual of the Clan Tremere, one that is (or was) the cornerstone of the pyramid.","fx":"It transforms into the blood of the Council of Seven within the drinker who counts as if they took a sip directly from the Council’s vein.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"327"},"tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (•••)."},"V4XzxG0K76MO2gUr":{"id":"V4XzxG0K76MO2gUr","n":"Degulo","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"pathofskulls","sum":"Path of Skulls Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Number of targets (skulls targeted), duration (the duration aspect is always counted as one higher) as well as one of the following","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"376"},"tag":"Path of Skulls Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Number of targets (skulls targeted), duration (the duration aspect is always counted as one higher) as well as one of the following"},"VCN90ybDy4Q7t7p9":{"id":"VCN90ybDy4Q7t7p9","n":"Ashen Relic","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"reanimation","sum":"This Ritual allows for the preservation of pieces of a vampire’s body even after they’ve been destroyed.","fx":"The necromancer preserves one small body part, such as a finger bone or a fang, while three successes in the margin can preserve a femur or skull.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"344"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Reanimation Ritual (••)."},"Vl49kzfwBxVORqhX":{"id":"Vl49kzfwBxVORqhX","n":"Death’s Communion","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"necromancy","sum":"The Giovanni are known for their own versions of the Christian mass, often twisting it in various directions that sometimes include mockery.","fx":"For this Ritual to work, the caster and the target must both possess at least one dot in Necromancy.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"333"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Necromancy Ritual (•)."},"VttPtvG6hbV33tla":{"id":"VttPtvG6hbV33tla","n":"Imbue with the Grace of Anubis","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"reanimation","sum":"An unthinking guardian is a potent defender for havens and temples, but sometimes a sorcerer requires Anubis to return more than a flicker of life.","fx":"The statblock of the reanimated cadaver may swap its Skills for that of the spirit’s at the moment of their death.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"346"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Reanimation Ritual (••••)."},"VyFweh4h7AQE4i1j":{"id":"VyFweh4h7AQE4i1j","n":"Healing Slumber","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"healing","sum":"The sorcerer puts their subject to sleep, calming their mind and allowing the healing process to accelerate.","fx":"The subject falls asleep for 9 hours; when they awake, Superficial Health damage equal to the Healing Aspect or margins if the target resists (Stamina + Resolve), whichever is lower.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"315"},"aspects":"Healing","tag":"Healing Ritual (•)."},"W3qHOR1lDcWXFzri":{"id":"W3qHOR1lDcWXFzri","n":"Vas Malum","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"pathofskulls","sum":"Using this ritual on a skull gives the caster the complete skillset of the individual it belonged to, including exceptional skills, specialties and attributes.","fx":"The skull functions as a thrown weapon that explodes on contact with a surface and deals the caster's Path rating to all targets within 3 meters, causing their flesh to decay while leaving inorganic items intact.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"377"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Path of Skulls Ritual (••••)."},"WNKj6FnMu8H0abWU":{"id":"WNKj6FnMu8H0abWU","n":"Hard-Light Constructs","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"illusion","sum":"A ritual that will be popularised technosorcerers in the 21st century, Hard-Light Constructs are illusions everyone involved knows are fake one person points it out.","fx":"An illusion is created that may be perceived by everybody.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"318"},"aspects":"Duration, Range (as a radius of the effect), Senses. Realism","tag":"Illusion Ritual (•••)."},"WYADfbjdkBwP1ZCx":{"id":"WYADfbjdkBwP1ZCx","n":"Into the Chasm","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"This ritual opens a portal into the Abyss itself. The mystic spends an hour painting a circle of glyphs using two Rouse Check’s worth of the blood in addition to the activation Rouse Check.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"255"},"seq":"Vampires who walk in the Abyss risk bringing a fragment of its alien malevolence back with them to the material world. After every sojourn, make a Willpower Test against a difficulty of trip’s duration in minutes (maximum Difficulty 6). A failure means the vampire gains the effects of the Ingrained Flaw of Obtenebration Discipline whether or not they do or are able to possess it.","tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Only"},"Wr9QE1QLtk0VeVWY":{"id":"Wr9QE1QLtk0VeVWY","n":"At Our Command It Breathes","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"enchantment","sum":"This ritual permits the creation of a Gargoyle from the dismembered parts of slain Cainites and is the process through which the first of that line came into being.","fx":"In addition to the activation Rouse Check for the ritual, there is a greater price in Blood that cannot be rerolled.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"298"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (•••••)."},"WzozhRCpphMVRvRv":{"id":"WzozhRCpphMVRvRv","n":"Bottle It","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"fortune","sum":"While not as potent as potions of Fortune sorcerers dabbling in Alchemy Path, practitioners of Fortune can still bottle up their magic to be sold as luck potions or weird fortune poisons.","fx":"The imbiber of the potion gains the effects as used. Curses may be resisted with Wits + Occult as normal.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"313"},"aspects":"Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special conditions), Number of Targets, Range and either Blessing or Curse Special Effects.","tag":"Fortune Ritual (••)."},"X36OC5MvASRns4y5":{"id":"X36OC5MvASRns4y5","n":"Smoke","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"elementalforces","sum":"A poisonous dark cloud, using Duration instead of Damage and counting Area as higher by 3.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"285"},"tag":"Elemental Forces Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Damage, Range, Area"},"XI0Fa2hIabE8xHEJ":{"id":"XI0Fa2hIabE8xHEJ","n":"Enhanced Painkillers","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"alchemy","sum":"A drug that lets the user ignore Physical Impairment until they suffer damage again.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"262"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•)."},"XMMTFkPru9e253R6":{"id":"XMMTFkPru9e253R6","n":"Amulet against Magic","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"enchantment","sum":"An amulet warding against magic (mortal or otherwise). Three times a day it subtracts two successes from spells and rituals targeting the wearer.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"290"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••). Aspects: The"},"XUHnsWiHiJF2z7Zn":{"id":"XUHnsWiHiJF2z7Zn","n":"Lightning Storm","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"weathercontrol","sum":"Same as storm. Each players makes an Intelligence + Science or Academics roll (difficulty 3) at the beginning of the night.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"359"},"tag":"Weather Control Ritual (•••••)."},"XfD4G6qQFV5yzjGa":{"id":"XfD4G6qQFV5yzjGa","n":"Blood Dance","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"necromancy","sum":"Blood Dance allows a ghost to communicate with the living. Many a necromancer has made a fortune by performing this Ritual to allow relatives of a ghost to communicate with it.","fx":"The ghost may speak and hear through the sand sigil as if they were there. Physically, the ghost remains in their current location.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"335"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Necromancy Ritual (••)."},"YlGaJg3uhYyRIZcV":{"id":"YlGaJg3uhYyRIZcV","n":"Prepare the Vessel","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"reanimation","sum":"Gifting ghosts another chance to roam this world in a physical body is a great bargaining chip or a weird torture tactic to be employed by the necromancer.","fx":"Every form of possession (ghost Puppetry, Auspex 5 Possesion, demon possession...) gains automatic successes equal to Possession Weakness on the attempt.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"345"},"aspects":"Duration, Number of Targets, Possesion Weakness (see below)","tag":"Reanimation Ritual (•••)."},"YtoWQvz66Lr906Rm":{"id":"YtoWQvz66Lr906Rm","n":"Depression","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"corruption","sum":"Corruption Special Effect (••). Aspects: Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special conditions), Number of Targets, Range and the Special Effects described below.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"279"},"tag":"Corruption Special Effect (••). Aspects: Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special conditions), Number of Targets, Range and the Special Effects described below. This form of casting requires either eye contact (Resolve + Intimidation vs the target’s Wits + Awareness) or for the sorcerer to make a certain hand gesture (detectable by Wits + Occult vs. the sorcerer’s Wits + Subterfuge)."},"YuBSQAb1iKYjQLex":{"id":"YuBSQAb1iKYjQLex","n":"Condense","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"alchemy","sum":"This formula condenses blood or liquids of lower volume than the amount used with the liquid typically then placed inside small vials.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"262"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (••)."},"Z2wKiNwzsH8qjOGS":{"id":"Z2wKiNwzsH8qjOGS","n":"Vis Memoriae","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"pathofskulls","sum":"Path of Skulls Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Number of targets (skulls targeted), duration (the duration aspect is always counted as one higher) as well as one of the following","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"376"},"tag":"Path of Skulls Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Number of targets (skulls targeted), duration (the duration aspect is always counted as one higher) as well as one of the following"},"Z38Y7LW0ClFypCDM":{"id":"Z38Y7LW0ClFypCDM","n":"Lie Detecting Serum","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"alchemy","sum":"A powder or a liquid that, when inhaled by mouth, reduces the Target’s Manipulation and Subterfuge by 1.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"265"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (••••)."},"ZEsjXaSYy89TA3lW":{"id":"ZEsjXaSYy89TA3lW","n":"Instant Feast","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"illusion","sum":"Illusory food is deceptively hard to create. Yes, a simple spell can create visuals of food as well as smell and touch and texture, but after devouring an entire feast by themselves, a guest will still feel hungry.","fx":"This can’t alleviate the physical effects of starvation, but can alleviate the mental ones.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"318"},"aspects":"Duration, Range (radius of the effect per casting: a dinner table would require Range 2), Number of Targets, Senses (taste, smell, visual image and texture; 4)","tag":"Illusion Ritual (••••)."},"ZKi4sA0rMSvTlK6s":{"id":"ZKi4sA0rMSvTlK6s","n":"Hellblade","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"elementalforces","sum":"The image of a flaming blade is terrifying and borderline demonic. With this, the sorcerer can cow mortals and annihilate even the most durable of vampires.","fx":"The ritual sets a melee weapon or a projectile aflame according to the magic used (Lure of Flames or Balefire, each with their own colour).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"286"},"aspects":"Damage, Duration","tag":"Elemental Forces Ritual (••)."},"ZbWu8gecQ3hjSoIV":{"id":"ZbWu8gecQ3hjSoIV","n":"Fire Projectile","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"alchemy","sum":"Coats one weapon or one attack’s worth of bullets per dose with a substance that bursts into flames on impact, dealing two additional points of Aggravated Health damage from fire.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"264"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•••)."},"ZfL7MpcMEgWGk37M":{"id":"ZfL7MpcMEgWGk37M","n":"Enhance Craftmanship","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"enchantment","sum":"Sometimes, instead of a magic item, what a magician needs is an otherwise normal but perfectly crafted object.","fx":"An object of great quality and durability is made. Blades and armour never break and clothes will eternally be “as new”.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"294"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (••)."},"Zkb0cFf5IyXaKZpP":{"id":"Zkb0cFf5IyXaKZpP","n":"Domain of the Genius","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"geniusloci","sum":"The koldun extends his awareness through the land upon which they thread, becoming the Genius Loci of legend.","fx":"The sorcerer’s perceptions extend all throughout the land except areas warded against spirits in a radius pulsing with the koldun’s will (the koldun may roll against these wards to pierce them).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"360"},"aspects":"Distance (counted as higher by one), Duration, Passengers","tag":"Genius Loci Ritual (•)."},"ZlRibBXhbNqVk50M":{"id":"ZlRibBXhbNqVk50M","n":"Beast Repellant","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"alchemy","sum":"A pungent chemical that drives back werewolves (and most humans, simply due to the smell).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"265"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•••••)."},"Zp0KePEEi0aoFFh8":{"id":"Zp0KePEEi0aoFFh8","n":"Monster Energy","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"alchemy","sum":"An energy drink that lets the user go an entire week sleeping one hour per night. For vampires, this adds a die to their awakening rolls.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"263"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (••)."},"Zur2agml7VrlB26p":{"id":"Zur2agml7VrlB26p","n":"Vessel of the Koldun","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"geniusloci","sum":"The kolduny are masters of spirits, and a Genius Loci is the lord of the world. With this ritual, the koldun may enter the spirit world known as the Astral Umbra and middle worlds between it and the material world.","fx":"The vessel is successfuly animated.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"362"},"aspects":"Distance (counted as higher by one; how far the vessel may move before the Ritual ends), Duration","tag":"Genius Loci Ritual (••••)."},"a0oRZA9kd3TcVjKY":{"id":"a0oRZA9kd3TcVjKY","n":"Fae Repellant","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"alchemy","sum":"Same as Beast Repellent, but against demons, changelings and bygones. Uses water blessed by a religious priest.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"265"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•••••)."},"a9ffwWbsfC2Osrhu":{"id":"a9ffwWbsfC2Osrhu","n":"Draugh of Earth’s Blood","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"The Blood of Caine holds great mystical power, but it is not the only power.","fx":"This matter can take nearly any form appropriate to the cray’s nature, from the mushrooms of a faerie ring to the soil of a spectre’s haunted grave.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"326"},"aspects":"Duration (Count ranks as higher by one).","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (•••)."},"a9n1drjBRLoEGKNy":{"id":"a9n1drjBRLoEGKNy","n":"Transylvanian Kraina (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"transylvaniankraina","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"366"},"tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"aNHbuHg8U94xHBIJ":{"id":"aNHbuHg8U94xHBIJ","n":"Waves (Major)","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"weathercontrol","sum":"The sorcerer may control waves moving people and ships around with their Spell Test (resisted by Strength or Stamina + Athletics of those trying to swim, Wits + Steer of those trying to steer ships, Strength + Athletics of those trying to row away)","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"358"},"tag":"Weather Control Ritual (•••)."},"aQgtdypv47CEBRNU":{"id":"aQgtdypv47CEBRNU","n":"Abyssal Blade","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"The ritualist kills a creature with a bladed weapon and makes their Ritual Test. On a win, the blade becomes drenched in permanent mixture of blood and shadow, becoming black or at least a dark shade of grey.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"253"},"seq":"After a month and a night, the blade rapidly corrodes and becomes useless. The ritual may be repeated prior to the blade’s expiry, however.","tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (••). Aspects: Only"},"ajfXSym6ZTytrdu5":{"id":"ajfXSym6ZTytrdu5","n":"Tempering","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"alchemy","sum":"If applied to a fully functioning weapon or object it grants extraordinary durability.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"262"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•)."},"awaoxnt08sWStxQB":{"id":"awaoxnt08sWStxQB","n":"Carved Fortune","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"fortune","sum":"Common among Einherjar and Lhiannan witches, the sorcerer carves out a sigil or a rune with symbols of fortune.","fx":"The onlooker upon the sigil gains the effects as used. Curses may be resisted with Wits + Occult as normal.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"314"},"aspects":"Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special condition), Number of Targets, Range and either Blessing or Curse Special Effects. The Ritual also uses the Inscribed Duration Aspect, identical to Duration (counted as higher by one) representing how long the magic remains potent to impact others.","tag":"Fortune Ritual (•••)."},"bCZYWjWDOxyXIeBH":{"id":"bCZYWjWDOxyXIeBH","n":"Revivify the Cold Vitae","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"reanimation","sum":"Cappadocian scholars spend much of their time away from the living and among the dead. This practice can make hunting for living blood problematic, and the blood of corpses loses its potency so quickly as to be useless.","fx":"The blood inside the corpse is made fit for vampire consumpion even without the Iron Gullet Merit.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"343"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Reanimation Ritual (•)."},"bMZ9laUaUav2my1I":{"id":"bMZ9laUaUav2my1I","n":"Better Weapons","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A weapon with a damage modifier modified by +1.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"290"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (••). Aspects: The"},"bsrNT2XKfiL4gL05":{"id":"bsrNT2XKfiL4gL05","n":"Greater Abyssal Possession","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"(prerequisite: Medium Abyssal Possession) With this ritual, the character is able to force a stronger abyssal spirit into living being or corpses.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"255"},"seq":"None.","tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Only"},"bwVnQmTcj21qzggl":{"id":"bwVnQmTcj21qzggl","n":"Body Failure","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"masteryofthemortalshell","sum":"The victim makes a Crippling Injury roll (Corebook, p. 303) as one of their body parts is simply disabled. Alternatively to the roll, the caster can pick one of the mundane injuries like blindness or a broken limb.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"329"},"tag":"Mastery of the Mortal Shell Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets, Range and the following."},"cAAyS7E7KG6CkmVK":{"id":"cAAyS7E7KG6CkmVK","n":"Glyph of Scrying","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"enchantment","sum":"By preparing special sigils and focusing on them later, the sorcerer may extend their senses through their wards. Paranoid Tremere princes can monitor their entire cities through these glyphs.","fx":"The vampire can then later establish a telepathic connection with any of their wards, but only one at a time that allows them to see and hear through it.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"296"},"aspects":"Duration (ranks count as doubled)","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (•••)."},"cCQR9MwsyfXXOcVN":{"id":"cCQR9MwsyfXXOcVN","n":"Ritual Clensing of the Mind","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"healing","sum":"The sorcerer clenses the target’s spirit, healing deep traumas and restoring the mind.","fx":"The subject heals Aggravated and Superficial Willpower damage equal to the Healing Aspect.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"316"},"aspects":"Healing","tag":"Healing Ritual (•••••)."},"cQbfZem91vRn2Z3I":{"id":"cQbfZem91vRn2Z3I","n":"Necromancy (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"necromancy","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"331"},"aspects":"Duration and the Necromancy Special Effects.","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"cfGsdiRue7CVcMiu":{"id":"cfGsdiRue7CVcMiu","n":"Illusions of Pontos","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"blackseakraina","sum":"Mastering illusions over water, the koldun no longer simply toys with senses of their victims but creates independent illusions of water, mist and light.","fx":"If anybody ever perceives the illusions to be a lie, this rite is nullified and must be performed again.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"364"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Black Sea Kraina Ritual (•••)."},"cj8KjC83QGhJuRab":{"id":"cj8KjC83QGhJuRab","n":"Master of Fire","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"elementalforces","sum":"Fire is one of the greatest dangers to vampires and is easily exploited by both hunters and vampires themselves against their own kind.","fx":"As long as the sorcerer has the wax on their person, the sorcerer may speak a word of power and make a Rouse Check (which counts as a level 3 power for the purposes of rerolling it) to make their Spell Test using Area Aspect + 2 as the difficulty.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"286"},"aspects":"Duration (how long you have access to the spell given by the ritual)","tag":"Elemental Forces Ritual (•••)."},"cledNEnAgwq3IvFT":{"id":"cledNEnAgwq3IvFT","n":"Mindless Corpse","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"reanimation","sum":"The necromancer raises a dead body as a Mindless Corpse.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"341"},"tag":"Reanimation Special Effect (•). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets, Range and the following"},"dFoqr4KqOOMcQopC":{"id":"dFoqr4KqOOMcQopC","n":"Alter Temperature","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"weathercontrol","sum":"The sorcerer can also alter the temperature by up to 10 degrees Fahrenheit or 5 degrees Celsius.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"357"},"tag":"Weather Control Special Effect (••). Aspects: Distance (treat the measurement as the radius of effect), Duration"},"dWyn0JwpwxV6Sysi":{"id":"dWyn0JwpwxV6Sysi","n":"Remember","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"divination","sum":"Divination works in symbolism and doesn’t give precise answers without high successes or the Storyteller needing a device to advance plot.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"283"},"tag":"Divination Special Effect (•). Aspects: Divination uses only three Aspects. Time Period (past, present or future) and"},"dgef6a4dl55q0u7S":{"id":"dgef6a4dl55q0u7S","n":"Intelligent Servant","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"reanimation","sum":"If rigor mortis has set in already, the Spell fails. A human is raised as an undead with its old intellect and traits. It may speak and behaves in a manner closer to a living human than not.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"342"},"tag":"Reanimation Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets, Range and the following"},"dsxnz7vyoJTNPzrg":{"id":"dsxnz7vyoJTNPzrg","n":"Balm of Bathory","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"alchemy","sum":"This formula requires one pint/half a liter of blood from a youthful victim (or victims) of clear complexion (the needed amount doubles per brewing, see below), chamomile flowers, and shea butter or sheep’s fat; optional essential oils for scent.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"264"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (••••)."},"e67J8g4HPxoAZbV2":{"id":"e67J8g4HPxoAZbV2","n":"Sweet Sins","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"corruption","sum":"Corruption Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special conditions), Number of Targets, Range and the Special Effects described below.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"279"},"tag":"Corruption Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special conditions), Number of Targets, Range and the Special Effects described below. This form of casting requires either eye contact (Resolve + Intimidation vs the target’s Wits + Awareness) or for the sorcerer to make a certain hand gesture (detectable by Wits + Occult vs. the sorcerer’s Wits + Subterfuge)."},"eQAdM1o6i3l8Rk4W":{"id":"eQAdM1o6i3l8Rk4W","n":"Master of the Weather","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"transylvaniankraina","sum":"The Carpathian Mountains and its basin see great changes in weather quickly.","fx":"The koldun may use these Weather Control dots to evoke only the effects that may be associated with Transylvania.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"366"},"aspects":"None, but the spell uses the same as Weather Control","tag":"Transylvanian Kraina Ritual (•)."},"ehoqOqiuWa2S2hLx":{"id":"ehoqOqiuWa2S2hLx","n":"Animate Curios","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"transylvaniankraina","sum":"As with Treasured Ornaments, the koldun rouses the spirits of objects around their haven.","fx":"An item is disabled if it is ever struck and all attacks against it suffer a -2 success penaly due to a required Called Shot (even if the item is a sword carried by an animated armour set: it moves in unnatural ways).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"367"},"aspects":"Number of Targets (how many items are animated)","tag":"Transylvanian Kraina Ritual (•••)."},"erpCsTPS7eDHfpF1":{"id":"erpCsTPS7eDHfpF1","n":"Black Sea Kraina (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"blackseakraina","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"363"},"tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"f5J7Di6vaZ7XowbV":{"id":"f5J7Di6vaZ7XowbV","n":"Shroud Manipulation","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"necromancy","sum":"The caster lowers or raises the Shroud rating by a single stage.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"333"},"tag":"Necromancy Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Duration and the Necromancy Special Effects."},"f5pEJOS8yM5enxQJ":{"id":"f5pEJOS8yM5enxQJ","n":"Herd Ward","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"bindingsummoningandwarding","sum":"This ritual protects the sorcerer’s herd from others who would feed on them.","fx":"When another vampire tries to feed on the warded kine, they must roll Stamina + Resolve against the Ritual Test.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"272"},"aspects":"Damage, Duration (ranks count as doubled)","tag":"Binding, Summoning and Warding Ritual (•••)."},"fBbFUSjtdhNTwJgk":{"id":"fBbFUSjtdhNTwJgk","n":"Scour Secrets","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"The Blood Sorcerer unleashes rivulets of their Blood primed to search for information on a subject of their choosing.","fx":"Going through a library can set your Academics, Investigation, Science, Technology or Occult at a certain rating if the information acquired matches the appropriate Skill for the roll.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"323"},"aspects":"Distance and Duration","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (••)."},"fFVCb1uyX6FnhWxR":{"id":"fFVCb1uyX6FnhWxR","n":"Protective Coating","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"alchemy","sum":"A substance that makes it permanently impossible to chip or break the object (+2 difficulty to destroy). One dose covers around a meter radius and the effect is permanent.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"262"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•)."},"fTWGjEo9hDUT2edR":{"id":"fTWGjEo9hDUT2edR","n":"My World","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"illusion","sum":"Reaching the mastery of the Path, the sorcerer is able to craft illusions directly into the world independent of the observers.","fx":"The caster may cast any spell or a ritual of the Illusion Path without the Number of Targets system.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"318"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Illusion Ritual (•••••)."},"fVdfhAxn4VGuBE9K":{"id":"fVdfhAxn4VGuBE9K","n":"Shape Blood","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"Learned mostly by the most ostentatious of Tremere, this Special Effect is used to manipulate blood or vitae into finely crafted images – whether entertaining your fellows at Elysium with gaudy magician’s tricks or…","fx":"To create shapes, more than one rank of Shape Bmust be used in a spell, varying with the pattern’s complexity: from a simple “SOS” (1 rank of Shape), to a portrait (3 ranks of Shape) or topologically complex sorcerous sigil (4 ranks of Shape Blood).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"322"},"aspects":"Duration and Shape as the Aspect determining the complexity of the shape.","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (•)."},"fd4IkldC0lRrmJV4":{"id":"fd4IkldC0lRrmJV4","n":"Fog over Sea","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"blackseakraina","sum":"Moving with the unnatural grace of a ghost, a koldun employing this power may stride across water as readily as land, leaving nary a ripple to mark their passing.","fx":"Upon successful completion of the rite, the koldun is granted granted the ability to activate Fog over Sea Spell (Aspects: Duration) by making a Rouse Check and dropping some of their blood into a body of water.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"364"},"aspects":"None.","tag":"Black Sea Kraina Ritual (•••)."},"fiCixgc7Avyb8BSC":{"id":"fiCixgc7Avyb8BSC","n":"Vox Mortui","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"reanimation","sum":"While some Cappadocians have learned Setite secrets of invoking a shade of a dead person to communicate with their memories as if they are a living, it is hotly debated who invented this Ritual first.","fx":"A win on the Ritual allows the body to speak as if it was living for the Duration. The body has self consciousness but lacks an actual soul as it is merely vestiges of the soul given voice.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"344"},"aspects":"Number of Targets, Duration","tag":"Reanimation Ritual (••)."},"fyAhgYl1509juqVH":{"id":"fyAhgYl1509juqVH","n":"Amulet of Protection","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"enchantment","sum":"An amulet of protection from physical harm. When worn, it subtracts three points of Health damage before halving like Toughness.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"292"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: The"},"g3bNFYmyQqH7rLjO":{"id":"g3bNFYmyQqH7rLjO","n":"Impregnable Soul","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"reanimation","sum":"Necromancers deal with wraiths on a frequent basis and so do their, often mortal, assistants.","fx":"They gain no special protections from powers that affect the mind.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"345"},"aspects":"Distance, Duration, Resistance (see below)","tag":"Reanimation Ritual (•••)."},"g88zwfjpVTMBRIZy":{"id":"g88zwfjpVTMBRIZy","n":"Pishacha’s Banquet","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"necromancy","sum":"This grisly Ritual was developed by the Nagaraja as a method of feeding in desperate circumstances, Pisacha’s Banquet allows one feasting on the dead to acquire more than just blood.","fx":"On a Win, the necromancer can choose one of the following effects. On a critical win (or 3+ margins), they can choose two (or the same one twice):","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"336"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Necromancy Ritual (•••)."},"g8QsLuSkC2q2HPGA":{"id":"g8QsLuSkC2q2HPGA","n":"Vertigo","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"masteryofthemortalshell","sum":"The sorcerer picks a body part to in which they will induce pain: head (Social and Mental), legs (Dexterity), arms (Strength). The victim cannot spend Willpower to reroll pools with Associated Attributes.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"329"},"tag":"Mastery of the Mortal Shell Special Effect (•). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets, Range and the following."},"g9QKU7ru2f7uIHH9":{"id":"g9QKU7ru2f7uIHH9","n":"Unshakable spirit","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"battle","sum":"Every target in range becomes immune to mundane intimidation and gains +2 dice to resist supernaturally aided attempts to do so or to influence their minds (Presence, Dominate...).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"267"},"tag":"Battle Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Number of Targets, Range (as a radius)"},"gDZx8St0GGjkPUn2":{"id":"gDZx8St0GGjkPUn2","n":"Blood of Potency","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"The vampire can concentrate their Blood, increasing its potency temporarily.","fx":"The sorcerer increases their Blood Potency by one for the Duration; a critical win increases it by two. The vampire can use this power to exceed their generation limit on Blood Potency.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"324"},"aspects":"Duration","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (•••)."},"gEIPb9zu2aE1iSBR":{"id":"gEIPb9zu2aE1iSBR","n":"Engaging the Vessel of Transference","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"“Beware the gifts of the Children of Haqim”, elders of the Dark Ages used to warm their childers as those childers now issue similar warnings to their childers regarding the Tremere and their gifts.","fx":"The container is ready.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"321"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (•)."},"gb2siWkzJjUlhOmd":{"id":"gb2siWkzJjUlhOmd","n":"Lightning Strike","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"weathercontrol","sum":"There must be clouds present. The sorcerer can make a Spell Test (Aspects:","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"358"},"tag":"Weather Control Ritual (••••)."},"gtg9FWCZt4j6o90k":{"id":"gtg9FWCZt4j6o90k","n":"Lure of Flames","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"elementalforces","sum":"On a successful Spell Test, the sorcerer conjures a flame in their palm which can provide light but is harmless until released. The sorcerer can release the flames at targets who can try to dodge the Spell Test.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"284"},"tag":"Elemental Forces Special Effect (•). Aspects: Damage, Range, Area"},"hKdjS8gBvJ5y6MQU":{"id":"hKdjS8gBvJ5y6MQU","n":"Vitae Preservative","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"alchemy","sum":"This formula preserves one Rouse Check or one Hunger’s Worth of vitae from the same vampire per dose in addition to one Rouse Check activation cost (blood in doses cannot exceed blood used as ingredients) and allows it…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"263"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (••)."},"hQ8uLnCC7FY3JC6H":{"id":"hQ8uLnCC7FY3JC6H","n":"Whip of Woe (Rosselini)","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"necromancy","sum":"After making a small wound, the caster draws their blood into a whip that may directly attack the ectoplasmic corpus of ghosts, dealing Aggravated Health damage even if they haven’t manifested.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"332"},"tag":"Necromancy Special Effect (••). Aspects: Duration and the Necromancy Special Effects."},"hZIgjVBDTZ6WIHJS":{"id":"hZIgjVBDTZ6WIHJS","n":"Ephemera (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"ephemera","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"303"},"aspects":"Metaphysical Weight and Spiritual Reach","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"hdoGKlJ2kkvgYrEV":{"id":"hdoGKlJ2kkvgYrEV","n":"Blood of Ahriman","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"The ritualist requires to have bound a Hungry Shade (see the Binding, Summoning and Warding Path, p. XX).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"254"},"seq":"For the duration, the character’s skin becomes covered in shadow regardless of the presence of light. If the character spends more days in this spectral state than their Composure at a time, their skin permanently becomes of shadow. Powers such as Sense the Unseen and Scry the Soul can detect the presence of the shade within the character.","tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Only"},"hmiaUvkqhRMnzsCh":{"id":"hmiaUvkqhRMnzsCh","n":"Pit of Contemplation","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"The vampire personally murders an innocent mortal. While innocence is subjective, traditional sacrifices are children, virgins, and holy individuals.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"257"},"tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Only"},"hyQM4Qp0CppxAgOB":{"id":"hyQM4Qp0CppxAgOB","n":"Drowning Tide","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"elementalforces","sum":"This requires an Olympic sized swimming pool or larger body of water like a river. Spell Test is opposed using Dexterity + Athletics or Strength + Athletics.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"285"},"tag":"Elemental Forces Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Damage, Range, Area"},"iFyTbI5ysnWR7d8U":{"id":"iFyTbI5ysnWR7d8U","n":"Animate Beasts","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"reanimation","sum":"The necromancer resurrects an animal, keeping its old stats while reducing Social Attributes to 1 and Mental to 0.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"342"},"tag":"Reanimation Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets, Range and the following"},"iJmYz2jXVSO4U6CJ":{"id":"iJmYz2jXVSO4U6CJ","n":"Eyes of Babel","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"alchemy","sum":"This formula requires an eyeball and/or a tongue to work. Those who ingest the formula can read (eyeball) mand/or speak (tongue) the languages the person from whom the eye/tongue came from can, at the same level.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"263"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (••)."},"igl109KcHXpX5tGL":{"id":"igl109KcHXpX5tGL","n":"Attrocity’s Release","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"The ritual allows the vampire to temporarily make any trace of diablerie on their part undetectable.","fx":"An unwilling target may resist with Resolve + Blood Potency, the Ritual’s Difficulty counting as the greater of the target’s successes or the standard difficulty.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"328"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (•••••)."},"izqQ1uAoBh9HVewY":{"id":"izqQ1uAoBh9HVewY","n":"Sigil of Discord","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"enchantment","sum":"The vampire inscribes a sigil of confusion to play with the minds of their victims, making them dizzy and without a sense of space and direction.","fx":"A miasma of confusion rises that may only be perceived by powers such as Sense the Unseen.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"297"},"aspects":"Range (as a radius), Duration (ranks count as doubled) and","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (•••)."},"jG6nZ4dd4Krhs5sa":{"id":"jG6nZ4dd4Krhs5sa","n":"Masterful shift","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"shapeshifting","sum":"Shapeshifting Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Duration, Scale and Subject described below. If the sorcerer is transforming others, then Range is also an Aspect.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"352"},"tag":"Shapeshifting Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Duration, Scale and Subject described below. If the sorcerer is transforming others, then Range is also an Aspect."},"jgm90ymitN5asY5a":{"id":"jgm90ymitN5asY5a","n":"Passage to Enoch","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"necromancy","sum":"By ritualistically killing themselves with a silver dagger plunged into heart (mortal variants of this Ritual do not tend to lethally damage the heart).","fx":"The caster falls asleep and awakens physically in the Shadowlands near Enoch.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"340"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Necromancy Ritual (•••••)."},"jtFl7kzBfRhR4lny":{"id":"jtFl7kzBfRhR4lny","n":"Circle of Secrecy","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"enchantment","sum":"In Ceoris and Alamut, those who wield great secrets can do what those wielding great magical powers can not.","fx":"This ritual creates a warding circle or a zone according to the Range.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"296"},"aspects":"Range (as a radius), Duration (ranks count as doubled)","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (•••)."},"k0crAzCQ2mRinUBo":{"id":"k0crAzCQ2mRinUBo","n":"Ghost Repellant","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"alchemy","sum":"Same as Beast Repellent, but against ghosts. Uses cold iron dust.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"265"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•••••)."},"k1FeCGOwMYc5Ht6M":{"id":"k1FeCGOwMYc5Ht6M","n":"Defender of the Haven","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"enchantment","sum":"The thaumaturge draws dozens of glyphs, runes or letters on a clay brick or a piece of stone and then draws those same symbols onto a clay brick or a stone within the building.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"302"},"tag":"Enchantment Ritual (••)."},"k5LcqtGZQtj7FO0P":{"id":"k5LcqtGZQtj7FO0P","n":"Inspired bravery","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"battle","sum":"Every target in range gains a specialty in a combat skills (athletics, firearms, melee or brawl). The caster may select one skill per Rank of Inspired Bravery Aspect which may be raised like a common Aspect.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"267"},"tag":"Battle Special Effect (•). Aspects: Number of Targets, Range (as a radius)"},"kCRQTQaj4qOHP14s":{"id":"kCRQTQaj4qOHP14s","n":"Homuncular Servant","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"reanimation","sum":"The necromancer animates a bodypart to raise a homuncular servant.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"341"},"tag":"Reanimation Special Effect (••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets, Range and the following"},"kGzpuDLVy7VXitqF":{"id":"kGzpuDLVy7VXitqF","n":"Belle/Beau/Bright of the Ball","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"fascination","sum":"With knowledge of an upcoming social event and proper preparation, a sorcerer can make themselves quite the sensation.","fx":"The caster gains the Allure dice bonus over anybody within the event who has not succeeded on a Composure + Resolve Test (Storytellers should make one roll for separate generic “groups” of types of people there.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"307"},"aspects":"Allure, Duration, Number of Targets","tag":"Fascination Ritual (•••)."},"kH6hsgpOxeQzZNgw":{"id":"kH6hsgpOxeQzZNgw","n":"Garb of Hades","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"reanimation","sum":"Often, necromancers wish to walk the streets without actually doing it themselves or negotiate with dangerous partners without placing themselves in harm’s way.","fx":"If the 2nd method was used and Number of Targets was adaquate, more than a single corpse may be possessed at once.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"348"},"aspects":"Duration (counted as higher by two), Number of Targets (the user may possess multiple cadavers at once like a hivemind)","tag":"Reanimation Ritual (•••••)."},"kdOC0X7AEHpfMzKv":{"id":"kdOC0X7AEHpfMzKv","n":"Healing Slumber of the Spirit","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"healing","sum":"The sorcerer puts their subject to sleep, calming their mind and allowing the healing process to accelerate.","fx":"The subject falls asleep for 9 hours; when they awake, Superficial Willpower damage equal to the Healing Aspect or margins if the target resists (Stamina + Resolve), whichever is lower.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"315"},"aspects":"Healing","tag":"Healing Ritual (••)."},"kfKhoauGutmUA1pV":{"id":"kfKhoauGutmUA1pV","n":"Certámen","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"Inherited from the days when the Tremere were still a house of mortal magi, certámen stands as one of the oldest means of settling disputes between Hermetic wizards.","fx":"For the duration of certámen after it has been successfully cast, a thaumaturge inside the circle who performs a Blood Surge to empower magic may add their Occult rating instead of the typical Blood Surge value if it is higher.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"325"},"aspects":"Duration (usually 2)","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (•••)."},"ksy8WpKz2qBBaLMH":{"id":"ksy8WpKz2qBBaLMH","n":"Lifeblood (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"319"},"aspects":"Range, Number of Targets, Hunger (see below) and the following special effects:","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"ktFVUEJW0cRcNJZh":{"id":"ktFVUEJW0cRcNJZh","n":"Deflection of Wooden Doom","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"enchantment","sum":"An object is enchanted and placed next to the heart to grant the user protection against heart-piercing wooden stakes by reducing the attacker’s successes by 2.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"290"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••). Aspects: The"},"kzG2GhiPjZnMFD98":{"id":"kzG2GhiPjZnMFD98","n":"Enchanted Mirror","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"enchantment","sum":"The mirror allows the usage of Scry the Soul power through it, with those who know of its functions rolling with Wits or Resolve + Occult.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"292"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: The"},"l0L2zzaSRrUE0bAP":{"id":"l0L2zzaSRrUE0bAP","n":"Awaken the Forest Giants","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"thegreenpath","sum":"The Green Path Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets (individual statblock as targets), Range and Green Power","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"353"},"tag":"The Green Path Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets (individual statblock as targets), Range and Green Power"},"l286ODUucZ6z49LT":{"id":"l286ODUucZ6z49LT","n":"Draining the Well of Life","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"necromancy","sum":"Ghosts feed on emotions. While many ghosts are perfectly capable of feeding themselves, some necromancers prefer to keep them locked away from the outside world and have to feed themselves.","fx":"Ghost retainers around the victim whose name was written onto the victim lower Pathos Degeneration equal to the Hunger drained from the victim.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"335"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Necromancy Ritual (••)."},"lpOUzu3cncHo8eIe":{"id":"lpOUzu3cncHo8eIe","n":"Flesh Golem","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"reanimation","sum":"The necromancer animates a flesh golem composed of at least 3 cadavers stiched together (Intelligence + Medicine Test Difficulty 4 required)","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"342"},"tag":"Reanimation Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets, Range and the following"},"lrGZQCGaXWDlNyKR":{"id":"lrGZQCGaXWDlNyKR","n":"Full Shift","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"shapeshifting","sum":"Shapeshifting Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Duration, Scale and Subject described below. If the sorcerer is transforming others, then Range is also an Aspect.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"351"},"tag":"Shapeshifting Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Duration, Scale and Subject described below. If the sorcerer is transforming others, then Range is also an Aspect."},"mC4xyQcGpjah8UID":{"id":"mC4xyQcGpjah8UID","n":"Binding, Summoning and Warding (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"bindingsummoningandwarding","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"268"},"aspects":"Duration (ranks count as doubled) Number of Targets, Metaphysical Weight, Sympathetic Connection (for Summoning and Binding only) and any combination of the following:","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"mVi4NZcvCOHjz2hz":{"id":"mVi4NZcvCOHjz2hz","n":"Infusion of the Kalif","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"thegreenpath","sum":"This ritual is important to all Sorcerers of Haqim, but its effects have been imperfectly duplicated by a number of blood magicians from a number of schools who abuse its ancient pedigree for a baser purpose: getting high.","fx":"A critical (or 3+ margins) on the ritual test will double the amount of kalif a plant can produce.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"355"},"aspects":"None","tag":"The Green Path Ritual (••)."},"maMpuiM803RA4360":{"id":"maMpuiM803RA4360","n":"Speed the Seed’s Passing","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"thegreenpath","sum":"The Green Path Special Effect (•). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets (individual statblock as targets), Range and Green Power","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"353"},"tag":"The Green Path Special Effect (•). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets (individual statblock as targets), Range and Green Power"},"mdTU57LmYglXDRH2":{"id":"mdTU57LmYglXDRH2","n":"Composite Abyssal Possession","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"Medium Abyssal Possession) Identical to Flesh Golem from the Path of Bone (p. XX), requiring at least the same number of cadavers stitched together.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"254"},"seq":"Unless bought as a three-dot retainer, it becomes rogue.","tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Only"},"mhjxiwCICGW69Usx":{"id":"mhjxiwCICGW69Usx","n":"Thaumaturgical Surgery","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"biothaumaturgy","sum":"By combining the arts of medicine and magic, the sorcerer is able to quicken regeneration and even heal what standard medicine cannot, including things like regrowing limbs.","fx":"The subject heals Health accoaccording to the Healing Aspect.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"370"},"aspects":"Healing","tag":"Biothaumaturgy Ritual (••)."},"n0qzlkPNJd6thS4n":{"id":"n0qzlkPNJd6thS4n","n":"Blood Creature","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"With this spell, the vampire creates a small intelligent servant out of their own blood that they can use to spy.","fx":"The animal obeys vampire’s orders and the two can telepathically communicate if they have a line of sight. Once the Duration Aspect expires, the animal dissolves.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"324"},"aspects":"Duration","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (•••)."},"nC535Ryg1Gk4lXpi":{"id":"nC535Ryg1Gk4lXpi","n":"Diviner’s Kit","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A crystal ball, a special tarot deck, a mirror or something else that a practitioner of divination uses.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"291"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••). Aspects: The"},"nQzXp8frOSoAL9kK":{"id":"nQzXp8frOSoAL9kK","n":"Walk the Abyss","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"abysscommunion","sum":"While the Path of Abyssal Infusion is able to open a portal into the Abyss, Walk the Abyss is a much another for those willing to visit the Abyss and is frequently employed by the mystics to host their most secretive gatherings far from the prying eyes and ears of others.","fx":"The mystic’s spirit suffers a point of Willpower damage and leaves their body and emerges in the Abyss.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"251"},"tag":"Abyss Communion Ritual (•••••)."},"ndfLvr04qRY7VLgx":{"id":"ndfLvr04qRY7VLgx","n":"Dancer’s Anklet","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A silver anklet adding two dice to rolls involving dance when worn and visible.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"290"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (••). Aspects: The"},"nfS7OnYqPkgh5VrJ":{"id":"nfS7OnYqPkgh5VrJ","n":"Two Ducats","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"reanimation","sum":"Necromancers who wish to find out more about the Underworld without making the journey themselves often task their ghouls to make it for them.","fx":"On a Win, the subject has been successfully expelled into the Shadowlands and may normally communicate with the caster from their own physical body.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"347"},"aspects":"Duration (counted as higher by two), Number of Targets","tag":"Reanimation Ritual (••••)."},"nmejx6HJbJo4HD79":{"id":"nmejx6HJbJo4HD79","n":"The Eternal Band","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A small golden charm alerting the wearer when a single person it is attuned to is in danger. It must be reset each time by sprinkling it with wine.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"290"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (••). Aspects: The"},"nuX4diTboXmi1OGC":{"id":"nuX4diTboXmi1OGC","n":"Skin of the Chameoleon","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"enchantment","sum":"After painting the skin of the Gargoyle with pigment, the Gargoyle gains the ability to change colour once per scene per Rouse Check activation, gaining a three-dice bonus to Stealth unless their colour pigments no…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"301"},"tag":"Enchantment Ritual (•)."},"oJRePtmffnFf5kM5":{"id":"oJRePtmffnFf5kM5","n":"The Green One (Blood Witchcraft)","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"reanimation","sum":"The necromancer raises a dead body as a Green One.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"342"},"tag":"Reanimation Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets, Range and the following"},"oOmRqbMhW00iV6wr":{"id":"oOmRqbMhW00iV6wr","n":"Rite of Introduction","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"Chantries and other strongholds of the clan Tremere are always meant to be kept a secret, especially during the Dark Ages when the young clan was constantly under siege.","fx":"The ritualist sends an impression of their face, their name, and a short, one-sentence message to any master of a Foundation of the Chantry (see below) within the same city.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"322"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (•)."},"oVpnpVMA2wgc7d0k":{"id":"oVpnpVMA2wgc7d0k","n":"Vanity Restored","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"alchemy","sum":"Requires one hair (eyelashes work) of a subject on whom this formula will be used. Once ingested, they begin to rapidly grow hair everywhere, even fixing balding. The hair can then be cut as normal.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"262"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•)."},"obcyrQefvw7TAQKK":{"id":"obcyrQefvw7TAQKK","n":"Object Permanence","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"conjuration","sum":"Sorcerers naturally have an easier time summoning targets they have a strong connection to, such as a beloved pet or the ritual knife their mentor gifted them.","fx":"The sorcerer also does not need to exact location of the object to summon it, but a relative (like a neighbourhood).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"275"},"aspects":"Duration (how long the familiarity stays)","tag":"Conjuration Ritual (•)."},"of3vr9smKGti1oi2":{"id":"of3vr9smKGti1oi2","n":"Servitors of the Genius","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"geniusloci","sum":"Known as Kupala’s Eyes and Ears among the Transylvanian kolduny, this ritual extends the koldun’s perceptions onto the more intelligent spirits of the land, the koldun may see as they do.","fx":"While in effect for the Duration (or until the koldun leaves the location of the Rite), the koldun is able to extend their senses spirits affected by this Rite, all at once like a spiritual hivemind.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"361"},"aspects":"Distance (counted as higher by one), Duration, Number of Targets, Passengers","tag":"Genius Loci Ritual (•••)."},"orXkKdpRaw9uCmWw":{"id":"orXkKdpRaw9uCmWw","n":"Teddy Bear of Resting","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A stuffed animal guaranteeing restful sleep to anyone sleeping in the same bed as it. They recover an additional point of Superficial Willpower when the awake.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"289"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•). Aspects: The"},"owxzzTtGZsEzvDJZ":{"id":"owxzzTtGZsEzvDJZ","n":"Sword against the Restless Dead","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A sword for ghost-slaying. It has a core of liquid mercury and can harm ghosts on in the Shadowlands, damage to them as they were alive.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"292"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (••••). Aspects: The"},"p37ONO7o6sE5Pjj5":{"id":"p37ONO7o6sE5Pjj5","n":"Haunting (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"haunting","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"373"},"aspects":"Duration, Range (as a radius of how big a single casting of an illusion may be; melee is something that fits in a plam), Senses and the following two:","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"p53tPctyvYUxcPHD":{"id":"p53tPctyvYUxcPHD","n":"Quick Cure","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"alchemy","sum":"A cure for the common cold or flu, at least for 24 hours. It can also halve the recovery time for the illness.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"262"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•)."},"pBo7dSEMMHuElyy4":{"id":"pBo7dSEMMHuElyy4","n":"Alter Temperature (Major)","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"weathercontrol","sum":"Alter Temperature (Major). The local temperature can be changed by up to 20 degrees Fahrenheit or 10 degrees Celsius.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"358"},"tag":"Weather Control Ritual (•••)."},"pDZnPa0ccolTLJr0":{"id":"pDZnPa0ccolTLJr0","n":"Fire’s Wheal","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"elementalforces","sum":"Fire is one of the most dangerous hazards, capable of destroying even the almost-indestructible supernatural creatures With this ritual, the magician can give protection against fire of all sorts.","fx":"The targets are protected from fire damage equal to double the protection Aspect (which cannot stack). Once Protection is spent, the subject burns as normal.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"286"},"aspects":"Duration, Number of Targets, Protection","tag":"Elemental Forces Ritual (••)."},"pIa0ojD6OKPc06So":{"id":"pIa0ojD6OKPc06So","n":"Projectile Magnet","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A pocket flask that attracts bullets and arrows when carried in a breast pocket. It can only take one impact, but it subtracts three points of damage before halving before being destroyed.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"291"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (••••). Aspects: The"},"pLeoFVGlNlipSIeg":{"id":"pLeoFVGlNlipSIeg","n":"Mastery of the Undead Form","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"corpseinthemonster","sum":"The necromancer learns complete control over their undead body.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"373"},"tag":"Corpse in the Monster Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Corpse State"},"pUdaRvhZVgrE4aXN":{"id":"pUdaRvhZVgrE4aXN","n":"All-Cleaner","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A handkerchief which can clean any mundane spill or stain, including blood.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"291"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••). Aspects: The"},"paOEkMB5UEBAstSz":{"id":"paOEkMB5UEBAstSz","n":"Seizure","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"masteryofthemortalshell","sum":"The victim experiences a seizure.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"330"},"tag":"Mastery of the Mortal Shell Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets, Range and the following."},"pejbtAO2NaRMVd6L":{"id":"pejbtAO2NaRMVd6L","n":"Purgation","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"Victim throws up a number of Hunger’s worth of blood equal to the Hunger Aspect or the margins, whichever is lower. Hunger is vomited one point per turn. While vomiting, victims halve their perception pools.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"319"},"tag":"Lifeblood Special Effect (••). Aspects: Range, Number of Targets, Hunger (see below) and the following special effects"},"pfpcW8yTDmIVXeej":{"id":"pfpcW8yTDmIVXeej","n":"Path of Skulls (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"pathofskulls","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"375"},"aspects":"Number of targets (skulls targeted), duration (the duration aspect is always counted as one higher) as well as one of the following Special Effects:","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"ppWuUt3kNHEl7Vft":{"id":"ppWuUt3kNHEl7Vft","n":"Restless Medias","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"transylvaniankraina","sum":"From time to time, the ground beneath the village of Medias will shake and roil, tearing buildings from their moorings and sometimes even killing the unwary.","fx":"Upon successful completion of the rite, the koldun is granted the power to use Restless Medias by making a Rouse Check and a Spell Test using the Aspects of Damage, Distance, Duration and Restless Medias (Aspect 5).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"369"},"aspects":"None, but the Spell uses Damage, Distance, Duration (one rank is one turn of effect)","tag":"Transylvanian Kraina Ritual (•••••)."},"pwJZtlqDw2inWZVV":{"id":"pwJZtlqDw2inWZVV","n":"Calvaria Emissa","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"pathofskulls","sum":"Path of Skulls Special Effect (•). Aspects: Number of targets (skulls targeted), duration (the duration aspect is always counted as one higher) as well as one of the following","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"375"},"tag":"Path of Skulls Special Effect (•). Aspects: Number of targets (skulls targeted), duration (the duration aspect is always counted as one higher) as well as one of the following"},"pyVTG3NG05M7l9sm":{"id":"pyVTG3NG05M7l9sm","n":"Mutate Vegetation","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"thegreenpath","sum":"The Green Path Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets (individual statblock as targets), Range and Green Power","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"353"},"tag":"The Green Path Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets (individual statblock as targets), Range and Green Power"},"qTsb5he1KSJWYpyR":{"id":"qTsb5he1KSJWYpyR","n":"Foxfire","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"necromancy","sum":"Folktales speak of sorcerer’s hut emitting an eerie bright-green light from a specially crafted candle to attract spirits.","fx":"The green fire shines brightly and may be seen from Distance in the Shadowlands, possibly attracting curious ghosts.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"335"},"aspects":"Distance, Duration","tag":"Necromancy Ritual (••)."},"qXkYGd7N4cXBPhlz":{"id":"qXkYGd7N4cXBPhlz","n":"Haunting","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"necromancy","sum":"The caster binds a ghost within the location, either within a room they’re in or in the building for the rest of Duration.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"333"},"tag":"Necromancy Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Duration and the Necromancy Special Effects."},"qYnCcNJJgzj1QOvm":{"id":"qYnCcNJJgzj1QOvm","n":"Conjuration (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"conjuration","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"273"},"aspects":"As this Path is composed of two primary spells, there is a set and system for each of them. The main difference is between application of Range to move objects close to the sorcerer and Distance to move them from far away, referred to as as summoning or conjuration.","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"qZQL2hR96RrYelwD":{"id":"qZQL2hR96RrYelwD","n":"Taunt","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"battle","sum":"Make the Spell Test against the opponent’s Wits + Resolve, on a win they take a -2 dice penalty to attacking anybody other than you.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"267"},"tag":"Battle Special Effect (••). Aspects: Number of Targets, Range (as a radius)"},"qfkakz6ciq7kArnx":{"id":"qfkakz6ciq7kArnx","n":"Blade of the Void","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"(prerequisite: Abyssal Blade) As Abyssal Blade, but the blade also avoids any protections from supernatural powers such as Fortitude. Natural resistances of vampires, demonic gifts and so on cannot be bypassed, however.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"255"},"seq":"After a month and a night, the blade rapidly corrodes and becomes useless. The ritual may be repeated prior to the blade’s expiry, however.","tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Only"},"qk8Tvt4AtAmJkZmS":{"id":"qk8Tvt4AtAmJkZmS","n":"Revealing the Crimson Trail","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"The ritual allows a vampire to easily spot traces of spilled blood, no matter how insignificant or old.","fx":"If the ritual is successful, the vampire can clearly see any spilled blood, dried or not, as long as they (or somebody else) keep looking through the eye of the needle.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"321"},"aspects":"Duration","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (•)."},"qlnaNgRbhEEo9DjW":{"id":"qlnaNgRbhEEo9DjW","n":"Better Bullets","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"enchantment","sum":"Bullets that increase the damage modifier by +1. Each success on the Enchantment roll creates one turn’s worth of bullets.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"289"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (••). Aspects: The"},"r0NYl4pbK1Q0xG3I":{"id":"r0NYl4pbK1Q0xG3I","n":"Hawk Amulet","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A silver chain bearing a hawk’s eye medallion with a chrysoprase in that can, once per day, add 2 dice to a long-distance sight-based Awareness rolls.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"289"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•). Aspects: The"},"r1sRPZPIfC8H5KQK":{"id":"r1sRPZPIfC8H5KQK","n":"Writ of Passage","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"bindingsummoningandwarding","sum":"A sorcerer probably does not want their guest to be shocked by just about every protective spell they set within their home, not to mention that the standard way of excluding people from effects of wards by using their…","fx":"Win on the Ritual Test allows a target carrying the copy of the permission to pass unharmed through the wards the sorcerer designated at the creation of the permission (any and all of the…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"272"},"aspects":"Duration (ranks count as doubled), Number of Targets","tag":"Binding, Summoning and Warding Ritual (••)."},"rNubSzTL649nW7G8":{"id":"rNubSzTL649nW7G8","n":"Unending Wealth","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A money pouch that never quite empties.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"293"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: The"},"rQrtIqyVmX7WPTrt":{"id":"rQrtIqyVmX7WPTrt","n":"Fetter Punishment (Giovanni)","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"necromancy","sum":"Any damage dealt to a Fetter is transferred to the ghost.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"333"},"tag":"Necromancy Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: Duration and the Necromancy Special Effects."},"rYz6UYqXcAhl08PQ":{"id":"rYz6UYqXcAhl08PQ","n":"Vampire Repellant","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"alchemy","sum":"Same as Beast Repellent, but against Cainites, ghouls and revenants. Uses garlic.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"266"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•••••)."},"rpFFd1dC41YQA52x":{"id":"rpFFd1dC41YQA52x","n":"Blood Mastery","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"Having its roots in the days when the Tremere were a house of mortal magicians, Blood Mastery allows the thaumaturge to utilise sympathetic magic in order to gain advantage over their target by symbolically crushing their blood.","fx":"Once it is broken by the thaumaturge, the they instantly gain a die bonus to all rolls against the target for the remainder of the Duration.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"320"},"aspects":"Duration","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (•)."},"rrCvI3Ec7l1WORit":{"id":"rrCvI3Ec7l1WORit","n":"Subvert","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"corruption","sum":"Corruption Special Effect (••). Aspects: Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special conditions), Number of Targets, Range and the Special Effects described below.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"279"},"tag":"Corruption Special Effect (••). Aspects: Duration (count as higher by one, can be ended sooner by resistance or special conditions), Number of Targets, Range and the Special Effects described below. This form of casting requires either eye contact (Resolve + Intimidation vs the target’s Wits + Awareness) or for the sorcerer to make a certain hand gesture (detectable by Wits + Occult vs. the sorcerer’s Wits + Subterfuge)."},"s4nE37Ck6UyantFA":{"id":"s4nE37Ck6UyantFA","n":"Future-Seeing Drugs","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"alchemy","sum":"An enhanced form of LSD, weed or incense that lets the taker either see a vision of the future or discover connections between disparate elements within the story.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"265"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (••••)."},"sKqejcEXp9lzBSCE":{"id":"sKqejcEXp9lzBSCE","n":"The Green Path (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"thegreenpath","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"353"},"aspects":"Duration, Number of Targets (individual statblock as targets), Range and Green Power Special Effects:","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"sOp7jNgL2eN6CmZF":{"id":"sOp7jNgL2eN6CmZF","n":"Sobering Tonic","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"alchemy","sum":"A tonic that instantly sobers the drinker up, no matter how drunk they are. The user does not suffer the negative effects of alcohol and drugs anymore.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"262"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•)."},"sPUHm4eBgcpJK8Sg":{"id":"sPUHm4eBgcpJK8Sg","n":"Strength Enhancer","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"alchemy","sum":"A metabolic accelerator that raises Strength and Stamina by one each. Any mortal who takes it will be hungry during the time to fuel the change. Attributes can go above above 5.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"265"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (••••)."},"sVEuZHRq1xoYetmq":{"id":"sVEuZHRq1xoYetmq","n":"Thaumaturgical Forensics","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"biothaumaturgy","sum":"Much like modern forensics, the thaumaturge takes a sample of the target’s body and examines it carefully, yielding a wealth of information to the user that they may then exploit or use to diagnose and treat ailment.","fx":"For every margin, the sorcerer can ask a single question and get a truthful answer from the storyteller.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"370"},"tag":"Biothaumaturgy Ritual (•)."},"sXI6vAiuXHtHiY8x":{"id":"sXI6vAiuXHtHiY8x","n":"Werewolf Recovery","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"alchemy","sum":"The drinker heals two points of Superficial or one point of Aggravated Health damage per turn (at its start) for the rest of the story.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"266"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•••••)."},"saGc5q1YPZCbg2mV":{"id":"saGc5q1YPZCbg2mV","n":"Treasured Ornaments","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"transylvaniankraina","sum":"Transylvania is the land of many tales, finding itself placed between the regions that have seen countless great deeds. Treasured Ornaments awakens the spirit of every ornament with a colorful past in the koldun’s haven.","fx":"Upon completion of the rite, the koldun can converse with important ornaments in their haven. The effects are permanent, though leaving the spirits in situ tends to aggravate them over time.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"366"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Transylvanian Kraina Ritual (•)."},"shO0O9MfKNwkqi4x":{"id":"shO0O9MfKNwkqi4x","n":"Communal Vigour","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"Based on sanguinary properties similar to the Vaulderie, this Ritual allows a Pack Priest to share their Blood Potency with their pack, while strengthening their own ability to keep those packmates in line.","fx":"The priest tears a nail from their finger and breaks it into pieces, one for each member of the Pack.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"326"},"aspects":"Duration","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (•••)."},"shcXALQ22jhWDysq":{"id":"shcXALQ22jhWDysq","n":"Grave of the Marea Neagra","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"blackseakraina","sum":"The Scythians of old had their own name for the great sea around which they dwelt: axšaina, which translates to “unlit” to our ears.","fx":"Upon successful completion of the rite, the koldun is granted the power to use Grave of the Marea Neagra by splashing their blood into a pool of body large enough to contain their volume,…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"364"},"aspects":"None, but the Spell uses Duration","tag":"Black Sea Kraina Ritual (••)."},"shvJG9N1RQJHfVn4":{"id":"shvJG9N1RQJHfVn4","n":"Bloodwine","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"alchemy","sum":"In addition to the Rouse Check activation cost, this formula mixes alcohol and one or more Hunger’s worth of blood which must be from the same creature.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"262"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (••)."},"t1PrXn2UIQK49CgI":{"id":"t1PrXn2UIQK49CgI","n":"Evoke Hunger","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"If the victim possesses Hunger tracker, they gain additional Hunger dice equal to the Hunger Aspect or the margins, whichever is lower.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"319"},"tag":"Lifeblood Special Effect (•). Aspects: Range, Number of Targets, Hunger (see below) and the following special effects"},"tFJSBV0FlIqdWe23":{"id":"tFJSBV0FlIqdWe23","n":"Rally","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"battle","sum":"All targets in range regain half rounded up path rating Superficial Willpower damage (only if said Willpower damage was sustained during the current scene).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"268"},"tag":"Battle Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Number of Targets, Range (as a radius)"},"tJhkcpf6KdE6XrCJ":{"id":"tJhkcpf6KdE6XrCJ","n":"Parting the Veil","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"necromancy","sum":"Said to have been first practiced at temples as sacrifices to the other side, Parting the Veil creates a bright blue flame in the Shadowlands that, when entered through the Skinlands, transports mortals to the other side.","fx":"Before making the Ritual roll, the caster must make a fire frenzy check against a Difficulty of 2 as they douse the flames with their own blood.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"338"},"aspects":"Passengers","tag":"Necromancy Ritual (••••)."},"tKM7KZ6kfpbSsSs5":{"id":"tKM7KZ6kfpbSsSs5","n":"Tretchery of Pontos","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"blackseakraina","sum":"In order to deterr enemies from their homeland, the kolduny of the Voivodate would conjure up armies and ships on the coasts of the Black Sea by manipulating water and how it allowed light to pass.","fx":"Upon successful completion of the Rite, the sorcerer gains a number of dots into the Illusion Path up to their rating of the Black Sea Kraina.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"364"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Black Sea Kraina Ritual (•)."},"tVQuEsGwNFkTpGhb":{"id":"tVQuEsGwNFkTpGhb","n":"Know the Unnatural Beast","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"enchantment","sum":"By drinking wolf blood and blood of one who knows Sense the Beast, the Gargoyle gains Sense the Beast (Animalism 1) power.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"301"},"tag":"Enchantment Ritual (•)."},"tYoczjtWO0ewIq6l":{"id":"tYoczjtWO0ewIq6l","n":"Shallow Slumber","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"reanimation","sum":"By temporarily dimming the vitality of their Blood, this ceremony can shorten a vampire’s time spent in torpor. Some even prepare themselves with this Ritual, in anticipation of future misfortune.","fx":"So long as the sigils remain on the target’s body, for each success in the margin on the Ritual, their Blood Potency counts as one lower for the purpose of torpor duration and premature awakening.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"346"},"aspects":"Duration (counted as double)","tag":"Reanimation Ritual (•••)."},"tamG5kuMd6lkaEAT":{"id":"tamG5kuMd6lkaEAT","n":"Extingish Vitae","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"Increases the targets Hunger equal to the Hunger Aspect or margins, whichever is lower.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"319"},"tag":"Lifeblood Special Effect (••). Aspects: Range, Number of Targets, Hunger (see below) and the following special effects"},"tdUoxIwRrOH5aIv6":{"id":"tdUoxIwRrOH5aIv6","n":"Bind","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"necromancy","sum":"Any ghost may be bound to the caster’s will. The necromancer makes their Spell Test against the ghost’s Composure + Resolve while speaking its True Name or holding its fetter.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"332"},"tag":"Necromancy Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Duration and the Necromancy Special Effects."},"tkEFGRJN7YHMpXjb":{"id":"tkEFGRJN7YHMpXjb","n":"Wrap the Shroud","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"necromancy","sum":"The caster places themselves on both sides the the Shroud, allowing them to interact with both the world of the living, but also to be harmed by both.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"333"},"tag":"Necromancy Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Duration and the Necromancy Special Effects."},"u72jFbhmRZtZEXSt":{"id":"u72jFbhmRZtZEXSt","n":"Corpse Suit","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"enchantment","sum":"The more successes caster has on the crafting Test, the nicer the Corpse Suit will look.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"291"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (••••). Aspects: The"},"uImeoP49y8Qb7ghQ":{"id":"uImeoP49y8Qb7ghQ","n":"Bind to Mortal Form","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"reanimation","sum":"Necromancers who have mastered this Ritual can extend a human life past its natural expiration date without making a ghoul out of the mortal.","fx":"Each rolled success adds a decade to the mortal’s natural lifespan, but if the test is not an overall win, or if the sorcerer fails to take the mortal’s blood to the grave within the…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"346"},"aspects":"Number of Targets, Duration","tag":"Reanimation Ritual (••••)."},"ueUsYhP9EY8bfK8v":{"id":"ueUsYhP9EY8bfK8v","n":"Bind the Accusing Tongue","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"bindingsummoningandwarding","sum":"The Tremere developed this ritual early in their ascent to power, which may help explain that ascent.","fx":"Win on the Ritual Test prevents the target from saying, writing, or otherwise directly communicating anything negative or harmful – even, or rather especially, if it’s true — about the…","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"271"},"aspects":"Duration (ranks count as doubled), Sympathetic Connection","tag":"Binding, Summoning and Warding Ritual (•)."},"vQrbEcI5Tsuud4cf":{"id":"vQrbEcI5Tsuud4cf","n":"Sing o Muse","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"enchantment","sum":"An instrument anyone can play like a master once they give a prayer to the nine Muses (by name). Those playing it count their Performance as 6.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"293"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: The"},"vbUPeTpr7AyQfEWk":{"id":"vbUPeTpr7AyQfEWk","n":"Taste of Blood","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"By tasting a drop of blood, the sorcerer can discern certain basic traits of the one to whom it belongs.","fx":"With a win, the following happens if the blood came from a creature: the sorcerer can determine the Resonance and intensity of the blood if human.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"322"},"tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (•)."},"vo7PWaj9vqH7G8m3":{"id":"vo7PWaj9vqH7G8m3","n":"Abyssal Infusion (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"252"},"aspects":"Only the following:","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"voZc2dQrovCA2mwL":{"id":"voZc2dQrovCA2mwL","n":"Subsume the Darkness","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"After meditating on Abyss, the mystic makes their Ritual Test. On a win, they may immediately spend a number of Rouse Checks to heal equal number of Aggravated Health damage or twice the amount of Superficial Damage.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"254"},"seq":"After use of this ritual, the Mystic’s blood becomes black and absorbs all light, creating a dark aura around itself. This effect clearly marks the Mystic as something terrifyingly alien.","tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (••). Aspects: Only"},"vtwofKwm0NyPQfur":{"id":"vtwofKwm0NyPQfur","n":"Borrowed Power","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"lifeblood","sum":"Nicknamed “Stolen Power” by Tzimisce kolduny, Borrowed Power allows a sorcerer to use the strength of another’s blood in order to enhance their own powers.","fx":"As the caster chants, the blood is condensed and may be placed in a small glass vial or a hallow object. As many doses are made with this ritual as Hunger was used.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"324"},"aspects":"Duration (how long the created potion remains potent; Count ranks as doubled).)","tag":"Lifeblood Ritual (•••)."},"vu7kkAj5bHlGwIKW":{"id":"vu7kkAj5bHlGwIKW","n":"Burebista’s Throne","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"transylvaniankraina","sum":"Legend has it that King Burebista, who terrorized the Greeks for centuries — first as the mortal king of Dacia, and later as a mighty koldun — built a great throne atop a mountain peak from which he could survey all his lands and track the movements of all his enemies.","fx":"On successful completion of the Rite, the koldun can send their senses soaring high into the air, or extend them beyond their body; how far the koldun may shift the point from which their perceive depends on the Aspect of Distance.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"366"},"aspects":"Duration, Distance, Range","tag":"Transylvanian Kraina Ritual (•)."},"vzB96AGiNBacyZzy":{"id":"vzB96AGiNBacyZzy","n":"Clinging of the Insect","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"alchemy","sum":"The one who ingests this formula is able to cling to walls and ceiling for the rest of the night. They must cling to the surface with both hands and feet; they move at approximately half their usual rate.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"265"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (••••)."},"w07ZYKdBrCBj7ZDV":{"id":"w07ZYKdBrCBj7ZDV","n":"Scientia Surrepta","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"pathofskulls","sum":"Path of Skulls Special Effect (•). Aspects: Number of targets (skulls targeted), duration (the duration aspect is always counted as one higher) as well as one of the following","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"375"},"tag":"Path of Skulls Special Effect (•). Aspects: Number of targets (skulls targeted), duration (the duration aspect is always counted as one higher) as well as one of the following"},"w3wHJSG1RRp0iuYh":{"id":"w3wHJSG1RRp0iuYh","n":"Twitch","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"reanimation","sum":"The necromancer forces movement of a corpse, usually a roll or a twitch. If it still has vocal cords, the body may be forced to speak.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"341"},"tag":"Reanimation Special Effect (•). Aspects: Duration, Number of Targets, Range and the following"},"wCqBASLnddhsmsRL":{"id":"wCqBASLnddhsmsRL","n":"Kupala’s Exhalation","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"transylvaniankraina","sum":"In the Berca basin, near the Eastern Orthodox monastery of Ratesti, vegetation ceases to grow and the strange gasses of the underworld bubble up into our world, forming tiny cones of mud that quickly harden while they exhale their frigid breaths.","fx":"Upon successful completion of the rite, the sorcerer is able to activate Kupala’s Exhalation. by making a Rouse Check and performing a Spell Test with Aspects: Damage, Duration, Number of Targets, Range and Kupala’ Exhalation (Aspect 2).","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"368"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Transylvanian Kraina Ritual (••••)."},"wJEozRqFlvpbUCQ0":{"id":"wJEozRqFlvpbUCQ0","n":"Harvest Servant","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"thegreenpath","sum":"Through the use of a viscera garden's properties, the sorcerer is able to imbue false life into bodies made of roots and cellulose, creating little furtive helpers capable of handling small tasks and chores.","fx":"It has the intelligence of a child and will be affectionate towards the first being it sees when it awakens, following any order it may be given to the letter.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"354"},"aspects":"Duration","tag":"The Green Path Ritual (••)."},"wYOksiAqn35ZPlzH":{"id":"wYOksiAqn35ZPlzH","n":"Obsidian Mirror","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A polished mirror that extends the user’s perceptions. All rolls of scrying and powers like those of Auspex (e.g. Sense the Unseen, Scry the Soul, Clairvoyance) or some of Dementation (e.g.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"291"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••). Aspects: The"},"wcK68I5YgGN95Pna":{"id":"wcK68I5YgGN95Pna","n":"Ritual of the Unearthed Fetter","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"necromancy","sum":"A necromancer may track down the location of a specific fetter if they possess certain body parts of a wraith.","fx":"If the person whose bone was used has not become a wraith, the needle does not move. Compass lasts until destroyed.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"335"},"aspects":"Distance, Duration","tag":"Necromancy Ritual (••)."},"wp0HtFgf96UI1qR7":{"id":"wp0HtFgf96UI1qR7","n":"Megafauna Transformation","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"shapeshifting","sum":"The Path of Shapeshifting allows the caster to assume animal forms, including partial transformations. But in the end, the caster can normally only fully transform into a normal animal or a human.","fx":"The transformation occurs as with the Path Spell, including the Control Test.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"352"},"aspects":"As the Path spell","tag":"Shapeshifting Ritual (•••••)."},"x7l7Jjp8ByG4J5q9":{"id":"x7l7Jjp8ByG4J5q9","n":"Alter Temperature (Minor)","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"weathercontrol","sum":"Alter Temperature (Minor). Alter the local temperature by up to 10 degrees Fahrenheit or 5 degrees Celsius.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"358"},"tag":"Weather Control Ritual (••)."},"xAivL1iRupWaulkF":{"id":"xAivL1iRupWaulkF","n":"Orpheic Sujourn","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"necromancy","sum":"Usually, necromancers can not bring back items from the Underworld which is why various necromantic bloodlines spending time in the Shadowlands have developed a Ritual that would allow them to do just that.","fx":"The next time the necromancer enters the Underworld, they may bring out items up to or equal to the mass of the object they sacrificed.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"339"},"aspects":"Weight","tag":"Necromancy Ritual (•••••)."},"xESQTE900DM21yuk":{"id":"xESQTE900DM21yuk","n":"Temportal","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"enchantment","sum":"As a master of their own Haven, the sorcerer may reshape it so that the doorways lead to rooms other than those they are physically connected to.","fx":"This ritual may be performed only in a Haven upon which the sorcerer’s Dedicate the Haven (level 4 ritual) is in effect.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"298"},"aspects":"Permanent due to Dedicate the Haven.","tag":"Enchantment Ritual (••••)."},"xTZiYtIeoOx0bioR":{"id":"xTZiYtIeoOx0bioR","n":"Jolt","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"healing","sum":"The sorcerer magically awakens a person who is sleeping, unconscious, or comatose.","fx":"This power doesn’t heal the underlying illness, injury, or poisoning, and the patient falls unconscious again at the end of the scene if the healer doesn’t resolve the underlying issue.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"316"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Healing Ritual (••)."},"xbca07okZ3rieFkW":{"id":"xbca07okZ3rieFkW","n":"Cursed Eucharist (Rosselini)","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"necromancy","sum":"The caster may perform Bite Attacks on ghosts and physically harm them in that manner, dealing damage as they normally would. The caster may also feast on the ectoplasm of ghosts.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"332"},"tag":"Necromancy Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Duration and the Necromancy Special Effects."},"xdpe2qbgtRrm17zu":{"id":"xdpe2qbgtRrm17zu","n":"Strike True","d":"sorcery","lv":2,"path":"battle","sum":"All targets in range ignore Called Shot penalties.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"267"},"tag":"Battle Special Effect (••). Aspects: Number of Targets, Range (as a radius)"},"xm71JcuORFhqSYRb":{"id":"xm71JcuORFhqSYRb","n":"The Sorcery of Life","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"reanimation","sum":"In Setite apocrypha, it is said Set’s favored servants were the immortal entities known as Bane Mummies.","fx":"One proto bane mummy counts as a 5-dot retainer and its owner may increase its Divinity by spending experience points.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"350"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Reanimation Ritual (•••••)."},"xxdr2cGboYfa0RRf":{"id":"xxdr2cGboYfa0RRf","n":"Waterspout","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"weathercontrol","sum":"Creates a waterspout with a Strength rating equal to the total number of successes on the casting roll to harm ships, drag or pull people. Attacks deal Aggravated Health damage to mortals, Superficial to others.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"359"},"tag":"Weather Control Ritual (•••••)."},"xydB8My4Uh75DSqt":{"id":"xydB8My4Uh75DSqt","n":"Torc of Hercules","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A silver torc granting superhuman Strength. The wearer gains two dots in Strength, up to 7, when using it. When not worn, it must be kept exposed to the moon whenever the moon is visible.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"292"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (••••). Aspects: The"},"yEw3PH2vnePtdJao":{"id":"yEw3PH2vnePtdJao","n":"Medium Abyssal Possession","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"abyssalinfusion","sum":"(prerequisite: Minor Abyssal Possession) identical to Minor Abyssal Possession except that the corpse raised is an Aggressive Corpse (p. XX)","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"254"},"seq":"When a corpse is raised in this manner, it is automatically hostile to everybody, but the sorcerer binds it to their will as necromancers do zombies if they possess a dot of Binding, Summoning and Warding Path. If not bought as a Retainer (one dot should suffice for 3 cadavers), the zombie becomes aggressive and uncontrollable after a story as the bond breaks.","tag":"Abyssal Infusion Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Only"},"yFk2uz2vBvK9CV98":{"id":"yFk2uz2vBvK9CV98","n":"Bastone del Diavolo","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"necromancy","sum":"One of the most feared (by ghosts, at least) weapons at the disposal of the Giovanni and their families is the infamous “stick of the Devil”.","fx":"Do not make the Ritual roll until the target has been beaten to death by their own femur. On a Win, the curses inscribed on the femur grow noticably darker.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"337"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Necromancy Ritual (••••)."},"yFplve6gcnGXCERy":{"id":"yFplve6gcnGXCERy","n":"Memory of the Sea","d":"rituals","lv":1,"path":"blackseakraina","sum":"The Black Sea has seen many civilisations rise and fall, carefully collecting its ships and dead on its bottoms.","fx":"On successful completion of the rite, the koldun can see into the past through the perspective of water where they dripped blood, going as far back as Time Period Aspect allows it.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"363"},"aspects":"Time Period","tag":"Black Sea Kraina Ritual (•)."},"yKmuaXUYIaZYc0Fs":{"id":"yKmuaXUYIaZYc0Fs","n":"Borne by Wind","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"transylvaniankraina","sum":"Transylvanian Mountains are always surrounded by howling winds as the spirits of air sing their songs.","fx":"With one turn’s focus, they begin traveling at the speed of the wind. For precise values, google or consult the Beaufort Scale on Wikipedia.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"367"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Transylvanian Kraina Ritual (••)."},"yZV9S3IbOjKHIFFD":{"id":"yZV9S3IbOjKHIFFD","n":"Conveyance (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"conveyance","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","fx":"Note that this Path can’t penetrate hermetically sealed chambers. Teleporting others requires knowledge of their exact location.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"276"},"aspects":"In addition to the Aspects of Distance, Travel Speed, and Passengers, the following each increase or decrease the Difficulty by:","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"ycABtHmKYyh6zCYR":{"id":"ycABtHmKYyh6zCYR","n":"Strike true","d":"sorcery","lv":4,"path":"battle","sum":"All targets in range add 2 successes to a melee or brawl attack roll done per turn.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"268"},"tag":"Battle Special Effect (••••). Aspects: Number of Targets, Range (as a radius)"},"yf4VLI3UEbJY3fyq":{"id":"yf4VLI3UEbJY3fyq","n":"Shitstorm","d":"rituals","lv":2,"path":"conjuration","sum":"Sometimes, accuracy of thrown objects is not as required as simply creating a safe zone for the sorcerer and their allies. Shitstorm provides exactly that by creating a swirling shell of many small inanimate objects","fx":"This adds +1 difficulty to hit anyone covered by the effect with a ranged attack for every 2 successes on the ritual roll.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"275"},"aspects":"Area, Duration.","tag":"Conjuration Ritual (••)."},"ykLejDVndeoEdGB5":{"id":"ykLejDVndeoEdGB5","n":"Stitch Intelligence","d":"rituals","lv":5,"path":"pathofskulls","sum":"With this ritual, a necromancer literally sitches intelligence onto an animated cadaver.","fx":"The cadaver gains Social and Mental Skills and Social and Mental Attributes that of the person whose head was reanimated and stitched onto the body.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"377"},"aspects":"None","tag":"Path of Skulls Ritual (•••••)."},"yrt6OgjioR0bo6nl":{"id":"yrt6OgjioR0bo6nl","n":"Mastery of the Mortal Shell (Path)","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"masteryofthemortalshell","sum":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"329"},"aspects":"Duration, Number of Targets, Range and the following.","tag":"Roll your School of Sorcery’s Casting Pool. The Spell Test Difficulty is the sum of all Aspect ranks, halved and rounded up."},"z2QzVNfqiLL0ZO8B":{"id":"z2QzVNfqiLL0ZO8B","n":"Damascus Steel/Unobtanium","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"alchemy","sum":"An extremely strong, light, and easy to work with metal alloy. It can retain an edge forever; melee edged weapons made from it deal an additional point of damage and ignore two points of armour.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"264"},"tag":"Alchemy Ritual (•••)."},"z5rgmsOoixIAoCxC":{"id":"z5rgmsOoixIAoCxC","n":"Warding Circle of Secrecy","d":"rituals","lv":3,"path":"bindingsummoningandwarding","sum":"In Ceoris and Alamut, those who wield great secrets can do what those wielding great magical powers can not.","fx":"This ritual creates a warding circle or a zone according to Range as a radius.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"273"},"aspects":"Duration (ranks count as doubled), Range (as a Radius)","tag":"Binding, Summoning and Warding Ritual (•••)."},"z70dYJP8HPb07qUM":{"id":"z70dYJP8HPb07qUM","n":"Enthralling","d":"sorcery","lv":5,"path":"fascination","sum":"Fascination Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: In addition to the Aspects of Number of Targets, Range, and Sympathetic Connection, Fascination uses the Allure and Willbending Aspects.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"307"},"tag":"Fascination Special Effect (•••••). Aspects: In addition to the Aspects of Number of Targets, Range, and Sympathetic Connection, Fascination uses the Allure and Willbending Aspects."},"z8iWWwhDNg6Gq5K0":{"id":"z8iWWwhDNg6Gq5K0","n":"Love Potion","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"fascination","sum":"With knowledge of an upcoming social event and proper preparation, a sorcerer can make themselves quite the sensation.","fx":"A lock of hair, a dram of blood, or a sentimental personal effect is required to create the right connection to the heart in question.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"307"},"aspects":"Duration, Sympathetic Connection (optional)","tag":"Fascination Ritual (••••)."},"zWaOruX10eIJBFre":{"id":"zWaOruX10eIJBFre","n":"Amulet against Vampires","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"enchantment","sum":"Same as Amulet against Magic except that it impacts Cainite and Ghoul Disciplines (not Blood Magic)","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"290"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•••). Aspects: The"},"zbrYjcYK25TLtP9i":{"id":"zbrYjcYK25TLtP9i","n":"Ward","d":"sorcery","lv":3,"path":"necromancy","sum":"The sorcerer wards themselves or an object (up to a meter across) or creates a Warding Circe (up to three meters radius) against spirits of the dead.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"332"},"tag":"Necromancy Special Effect (•••). Aspects: Duration and the Necromancy Special Effects."},"znRhQ6RIWWU36aUX":{"id":"znRhQ6RIWWU36aUX","n":"Whirlpool/Undertow","d":"rituals","lv":4,"path":"weathercontrol","sum":"A whirlpool/undertow acts as a creature with a Strength rating equal to the total number of successes on the casting roll to harm ships, drag or pull people.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"358"},"tag":"Weather Control Ritual (••••)."},"zpoaTlaxBL6g9VSw":{"id":"zpoaTlaxBL6g9VSw","n":"Reliable Firearm","d":"sorcery","lv":1,"path":"enchantment","sum":"A custom Aim Skill weapon subtracting one from the success penalty of all called shots.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"289"},"tag":"Enchantment Special Effect (•). Aspects: The"},"JhlfzmCt7iEbFgMt":{"id":"JhlfzmCt7iEbFgMt","n":"School: Hermetic Thaumaturgy","d":"sorcery","lv":0,"sum":"Originally, the House of Tremere were a house of hermetic magi using their own will to shape the reality. After their long and secretive ritual turned into vampires to escape death, the Tremere lost access to their old dynamic magic and found themselves powerless.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"237"}},"LsPvUugiDSRFOuNZ":{"id":"LsPvUugiDSRFOuNZ","n":"School: Koldunism","d":"sorcery","lv":0,"sum":"Power is ever circular. We sacrifice of ourselves in tribute to the earth, so the earth may give of itself to us. You must bleed for your homeland, so that your homeland will bleed for you.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"240"}},"8Uz2QPWQKlKEv4g5":{"id":"8Uz2QPWQKlKEv4g5","n":"School: Mortis","d":"sorcery","lv":0,"sum":"The Cappadocians carefully guard the secret of the Mortis Discipline. Clan legend has it that the knowledge of this sorcery was handed down to the Clan’s Methuselahs by Cappadocius himself. Mortis allows its user to unlock and use the secrets of death itself.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"244"}},"F9dayzErlu0elkgm":{"id":"F9dayzErlu0elkgm","n":"School: Akhu","d":"sorcery","lv":0,"sum":"Akhu, often called Setite Sorcery by outsiders, is the ancient magical tradition of the Followers of Set. In Egypt's heyday, before its conversion to Christianity at the hands of the Roman Empire, magic was pretty much commonplace, practiced by mortal and vampire alike.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"228"}},"5cogjvsqj9D12aWQ":{"id":"5cogjvsqj9D12aWQ","n":"School: Dur-An-Ki","d":"sorcery","lv":0,"sum":"“Mastery of the Heaven and the Earth” in Sumerian, also known as Assamite Sorcery, Dur- An-Ki is considered by many to be the oldest Blood Sorcery. It is drawn from a huge variety of mortal religious traditions, allowing it to evolve as humans do.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"232"}},"8jVlyUPwymWwKXWJ":{"id":"8jVlyUPwymWwKXWJ","n":"School: Sihr","d":"sorcery","lv":0,"sum":"While Thaumaturgy and other forms of blood magic are considered to be blasphemy in Islam (as they seek a power other than God's to aid someone), many of the practitioners of Sihr believes that Sihr’s power comes through God only.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"248"}},"V9rn9BCTq8ll7bD3":{"id":"V9rn9BCTq8ll7bD3","n":"School: Abyss Mysticism","d":"sorcery","lv":0,"sum":"As pragmatic as they are ruthless, most Lasombra regard Obtenebration as a tool. It is an important tool and a gift from their founder, but ultimately just one power among many. Only the most eccentric and arcane savants among the Clan understand the true significance of their dark art.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"227"}},"Yxh57kIJo3JUAIpR":{"id":"Yxh57kIJo3JUAIpR","n":"School: Sielanic Thaumaturgy","d":"sorcery","lv":0,"sum":"Distanic themselves from the Tremere pyramid and its oppressive ways, the Telyavelic Tremere learned to utilise the power of siela, the animistic spirit latent in the earth, stone, plants, and animals of their adopted homeland.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"247"}},"Zw4cKaltinxnwJQW":{"id":"Zw4cKaltinxnwJQW","n":"School: Hacktivist Thaumaturgy","d":"sorcery","lv":0,"sum":"One of the four schools of Anarch Blood Magic, Hacktivist Thaumaturgy places technological advancements at the forefront of their study. It is a narrow practice, yet one of the more popular among the elite sorcerers within the Anarch Movement.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"235"}},"dqvPVCB5ygqwz8xL":{"id":"dqvPVCB5ygqwz8xL","n":"School: Dibu e Debu","d":"sorcery","lv":0,"sum":"Meaning, “to the gods and goddesses”, Dibu e Debu is an ancient form of sorcery predating Thaumurgy by more than a millenia. It is commonly practiced by the Mnemachian Nosferatu and is based primarily on Celtic druidism.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"231"}},"l2XLLTL7OwsIHvfH":{"id":"l2XLLTL7OwsIHvfH","n":"School: Mechanical Thaumaturgy","d":"sorcery","lv":0,"sum":"Magical clockwork, cannons and superscience. In the world where magic slides from a mage’s tongue, and especially in the middle ages when most believe in powers of the magi and witches, it might seem unusual that a group of magicians would dedicate themselves to supernatural science.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"243"}},"ldV3ksDf88Cau1Qw":{"id":"ldV3ksDf88Cau1Qw","n":"School: Fjölkynngi","d":"sorcery","lv":0,"sum":"Said to be a gift of Odin (the Aesir Odin or the vampire priest of Odin named Odin, lines blur), Fjölkynngi (meaning Witchcraft) is the magic common to Norse vampires. While it is a school, it is further split into two distinct variations: Galdr, verbal and fast, and Runeworking, slow but powerful.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"234"}},"pIg5kbzblpna89RQ":{"id":"pIg5kbzblpna89RQ","n":"School: Blood Witchcraft","d":"sorcery","lv":0,"sum":"Practiced by the Bahari, worshippers of Lilith who revere her as the mother of monsters and vampires, Blood Witchcraft is relatively common for those who know where to look.","src":{"book":"Dark Gifts: Disciplines Restored","page":"230"}}};
